{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.279439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de3264e583e09e7cff30a844987dfa1f14c6704f9c83f457940bddb69f2ec281","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] For each $M>0$, $\xi\in H$ and for any fixed $t_0\in \mathbb{R}$, the maps $G_{t_0,\xi}: v\mapsto X^{0,v}_{\cdot;t_0,\xi}$ and $G_{-\infty}: v \mapsto \cY^{0,v}$ are continuous from $S_M$ to $\sC_{t_0}$. Thus, the following sets
