{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.088051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de3c44a3be7d2c0bbd0d81252c480e852fdc68b0039cd9d54f7b55c2e61bb83f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-correspondence of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] There exists a one-to-one almost sure correspondence between a purely atomic random signed measures $\xi$ and a marked signed point process on $\mathcal{S}$, $N_\xi$ say, satisfying
	\begin{equation}
		\int_{A\times \mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}} |s|N_{\xi}(ds\times dx)<\infty\quad\textnormal{a.s.}
	\end{equation}
	for every $A\in\hat{\mathcal{S}}$; the correspondence is the following: almost surely we have that for every $A\in\hat{\mathcal{S}}$ and every $B\in \mathcal{B} (\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\})$ such that $0\notin\bar{B}$
