{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.473220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de41c01806f593df2211a9fff37b1bc1932fa27018ee8a9ced7f6901d840714c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:liftdiffusion of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_t = \exp(tL)$ and $\hat{P}_t = \exp(t \hat{L})$ be the Markov diffusion processes defined as above. We say that $\hat{P}_t$ is a lift of $P_t$ if
