{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.288321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de461ed19cec78990f9e1cd639a2896614a4dc1a325f418e28b37d3545da4dc0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 (L\'{e}pingle's inequality) of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] For every $q\in[1,\infty)$, there exists a constant $C_q<\infty$ such that, for every $p>2$, and every martingale $M:[0,\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^d$, we have
