{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.032781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de4c9dc0a5279ddfa2b6217c0ba248aabfc29074533a365d2f54b0256782712f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 21 of arXiv:2606.07290, 'Boundary behaviour of the Volterra square-root process'] For $\gamma \in (0,1]$, the function space $S_{L, \gamma}$ consists of all functions $f \in C_{\mathrm{loc}}^{\gamma}(0, T] \cap L^1(0, T)$ such that $L \ast f \in C^1(0,T])$. For $f \in S_{L,\gamma}$, the generalized fractional derivative is defined for $t \in (0, T]$ as:
