{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.909154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de5f4282c1f473bced51e3850d87877e57552c69fdb512720ac532b863052b2e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:controller of arXiv:2411.06935, 'Correction to: Multivariate CARMA processes, continuous-time state space models and comple'] For the output process $\mathbf{Y}$ of a L\'evy-driven state space model of the form (P3.5) there exist a $p\in\mathbb{N}$ and matrices $\mathfrak{A,B,C}$ of the form 
