{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.876835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de74eab9880f99460984bec99c259decc3e380cb4b7d17215970a5d558fe9690","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2609.02065, '\textbf{From Bowditch's question to Goldman's conjecture for type-preserving representatio'] \cite[Proposition 3.7]{goldman}
        Let $\Sigma = \Sigma_{g,p},$ let $\gamma$ be a separating simple closed curve on $\Sigma,$ and let $\Sigma_1$ and $\Sigma_2$ respectively be the two components of the complement $\Sigma\setminus \gamma.$ 
