{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.959496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de7608885cc034dc20b96dad798ae9f5c3e339841bd242671f8b11aeded260ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] Suppose the process $\mathbf{X}=\{X_n:n\geq0\}$ is defined by \eqref{111} and satisfies {\bf (C)}. Then as $n\to \infty$,  
