\end{align*}
where  $\{a_n\}$ is an integer-valued sequence satisfying $na_n^{-\gamma}l_3(a_n)\to(1-m)^\gamma\Gamma(1-\gamma)^{-1}$, and $T$ is a positive random variable with Laplace transform $\mathrm{e}^{-s^\gamma}$ ($s>0$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.751819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de790121f6778ac4964e66b6afc1ca1e33fa731e65dce0854e84bc9d5e92f6d1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:well_posed_lin of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$. We say that SDE$(b,\sigma;s)$ enjoys
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] \emph{\textcolor{black}{weak} existence}, if there exists a solution to SDE$(b,\sigma;s,\textcolor{black}{\nu})$ for any $\nu\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$;
\item[-] \emph{\textcolor{black}{weak} uniqueness}, if, for any $\nu\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, two solutions to SDE$(b,\sigma;s,\textcolor{black}{\nu})$ have the same law;
\item[-] \emph{\textcolor{black}{pathwise} existence}, if there exists a solution to SDE$(b,\sigma;s,\textcolor{black}{\xi, W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t})$ for any $(W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t )$ Brownian motion  and any \textcolor{black}{$\xi\in m\mathcal{F}_s$};
\item[-] \emph{\textcolor{black}{pathwise} uniqueness}, if, for any pair of general solutions $(( \mathcal{F}_t)_{t},W, X)$, $( (\mathcal{F}_t)_{t},W, X')$ to SDE$(b,\sigma;s)$ with $X_s = X'_s$ almost surely, $X = X'$ almost surely.
\end{itemize} 

We say that SDE$(b,\sigma;s)$ is weakly (or pathwise) well-posed if weak (or pathwise) existence and uniqueness hold.

Finally, we say that SDE$(b,\sigma)$ is weakly (or pathwise) well-posed if SDE$(b,\sigma;s)$ is weakly (or pathwise) well-posed for any $s\in [0,T)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.225881+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de79c3170e96dab4176548b5996185505b7e77d705c0037a7333892445ef33d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor CLT of arXiv:2608.23156, 'Disc counting statistics of the real Ginibre ensemble'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm: cumulants of the paper), as $N\to\infty$,
