{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.332480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de980e41c320f1cebbf8cc4bd38a3c4102994e94b2f0c824a44edff4e9f878ef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2606.16259, 'Super-Arrhenius relaxation of the triangular plaquette model in any dimension'] There exist $\alpha_2>0$ and $n_2\in\mathbb N$ such that, for any $n\geqslant n_2$, there exists $w\in\{a,x^{\pm1},y^{\pm1}\}$ with the following properties:
