{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.584645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de9afd9f676dd2227118f4fd560200b62e00d2d628ed2718cb8ed5c3d37d9013","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.01333, '2609.01333'] There exists $\gamma_* \in \big(0, \, \frac{1}{2\pi} \tfrac{1}{\frac{1}{\kappa} - \frac{1}{\sqrt{\kappa^2+1}}}\big)$
