    Here $\lambda_0 > 0$ depends on the same parameters as $c_0$. 
    Further, if $R<r$, (equation e.nonvacuum_on_compacts of the paper)-(equation e.coercivity of the paper) hold even up to $t_0 = 0$, with constants that also depend on $r-R$ and deteriorate as $R \uparrow r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.161069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dea8cdca38c18b38ec817264f8946c8e55a8e58e9cdc24a27804d1723c2297fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.16795, '2604.16795'] Under Assumption {\rm\ref{A0}}, if
