{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.439196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_deb18ab781d8ef37b02ca8fa78576a87446c2bcd333ef6f029f6ca9c550f4145","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:PI of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Fix $p \geq 1$ and let $\mathcal{F}_p$ and $\Gamma_p$ be as in (1)-(2) of Definition (def:SSS of the paper).
    For a given scale function $\Psi$, we say that the pair  $(\mathcal{F}_p,\Gamma_p)$ satisfies the \emph{Poincar\'e inequality} (eq:PI of the paper) if there are constants $C,\sigma \geq 1$ satisfying the following condition.
