{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.441866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debb1639ec89c020a2faf3aeaf96f2250f2f461b8e514276b857f69b8984f88a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition arf_prop of arXiv:2608.25513, 'Adaptive Regularization for Random Features: A Neighboring Early-Stopping Rule with Oracle'] Suppose Assumptions (ass1 of the paper)--(ass5 of the paper) hold. Let $0<\widetilde\lambda\leq\lambda\leq1$ satisfy
\begin{align}
\tilde{\lambda} \geq 4\kappa^2/|D| \ \text{and} \ \max\{{\cal U}_{D,\lambda,\delta},{\cal U}_{D,\tilde{\lambda},\delta} \}\leq 1/2,
\end{align} 
If the number of random features $M$ satisfies
\begin{align}
M\gtrsim 
\begin{cases}
c_{\mathrm{RF}}\widetilde\lambda^{-\alpha}\log\frac{384\kappa^3|D|}{\delta}, & 0<r<\frac12,\\
c_{\mathrm{RF}} \widetilde\lambda^{-[(2r-1)(1+\gamma-\alpha)+\alpha]}\log\frac{384\kappa^3|D|}{\delta}, & \frac12\leq r\leq1,
