{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.491499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ded0b24abc687f6be1e75e5e5729a4e295ad5b8ae5a6a1a8e047bf74a14098cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 229 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] If $H = 3$ and $\theta_{g,h} = \theta > 0$ for all $g,h \in \{1,2,3\}$, we have
\[
\mathcal{F}(z,w) = \frac{1}{4\theta\sigma(z)\sigma(w)}\left(\frac{\sigma(z) - \sigma(w)}{z - w}\right)^2 + \frac{\hat{P}(z,w) + c_{0,0} + c_{0,1}(z + w) + c_{1,1}zw}{\theta\sigma(z)\sigma(w)}.
\]
with the polynomials
\begin{equation}
 \begin{split}
\hat{P}(z,w) & = \frac{1}{4}\left(-(z^2 + wz + w^2)^2 + \mathsf{e}_1(z + w)(z^2 + zw + w^2) - \mathsf{e}_2(z + w)^2 + \frac{3\mathsf{e}_3}{2}(z + w) - \mathsf{e}_4\right), \\
Q_0(z) & = \frac{z^4}{2} - \frac{3\mathsf{e}_1z^3}{8} + \frac{\mathsf{e}_2z^2}{4} - \frac{\mathsf{e}_3z}{8}, \qquad Q_1(z) = \frac{z^3}{4} - \frac{\mathsf{e}_1 z^2}{8} + \frac{\mathsf{e}_3}{8}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}
The remaining constants are solution of the system of equation for $h \in \{1,2\}$:
\begin{equation}
\oint_{\gamma_h} \frac{(c_{0,0} + c_{0,1}z)\dd z}{\sigma(z)} = \oint_{\gamma_h} \frac{Q_0(z) \dd z }{\sigma(z)} \qquad \textnormal{and}\qquad \oint_{\gamma_h} \frac{(c_{0,1} + c_{1,1}z) \dd z}{\sigma(z)} = \oint_{\gamma_h} \frac{Q_1(z)\dd z}{\sigma(z)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.807051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ded5fdf55553d1de4bc498a5fbbf88271e65ac43bf8005be91e4ab32e9773024","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] Let $0<a\le b<1$ and $A=[a,b]$. For any $n\ge 0$ and any real numbers $0=s_0< s_1 < s_2 < s_n<t=s_{n+1}$, conditionally to the event $\{ e_1^\varepsilon \ge t\}$, the random vector
