{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590544+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dee7d1a017b89fd060100d4ae0b5b735a8865fedc4191dcf6b3e8c15f89ec9b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LASS of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $X^{(n)}_H$ be an $n$-MFSM satisfying Assumption~(ass:params of the paper)
with $H \in \mathcal{C}^n(\mathbb{R})$ (i.e., $H$ is $n$-times continuously
differentiable; for $n=1$ this is equivalent to $\beta > 1$).
Then for each $t_0 \in \mathbb{R}$:
\begin{equation}

\left\{
\frac{X^{(n)}_H(t_0 + \varepsilon\tau)
  - \displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{X^{(n,k)}_H(t_0)}{k!}\,
  (\varepsilon\tau)^k}
{\varepsilon^{H(t_0)}}
\right\}_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}}
\overset{\mathrm{f.d.d.}}{\longrightarrow}
\bigl\{Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}(\tau)\bigr\}_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}}
\quad \text{as } \varepsilon \to 0^+,
\end{equation}
where $Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}$ is an $n$-FSM (in the sense of [Kawai2016])
with constant Hurst parameter $H(t_0)$ and stability index $\alpha$,
whose moving-average representation is
\begin{equation}

Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}(\tau)
= \int_\mathbb{R}
\frac{(\tau-u)_+^{H(t_0)-1/\alpha}}{\Gamma(H(t_0)+1-1/\alpha)}
\,dM_\alpha(u).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

