{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.889975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_def7167b82f3425cf260fc47bfd777f0b0d03274298c91a6ef6b9349cd9265bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:detjacobian of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $\mu$ be a finite Borel measure on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and assume that $\mu$ is not absolutely continuous
