{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.006811+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df2fe780eb65d95327aef1525b8dc7e983bb58428a3f8d08f02af938db0b5ce4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm7a of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Let $k \ge 3$ be an odd integer, $k_n=k$ for all $n$ and $r$ be a positive integer. Then for all sufficiently large $n$, 
