{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.777631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3eeb8efb00ddfc6571e4d745a432e0f0023ef32ee3e07343f54bbf3e4db2f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2609.02225, '\textbf{The direct moving plane method for weak solutions of the fractional $p$-Laplacian}'] There exists \(c_H=c_H(n,s,p)>0\) such that, for every \(\lambda\in\mathbb R\) and \(x\in\Sigma_\lambda^-\),
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\Sigma_\lambda}
