Let \(I\subset\mathbb R\) be a bounded interval and set $L_I:=\max\left\{1,\sup_{\mu\in I}|\mu|\right\}$. Then, for every \(\lambda\in I\) and every \(x\in\Sigma_\lambda^-\) with \(|x|\ge L_I\), there exists \(c_H'=c_H'(n,s,p)>0\) such that
\begin{equation}
   \int_{\Sigma_\lambda}
