{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.057156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df425a7616b0361b707e0b3db514589fc3e648dfb192467c330efabae9f9870d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:R<p/q of arXiv:2607.14062, 'Gilbert's disc model conditioned on the square lattice'] Let $a,b\in \mathbb{Z}_{>0} = \{1,2,\dots\}$, let $R \in (0, a/b)$, and let $u_0,\ldots,u_n\in\mathbb{Z}^2$. If there exists $P\in\mathcal P$ such that $u=(u_0,\ldots,u_n)$ is a path of $\Gamma_{p,R}^{\texttt{CN}}(P)$ (resp.\ of $\Gamma^{\texttt{NN}}_{p,R}(P)$), then 
