{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.393359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df45b11f81c7571f74a0591116316126d7b4419dd0d96385f4c2b35686c3b7b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:F of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] There exists $C>0$ such that, for all $1/2<\lambda \le 7/8$, $T>0$ and $N$ large enough,
