{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.569579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df46a9329bb32c6e0e16c6580ed3668567197610f51958581e1f387142308ced","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2606.14170, 'Uniform-in-time error estimates for McKean-Vlasov SDEs with common noise and stochastic al'] Let $\sigma_0\sigma_1\neq 0$. Suppose that Assumptions \ref{A1}, \ref{A2}, \ref{S1}-\ref{N2-1} hold with $\lambda_1>2\lambda_2$ and $\overline\lambda_1>2\overline\lambda_2$. Then there exists $C>0$ such that for any $\lambda_2\in [0,\lambda_2^*), L\in[0,L^*]$, $h\in (0,h^*]$,  $t>0$ and $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{W}_1\big(\mathcal{L}(\mu_t^i),\mathcal{L}(\overline \nu_t^{i,N,h})\big)\le C\left\{{\rm e}^{-\lambda_0t}\mathbb{W}_1(\mu,\nu)+\psi(N)+\left(1+\mathbb{E}|\overline X_0^{i,N,h}|^{2(l+1)^2}\right)h^{1/2}\right\}
