{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.655930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df4ee651b4a3d686bb7ad80dfb8b09280f1875c3038bc0194abc72e21cee8234","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 of arXiv:2605.07411, '\bf {A note on the equivalence of super-Poincar\'e inequality}'] The following statements hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item [(1)] Suppose that SPI \eqref{e1-1} holds with associated rate function
$\beta_{{\rm SP}}(\cdot)$ and the following weak Poincar\'e inequality holds,
\begin{equation}
\mu(f^2)-\mu(f)^2\le \beta_{{\rm WP}}(s)\E(f,f)+s\|f\|_\infty^2,\ s>0,\ f\in \D(\E),
\end{equation}
where $\beta_{{\rm WP}}:\R_+ \to \R_+$ is non-increasing.
Then $\mu$ satisfies the WLSI \eqref{e1-3}
with the rate function $\beta_{{\rm WL}}:\R_+ \to \R_+$ as
\begin{equation}
\beta_{{\rm WL}}(s):=
\begin{cases}
C_1\inf\left\{\sup_{n_0\le n \le k}n\xi_1(\delta^{-n+1});
\ k\ge n_0\ {\rm satisfies}\ C_2k\delta^{-k}\le s\right\},\ &s\in (0,s_0],\\
\beta_{{\rm WL}}(s_0),\ &s\in (s_0,+\infty).
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Here $C_1$, $C_2$, $s_0$, $\delta>2$, $n_0\ge 2$ are some positive constants,
\begin{equation}
\xi_1(t):=\inf\left\{\frac{r}{1-t\beta_{{\rm SP}}(r)};r>0\ {\rm such\ that}\ 1-t\beta_{{\rm SP}}(r)>0\right\},\ t>0,
\end{equation}
and we use the convention that $\inf \emptyset=-\infty$.

\medskip
\item [(2)] Suppose that WLSI \eqref{e1-3} holds with associated rate function $\beta_{{\rm WL}}(\cdot)$,
and there exist $\theta>0$, $\delta\ge 2$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\beta_{{\rm WL}}\left(\delta^{-n}n^{-\theta}\right)}{n}=0,
\end{equation}
then
the SPI \eqref{e1-1} is true with the following rate function,
\begin{equation}
\beta_{{\rm SP}}(s)=
\begin{cases}
C_3\inf\left\{\delta^k; k\ge n_0\ {\rm\ such\ that}\ \sup_{n\ge k}\frac{\beta_{{\rm WL}}\left(\delta^{-n}n^{-\theta}\right)}{n}\le s\right\},
\ &\ s\in (0,s_0],\\
\beta_{{\rm SP}}(s_0),\ &\ s\in (s_0,+\infty),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where $C_3$, $n_0$, $s_0$ are some positive constants.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.321436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df53252fd733b3c864189d6ad1ec23024c7fc38019648f35dfb2190f8d73c3ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 17 of arXiv:2506.21087, 'Quasi-Stationary Distributions of Interacting Dynamical Systems and their approximation'] Assume \ref{condhzero}, \ref{condhun} and \ref{condhquatre}. Then, 
