{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.816846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df88193d092609f25dd6b2456bb9920a62f1b97a1ccd59e9952a57750ae50720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-order-m of arXiv:2607.17048, 'Concentration Inequalities for Incomplete U-statistics over Arbitrary Sampling Graphs'] Suppose for every $e=(i_1, i_2,\ldots,i_m)\in E$, there exists $\sigma_e>0$ such that 
\begin{equation} 
