\end{equation}
If there exists a proper $K$-edge-coloring of $G$, then for all $t>0$, 
\[
\mathbb{P}(U-\mathbb{E}U>t)\leq \exp\biggl\{ - \frac{t^2}{2K\sum_{e\in E}\sigma_e^2}\biggr\}. 
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.338114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df8a1b05934bee3599098472f7789b5e1ddd428c4e2483b63ee0bfb63c899cd0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:limproj of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] Let $\mu,\,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(H^{-s}(\Lambda_{L}))$, for any $M\in\mathbb{N}$ we consider $P_M\#\mu=\mu^M$, $P_M\#\nu=\nu^M\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^M)$ be their associated finite dimensional projections. Then, we have the limits
