{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.368666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df9b2ec66f8a5d8c618cd9499f1afa97f42f08fcea8f5ccc17f12d9ea2ac1a59","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor topo of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $z_1, \dots, z_n$ be distinct points in $D$. Let $A \subseteq D$ be a closed connected set not containing any of the $z_j$, such that $D \setminus A$ has countably many connected components,  the boundary of each connected component is a Jordan curve, and for every $\varepsilon > 0$ only finitely many of these curves have diameter more than 
$\varepsilon$. 
Let $(A_m)_{m \geq 1}$ be closed sets that converge to $A$ in the sense that $A_m$ converges to $A$ in the Hausdorff distance, as do the outer boundary and all boundaries of the connected components of $z_1, \dots, z_n$ in $D\setminus A_m$. 

Then there exists a closed path $\gamma \subseteq A$ with $\sum_{j=1}^{n}
\indx_{\gamma}(z_j) \text{ odd}$ and $\gamma \cap \bigcup_{j=1}^n\mathbb{D}(z_j, \varepsilon_j) = \emptyset$ if for all $m \geq m_0$ the same holds for some $\gamma \in A_m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.972679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df9c771f426248ceec4e444b4ea5602b999421c68a8f163c8f735ed866b805d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.10313, '\textbf{Invariance principles for additive functionals of voter models}'] Let $\eta_0$ be distributed with $\mu_p$.
