{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.771949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dfafbe308b9f203dbdd3e23f79ae9eefc1d16a8cdd9c3537d15b24eae2c8a68d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor sufficient-inequalities-new of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $({\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ be a $(d,0)$-non-degenerate weight pair with $d\geq 1$ and assume that $r=r_{d,0}({\mathbf{a}})$ is finite.
	Assume that the following inequalities hold for all $n\geq 0$, all $q\leq q'$ in $\{0,\dots,r-1\}$, and all $s \leq s'$ in $\{0,\dots,d-1\}$,
	\begin{equation}
	\frac{b_{nd+1}}{b_{(n-1)d+1}}
	\leq
	\frac{
		\PFComp{\shift{q' d+s'}{\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}}}{nd+(d-s')}
	}{
		\PFComp{\shift{q' d+s'}{\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}}}{(n-1)d+(d-s')}}
