	where we omit the ill-defined inequality on the left when $n=0$.
	Then $({\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ is $(d,0)$-admissible, and $(\shift{qd+s}{\mathbf{a}},{\mathbf{b}})$ is $(d,\overline{d-s})$-admissible for every $s\in\{0,\dots,d-1\}$ and $q\in\{0,\dots,r-1\}$.","status":"unverified"}

