for some $c'>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.774448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e00597c711eab023d7470fa3b842455c4b86f4a46621ee324e40d932d20ce4ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For any $h\in\mathbb{R}$, there exists some $c=c(h)>0$ such that
