{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.968107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0060232e6c8335abf16970a6a6c3a4dd1563c6aead1042298c345966a28d86e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Punctured intertwining) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] For every $A\subset D$, every $y\in D$, we have:
