{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.317280+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0070fec2997342eb4533d0c2559580cb5e94ab7ac42f9b1f5737b5282362e06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem fplinax of arXiv:2411.06131, 'Non-Markovian dynamics: the memory-dependent probability density evolution equations'] Let $ X_t $ be the solution of ((mSDEline of the paper)). If $ A_t, B_t $ and $ C_t $ satisfy the conditions of Lemma (Malianx of the paper). Then the memory-dependent PDEEs for PDFs $ p(x,t) $ of the solutions $ X_t $, satisfies the following equation
