{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.179808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0210ac3547df4857374cf07ca25ac1655e8acc73558520d8c1cf98296ed5b60","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:equiv of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] For $t \geqslant 0$, let $d_{\mathrm{bal}}(t)$ and $d_{\mathrm{lab}}(t)$ denote the worst case total variation distance from stationarity at time $t$ for the $(d, n, \mu)$ balanced and labeled chains, respectively. Then, we have
