{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.905021+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e02e751b199f26ec38d1f394d28bdb2459362af9897adc2106dffbe4c544af95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:doublecurrent-loop of arXiv:2506.10765, 'A General Coupling for Ising Models and Beyond'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite connected graph and fix     $A\subset V$ with $|A|$ even, $\Omega:=\{0,1\}^E$ and $\Sigma:=\{F\subset E \mid \partial F=A\}$ be the set of subgraphs of $G$ with sources $A$. Let $f:\Omega\to 2^{\Sigma}$ be defined by $f(\omega)=\{F\subset \omega \mid \partial F=A\}$ and
	\[\rho[\omega]\propto 1\! \!1[\omega\in\mathcal{F}_A] (\ell^{A \triangle B} \cup \mathbb{P}_{t^2})[\omega],~\forall \omega\in \Omega, ~\gamma[\eta]\propto 1, ~\forall \eta\in \Sigma.\]
	Then, under the coupling measure $\mathscr{P}$ defined in Theorem (thm:generalcoupling of the paper), 
\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(a)] The marginal of $\mathscr{P}$ on $\Sigma$ is $\ell^{A}$. For each $\omega\in\Omega$ with $\omega\in\mathcal{F}_A \cap \mathcal{F}_B$, the conditional measure is given by  $\mathscr{P}[\;\cdot \mid \omega] = \mathtt{UG}^A[\omega]$, the uniform $\omega$-subgraph with sources $A$.
		\item[(b)] The marginal of $\mathscr{P}$ on $\Omega$ is $\mathbf{P}^{A,B}$.  For each $\eta\in\Sigma$, the conditional measure $\mathscr{P}[\;\cdot \mid \eta]$ is $\ell^B \cup \mathbb{P}_{t^2} \cup \delta_{\eta}$ where $\delta_{\eta}$ is the Dirac measure concentrated at $\eta$.
	\end{enumerate}
In particular, the uniform graph with sources $A$ of the double random current measure with sources $A$ and $B$ is the loop $\mathrm{O}(1)$ model with sources $A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.460594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e030ce7a664b31b99dc4177f0b71e9e4201ceb6095b2a615792930b0fc8db485","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 52 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] For any $\alpha \in \{ - 1, 0, 1 \}$, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $\varepsilon$ such that for all $F\in\mathcal{C}$, we have 
\begin{equation}
\| \mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda} F \|_{\mathcal{H}^{- 1}_{\alpha}}
     \lesssim \| F \|_{\mathcal{H}^1_{\alpha}}, \quad\| \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon F \|_{\mathcal{H}^{- 1}_{\alpha}}
     \lesssim \| F \|_{\mathcal{H}^1_{\alpha+1}}\,,
\end{equation}
and the limit 
$
\mathcal{G}F=\lim_\varepsilon \mathcal{G}^\varepsilon F,
$
exists in $\mathcal{H}^{- 1}_{0}$. Thus, $\mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda}$ (resp. $\mathcal{G}$) can be extended to a bounded operator
  $\mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda} \in L (\mathcal{H}^1_{\alpha}, \mathcal{H}^{-
  1}_{\alpha})$ (resp. $\mathcal{G}\in L (\mathcal{H}^1_{\alpha+1}, \mathcal{H}^{-
  1}_{\alpha})$) for any $ \alpha \in \{ - 1, 0, 1 \}$.
  Furthermore, the operators $\mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda}$ and $\mathcal{G}$ are antisymmetric, i.e. $\langle G,
  \mathcal{T} F \rangle_{L^2 (\mu)} = - \langle
  \mathcal{T} G, F \rangle_{L^2 (\mu)}$, for $\mathcal{T}\in\{\mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda},\mathcal{G}\}$ and
  \begin{equation}
    [\mathcal{A}_{\gamma, \lambda}, \mathcal{N}] = 0 , 
  \end{equation}
as well as
\begin{equation*}
    [\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{N}]  \in L (\mathcal{H}^1_{\alpha+1}, \mathcal{H}^{-
  1}_{\alpha}),
  \end{equation*}
  for any $ \alpha \in \{ - 1, 0, 1 \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.775485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e03104b8a6137c2b001683d03005d2eaa4352224233248c08ec0767208ca4c92","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] There is a constant $\rho>0$ such that for any integer $k\in[N(\log N)^{-1},N/2]$ and any $h\le\sqrt{\log N}$, we have
