{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.851504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e031d63662d6be43326eeac46a240b0931de0ec1fe9e401439956701db0043b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop main2_2 of arXiv:2607.10105, 'The four-dimensional Anderson model: a case study for critical SPDEs'] Let $(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n,m_\mathfrak l)$ be a fixed marked Hepp tree with multiplicities $m_\mathfrak l\geq 2$, and with both simple and compound leaves (Definition (def.mul of the paper)). Let $(y_1,\cdots,y_m)$ be a fixed vector (where $m=\sum_\mathfrak l m_\mathfrak l$), such that the multiset $\{y_1,\cdots,y_m\}=\cup_\mathfrak l \{\textrm{$m_\mathfrak l$ copies of $z_\mathfrak l$}\}$, where $(z_\mathfrak l)$ satisfies Definition (def.hepp_3 of the paper) (a); moreover, instead of Definition (def.hepp_3 of the paper) (b), we assume that for each $\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B$ and two leaves $\mathfrak l,\mathfrak l'\in\mathcal L_\mathfrak n$, we have \begin{equation}|z_{\mathfrak l}-z_{\mathfrak l'}|\leq\sum_{\mathfrak m\leq\mathfrak n}\gamma_\mathfrak m^\infty\cdot N_\mathfrak m.
