{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e05bb61adb50b0dddaaa736fe282b0268f6c7e2f93d979c34f9892c148840d7f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:central-tower of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] The truncations $\pi_N:G^{(N+1)}\to G^{(N)}$ are surjective group homomorphisms with central kernel
\begin{equation}
\ker\pi_N=\exp(\mathfrak{L}_{N+1})\cong\mathbb{R}^{\ell_d(N+1)}.
\end{equation}
Hence the representation ladder
\begin{equation}
\cdots\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N+1)}\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N)}\twoheadrightarrow\cdots
\end{equation}
is a tower of central extensions, each step forgetting exactly the top-degree free-Lie directions, of dimension the Witt number $\ell_d(N+1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.650197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e05bbc06be13c4e45f053886f2dfdb9795365da9c3454bc679a8ba278e870eac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 27 ({\cite[Corollary~2.10) of arXiv:2609.01389, 'K-stability and birational rigidity of Fano 3-fold weighted complete intersections'] {CO}}]

Let $X$ be a Fano variety of Picard number $1$ and let $\Sigma$ be a set of closed points of $X$ including all the zero dimensional maximal centers of $X$.
If $\delta_{\msp} (X) > 1$ for any closed point $\msp \in \Sigma$ and if $\alpha_{\msq} (X) \ge 1/2$ for any closed point $\msq \in X \setminus \Sigma$, then $X$ is K-stable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.993078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e05c7171ae6e1d1f908af6a22feb88264088de4c256da8b9b396fa695931533e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-LDPforXi of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Fix a window $W=[-R,R]^d$ and any $\psi\in{\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal T }_W)$.  Then, under ${{\tt Q}}^{\ssup{\Lambda_N,{\rm bc}}}$ conditioned on $\{\partial\Pi_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\Xi_{N,R})=\psi_N\}$ for some $\psi_N\to\psi$, the sequence $(\Xi_{N,R})_{N\in\mathbb{N}}$ satisfies an LDP on ${\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal L }_W\times{\mathcal S }_W)$ with speed $|\Lambda_N|$ with rate function
\begin{equation}
J_{W}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\psi}})}}}(\xi) =\begin{cases}\frac 1{|W|} H_{{\mathcal L }_W\times{\mathcal S }_W}\big(\xi\,\big|\,\Pi_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal L }})}}}({\tt Q})\otimes [\psi\otimes {\tt K}_{W}]\big)&\mbox{if }\partial\Pi_W^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\xi)=\psi\mbox{ and }\xi\in\bigcap_{k\in\mathbb{N}}{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({k}})}}}({\mathcal L }_W\times{\mathcal S }_W),\\
+\infty&\mbox{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.508402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e05d9e279fdfe20d4f7c98791390ca26bbc350fdbd8a5bc6328c81e605f28359","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:char_func of arXiv:2607.14266, 'The Swapping Mechanism for Interacting Diffusions: Framework, Comparison with Switching, a'] Let $Q(k_x,k_y,t):=\mathbb{E}[e^{i(k_xX_t+k_yY_t)}]$ with initial condition
		$(X_0,Y_0)=(x_0,y_0)$. Then
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{aligned}
				Q(k_x,k_y,t)
				&=\frac{e^{i(k_xx_0+k_yy_0)}\bigl(\kappa_-+\sqrt{\kappa_-^2+4s^2}\bigr)+2s\,e^{i(k_yx_0+k_xy_0)}}{2\sqrt{\kappa_-^2+4s^2}}\,e^{-tR_+}\\
				&\quad-\frac{e^{i(k_xx_0+k_yy_0)}\bigl(\kappa_--\sqrt{\kappa_-^2+4s^2}\bigr)+2s\,e^{i(k_yx_0+k_xy_0)}}{2\sqrt{\kappa_-^2+4s^2}}\,e^{-tR_-},
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}
		where
		\begin{equation}
			\kappa_\pm
			=\tfrac{\sigma_1^2\pm\sigma_2^2}{2}(k_x^2\pm k_y^2)
			+i(\mu_1\pm\mu_2)(k_x\pm k_y),
			\qquad
			R_\pm=\frac{2s+\kappa_+\pm\sqrt{\kappa_-^2+4s^2}}{2}.
		\end{equation}
		The complex square root is chosen with non-negative real part.","status":"unverified"}

