{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.388723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e064418923d344dd3b30258d0d9cc7edef1a09f540416889ebb2b785b11f69f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:distribution of the number of customers of arXiv:2412.06452, 'Time-dependent queue length distribution in queues fed by $K$ customers in a finite interv'] The time-dependent pmf $\pi_{\ell}(t,K)=\Pr[L(t)=\ell]$ of the queue
