{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.357845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0730ec6e9ddac305b5eb428008ab02816237cb4b5fb570def40809fa1f9e7b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Assume \eqref{H1}--\eqref{H2}. Define $\alpha(t) :=\frac{1}{4}\int_0^t\sigma(W^{\ell^\sigma}_s)^2\d s$. Let $\alpha^{-1}(t)$ be the inverse of $\alpha(t)$.\footnote{We will verify in Lemma~\ref{lem:alpha} that $\alpha$ is a.s. strictly increasing, so $\alpha^{-1}(t)$ is well-defined.} Then
