{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.219093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e082520649173c034206fe60defab96f68e155b4f9f4593f77a4f2db572b9774","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:M of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Assume that the test function $h(q)$ has bounded variation on $[0,1]$ and is such that
