{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.822814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e08bae882efc4b6f8793811d3f23ff84a065f1a4b875f90d331e43af2cb8783e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:aladavie of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1]$, $N:=\lfloor \frac1\alpha\rfloor$ and let $\mathbb X$ be an $\alpha$-branched rough path lift of $X\in\mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)$ in the sense of Definition (Def: branched rough paths of the paper). Consider $\sigma\in C^{N-1}(\mathbb{R}^n,\mathbb{R}^n\otimes(\mathbb{R}^d)^\ast)$.
