{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0da4e6a9d7f9d97ab006ff3358f997f4005f557dbd451edf1015812bed779b7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2606.04950, 'The Tricomi equation in the hyperbolic half plane under additive space-time Gaussian White'] For any $t>0$ the stochastic process $\{U(t,x)\}_{x\in\mathbb{R}}$ is second order stationary with expectation
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}[U(t,x)]=0\quad\mbox{ for all }x\in\mathbb{R}
\end{align*}
and covariance
\begin{align}
\mathtt{cov}(U(t,x),U(t,y))=\frac{1}{2\pi^2}\int_0^{+\infty}\cos(\rho |x-y|)\int_0^t|C(t,s,\rho)|^2dsd\rho\quad\mbox{ for all }x,y\in\mathbb{R}.
\end{align}
Moreover, the correlation function
\begin{align*}
r_t(h):=\frac{\mathtt{cov}(U(t,x+h),U(t,x))}{\mathbb{V}[U(t,x)]},\quad t>0,x,h\in\mathbb{R},
\end{align*}
verifies
\begin{align*}
r_t(h)=1-\alpha_t|h|+o(|h|)\mbox{ as $|h|$ tends to zero},
\end{align*}
with
\begin{align*}
\alpha_t:=\frac{\pi}{2\int_0^{+\infty}\int_0^{t}\left|C(t,s,\rho)\right|^2ds d\rho}.
\end{align*}
In particular, the stochastic process $\{U(t,x)\}_{x\in\mathbb{R}}$ admits a continuous modification. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

