{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.298275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0dc832b1af0dcc87a1782931b644f8945eb7ed75b55ed2196849a4180e35d47","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2DHD-cor6.7 of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Under the hypotheses of Lemma (2DHD-lemma6.3 of the paper). For every $\tau \in \mathbb{R}$, $D=\{D(t):t\in \mathbb{R}\}\in \mathscr{D}$, there exists $\varepsilon_0=\min\left\{\sqrt{\frac{\mu\lambda_1}{2\widehat{L}_{gv}}},\sqrt{\frac{\mu\lambda_1}{12L_g+2\mathbf{c}_4L_g+8\mathbf{c}_4\widetilde{L}_g}}\right\}$ and $T:=T(\tau,D)> 1$ such that for all $t\geq T$ and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2 \in (0,\varepsilon_0]$, the solution $ u$ of system ((2DHD-1.1 of the paper)) satisfies
	\begin{align}
		&~\mathbb{ E}\left[\|u(\tau,\tau-t,u_{\tau-t})\|_{H}^4\right]\leq \rho_5 +\rho_5\int_{-\infty}^{\tau}e^{-\widetilde{\kappa} (\tau-s)} \|f(s)\|_{H}^{4} ds,
