{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.708352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0e323e651b1626b992414dd38578b100ec0a30347dea40e748d4d818b8261bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop R_1< R_0 of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $O_n$ be the event defined in (equation definition of O_n of the paper) and $S_n$ is the random walk defined in (equation def of S_n and S_n hat of the paper). Then, for some absolute constant $C$, 
