{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.144786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0e93600c34a60580c77838b065166682e59a9ce6cd8814b8871fa0fe66add49","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 16 (Existence of the solution to \eqref{eq:Gstareq}) of arXiv:2604.06122, 'REM universality for linear random energy'] There exists $ N_{\e}>0$ such that for any $n>N_{\e}$ and $h\in \mathfrak{L}^{\e}_{n}$ and $x\in \mathfrak{R}_{n,\lambda^*}(h)$ the system of equations \eqref{eq:Gstareq} admits a solution \been{
