{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.293816+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0fef94159d272bb19f57a87cc5762fcbc2d7a4d75b2abc3eabe956c8554956a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:wpsle_ub of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] There exists $c>0$ such that if $\eta$ denotes a two-sided whole-plane ${\rm SLE}_\kappa$ in $\mathbf{C}$ from $\infty$ to $\infty$ through $0$, parameterized according to the natural parameterization with $\eta(0) = 0$, then
