as $r\to\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.771789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e101d21da9fa1009c35d1f8d9efe1006dc241577954623c0875694280ff2ba3a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cormain of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] Fix $ \beta \in (0,\infty) $ and assume that $ {\mathfrak m} $ is either a positive finite measure on $\mathbb{R}^d$, or a $\sigma-$ finite measure which is absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure, with continuous and bounded density. Fix some continuous and bounded function $g\colon\mathbb{R}^d\times \mathbb{R}^d\to(0,\infty)$ and replace $\mathbb{P}_{x,y}^\beta$ by $g(x,y)\mathbb{P}_{x,y}^\beta$ in the definition (equation Psymdef of the paper) of $\mathbb{P}_{{\mathfrak m},N}^{\ssup{{\rm sym}}}$. Then 
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] Proposition~(main of the paper) remains true. The corresponding rate function is
\begin{equation}
    \mu\mapsto I^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm sym}})}}_{W,{\mathfrak m},g}(\mu)-\langle \mu_{0,\beta},\log g\rangle-\inf_{\mu \in {\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal C }_\beta)}\Bigl\{I^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm sym}})}}_{W,{\mathfrak m}}(\mu)-\langle \mu_{0,\beta},\log g\rangle\Bigr\}.
\end{equation}

\item[(ii)] Corollary~(main2 of the paper) remains true. The corresponding rate function is
\begin{equation}
J^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm sym}})}}_{{\mathfrak m},W,g}(p)=\widetilde{J}_{g,W,N}(p)-\inf_{p\in {\mathcal M }_1(\mathbb{R} ^ d)}\{\widetilde{J}_{g,W,N}(p)\},\qquad p\in{\mathcal M }_1(\mathbb{R}^d),
\end{equation}
where 
\[\widetilde{J}_{g,W,N}(p)=\inf\limits_{q\in{\mathcal M }_1^{\ssup{{\rm s}}}(\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d)}\Big\{H(q|\overline{q}\otimes{\mathfrak m})+J^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({q}})}}(p)+\langle W, p\rangle-\langle q,\log g\rangle\Big\}.\]
