{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1092bf9e5bef854308896dcc21460e2c0ab8dd4951b59dd565040d7ced824de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $\mu$ and $\nu$ be the graph signal distributions of $G=C_n(1,\cdots, m)$ and $G'=C_n(1,\cdots, m')$, respectively. Then
