{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.446298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e12db37f6530861b762bb8278b76dcc35b6cd3433243da02fb049287d128e631","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition XY height function on a percolation configuration of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, an integer $n\geq 2$, a parameter $\lambda > 0$, two inverse temperatures $\beta_1 , \beta_2 \geq 0$ and a percolation configuration $r \in \{0,1\}^{\Lambda_L},$ we define
