{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.774818+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1364adb2d42e59d2a46ebb3c36061ca0f6149679f7d83a30e75a895b4ba3cae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma T_L_is_nice of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Under the same assumptions and the choice of $\beta_0$ as in Lemma (lemma: recursion of the paper), let $\mathcal{G}$ denote the event that $\mathbb{T}^d_m$ is nice, i.e., the $m_{k_2}$-box is nice. Then $\beta_1 \ge \beta_0$ implies
