{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.729345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e141fb3e05fe736ddaf4e6b0c6e3065e77a184ce9e96b71c07026cc909a36988","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:LMP of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] A \emph{(normal, time-homogeneous) linear Markov process} is a family $\{P^z
