{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.296754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e148045e0b7b3697624df59a20b4b19a918701745ed3fa1a44d19317100578d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem central_midpoint_stability of arXiv:2609.03129, 'A Closed-Form Formula for Consistent Lipschitz Regression on Metric Spaces with Sparse Neu'] Let $(X,\rho)$ be a metric space, let $L>0$, and let $f:X\to\mathbb{R}$ be $L$-Lipschitz. Let $K\in\mathbb{N}_+$, let $x_1,\ldots,x_K\in X$, and suppose that there exists $\eta\ge0$ such that
\begin{equation}

    \sup_{x\in X}
    \min_{k\in[K]_+}
    \rho(x,x_k)
    \le
    \eta.
\end{equation}
Let $v_1,\ldots,v_K\in\mathbb{R}$ and suppose that, for some $\Delta\ge0$, one has $\max_{k\in[K]_+}|v_k-f(x_k)|\le\Delta$.
For every $x\in X$, define
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
    U(x)
    &\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \min_{k\in[K]_+}
    \left\{
        v_k+L\rho(x,x_k)
    \right\},
    \\
    W(x)
    &\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \max_{k\in[K]_+}
    \left\{
        v_k-L\rho(x,x_k)
    \right\},
    \\
    \hat{f}(x)
    &\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
    \frac{U(x)+W(x)}{2}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
Then $U$, $W$, and $\hat{f}$ are $L$-Lipschitz and for every $x\in X$
\begin{equation}

    |\hat{f}(x)-f(x)|
\le
    \Delta+L\eta.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1482bd8abe8f617fd66b74a332380f6e9277d81962b84fee496e6ec2f358f76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma convergence of s-periods of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda_n,C^2_n) \to (\lambda, C^2) \in S^0 \cup \partial S_{1}^0$ such that $(\lambda,C^2) \neq (\frac{p-1}{2},0)$ and $\lambda<p-1$. 
