{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.541342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e173275f12e14cf0bcae1b486d12c5e2f13ac13250b8416c482617f138a498a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:Integration_by_parts of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every $\mathbf{a}, \widetilde{\mathbf{a}} \in \{0,1\}^{E_d}$ such that $\mathbf{a} \leqslant \widetilde{\mathbf{a}}$, we have 
		\begin{multline}
			\left \langle \nabla v_m(\widetilde{\mathbf{a}})-\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}), (\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}-\mathbf{a})\big(\nabla v_m(\widetilde{\mathbf{a}})-\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a})\big)\right \rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m}\\
			\leqslant 
			\big|\left \langle \nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}), (\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}-\mathbf{a})\big(\nabla v_m(\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}) - \nabla v_m(\mathbf{a})\big)\right \rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m}\big|\\
			\leqslant \left \langle \nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}), (\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}-\mathbf{a})\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a})\right \rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m}.
