		As a consequence, the following estimate holds
		\begin{equation}
			0 \leqslant \langle\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}), (\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}-\mathbf{a})\nabla v_m(\widetilde{\mathbf{a}})\rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m} \leqslant 2 \langle\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a}), (\widetilde{\mathbf{a}}-\mathbf{a})\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a})\rangle_{{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m}.
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.210495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e173c3f2e6478b2f5960e736f6807f264e53a01ec4422e307c1bfa22eb163d15","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] For any \(1/2<H<1\) we have that 
