{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.974264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e179dd025e8992ef94bf071559b50fcd5c93e3a917505e6a38d940f883a321bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:restrictionforest of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] We introduce function spaces for our $\widehat{\CT}$-indexed cumulants. 
Analogously to how we worked with trees in Section~(subsec:tree_coord of the paper), it will be convenient to define operations at the level of labelled forests but have the cumulants themselves indexed by (unlabelled) forests. 

Given  ${\boldsymbol{\tau}} = \big( (\tau_{i},r_{i},u_i) \big)_{i=1}^{p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})} \in \text{$   \widehat\mathcal{T}$}$, a labelling $\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}$ of ${\boldsymbol{\tau}}$  is a tuple
$\big( (\underline{\tau}_{i},r_{i},u_i) \big)_{i=1}^{p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})}$ where, for any $i \in [p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})]$, we have $\underline{\tau}_{i} \in \tau_{i}$ (that is, $\underline{\tau}_{i}$ is a labelling of the tree $\tau_i$) and for any distinct $i,j \in [p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})]$, 
\begin{equs}
  N(\underline{\tau}_i)\cap N(\underline{\tau}_j)=\emptyset
\end{equs}
We call $\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}$ a labelled forest, and also set 
\begin{equs}
 N(\underline{\boldsymbol{\tau}})\eqdef\bigcup_{i\in[p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})]}N(\underline{\tau}_i)\,.
\end{equs}

Note that every forest ${\boldsymbol{\tau}}$ has at least one labelling, and we can also view elements of ${\widehat{\CT}}$ as sets of all the labelled forests $\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}} \in {\boldsymbol{\tau}}$ that label them. 

Given a labelled forest $\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}$ as above, we define the functional space 
\begin{equs} 
    \text{${\mcb{C}}$}\text{$[\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}]$}
\eqdef
\bigotimes_{i \in p({\boldsymbol{\tau}})}
\text{${\mcb{C}}[\underline{\tau}_i]$}\,.
\end{equs}
Note that, thanks to (equation eq:restrictionforest of the paper), one can really view elements of ${\mcb{C}}[\underline{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}]$ are really functions of time variables $\big(t_{v}: v \in N(\underline{\boldsymbol{\tau}}) \big)$. 

Analogously to what we did for labelled vs unlabelled trees, we define for each unlabelled forest ${\boldsymbol{\tau}} \in \widehat{\CT}$ a corresponding spaces  ${\mcb{C}}[{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}]$ defined using relabelling-invariant sections taking value in ${\mcb{C}}[{{\boldsymbol{\tau}}}]$","status":"unverified"}

