{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.348859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1970ef833954e5709c37522cf147e22b0db4b80763d2b30babebca1b8cb1ea4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn:sub-stop of arXiv:2601.07045, 'From Continuous to Discrete: \\ a No-U-Turn Sampler for Permutations'] Let $\mathcal{O}$ be an orbit of length $2^j$, and let
