{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.584537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1ad17e70fb5b10457bffc08c3d94d9d43d97ad65e84a4a7e9e5391a668cb307","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2605.16868, '\ttl'] For $\boldsymbol{F}\in\mathcal{R}$, the reflection map $R_F \coloneq (\Psi_F,\Phi_F)$ is Lipschitz.  Namely, for bounded parameters $(\gamma, k)$ we have
