{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.436100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1ad9d38cf39c96d71f0ea88371d1a479ca3a9d6f8dd772192a7ae9199f32ef7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ApprxSplit of arXiv:2609.02180, 'Helly-Type Theorems for Splitting Point Sets \thanks{A preliminary version of this article'] Let $P\subset {\mathbb R}^d$ be an $m$-point set, $1\leq k \leq d-1$, and let $\epsilon >0$. There exists a set $A\subseteq P$ of size at most $O\br{\frac{d}{\epsilon^2}\ln(\frac{d}{\epsilon})}$ with the following property:
