{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1ae54d4ba16b3476d1ed13e19b0b782f655b79dc61395cccde1cd19f9ab4b1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nmlsi of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] For any $p\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\O)$, let $h=h(m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p))$ denote the unique $h\in\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ such that $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\mu_{J,h})=m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p)$, and let \(p_t\) denote the solution of (equation non-linear rqs of the paper) with initial datum $p$. If the system satisfies the Nonlinear MLSI with rate function $\ensuremath{\mathcal I}$, then 
