{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.731904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1b1c7e769264c0381eadecf1402d1932a5581f68e12d00ed20d388e65d69dac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem cA5 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] For any $q\in(0,p)$,
there exists $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}

 \sup_{t\in[0, T]}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^q\Big]
\leq C^{N+1}h_n^{\frac{p-q}{\chi}\wedge q}(1+2\|x\|^p) +(2N+1) C^{N+1}h_n^{\frac{q}{2}\wedge 1}
