{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.166451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1c11f22b1368a6fd557e42a1a84fcc18a6967b927a34d30412f5b9c38ed6c9e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 36 of arXiv:2607.02777, 'Hypocoercivity for Hamiltonian Diffusions \\ with Singular Drift'] Let $h \in L^2(\mu)$ be a probability density with respect to $\mu$ and $\sigma\colon \Omega_2 \to \mathbb{R}^{d_2 \times d_2}$ be continuous with $\Sigma = \sigma \sigma^*$.
