{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.587654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1d022ecc9131ec208e4fee4ed1977737bf2d453c2b3c80fcad25bd4c8e99c2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm strictly_smaller_free_energy of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For $\mathsf{P}_i\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with  $\mathcal F_{\beta}({\mathsf{P}_i})<\infty$, $i=0,1$, there exists $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ with \begin{align}  
