for both $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Was}$ and $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Kol}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e20cf380b9082957249aa091cf079541b432960c1659ef8f6d240f3b845693cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Pathwise uniqueness in the non-sticky class) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume that one of the following two uniqueness regimes holds.

    \begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
