{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.979604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e22b3d7b6c94be36d3c42e63a25f576366b8a0615c4c1ffdfd3c1c9c1e5931ef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.11389, 'Instability of a nonlinear oscillator with small friction and small additive noise'] Suppose ${\cal U}''(x)$ is unbounded above.  Given any initial condition $(x_0,y_0, \theta_0) \in \R^2 \times \R/(2 \pi Z)$, any target point $(x_1,y_1,\theta_1) \in \R^2 \times \R/(2 \pi Z)$ and any $\e > 0$ and any $T \ge 0$ there exists a piecewise continuous $h: [0,T] \to \R$ such that the unique solution of 
     \begin{equation} 
     (\dot{x}(t),\dot{y}(t),\dot{\theta}(t)) = X_0(x(t),y(t),\theta(t)) + h(t)X_1(x(t),y(t),\theta(t))
     \end{equation}
with initial condition $(x_0,y_0,\theta_0)$ satisfies $\|(x(T),y(T),\theta(T)) - (x_1,y_1,\theta_1)\| < \e$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e22c3dfce0d4eb0e8dbacb131a9ecf1340f3d6730c5864caae36390748afd1d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem le:sup_Lp_concentration of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $p\in \mathbf{N}^*$. There exists some constant $C = C(p)$ such that for any $j, N \geq 1$, we have
	\begin{equ}

		\mathbb{E} \sup_{0\leq t \leq 1} \|\Delta_j X[t]\|_{L^{2p}}^{2N} \leq  2^{4j}(C\alpha_0)^{2N} \Big(1 + N^{N} 2^{-jN/p}\Big)\;.
	\end{equ}
	As a result, there exists $j_*$ such that for $j \geq j_*$, we have 
	\begin{equ}

		\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{0\leq t \leq 1} \|\Delta_j X[t]\|_{L^{2p}} \geq j^{1/2}\alpha_0  \right) \leq C 2^{-6j}\;.
	\end{equ}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.294878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e232a1354dab80359717dab2297588653fe2ccbd908c95e6d97e5e9f3ac5e93f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] We consider the setting of Theorem~(thm_main_R of the paper) and $\mathcal H_t $ be the event $\{\tau^{X}_0<t\} = \{\exists\; s \in [0,t) \colon  X_s = 0\}$.
