{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.372068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2357033604d0c642a2fd3f13e1391d43e7fdd5919c53fd4cd22b3988e323ea3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro SupportH of arXiv:2411.13465, 'Height-offset variables and pinning at infinity for gradient Gibbs measures on trees'] Let $\nu$ be the free state (a spatially homogeneous GGM of height-period $2$ with a fuzzy Markov chain $\bar{\mu}$, resp.), $H$ be the height-offset variable which is given by Proposition (pro: MartingaleFree of the paper) (Proposition (pro: MartingaleHiddenIsing of the paper), resp.) and $H^{\rho,0}$ the push-forward of $H$ to the gradient field under 
