{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.667776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e24f2b8e7e2c1f91617758db42eb26391650c829f2a5a18748cc7f1476e5c24a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2608.30859, 'Conservation Laws with Discontinuous Flux:\\ A First Application to Traffic Flow'] There exists \( t_0 > 0 \) sufficiently small such that the Picard operator \eqref{eq:PicardOp2B} is a contraction mapping on the complete metric space $(\mathcal{F}, d)$ where $\mathcal{F}$
