{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.086028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e25e6246ec18bcbb471b35d79c09378fc7f32de282baf0a38627cc4a7f854daf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:conv_appro_1 of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Fix $(a,r)\in{\mathbb R}^2$. Let $(\sigma_n,b_n)_{n\ge1}$ and $(\sigma,b)$ satisfy Assumption~(assu:H of the paper) and conditions~(item:1a of the paper), (item:1b of the paper), (item:2c of the paper), and~(item:2d of the paper). Assume that $(\sigma_n)_{n\ge1}$ has the same sign as $\sigma$, i.e., $\sigma_n\sigma\ge0$ for all $n$. Let $\mathcal S^n_{r,\cdot}(a)$, $n\ge1$, and $\mathcal S_{r,\cdot}(a)$ denote the unique strong solutions to~(equation eq:SDE_gener of the paper) corresponding to $(\sigma_n,b_n)$ and $(\sigma,b)$, respectively. Suppose that:
\vspace{-0.5em}
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item for any compact set $K\subset{\mathbb R}$ and all $T\ge r$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{gathered}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\sup_{r\le t\le T}\sup_{x\in K}\int_{{\mathbb R}}(\sigma_n(x,t,s)-\sigma(x,t,s))^2\,\ensuremath{\mathrm{d}} s=0,\\
\lim_{n\to\infty}\sup_{r\le t\le T}\sup_{x\in K}|b_n(x,t)-b(x,t)|=0;
\end{gathered}
\end{equation}
\vspace{-1.5em}
\item for any $T\ge r$, there exist positive constants $K_b'=K_b'(T)$ and $K_\sigma'=K_\sigma'(T)$ such that, for all $x\in{\mathbb R}$, $r\le t\le T$, and $n\ge1$,
\begin{align}
|b_n(x,t)| \le K_b'(1+|x|), \qquad 
\bar\sigma_n(x,t):=\int_{{\mathbb R}}\sigma_n(x,t,s)^2\,\ensuremath{\mathrm{d}} s \le K_\sigma'(1+|x|)^2.
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}
\vspace{-0.5em}
Then $\mathcal S^n_{r,\cdot}(a)\to \mathcal S_{r,\cdot}(a)$ in probability in $C([r,\infty))$. In particular, there exists a subsequence of $\{\mathcal S^n_{r,\cdot}(a)\}$ that converges almost surely uniformly on compact intervals to $\mathcal S_{r,\cdot}(a)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.364196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2614a860681c2245798fc1011257ea1d6f4d4d630207f92aed381f24f1b1618","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] For any $p\geqslant1$, the following second order
asymptotics holds true for the solution $u(t,x)$ to the PAM (\ref{eq:GlobalPAM}):
\begin{equation}
