{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.921964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e26603b073aeb7770448a6d872e4ef817b2c5d445e2387ffff4cbc9138362358","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:globalremainderest of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Let $u$ be a URD solution to (equation eq:modeleqn of the paper). Then $R^u\in C^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}\textrm{-var}}([0,T]; H^{-2})$. Moreover:
