{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.720726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e26bc93080be8dbfc87d405c0e2307bf54b58e6a7a467ae812708dce804da5c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hi_invariance of arXiv:2605.31054, 'On the empirical spectral distribution of matrix perpetuities'] Assume that ${\mathbf u}{\mathbf A}{\mathbf A}^\top\,{\mathbf u}^\top\stackrel{d}{=}{\mathbf A}{\mathbf A}^\top$ for every orthogonal matrix ${\mathbf u}$. Fix $k\in\{1,\ldots,N\}$ and let $s>0$ be such that
$ {\mathbb E}\left[ \prod_{i=1}^k \lambda_i({\mathbf A}{\mathbf A}^\top)^{s/k}\right]<\infty$.
Then
\begin{align}
