{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.769612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2868175a18d3efa819bbe2b1d2e5fa9304be49ddcf78899b4dd4669cbced3c2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 (Positive exponential moments) of arXiv:2605.14511, 'Clumsy and Careless:\\ Stationary-Entry Flux in Non-monotone Coupon Collectors'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:reset-rare-success}.  If, for a fixed $a\in(0,1)$,
