{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.643932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e29928ddce7651c06159a673ee0ef8bfbf1ba8fe2c211709e39d441aaeeb67fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 (Shift of the speed function) of arXiv:2605.13512, '2605.13512'] Suppose that we have a speed function $c(x,y) : \bR \times \bR \to \bR_{+}$ that satisfies Assumptions \ref{ass:c}, \ref{ass:c2}, \ref{ass:c0}. 
Fix $(a,b) \in \bR^{2}$ and consider the shifted $(T_{a,b}c)(s,t) = c(s+a, t+b)$.
Suppose that we then discretize both $c$ and $T_{a,b}c$ separately as 
 \[ c^{n}(i,j) = c\left(i/n, j/n \right) \text{ and } (T_{a,b}c)^n(i,j) = T_{a,b}c\left(i/n, j/n \right).\]

Denote by $G^{(n),c}$ and $G^{(n), (T_{a,b}c)}$ the last passage times using the speed functions $c$ and $T_{a,b}c$ respectively. We then have the scaling limits
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{n \to \infty}n^{-1}G^{(n),c}_{{\bf 0},(\ce{nx}, \ce{ny})} = \Gamma_{c}(x,y), \hspace{15.pt} \bP \text{ - a.s,}
\end{equation*}
and 
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{n \to \infty}n^{-1}G^{(n),T_{a,b}c}_{{\bf 0}, (\ce{nx}, \ce{ny})} = \Gamma_{T_{a,b}c}(x,y), \hspace{15.pt} \bP \text{ - a.s.}
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, we have that
\begin{equation}
    \Gamma_{T_{a,b}c}(x,y) = \Gamma_{c}((a,b),(x+a,y+b)), \hspace{15.pt} \bP \text{ - a.s.}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

