{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.032046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e29e38b5d878abbc9cb50362148c4395a5740db427d8c6fdf4f4bcc991e07e95","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2605.02771, 'Universality in Deep Neural Networks:\\ An approach via the Lindeberg exchange principle'] For \(K=-1,\ldots,L-1\), we define \(z^{(L+1;L-K)}(x)\) to be the output of a DNN with weights \(\tilde{W}^{(\ell)}\) defined as 
\[
    \tilde{W}^{(\ell)}=\begin{cases}
                        W^{(\ell)},\quad \text{if}\quad l=1,\ldots L-K,\\
                        G^{(\ell)},\quad \text{if}\quad l=L-K+1,\ldots,L+1,
