{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.749557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2bcdc6a65df74918dddc58950a71b473d820554f3bb275348ef6c4348ba75c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (\cite{VanDenBergPerimeter,VanDenBergDavies}) of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] If $\partial D$ is sufficiently regular
