{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.321077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2c2e0986a51ed816c5953c4f5f9eec41c51343517c5e9ed22e7a9b357bd857d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma h-cof-compute-po of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $G$ be a compact Lie group, and let
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{tikzcd}
            A\arrow[r,"i"]\arrow[d,"f"']\arrow[dr,phantom,"\ulcorner"{very near end}] & B\arrow[d]\\
            C\arrow[r] & D
        \end{tikzcd}
    \end{equation}
    be any pushout in $\cat{$\bm{G}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}_*$ such that $i$ is an unbased h-cofibration. Then $((diag:pushout-h-cof of the paper))$ is a homotopy pushout in the $G$-global model structure.

    The analogous statement holds for homotopy pushouts in the ${\mathcal{F}}$-model structure on $\textbf{\textup{$\bm G$-Top}}_*$ for any collection ${\mathcal{F}}$ of closed subgroups.
    \begin{proof}
        The second statement follows immediately from the corresponding unbased statement (Lemma~(lemma:h-cof-compute-po-unbased of the paper)) as weak equivalences, cofibrations, and pushouts are created by the forgetful functor to $\textbf{\textup{$\bm G$-Top}}$.

        For the first statement, we then factor $f$ into a level cofibration $A\to C_0$ followed by a $G$-global level weak equivalence. Then $i(V)$ is an h-cofibration in $\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-Top}$ by [schwede2018global]*{Corollary~A.30(ii)}, so applying the second claim levelwise shows that the induced map $B\amalg_AC_0\to B\amalg_AC=D$ is even a $G$-global level weak equivalence, so that $((diag:pushout-h-cof of the paper))$ is a homotopy pushout as claimed.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.273309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2c32a5c157eb91f97fb14228c0abf8fe3d5817a50af8172af15ddca665c7936","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mydef b2.1 of arXiv:2411.08430, 'The Restricted Isometry Property of Block Diagonal Matrices Generated by $\varphi$-Sub-Gau'] A matrix \( \mathbf{B} \in \mathbb{C}^{M \times D} \) is said to have the group restricted isometry property (group-RIP) of order \( s \) if there exists a constant \( \delta \in (0, 1) \) such that, for all $\mathbf{x} \in \Sigma_{\mathcal{S}, s}$, the following inequality holds:

	\begin{equation}
		(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{x}\|_2^2 \leq\|\mathbf{B} \mathbf{x}\|_2^2 \leq(1+\delta)\|\mathbf{x}\|_2^2 \quad \forall \mathbf{x} \in \Sigma_{\mathcal{S}, s}
	\end{equation}

The smallest constant \( \delta_s \leq \delta \) satisfying this inequality is referred to as the group restricted isometry constant (group-RIC) of $\mathbf{B}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.496139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2c3ad4d97fa32daf9d0a2d4a0219a346672658e2bb30c4233358f1b6ffbd1de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem 40 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] For each $x \ge 0$, show that 
