where $F_{\emph{GOE}} (x)$ is the GOE \emph{level-spacing distribution}. (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.112071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2c4549ae2ce02ef8d52a717d68a3ad19ffc2b9c569d3a176cffd2ee2dec8bc8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm:complete-linear-estimates of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Let $\alpha\geq0$ and let $w$ be a regular weight of order $\alpha$.
Suppose that Assumption~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper) holds and $C_w(X)<\infty$, and take
$F\in L_\alpha^2$ and $\psi\in H^1(\mu_T)$.  If $\psi$ is not
spatially constant, also assume Assumption~(ass:drift-multiplier of the paper).  Then
$u:=\mathcal U(F,\psi)=SF+v^\psi$ is the unique order-$\alpha$ occupation Sobolev solution with data
$(F,\psi)$.  Its Hessian is
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{Hess}_gu=\mathsf T_wF+\operatorname{Hess}_gv^\psi, \qquad
 D_x^2u=D_x^2SF+D_x^2v^\psi.

\end{equation}
There exists a constant
$C=C(T,\lambda,\Lambda,M_1(a),\operatorname{osc}_\alpha(w),
C_w(X),\Lambda_b)>0$ such that, for every $\kappa\geq1$,
\begin{align}
 \left\lVert u\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 &\leq e^{\operatorname{osc}_\alpha(w)/2}\kappa^{-1}
       \left\lVert F\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
       +CT^{\alpha/2}\norm\psi_{H^1(\mu_T)},\notag\\
 \left\lVert \mathsf Z u\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 &\leq e^{\operatorname{osc}_\alpha(w)/2}\kappa^{-1/2}
       \left\lVert F\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
       +CT^{\alpha/2}\norm\psi_{H^1(\mu_T)},\notag\\
 \left\lVert \mathsf G u\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 &\leq C_{w_\kappa}(X)\left\lVert F\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 +\frac32\Lambda^2\lambda^{-5/2}M_1(a)
        \kappa^{-1/2}
\times e^{\operatorname{osc}_\alpha(w)/2}
        \left\lVert F\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 +CT^{\alpha/2}\norm\psi_{H^1(\mu_T)}.

\end{align}
The corresponding canonical estimate is
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{j=0}^2\left\lVert D_x^ju\right\rVert_\alpha
 \leq C\left(\left\lVert F\right\rVert_\alpha
       +T^{\alpha/2}\norm\psi_{H^1(\mu_T)}\right).

\end{equation}
If $\psi$ is spatially constant, $C$ may be chosen without dependence on
$\Lambda_b$.
For every $s\in(0,T)$, its composition admits a continuous version on
$[s,T]$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
 u(t,X_t)=\mathbb E_t\left[\psi(X_T)+\int_t^TF(r,X_r)\,\mathrm d r\right],
 \qquad s\leq t\leq T.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.358889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2c627eb2e938d22f45cab775986d15329f1cf039b84a0cc56fdf1ad98b88a0e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem le.finitealpha-s of arXiv:2411.13099, 'Long time behavior of killed Feynman-Kac semigroups with singular Schr{ö}dinger potentials'] Assume {\rm \textbf{[L1]}}. 
