{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.791105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2e9c8988f9e2853f80a78d16ebb4ecb439215f010eeedfbbeffceabd14c2a1b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 6 (Large deviation principle for the normalised mass function) of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] The normalised mass function of the unconstrained model $\Pi_{N}$ obeys a large deviation principle
at speed $N$ and rate function $I - \!\! \underset{\mu \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})}{\inf}\!\! I[\mu ]$.
That is, for any open set $O \subset \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$,

\begin{align}

\liminf_{N \to +\infty} \frac{1}{N}\ln \Pi_{N}[O] \geq

- \Big\{ \inf_{\mu \in O}I[\mu] - \inf_{\mu \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})} \hspace{-3mm} I[\mu] \Big\}

\end{align}

and, for any closed set $F \subset \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$,

\begin{align}
    \limsup_{N \to +\infty} \frac{1}{N}\ln \Pi_{N}[F] \leq

- \Big\{ \inf_{\mu \in F}I[\mu]-\inf_{\mu \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})} \hspace{-3mm} I[\mu] \Big\} \, .

\end{align}

Likewise the normalised mass function of the constrained model $\Pi_{N,\mathsf{c}}$ also obeys a large deviation principle
on  $ \mathcal{M}_{1,\mathsf{c} }(\mathbb{R})$  at speed $N$ and rate function $I- \underset{ \mu \in \mathcal{M}_{1,\mathsf{c}}(\mathbb{R})}{\inf}\hspace{-3mm}I[\mu]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2ea1ea9aece55dac9c9c800afdb7481c92235d0d46b69e740120cffe79b9c6c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:PoissonApproximation of arXiv:2607.22291, 'Rare subtree patterns in size-conditioned Bienaymé trees: Poisson approximation and declum'] Assume that $\mu$ is critical and belongs to the domain of
