{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.924158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2f8370e1c91cd1ffc46de4a4945b3d33617d48b897992fb04e3202bad2ff851","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:2 of arXiv:2412.02160, 'A functional central limit theorem for weighted occupancy processes of the Karlin model'] Assume that $(p_j)_{j\in{\mathbb N}}$ satisfies (equation eq:p RV of the paper) with $\alpha\in(0,1)$. Assume that there exists $\beta\in[0,\alpha^2/2)$ such that $(a_j)_{j\in{\mathbb N}}$ satisfies that 
