{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.183177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3006856be112d52419dc46b5bcfd0bed7743e04e30db33696c15bafe830298c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition it:boundary_conditions of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Let $a,b>0$ and let $h$ be a GFF in a proper simply connected domain $G \subseteq \BC$. We say that a local set $A$ of $h$ is a \emph{two-valued local set} of $h$ of levels $-a$ and $b$ if it satisfies the following properties.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item 
		If $h_{A}$ denotes the harmonic extension to $G\setminus A$ of the boundary values of $h$ on $A$, then we have that $h_{A} \in \{-a,b\}$ a.s.
		\item 
		For any smooth test function $f \in C_0^{\infty}(G)$, a.s.,
		\begin{align*}
			(h,f) = (h-h_{A} , f) + \int_{G \setminus A} h_{A}(x) f(x) \mathrm{d}x.
		\end{align*}
		\item  The set $A \cup \partial G$ has a finite number of connected components.
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

