{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.592604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3067e24d90fd762a0246de324fdd91d43a82b04a1e826e556f667a520afe7a1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq8 of arXiv:2608.30592, 'Infinite Matrix Operators and $E$-Frames in Hilbert Spaces'] We say a sequence $\Psi=\lbrace \psi_k\rbrace_{k=1}^{\infty}$ is an $E$-sequence in $\mathcal{H}$ if, its $E$-transform, i.e. the sequence 
