{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.078440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3088422d23ff9327b435cb997b46639ac67361f13437f38c606b552d60ffc23","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 (Jiang--Lee--Vempala conjecture) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] Assume the estimates in \cref{thm:letwin}.  If \(X,Y\in\R^n\) are
independent isotropic log-concave random vectors and \(G\sim N(0,1)\), then
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  W_2^2\!\left(
    \Law\!\left(\frac{\langle X,Y\rangle}{\sqrt n}\right),
    \Law(G)
  \right)
  \leq\frac{20}{n}.}
  \tag{5.12}
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if \(G_n\sim N(0,n)\), then
\begin{equation}
  W_2^2\!\left(\Law(\langle X,Y\rangle),\Law(G_n)\right)\leq20.
  \tag{5.13}
\end{equation}
Thus the dimension-free central limit conjecture of
Jiang, Lee, and Vempala \cite{JLV} follows from the cited estimates.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.197323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3090e2ae4a21b88321bd77e5ff431c7ca9e6866697a90b15c3945f6b2c3bdd6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 39 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] If $\delta$, $\chi$, $\varepsilon$ are as in \eqref{eq:small-params}, the following properties hold for each $y\in \mathcal A$.
