{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.822014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e30b3e13b052b7839bb70de4d495661ca9fe8b9a0f3bf76d370ea0f39f10df01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:occupation_bounds of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] There exists a constant $c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:occupation of the paper)}}(\Gamma_+) > 0$ such that, for any time horizon $T \ge 0$ and any site $x$, the occupation at $x$ satisfies the following bounds.

  For any threshold $M \ge 1$ and any choice of $K \le c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:occupation of the paper)}} M$:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}_\rho\Big( \sup_{t \in [0, T]} \eta_t(x) \ge M \Big) \le (T + 1) \Big[ \mathbb{P}_\rho\big( \eta_0(x) \ge K \big) + e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:occupation of the paper)}} M} \Big].
  \end{equation}

  For any threshold $m \ge 1$ and any choice of $K \ge c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:occupation of the paper)}}^{-1} m$:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}_\rho\Big( \inf_{t \in [0, T]} \eta_t(x) \le m \Big) \le (T + 1) \Big[ \mathbb{P}_\rho\big( \eta_0(x) \le K \big) + e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:occupation of the paper)}} K} \Big].
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.809695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e30cd4030dca14dabefd7ef0ea91ec32c163bcbe19c2b6d38719791500a8313c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:FB_HS_norm_in_L2 of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $M \in H^{-d/2-\alpha}_{\div}$, $\widehat G \in \mathcal{S}$, $\widehat G \ge 0$ and $\gamma(\mathrm{d}n) \coloneqq \widehat G (n) \mathrm{d}n$. Then,
