{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.624555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e32c58f5681e5737b8999485024294237cd48e00efc0b5a3c7891ffd3ab37384","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:uncountable many mixing measure of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] The $G$-Brownian motion $B_t(\omega)=\omega_t$ is a martingale on $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},(\mathcal{F}_t)_{t\geq 0}, P_{\eta})$ for each $\eta\in \mathcal{A}_{0,\infty}^{Q}$ and
