\end{enumeratea} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.445557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e33c85e7bd5172b34261613f1867caf84e843b13170d801ad7a814467b4cd460","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: cond Lind for general time scale of arXiv:2505.05921, 'Limit Theorems for step reinforced random walks\\ with regularly varying memory'] {}
    Let $\{S_n\}$ be the SRRW-RVM with zero mean, unit variance innovation sequence $\{\xi_n\}$, $\mu_n = n^\gamma (\log n)^{-(\gamma+1)}$ and $p=p_c$. Then, the martingale difference array defined in (equation eq: mg array in critical of the paper) satisfies, for $t>0$,
