{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.743530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3564bde601d7c6e097b6352107e00cd68320998109f7bdf6e5e7f4eb33bf456","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Continuity of the distribution of $\beta$-LRP metric) of arXiv:2506.10511, '2506.10511'] For all $d\geq 1$ and $\beta>0$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{\varepsilon\to 0^+}\mathds{P}\left[D({\bm 0},\bm x)\in (a-\varepsilon,a+\varepsilon)\right]=0
