{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.088056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e36cf8e113c0b92a02fc36769758cea2729222550a97e95971b261a4802feec2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 19 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume that assumptions \ref{H0}, \ref{H0.5}, \ref{H1}, \ref{H2b}, \ref{H3} and 
\begin{equation*}
\beta+\delta<\frac12\min\{\alpha,1-\alpha\}
\end{equation*}
hold. Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,(\mathcal F_t)_{t\geq0}, \mathbb P, W,X)$ be a weak mild solution to \eqref{abstract_formulation}. For every $n\in\N$ and $x\in H$, the process $\{X_n(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$ defined by \eqref{Def:mild_form_approx_process} satisfies the following representation: 
\begin{align}
X_n(t,x)&=e^{tA_n}\left[P_nx+u_n(0,P_nx)\right]-u_n(t,X_n(t,x)) \notag \\
&-({\mathfrak c}+1)A_n\int_0^t e^{(t-s)A_n}u_n(s,X_n(s,x))ds \notag \\
