{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.422545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e376c76203383df0d7db043a0c57371c26d3a0ec30045174c71d4200439feeef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:Z-def of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:regularized-Z}
For a Borel measurable function \(V\) bounded below,
\(f\in\mathcal F_m\) or \(f=\ell_\eta\) with fixed \(\eta>0\), and
\(\varepsilon>0\), define
\begin{align}
 \mathcal Z_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,f)
 :=\omega_N\int_{\mathcal O_{N,L}}
 &\exp\biggl\{-NV\bigl(h_J(O)\bigr)
 +\sum_{a=1}^n\log\kappa_\varepsilon\bigl(g_{a,J}(O)\bigr)\notag\\
 &\hspace{36mm}+\operatorname{Tr} f\bigl(A_J(O)\bigr)\biggr\}\,\nu_N(\,\mathrm d O).

\end{align}
Its annealed pressure is
\begin{equation}
 \Phi_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,f)
 :=\frac1N\log\mathbb E\mathcal Z_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,f).
