{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.368669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3778a280e5f9707b6261d4924e4f22a5278e728c8d5ede2e9258ddb74b878b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LSI:zergalinski of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\lambda$ be a 1-MRF on $\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{\mathbb{T}_2^n}$. Recall the notation $\mathbf{x}^{(n)}$ defined in Definition (def:results:Tn2 of the paper). For $v \in \mathbb{T}_2^n$ and $\mathbf{x}^{(n)} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}$, let $\hat{\mathbf{x}}_v := \{x_u\}_{u \neq v} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{2n}$. Denote the corresponding family of specifications (i.e. marginal conditional measures) of $\lambda$ by $ \lambda_v(x_v | \hat{\mathbf{x}}_v)$. 

     Suppose the following two properties hold.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Expressed in terms of the constant $C_{LS}$ from Definition (def:LSI of the paper), the specifications $\{\lambda_v\}_{v \in \mathbb{T}^n_2}$ satisfy the uniform log-Sobolev inequality,
        \begin{align*}
            \tilde{C}_{LS, n} = \sup_{v \in \mathbb{T}^n_2, \, \hat{\mathbf{x}}_v \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{2n}} C_{LS}\Big(\lambda_v\big(\cdot \big| \hat{\mathbf{x}}_v\big)\Big) < \infty.
        \end{align*}
        \item There exist constants $c^n_{uv}(\lambda) \geq 0$ for every $u, v \in \mathbb{T}_2^n$, such that every smooth strictly positive function $f: \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{\mathbb{T}_2^n} \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ satisfies the following for all $\hat{\mathbf{x}}_v \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{2n}$ :
        \begin{equation}

            \bigg | \nabla_{x_u} \sqrt{ \mathbb E^{\lambda_v}[f^2|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_v]}\bigg| \leq \sqrt{\mathbb E^{\lambda_v}[|\nabla_{x_u}f|^2|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_v]} + c^n_{uv}(\lambda) \sqrt{\mathbb E^{\lambda_v}[|\nabla_{x_v}f|^2|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_v]},
        \end{equation}
        where there exists $\delta \in (0, 1)$ such that
        \begin{equation}
            \sup_{u \in \mathbb{T}_2^n} \max\bigg\{ \sum_{v \in \mathbb{T}_2^n} c^n_{uv}(\lambda), \sum_{v \in \mathbb{T}_2^n} c^n_{vu}(\lambda)\bigg\} \leq \delta < 1.

        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} 
    Then $\lambda$ satisfies an LSI with constant
        \begin{align*}
            C_{LS}(\lambda) \leq \frac{\tilde{C}_{LS, n}}{(1 - \delta)^2}.
        \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

