{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.654655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e388949aa132974121764dbedf8c8ffc4ad452cdfffd6503bbba941868669acc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.17296, 'Zero correlations and averaged fields of orthonormal Gaussian Functions'] For fixed $k \ge 1$, as $n\rightarrow \infty $, 
\begin{equation*}
g_{n,n+k}(z,z) = 
\begin{cases}
\disp 1-\frac{5}{4n^{2}}+O\left( \frac{1}{n^{3}}\right) <1 &
 \text{if $k=1$}, \\
\disp \frac{4}{3}
+\frac{1}{12n^2}+O\left( \frac{1}{n^3}\right) 
>1 &
 \text{if $k=2$},  \\
\disp 1 & \text{if $k\geq 3$}.  
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
Thus, the short-range correlations between $\cZ_{f_{n}}$ and $
\cZ_{f_{n+k}}$ display repulsion if $k=1$, attraction if $k=2$ and
no correlations if $k\geq 3$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.613221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e38ae78b530b75315e50af15a346aeac6162e772f55586dc8586a7dbf64ee4b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 49 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] As $n\to\infty$ we have 
