{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.997422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e39435f068e7b5d95bd324ba659e819da6a3d153cf1b0e7af85d31b694237f11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:GAP2 of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $Q\ge 2$, and let $d>0$ be a large constant. Then there exist $c>0$ and $C>0$  such that if $\phi \in \mathcal{C}_Q$ with $\phi(-\infty)=0$ and $\phi(\infty)=2\pi Q$ satisfies 
