{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292483+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e39bd705cb65e655148ee695d07f8a96b7880608e5ab9c92816feb67b70c56b0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:C_reg of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $\Omega$ be defined as in Theorem~(theo:main of the paper). Fix (small) $c_0,\varepsilon>0$. For any $f_1,f_2\in H_0^{2}(\Omega)$ and $x_j,x_j'\in [c_0,1]$, $j=1,2$, it holds that
