{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3b9a241ef1ca87339fd97ea5697e07464b7ffc91a16d0039b7b493b2d8be4d0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cumulant-comparison of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For any smooth test function $f : \mathbb{R}^K \to \mathbb{R}$ with bounded derivatives up to order 4, and overlaps $\mathbf{X} = (X_2^{(\mathbf{q})}, \ldots, X_{K+1}^{(\mathbf{q})})$ at the edge:
