{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.315131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3d8266aedf8f60fb7f4a6d29b0b9ca1c3c9873b0726e3ff47a00d6fff6e8085","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma compare of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Let $a<b<c$. For any closed set $A$, we have 
