{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.284929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e40597e04f41d00fd4bd2235e0fff97ebed9c78428bc9b2907a1214c9fee83c9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Reduced-form PX-EM loading objective) of arXiv:2608.21551, '\bf Sparse Separable Factor Analysis in the Complex Domain with an Application to Local Fi'] After updating $\Gammab$ according to \eqref{eq:app_gamma_update} and applying the parameter-reduction map in  \eqref{eq:lam_construction}, the loading-dependent part of the normalized PX-EM objective in \eqref{eq:vec-comp-llk_app} satisfies
