  \begin{align*}
    \Abs{\phi}_{\mathring K_\lambda^k}
    &\coloneq
      \Abs{\phi}_{H_b^{k+2}}
      + \Abs{\partial_r \phi}_{H_b^{k+1}}
      + \Abs{\tfrac{\lambda}{r} \phi}_{H_b^{k+1}} 
      + \Abs{w_{\log}\paren{\partial_r - \tfrac{\lambda}{r}}\phi}_{H_b^{k+1}} \\
    &\quad
      + \Abs{\partial_r w_{\log}\paren{\partial_r - \tfrac{\lambda}{r}}\phi}_{H_b^k}
      + \Abs{\tfrac{\lambda}{r} w_{\log}\paren{\partial_r - \tfrac{\lambda}{r}} \phi}_{H_b^k}.
  \end{align*}
  There is a family of smoothing operators $(S_\varepsilon : \varepsilon \in (0,1))$ satisfying the analogues of (Eq_SmoothingOperators_Smoothing of the paper), (Eq_SmoothingOperators_Approximation of the paper), (Eq_SmoothingOperators_Derivative- of the paper), and (Eq_SmoothingOperators_Derivative+ of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

