{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.182025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4862c7482bcc63d7f92422d7a2a63c70b0d7e45b37a9302b4de144949a098a6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Identify of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $\delta \in (0, 1/2]$. There exists a constant $c_0 > 0$, depending only on $m$ and $d$, such that for all $r < \delta n$, and all $\eta \in \mathrm{Macro}(\delta)$, we have  
