{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.251214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e491baf1d0fdc96f05e9cd8412d07ffdfd876623944589f58daf5f3a2e3d5520","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Integrated Davies trick) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] For any $q\in[1,\infty]$, denote by $q'$ its H\"older conjugate and let $0\leq V,W\in\ell^\infty(X),$ $I\subset \RR$. Then, for any $q$-norm with respect to any measure on $X$, we have 
\begin{multline*}
\left(
\fint_I \|VP_{2\tau}W\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^\frac{2}{q}
=
\left(
\fint_I \|WP_\tau V\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^{\frac{2}{q}}
\\
\leq 
\inf_{\omega\in\ell^\infty(X)}
\sup_{\supp V}\euler^{-\omega}
\sup_{\supp W}\euler^{\omega}
\left(
\fint_I
\|V P_\tau^\omega\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}
\left(
\fint_I
\|W P_\tau^{-\omega}\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}.
\end{multline*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.941750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e49366e27e803930dcac3733b5215aed7387cda6048d1b80de422d1c09febb40","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 47 (Fixed-rank Laurent integrality) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every zero-framed knot $K$, every fixed $n\ge2$, and every $k\ge0$,
