{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.597750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e499425bc122e7f8baef47cdb842d93a016845f1d7ba56de2c7f5b2b8e7b1b13","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2412.03415, 'Critical first passage percolation on random graphs'] \begin{enumeratea}
\item If the associated branching process {\bf does not} explode i.e., $\theta_\ell \uparrow \infty$ as $\ell \uparrow \infty$ then $T_n(u,v) \stackrel{P}{\longrightarrow} \infty$ as $n\to \infty$. 
