{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.328896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4e0d472bbb10efb4a8b4bba8c5a54c7e300e4a0f2a4b414f2187a3920e914b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:error_uniform_bound of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $Q$ be a parabolic cylinder with side length $\varrho\in (0,1/2]$ and center $(t_0,x_0)\in {\mathbb R}_+\times {\mathbb R}^d$.
