{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.726155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e4f2f8b5f720f9585e241355a7c54a0dd0d17e033933f416cbc2d3aace7c0e41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] Under the assumptions in Theorem \ref{theorem12121}, assume further that there exists some $M>0$ such that 
