{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.316014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e517a19d2c591da0243019ea9cfacc72fd886ecb27fbedbb5f3fe2866a0b229d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Glem1 of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] Let $T> 0$ and $\mathbf B \in \mathscr{C}^\gamma([0,T]; \mathbb R^d)$ for some $\gamma \in (1/3, \gamma_0)$. Then for any $(Y, Y^\prime) \in \mathcal{D} _{\mathbf B}^{2\gamma , \eta }([ 0, T] ; \mathcal{H} )$ with $\eta \in [0,\gamma)$ and $ G_1 \in C_{- 2\gamma , 0}^3( \mathcal{H} ; \mathcal{H}^d)$, we have
$$\Big(\int_0^\cdot S_{\cdot-u} G_1 (Y_u) d\mathbf{B}_u, G_1(Y) \Big) \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathbf B}^{2\gamma,\eta}([0,T];\mathcal{H}),$$
