{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.654808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e53c533a78f506d05754e24e04ca08a2b70c60142cb1d561ae4c144c1dd09285","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.04631, 'Existence of Martingale Solutions to Stochastic Constrained Heat Equation'] The space consisting of the continuous and square-integrable processes, which are martingales and have values in $\mathcal{H}$, is represented by $\mathbb{M}_{T}^{2}$. Moreover, it can be shown that $\mathbb{M}_{T}^{2}$ is a Banach space w.r.t following norm, 
