{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.564181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e53daa6366cefe3c3a4752515497b484b1d97ad1444c786bd74dc28d93392978","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.27249, 'Torus actions, almost non-negative curvature and fundamental groups'] For all \(m\in \mathbb{N}\), there is a constant \(0<C(m)<\infty\), such that the fundamental group of every almost non-negatively curved closed manifold \(M\) of dimension \(m\), which admits an action of a torus \(T\) satisfying the above assumption, contains a abelian subgroup of index \(<C(m)\).

