{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.970747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e54aaa63c412c55ec463d59e8ebb8999f97aeb592f3bd150276e1b185bcc0ade","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_error_rmulmc of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Assume that $-\beta I \preceq \nabla^2 V \preceq \beta I$, $h \lesssim \beta^{-1/2} \wedge \gamma/\beta$, and $\gamma \lesssim \sqrt{\beta}$. Then, the local errors for~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) are bounded as follows:
