{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.448839+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e54c6ff540dce3f7c4da6410da122187a30f4cc5c638b6cb3885ed4d7f131181","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:prop4.15 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any probability $p > 1/2$, their exist two constants $C , c \in (0, \infty)$ (depending on $p$) such that, for any $x \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2)^*$,
