weakly in the sense of measures. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.959024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e55d6ad34798a61207624d45c1aa9cd0eda4284bf3e3e901fdc78f32763355a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 (Simultaneous pathwise block bound) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Assume, in addition to Assumption~\ref{ass:time}, the Galerkin-state finite-state condition stated there.  Fix a final loss $\eps>0$.  Choose $0<\eps_0<\eps$ and $\rho>0$ so that
