{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.705813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e56edf8e64ad4e64cac46ca7d55de991b857566aec6301d6d50ad0b7d5e40778","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:remvit of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Let $g$ be a smooth, compactly supported function with $\textup{dist}(\supp g, x_0)=c_1>0$, where $x_0\in \mathbb{T}_{L}$. Then, we have
