{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.907676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e581f97c7846619b431ce829015c27151be7a86bf7d25d46cf1533bda8a2a84e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:global:majorization:onesided of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$, let $\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}: \R^{d_1 \times d_2}  \to \R$ be the $\varepsilon$-smoothed nuclear norm (eq:smoothedell1:objective of the paper) and $Q_{\varepsilon}(\cdot \mid \mathbf{X}): \R^{d_1 \times d_2} \to \R$ be the quadratic model function of (eq:smoothedell1:IRLSmajorizer of the paper) defined by the left-sided or right-sided weight operator (eq:W:operator:action of the paper) using core matrix (eq:leftsided:mean of the paper) or (eq:rightsided:mean of the paper), respectively. Then, $Q_{\varepsilon}(\cdot \mid \mathbf{X})$ majorizes $\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}$ globally:
