{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.559448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e587b60704797823389e2557351986687116f456033eb6e5fd5a1e8760252abb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma enormous_bound_lite of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Let $Y$ be a real-valued random variable. If the degree of the polynomial $N$ is even with leading coefficient $p_N$ such that  $\, \mathfrak{Re}(p_N) < 0$, then the map $x \mapsto \mathbb{E}\left[\exp({p(x + Y)})\right]$ is entire; that is, there exists a complex sequence $\bm{u} = (\bm{u}^0, \bm{u}^1, \ldots)$ such that
