{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.344966+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5906c2bd4a94e183db8956e470cf8c1f51a41d6fe3a81d1df986b5f0befb0b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:AT+LSI of arXiv:2507.08692, 'Some notes on higher order concentration of measure'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on a product of of finite sets $\mathcal{X} = \otimes_{i = 1}^n \mathcal{X}_i$. Assume that there are $\alpha_1, \alpha_2 \in (0,1)$ such that $\tilde{\beta}(\mu) \ge \alpha_1$ and that there is some interdependence matrix $J$ such that $\lvert J \rvert_\mathrm{op} \le 1 - \alpha_2$.
