{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.355152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e593a3349110966084f2a59440d8a95d6aa08c72140372f871f1b572b8040580","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] There are \(n_0\geq 1\), \(c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), any \(1\leq l< k\leq n\) with \(n^{2/3} \leq k-l \leq 2n^{2/3}\), and any \(x\geq 0\),
