{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.921467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5c76bf183878ba69eefdf4fb85aaea4a355c5fd1d86540a80ecc9b3e0b8bde3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $r\ge 1$ and $n\ge 2$ be integers. Let $p$ be a prime number such that $p>n-1$.
    Then
    \[
    p \text{ divides } \binom{n+(pr-1)-1}{pr-1}={(-1)}^{pr-1}\binom{-n}{pr-1}
    \]
