{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.848947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e15b8ebf3559d1dc882dd4061fa2fa5e57c682ff0c7b3eac29656430fc852c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 56 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] Let $E\subset F$ be a super order dense sublattice and let $B\subset F$ be solid. The following sets are equal:
\item[(i)] The set of all $f\in F$ such that there is $Q\subset B_{+}$ with $Q\uparrow\left|f\right|$;
\item[(i')] The set of all $f\in F$ such that there is $Q\subset B_{+}\cap E$ with $Q\uparrow\left|f\right|$;
\item[(ii)] The order adherence of $B$ in $F$;
\item[(ii')] The order adherence of $B\cap E$ in $F$;
\item[(iii)] The uo adherence of $B$ in $F$;
\item[(iii')] The uo adherence of $B\cap E$ in $F$.\medskip

This set is solid and its intersection with $E$ is the common $\sigma$-order and $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ adherence of $B\cap E$ in $E$. The $\sigma$-order and $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ closures of $B$ and $B\cap E$ also coincide, and are a solid set. Both the adherence and the closure are convex, whenever $B$ is. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.011073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e1f76a6700bbf05ec8c5f429344fcda99030f0a2e45922d03c6313b98476d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] The graph $\mathfrak C(\mathbf r(u),\mathbf 1,\mathbf d)$ is balanced
at every non-root vertex if and only if
\begin{equation}
 d_j\ge\varepsilon_j(u)
 \qquad(1\le j<n).
\end{equation}
No condition is required in rank $n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.612254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e2570fd12e1cd94c408c5033a813b4d699cad284731f036c9a38050b6d43f8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 15 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] We have the equality,
	\begin{align*}
		Z_2(\mu,\nu) &=  \min\left\{ \int_X \! \int_Y \!\frac{1}{2} \bigg( \Big| \frac{dq}{d\gamma}(x,y) - x \Big|^2\! \!\!+ \Big| \frac{dq}{d\gamma}(x,y) - y \Big|^2  \bigg)   \gamma(dxdy) \, : \, 	(\gamma,q) \in \Gamma Q(\mu,\nu)  \right\}
