	and the set of minimizers is identical to the set of minimizers in \eqref{eq:C_gammaq}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.524528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e3c2e3251aef8696847b20f2d9e960d0e3ae531804a1efb59b36ee2ce64083","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:Jrr-sharper of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:averaged_ball_connection}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha>1$.

     Let $\varepsilon \in(0,1)$.

    Then there exists $c = c(G,J)$ such that for all $k\in \mathbf{N}$, at least $(1-\varepsilon)$ proportion of the radii $r \in [2^{k-1},2^k]$ satisfy

    \begin{equation}

        J
        \left(
            B(r), 
            B(r)^c
        \right)
        \leq 
         \frac{c}{\varepsilon}
        r^{
        \max
        \left(
            d(2-\alpha),
            d - 1
        \right)  
        }
        \log(r)^{
            \mathbf{1}
            \left(
                \alpha=1+1/d
            \right)
        }.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.313584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e45ab935f777e66990b3d2c2eda7e7a48b6d4aa562ea6f712e3b8129993848","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ito-formula of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] \textbf{(It\={o}-Formula for $\|\phi\|^2_{V}$})
Let $\phi(t)$ be a solution of (equation eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper), then it holds 
\begin{align*}
   |\phi(t)|^2 + |\nabla \phi(t)|^2 + 2\int_0^t|A^{1/2} \phi(s)|^2ds = |\phi_0|^2 + |\nabla \phi_0|^2 + \kappa t + 2\int_0^t\left\langle\phi(s), dW_s\right\rangle,
\end{align*}
where $\kappa := \sum_k \sigma_k^2|(I-\Delta)^{-1/2}f_k|^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.575078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5e76fe45784fc68e517182fdc8960eb9ce90d9422341e51185c098e3e275942","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 55 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:rand_sc_eq}, for every fixed integer $r\geq1$, uniformly for deterministic vectors $\bbv,\bbw\in\C^L$,
        \begin{align}
                \abs{\partial_{i\mu}^r(Q)_{\bbv\bbw}} \prec (1+\phi)^{r+1}\frac{\vphi+\eta}{N\eta}\|\bbv\|\|\bbw\|. 
        \end{align}
        Moreover,
        \begin{align}
                \abs{(Q)_{\bbv\bbw}} \prec (1+\phi)^4\left(\frac{\vphi+\eta}{N\eta}\right)^{3/2}\|\bbv\|\|\bbw\|. 
        \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.572223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e5ebb2ce834ee92dbb854f47c02e6dbb4ae5bad29ddbe36e46aac27fe33e8678","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. For $\eps_*>0$ sufficiently small, every $z$ with $|z-E_*|<\eps_*$ and $\Im z\geq0$ satisfies
        \begin{align}
