{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.732660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e602539e0ae9c14fc42e3e0c146a827c67c1d53ac18dd863fc74d0e1d602a23f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2605.18136, 'L\'evy processes with partially stochastic resetting'] Let $q,\lambda >0$, $p \in (0,1)$ and $[u_1,u_2] \subset \B$ s.t.~$[pu_1,pu_2] \subset \B$. Then, for $x \in \B$ and $f \in C_\mathrm{b}(\B)$, 
