{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.668329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e67d6211542d5022d0f7fc0d50a33ddef0cb9349ce3bb4b5ed756962b1a7b69a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Almost Covering Maps) of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] A continuous proper surjection $ f: X \longrightarrow Y$ between path-connected, locally compact, Hausdorff spaces $X$ and $Y$ is called an \textbf{almost covering map}
    	if 
    	\begin{enumerate}
    	\item there exists a nowhere dense closed set $R \subset Y$ such that the restriction $f \vert_{f^{-1}(Y \setminus R)} : f^{-1}(Y \setminus R) \longrightarrow
    	Y \setminus R$ is a finite covering map, and
    	\item there is a finite decomposition $R=\bigsqcup_{\beta}T_{\beta}$ such that the restriction $f \vert_{f^{-1}(T_{\beta})}:f^{-1}(T_{\beta}) \longrightarrow T_{\beta}$ is a fiber bundle for each $\beta$.
        \end{enumerate}
        The set $Y \setminus R$ is called the regular set of the almost covering map $f$, and the set $R$ is referred to as a fibered set of the map $f$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.134222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e67f8e4bec4cec1b027b1f60970444f5a02ddbb1397ff74eeadb512dbb25ff65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.10515, 'Limiting Law of Local Fields for the Mean Field Ghatak-Sherrington Model'] There exists $a_0>0$, depending only on $S,D,h$ and the high-temperature bound, such that
