{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.701331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6926c5ea189040fdfd81b21b7ea957e71cde27bbcb40db0d8825150939e95b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem tail of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] There exists a constant $C>1$ that depends on $\mathbf{k}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{k}_{l}$ and $\sigma$, and is uniform in $N$, such that for all $N\ge 100$,
