{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.245684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e6c80137abc249b680d0242c63c3a6588bd26ad1a9a32accbae69a85da31f433","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Given $H_+,H_-:\mX_{a,b,c}\mapsto \mathbb R$, with ${H_-}\le {H_+}$ pointwise,
