{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.046129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e708bd3c2fb668e5de9630bf92115f8c495b81719dffbbc1d3652209e0985a46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] Assume that under $\bbQ$ the conductances are i.i.d.\ (or more generally that $\bbQ$ satisfies a mixing condition, see Remark~\ref{rem:Discussion}, 1)). Then, there exists $\Omega_{\mathrm{typ}}$ with full $\bbQ$-measure such that for all $\omega\in \Omega_{\mathrm{typ}}$
