    Then, for all $z\in \C$, $t\geq 0$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{L}\pr{\acc{(x,\xi)\in [0,1]^d\times \T^d\m;\m \bb{p(x,\xi)-z}^2\leq t}}\leq Ct^\kappa
    \end{equation}
    where
    \begin{equation}
        \kappa=\frac{1}{2S}\mm\text{and}\mm C= 14d\pr{\frac{\sqrt{\Xi}}{m}}^{\frac{1}{S}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.505382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e727f549549714c50a906533ce39111973390717279c7af4297b208727b5a5a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 94 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] The convolution operator
\begin{align*}
\mathscr{I} : \big( C([0,T],D(A)), \| \cdot \|_{\infty} \big) \to \big( \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W), \interleave \cdot \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \big)
