{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.854389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e735ca06ecf990c854134cdc82a86c08b554307669258d91ba3f2a4642783da0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:l_and_bb_pin of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $x \in (0,1)$, and let $l^x \in C_0$ be defined by
	\begin{equation*}
		l^x_{\xi} \coloneqq \frac{\xi}{x} \, \mathds{1}_{[0,x]}(\xi) + \frac{1-\xi}{1-x} \, \mathds{1}_{(x,1]}(\xi), \quad \xi \in [0,1].
	\end{equation*}
	Consequently, we define the stochastic process $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x} \coloneqq \big(\beta_{\xi} - \beta_x  l_{\xi}^x \big)_{\xi \in [0,1]}$. Note that the paths of $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}$ are in $C_0$, and we have $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}_x = 0$ by construction.","status":"unverified"}

