\end{align}
All constants are uniform in \(J,N,O\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.433009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7499bd48b6e4ae49c74e5e575cca7979e2ed3443eb7ad7d0d7d0151f317a5ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma10.444 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Under the assumption of Theorem (Theorem1.2 of the paper), for any $\delta_1,\delta_2\geq e^{-cn^{\sigma}}$, any $u\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$, and any $p>1$, we have the following estimate:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\mathbb{E}_{A_n}\sup_{r_1,r_2\in\mathbb{R}}\mathbb{P}_X\left(
    \frac{|\langle (A_n-\lambda_i I_n)^{-1}X,X\rangle-r_i|}{\|(A_n-\lambda_i I_n)^{-1}\|_*}\leq\delta_i
