    where the constant $c>0$ in the assumption $\delta_i\geq e^{-cn^\sigma}$ and the implied constant in the inequality $\lesssim$ depend on all the constants $B,\kappa,\Delta,\sigma$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.787517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e74a11a3b8ff8b4040dc4dd213bf7e9c331285c6cf8b6234a98b3c1ff2fec83d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Survival along a sequence of stars) of arXiv:2604.00630, 'The contact process on a bipartite spatial network'] Let~$G$ be a bipartite graph. Let~$(x_k)_{k\ge 0}$ and~$(y_k)_{k \ge 1}$ be sequences of vertices of~$G$ such that:
	\begin{itemize}
