{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.061833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e74e0010fb2bd03aa40a2186e09bcd4739f185e62ec90f528c3b0da343f7be1b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem branching_rate_upper_bound of arXiv:2506.10623, 'Polynomial slowdown in an angle-dependent 2d branching Brownian motion'] There exists $\sigma,L > 0$ such that, for any $0 \leq s_0 \leq t$,  on the event $\{ \forall s \in [s_0,t], X_s \leq \sqrt{2} s \text{ and } \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\lvert\theta_s\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rvert < \sigma \}$ as well as on the event $\{ \forall s \in [s_0,t], X_s \leq \sqrt{2} s \text{ and } \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\lvertY_s\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rvert < \sigma s \}$, we have

