{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.856867+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e753e6f256741cbc8399f82d60748613d22e73def92d026a981494c3dd64a9cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.20519, '\textbf{High-dimensional limits arising from \\ hyperbolic Poisson $k$-plane processes}'] Let $(d_n,k_n)_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence satisfying $k_n < d_n$, $2k_n > d_n+1$ and $d_n \to \infty$ as $n\to\infty$.
