{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.070273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e75c25face46a4b97c4dd84a32a20db9fcfddae3357949e72519cce26d6483c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.01832, 'MA(1) processes with uniform innovations conditioned to stay positive in the non-expanding'] For $\theta\in[-1,1)$ and $a>-1$, there is some $t\in\{a,-\frac{1}{\theta},0\}$ such that for $y\in[-t,1]$, the limiting process $M'$ in \eqref{def_lim_process} exists and is a time-homogeneous Markov chain on $[-t,1]$ with reduced transition kernel 
\begin{align*}
     p'(x_1,\d x_2)&\coloneqq \mathds{1}_S(x_2,x_1)\frac{h(x_2)}{h(x_1)}\frac{1}{\lambda}\frac{1}{a+1}\,\d x_2,~~~~~~~~x_1,x_2\in[-t,1],
\end{align*}
 where $h:\R\to\R$ is the unique (up to multiplication with a constant) and positive (on the effective state space) eigenfunction satisfying the eigenvalue equation
