{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.743762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7816bdc1f8909c9362dba9eda0db75302e288da8f35227c9052e00c0a6a841a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor lem:simplyconnleaves of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a cooriented $C^0$-foliation on $M$ transverse to $\partial M$ (if nonempty). If $\Lambda$ is a minimal set of $\mathcal{F}$ consisting of simply connected leaves, then one of the cases in the following table holds:

