		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.076965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e78497ca4c4d5b5c73e13211624a5c8d24345f2d51384c88a683b0a257ff4b12","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.02570, 'Stochastic completeness for landmark space'] Suppose the radial scalar function $k\colon [0,\infty)\to\R$ is smooth on $(0,\infty)$. Fix $\lmz\in \Land$ and let $R>0$. We then have, for all $\lm\in B(\lmz,R)$ and all $i,j\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ with $i\not=j$,
