{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.655306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e78c566c7dbb8cfdb06f7877289abf8d232f80ee9718b6f22a4bc78e0e3d59b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:v-is-concave of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] The function defined in equation (equation eq:log-Wilson-loop of the paper) satisfies the following properties.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $v(R,T)$ is concave in both variables. That is for all $R,T,r,t \in \N$ with $r \leq R$ and $t \leq T$,
        \begin{equs}
            v(R,T) &\geq \frac{1}{2}(v(R+r,T)+v(R-r,T)),\\
            v(R,T) & \geq \frac{1}{2}(v(R,T+t)+v(R,T-t)).
        \end{equs}
