{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.792650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e78e6682a1e133e7de72b7fec205ce58bf138dd8c0f9e32e383904741ddb1087","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:SRBM_d3 of arXiv:2509.20779, 'Diffusive Scaling limit of stochastic Box-Ball systems and P\MakeLowercase{ush}TASEP'] Let $(\zeta_{\lfloor t\rfloor})_{t\ge 0}$ denote the continuous-time SBBS with $d=3$, capacity $c\ge 3$, and  error probability $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$. As $n\rightarrow\infty$, 
			\begin{align}
