{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.121104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7928143765f644f195762e410cce1a05d93ad1fda6cfdcb687f291c0f9e0d6a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 12 (Super-regular pair) of arXiv:2604.05138, 'Convergence rate of $H$-property for step-graphons'] Let $G$ be an undirected graph, and $A,B$ be two disjoint subsets of $V(G)$.
The pair $(A,B)$ is {\bf $(\epsilon,\delta)$-super-regular} if
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(X,Y) &> \delta |X||Y|, 
\\
&\text{for any } X \subseteq A,\; Y \subseteq B
\\
&\text{with } |X| > \epsilon |A|,\; |Y| > \epsilon |B|,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and, moreover,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(a,B) &> \delta |B|, && \mbox{for all } a \in A, \\
e(b,A) &> \delta |A|, && \mbox{for all } b \in B.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.590231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e794ca63865fb20e69072f3490d661667140ca2125c3e34270407a5080adc762","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem CTSE-O-C of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $\gamma  \in \left[ {0,\frac{1}{3}} \right)$, assume that $\mathrm{Tr} \left( {Q + {Q^{\frac{1}{2}}}{{\left( { - \Delta } \right)}^{\frac{1 + \gamma }{2} + \rho}}{{\left( {{Q^{\frac{1}{2}}}} \right)}^*}} \right) <  \infty$ with $0 < \rho \ll 1$, where $Q$ denotes the covariance operator of ${\mathfrak{W}}\left( {t} \right)$. Then, there exists a stopping time $\mathfrak{t}$ satisfying $\mathbb{P}\left( {0 < {\mathfrak{t}} \leqslant T} \right) = 1 $ such that Eq.(equation 2DEEUGE1 of the paper) admits martingale solutions 
