{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.612047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7af239e0142fa5f24c000cacb5c1c37a8ce16539b2157c3def14f803dd15d11","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 34 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Assume $1\ll a_n\le (\log n)^{1/2}$. There exists a coupling between $\Lambda_{n,\beta,2a_n}=\{\lambda_{1,2a_n}^{(n)}<\lambda_{2,2a_n}^{(n)}<\cdots<\lambda_{n,2a_n}^{(n)}\}$ and $\Bessel_{\beta,2a_n}=\{\lambda_{1,2a_n}^B<\lambda_{2,2a_n}^B<\cdots\}$ so that for any fixed $k$ and $0<\alpha<1$ we have 
