{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.706307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7b233f0d76717f6153a1272f033a00e6060c8b7f77b3552f27d4b69dd8b85fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_time_0 of arXiv:2604.10214, 'Large deviations for maximum local time of simple random walk in dimensions \texorpdfstrin'] For any $m\in \mathbb N$ and $s\ge 0$,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb P}\big(\xi(\infty,0)> m\big)=(1-\gamma)^m;
\qquad
{\mathbb P}\big(\ell(\infty,0)> s\big)=e^{-\gamma s}.
\end{align}
In particular, for $\beta>0$, $n\in\mathbb N$ and $t>0$,
\begin{align}
\begin{aligned}
