    Moreover if $\psi^N $ attains a minimum at time $ t= \overline t  $, then $ \psi^N $ is constant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.246499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7cfa7365ce4d6a65045acc26cdcbf0b5d626482938204688371327aeafaf296","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] The {\em relative Faber-Krahn inequality} $FK_a(n,r_1,r_2)$ holds in $B$, if for all $x\in B$, $r\in[r_1,r_2]$ and $U\subset B_x(r) $, we have
