{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.906062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7d3ed4042bf001f7caf74f2b1e06d66c8544a95e97ca9ecc3260d4098ac511b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:core of process of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $V$ be an  upper probability on a measurable space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$, and  $\textbf{Y}=\{Y_n\}_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a bounded stationary process on a capacity space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V)$. Then for any $\widetilde{P}\in \operatorname{core}(V_{\textbf{Y}})$, there exists  $P'\in\operatorname{core}(V)$ such that 
