{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.346588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7d9a0283d35c78c8958e699697fbae250d3cfbdf9ad7f2555dfc6e0e04e01e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:transport of arXiv:2607.24705, 'Derangetropy Operators'] Let $f_{0} \in \mathcal{D}_{+}^{2}$ and let $f_{t}$ solve the
		canonical flow~(equation eq:flow of the paper), with inverse transport
		$B_{t} = A_{t}^{-1}$ given in the coordinate
		$V(z) = \tan(\pi(z - \tfrac12))$ by
		\begin{equation}
			V\circ B_{t} = e^{-t}\,V,
			\qquad
			B_{t}'(z) = \frac{e^{-t}\big(1 + V(z)^{2}\big)}
