		Schwarzian anomaly. The same holds for every element of the isotropy
		group of Theorem~(thm:exceptional of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.777192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7de19b10da2a35b785111d7d4c69c1fd66f44c685337ec2fe7965232a15914c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] We define maps  $\bb_0$ and $r_0$ by
    \begin{equation}
      \bb_0: \StokesV \times \StokesV \times \StokesV\ni(\bu,\bv,\bw)\mapsto \sum_{i,j= 1}^{d} \int_{\domO} \bu^i(x)\, \partial_i \bv^j(x)\,\bw^j(x) \in \mathbb{R}
    \end{equation}
and
   \begin{align}
       r_0: W^{1,4}(\domO) \times W^{1,4}(\domO) \times \StokesV \ni  (\phi,\psi, \bu)&\mapsto  \sum_{i,j=1}^d \int_{\domO} \partial_i \phi(x)\, \partial_j \psi(x)\, \partial_j \bu^i(x)\,\d x \in \mathbb{R}.
      \end{align}

By the H\"older inequality, there exists a generic constant $C>0$ such that 
   \begin{equation}
      \lvert \bb_0(\bu,\bv,\bw) \rvert \leq C \Vert \bu \Vert_{\mathbb{L}^4} \lvert \nabla\bw \rvert_{\mathbb{L}^2} \Vert \bv \Vert_{\mathbb{L}^4}, \;\;\forall \bu,\,\bv,\,\bw \in \StokesV. 
   \end{equation}
   and
   \begin{equation}
      \lvert r_0(\phi,\psi,\bu) \rvert \leq C \Vert \bu \Vert_{\StokesV} \Vert \nabla \phi \Vert_{\mathbb{L}^4} \Vert \nabla \psi  \Vert_{\mathbb{L}^4} , \;\;\forall \bu \in \StokesV,\, \phi,\, \psi \in W^{1,4}(\domO).
   \end{equation}
In view of the Gagliardo-Nirenberg inequality \eqref{Gagliardo-Nirenberg-inequality}, employing a standard density argument, we deduce the following inequality and Lemma
   \begin{equation}
      \lvert \bb_0(\bu,\bv,\bw) \rvert  \leq  C \lvert \bu \rvert_{\StokesH}^{1 -\frac d4} \lvert \nabla \bu \rvert_{\mathbb{L}^2}^{\frac d4} \lvert \bv \rvert_{\StokesH}^{1 - \frac d4} \lvert \nabla \bv \rvert_{\mathbb{L}^2}^{\frac d4} \lvert \nabla \bw \rvert_{\mathbb{L}^2}, \;\;\;\forall \bu,\,\bv,\,\bw \in \StokesV,
   \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

