{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.951956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7e14a75dee84d4ff926d234f35cb1b376b7e4f40626eafc9a9a79a8712b1564","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 (Sharp Small-Coefficient  Variant of Khintchine's Inequality) of arXiv:2608.29703, 'A Sharp Small-Coefficient Variant of Khintchine's Inequality and the Sharp $\pi/2$ Theorem'] There exist universal constants $C,\beta_{0}>0$
