{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.761442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7eda1a40f22dfff1dcc098212dbc840db97546bfd89eca5d09b466a7f46c8a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition increment-moments of arXiv:2604.27682, 'Multifractional Stable Motion with Random Hurst Exponent'] Under condition (equation eq: continuity assumption on H of the paper), for any $\delta>0$, there are constants $C > 0$ and $\epsilon > 0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
