{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.875334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e80638c12ba59196d8e69662b7021d53a9b28bf8d7956389a018b8c8bd846b30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:modularity_function of arXiv:2605.10911, 'The stochastic block model has the overlap graph property for modularity'] Fix $a>b>0$ and integer $k\geq 2$. Let $p=p(n)=\omega\; a / n$ and $q=q(n)=\omega \; b/n$. For any $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $c=c(\varepsilon)$ such that, if $\omega>c$ for $n$ large enough, then the following holds with probability at least $1-\varepsilon$ provided $n$ is large enough.

Let $G \in \mathcal{G}(n,k,p,q)$ and denote the planted partition by $\mathcal{P}$. Then,
\begin{equation}
\left| q_\mathcal{P}(G)  - \frac {a-b}{a+(k-1)b} \left( 1 - \frac {1}{k} \right) \right| \le \frac {\varepsilon}{2}
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
\Big| q^{\star}(G) - q_\mathcal{P}(G) \Big| \le \frac {\varepsilon}{2}.
\end{equation}
As a result, 
$$
\left| q^{\star}(G)  - \frac {a-b}{a+(k-1)b} \left( 1 - \frac {1}{k} \right) \right| \le \varepsilon.
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

