{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.580728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8090465f34c7ac4668454d3cc0143e14809969d4be72a4eb0ef772b483b5cd1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmanvnowvowv of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] Let 
\begin{equation}

w_{\gamma,\nu}(k)=\frac{\Gamma(\gamma-1-k)\Gamma(\nu+k+2)}{\Gamma(\gamma-1)},\ \ k\in \Bbb N.
\end{equation}
then:\\ 
\begin{enumerate}
\item  value for $k\ge K$: $\forall j\ge 0$, 
