{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.993980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8389dc105a3b5871fbbcbc926f5758d63faf6b6a6efe09a9ac67c8205f4eb89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ratio of arXiv:2608.25362, 'Fluctuations of the free energy of the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model with ferromagnetic i'] For $\beta< 1$ and a sequence of non-negative numbers $ (\gamma_N)_{N \geqslant 1}$ satisfying $\gamma_N < 1$ and $ \sqrt{N} (1 - \gamma_N) \to \infty$, we have
