{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.056149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e83a14da08fab67fb51053aa5b8b3adc658c55bc8f002b43b639a3498311a941","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\mathcal{H}_m$ be a Euclidean class with exponent $V$. Then for any $j \in [m]$, 
