{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.667545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e886593d0239e495397974be05718886be3957333501a70f52b346e2ea1185f5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition_RL_functions of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Let $m \in \mathbb{Z}$ and suppose that for all $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(\overline{\mathbb{Z}})$,
