{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.849970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e88a4b8b660d93021a75406b53ed84978bd3a37494cc06d65efb3ebba4c09868","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2609.03869, '\bf Sharp asymptotics for a transport model with a nonlocal condition of the Fisher-KPP ty'] Let $\lambda(\xi)\in\mathbb{C}$ be the  unique solution of \eqref{A4} for  $\xi\in[-\varep,\varep]$, with $\varep>0$ as given in Lemma  \ref{lem_analysis of lambda} (ii). Then, the Fourier transform $\widehat\Phi$ of the function $\Phi$ given in \eqref{renewal eqn=3} satisfies the following property:
