{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.827372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8bc922d98e73d8203dd11b5b6532ef5461d7878d08e4cf9211c08a0c03dfdbe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition signature of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $x:[0,T]\to E$ be a path of bounded variation. Its signature over $[s,t]$ is
\begin{equation}
