{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.627973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e92708e5d67dd0603e4c160c50c624df5156b7232300f4d3c605bb23136741f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:normal_domain_comonotonic of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{Z}$ be $\alpha$-stable with $\alpha \in (0,2)$ and $\bm{X}$ be in its domain of normal attraction. Let Assumption~(\nameref{asm:C}) (with constant $H\equiv G$ and $Q\equiv 1$) hold for some $p\in(0,\infty)\setminus\{\alpha-1\}$. Then, for any $q\in(0,1]\cap(0,\alpha)$ with $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^q]<\infty$, we have, as $t \downarrow 0$, 
\[
