{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.805606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e942618fe57ea5fa06fe61236ab1045ba378d22ab76ef3fe19e9387e5e0e8d3a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:Int-4 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] For $0 \le u \le s \le w \le r \le t$, let the term $\mathcal{J}_4(t;\varepsilon,\eta)$ be defined as follows:
\begin{multline*}
\mathcal{J}_4(t;\varepsilon,\eta)  \triangleq  K \int_{u=0}^t \int_{s=u}^t \int_{w=s}^t \int_{r=w}^t  (\varepsilon+ \eta + \sqrt{\varepsilon \eta})^2 e^{-2 \alpha (t-u)} e^{-\alpha(t-w)} e^{-\alpha(t-r)} e^{-\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r-w)} \\
\times  e^{-\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (w-s)}     dr \thinspace dw \thinspace ds \thinspace du.  
\end{multline*}
Then, there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
$$ \mathcal{J}_4(t;\varepsilon,\eta) \le K \thinspace \eta^2 \thinspace (\varepsilon+ \eta + \sqrt{\varepsilon \eta})^2 .$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.823200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e946081da7dc9fb76e47ab57941e0ca1f80658adae3d29b196e994780cec5162","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:half_crossing of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] Let $B=[-w,w]\times[s,s+h]$ be a space-time box, and let $B^+=[0,w]\times[s,s+h]$ and $B^-=[-w,0]\times[s,s+h]$ denote its right and left halves, respectively.

  We define the following events with respect to the genealogical paths introduced in (def:jump_path of the paper):

  \begin{description}
    \item[Right spatial half-crossing] $S^+(B)$ is the event that there exists a genealogical path starting from $\{0\}\times[s,s+h]$ that reaches $\{w\}\times[s,s+h]$ while remaining entirely inside $B^+$.

    \item[Left spatial half-crossing] $S^-(B)$ is the event that there exists a genealogical path starting from $\{0\}\times[s,s+h]$ that reaches $\{-w\}\times[s,s+h]$ while remaining entirely inside $B^-$.

    \item[Temporal half-crossing] $T(B)$ is the event that there exists a genealogical path starting from $[-w,w] \times \{s\}$ that reaches $[-w,w] \times \{s+h/2\}$ while remaining entirely inside $B$.
  \end{description}
  The \emph{half-crossing event} of $B$ is defined as the union
  \begin{equation}
    H(B) = S^+(B) \cup S^-(B) \cup T(B).
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.252247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e94636eec3d50d3935d2db0a8013a8e9652fb41defe160b0053ccc921f7790cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Wasserstein-$p$ bound SSQ reduction of arXiv:2603.14163, '\LARGE \bf Tail Bounds for Queues with Abandonment: Constant, Moderate, Large Deviations, '] \textnormal{(Wasserstein-$p$ Bound Reduction for SSQ)}
    With the same notations above, for $p \leq \lambda/(2\gamma)$: 
    \begin{align*}
        W_p(\mathcal{L}(\tilde{q}), \mathcal{L}(Z))&\leq C_{10, \lambda, \mu} \cdot \big(p\sqrt{\gamma} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{\gamma}} \|\mathbf{1}_{q=0} \|_{L^p} +\gamma\sqrt{p} \| q - \frac{\lambda-\mu}{\gamma}\|_{L^p} \big)
    \end{align*}
    Here $C_{10, \lambda,\mu}$ is constant independent of $\gamma$ and $p$, defined in (equation eq: C_10, lambda, mu of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

