{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.822094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e974d6c547e3352f71db91e289ea21e040100c0af77ac9d0220e3496b80d4777","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thmmin of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Assume that the minimal $\mathrm{CBDI}$ processes $X^{\mathrm{m}}$ and $Y^{\mathrm{m}}$ with mechanisms respectively $(\Psi,\hat{\Psi})$ and $(\hat{\Psi},\Psi)$ do not explode. Then, under the convention $0^+\cdot \infty,\ \infty\cdot 0^+,$
