{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.538253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e979ebb05ff28d82c19f9486734372664fe752b0a294621e0bd3bc6084916759","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cor1:sig:gam of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)}, \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:lip of the paper)} and \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:super of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:derv:liningam of the paper)}  hold, then for   $ 2\leq p_0\leq \min\{{\bar p}/((\eta+1)
