{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.622640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e97fd089928c8f85d0105ffb921ff7e4010c340cba4a0f57e7c4a6025934a565","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Stopped estimates) of arXiv:2608.16256, 'Error Distribution of the Local Linearization Method for Stochastic Differential Equations'] \label[lemma]{le:ll_stopped_int_l2}
For every \(\rho>0\), there exists \(C_\rho<\infty\) such that, for
\(p=2,4\),
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        \sup_{s\in I_m^n}
        \left|
            \hat X^n_{s\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}
            -
            \hat X^n_{t_{m-1}^n\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}
        \right|^p
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-p/2}.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        \int_0^{\tau_{n,\rho}}
        |\hat X_s^n-\hat X_{\varphi_n(s)}^n|^2\,ds
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-1},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        \left(
            \int_0^{\tau_{n,\rho}}
            |\hat X_s^n-\hat X_{\varphi_n(s)}^n|^2\,ds
        \right)^2
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-2},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        \sup_{t\le1}
        |X_{t\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}-
        \hat X^n_{t\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}|^2
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-3} .
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        \int_0^{\tau_{n,\rho}}|X_s-\hat X_s^n|^2\,ds
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-3},
\end{equation}
and, for \(m=0,\dots,n\),
\begin{equation}
    \Exp*{}{
        |X_{t_m^n\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}
        -\hat X^n_{t_m^n\wedge\tau_{n,\rho}}|^2
    }
    \le
    C_\rho n^{-3} .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.420482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9808e203cc9af03d6ea2d2f23fbb21b897da2ac4d27650f480a7b8b771a648c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2605.16733, 'Concentration Inequalities for Sample Cross-Covariances'] Let \((X_i,Y_i)_{i=1}^N\) be i.i.d. copies of a centered Gaussian random
