{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.310898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e985256e152fb3ca6f6d56cd723fff9ea174b38b4d66c0df0b5143c15869c7e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] For any $0 <\gamma < \frac{2q}{q-1}$, the distributions $\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_t \circ (\widetilde{L}_t)^{-1}$ under the Gibbs measure \eqref{eq:self-gibbs-measure} satisfy an LDP in $\widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1}(\mathbb{R})$ with good rate function
