{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.634563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9b82ac96dab24992c437d92f166326ac830a46989bd8386b505486988dad2c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: profil pour les involutions aléatoires of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $p\in (0,1)$.
    Let $a\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $. Let $S\subset {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} $ and $(t_n)_{n\in S}$ be a sequence of integers such that $t_n =\frac{\ln n +a+o(1)}{\ln(1/p)} $.
    As $S \ni n\to \infty$ we have 
\begin{equation}
    \ensuremath{\textup{d}_\textup{TV}} \left( \left(\ensuremath{\textup{RI}}_{n,p}\right)^{*t_n}, \ensuremath{\textup{Unif}}_{{\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n}\right) \to \ensuremath{\textup{d}_\textup{TV}}\left(  \ensuremath{\textup{Poiss}}\left( 1+e^{-a}\right), \ensuremath{\textup{Poiss}}(1)\right).
