{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:26:47.149686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e9d42c624c189484810d26e4ae31d484642b41de7ad84beafcd4e174d4794c35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2608.29361, 'Convergence of the subcritical $\gamma$-LQG metric to the critical $2$-LQG metric as $\gam'] Fix a bounded open set $U \subseteq \CC$ and let $\varepsilon \in (0,1), \alpha \in (0,1/4), A \in (2,\infty)$ be such that $\alpha (1+2/A) < 1/4$. Suppose that the functions $b,M$ are chosen such that $b(\xi) \sqrt{M(\xi)} > 20 A$. Then, there exists a constant $C \in (0,\infty)$ depending only on $\varepsilon,\alpha,A$, and $U$, such that the following hold with probability at least $1-\varepsilon$. For all $z \in U$, we have that
