{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.846356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea12ba6c521dea5da941aba89fb55fc677fcd89c48263dbd3636db1892c71436","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:WishartDiscrepancy of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $W_1,\ldots,W_n$ be a sequence of independent $m \times m$ Wishart matrices with rank $r \leq m$. There exist constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ such that, for $n \ll m^2$,
