{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.826492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea163e08d12b20a068d025cd8d1fbdfed0d24be586ac01322f20388804df5313","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop variational-representation-chi-square of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Given two distributions $P, Q$ with countable supports and let $\cG_Q$ be a collection of functions $g: \R \rightarrow \R$ such that $\E_Q\sqbr{g(X)^2} < \infty\}$, we have
