{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.963392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea240042278f4b74096cea1e306dc2726a498c4e71f5f298e86098400fd25617","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:mass_ex_lvl_set of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C$ be a $d$-dimensional Archimedean copula and $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d}$ its corresponding Williamson measure. Moreover, let $s_1,s_2 \in \mathbb{I}$, with $s_1 \leq s_2$. Then the following assertion holds:
