{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.767901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea71953d3c4555670a8179dcdf4b0e82e0fcafb842ab6345562e31cc32b38014","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Ingredient 21 of arXiv:2608.26803, 'On bubbling of Fueter maps'] Let $V$ be a Hausdorff topological vector space, $W$ a Banach space and $j: V \to W$ a continuous linear map with dense image. Let $K$ be a compact smooth manifold of dimension $k$ and let $\cR \subset W$ be Fredholm $C^1$-rectifiable of codimension $n$. If $k<n$, then 
