{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.070070+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea798af1d08e824d75bfb658d2e2b9b78fa5d9961afcdf0e6951c6bee22b54fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem3 of arXiv:2606.28631, '\Large \bf On the maximal displacement of subcritical branching random walks with stretche'] Define $\psi(u):=\sum_{n=0}^\infty p_n(1-u)^n+ mu-1$ with the convension $0^0=1$. Then the function $u(x):= \mathbb{P}(M>x)$ satisfies
