{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.276033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea869d179c0107252cd8cf7b315961f5f41dc3127f332bf7713701de116b9436","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2606.21394, 'McKean-Vlasov Equations for Large Networks of Neurons with Adaptive Asymmetric Edges'] For any $\epsilon > 0$, there exists $a_{\epsilon} > 0$ such that $\mathbb{P}$-almost-surely,
