{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.663780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea889bf7197ffe6ce4a9a32d5da2724ab7f6bb0e2088b552468628de92ffb0cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 (\bf High-Order Energy Estimate) of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] Let $u^{\epsilon}$ be the classical solution of \eqref{approxnondiv}, then there exists a universal constant $\delta_{0}>0$ such that under the assumptions in Theorem \ref{main} we have
