\mathcal M[F]=\sum_{i<j}\operatorname{Hess}F(V_{ij},V_{ij}).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.209204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea8bda30ce78a94cd980371fb53c6f4756230708d6eafe2916568489c6e08598","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Some estimates due to Aronson) of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] There exists a constant $M > 0$ such that, for all $t > 0$ and $z_0 \in \R^2$,
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{Mt} \, e^{-M|z - z_0|^2 / t - Mt} \leq p_t^{z_0}(z) \leq \frac{M}{t} \, e^{-|z - z_0|^2 / Mt + Mt}.
\end{equation}
Let $g_t^{z_0}(z)$ be defined by
\[
g_t^{z_0}(z) := \int_0^t p_s^{z_0}(u, 0) \, ds.
\]
Then,
\begin{equation}
g_t^{z_0}(z) \leq \frac{M^2 \, e^{ -\frac{|z - z_0|^2}{Mt} + Mt }}{|z - z_0|^2} \, t.
\end{equation}
Finally, for all $z_0 = (a_0, b_0) \in \R^2$ and $x \in \R$,
\begin{equation}
\E_{(a_0, b_0)}\left[e^{x A_t}\right] \leq e^{x^2 M t + a_0 x}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.642142+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea8c01cdcf7c7c1adc5c9a21004d2bba98848b15d1a680cf9c906e37f370af07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2506.18063, 'Reduced critical branching processes in non-favorable random environment \thanks{ This wor'] (Theorem 1 in \cite{VD2023B}). Let Conditions B1 and B2 be
