{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea8ff50848af27288ebf592feec200c671b8be6c404f89e50663da2df1689762","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma re4D of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Under the same assumption as in Lemma (keyI of the paper), let $\tilde{x}_N(s)=\tilde{\mu}_{n,N}-\tilde{\sigma}_{n,N}s$ with
\begin{equation}
    \tilde{\mu}_{n,N}=\left(\frac{1}{\sigma_{n-1,N}^{1/2}}+\frac{1}{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{1/2}}\right)\left(\frac{1}{\mu_{n-1,N}\sigma_{n-1,N}^{1/2}}+\frac{1}{\mu_{n,N-1}\sigma_{n,N-1}^{1/2}}\right)^{-1}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    \tilde{\sigma}_{n,N}=\left(\frac{\sigma_{n-1,N}^{1/2}}{\mu_{n-1,N}}+\frac{\sigma_{n,N-1}^{1/2}}{\mu_{n,N-1}}\right)\left(\frac{1}{\mu_{n-1,N}\sigma_{n-1,N}^{1/2}}+\frac{1}{\mu_{n,N-1}\sigma_{n,N-1}^{1/2}}\right)^{-1}.
\end{equation} 
Then
\begin{equation*}
    N^{\frac{2}{3}}D(\tilde{x}_N(s))\le C(s_0,\gamma)e^{-\frac{s}{2}}
\end{equation*}
holds for any $s\in\left[s_0,\frac{e_0\tilde{\mu}_{n,N}}{\tilde{\sigma}_{n,N}}\right]$ when $N$ large enough.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.590778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea901fd0ee23a6de700bd5efdd027662f4f9719b26bdec6db9a6eeaa8b454bbe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:eqM of arXiv:2412.04973, 'On the Laplace equation with non-local dynamical boundary conditions'] Let us write $M_\Phi(t, \theta) = \mathbf{E}_0[\exp(-\theta L_t)]$, $t>0$, $\theta>0$. Then, $\varphi(t) = M^0_\Phi(t, \theta)$ is the unique solution to
