{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.899224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eab94d15d8aaf6ccea9ff7429d396ac543e2dd60711092e7b4998a901367c8eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition randomwalk of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] Let $\left(X_n\right)_{n \geq 0}$ be a birth--death chain with transition probabilities $\left(p_i, q_i, r_i\right)$, and define $\theta_n = \frac{\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}p_i}{\prod_{i=1}^{n}q_i}$. Consider the sequence of polynomials $\{R_n\}_{n \geq 0}$ determined by the three-term recurrence
