{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.877872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eaca5eca365c837e0a5aa9156273cad0a677d07c01f19b16629fe1beb5d97c22","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro cor:momentmatching of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Suppose that $c_1, \ldots, c_m$ are the first $m \geq 1$ terms of an admissible sequence for $[a,b]$. Then for every integer $k \geq 0$, 
