{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.279015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eaea655081b8425646887733437c42c17631c17e77dcd7142bf54c236a7fc6e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:small-set-return of arXiv:2601.08184, 'Wasserstein-p Central Limit Theorem Rates: From Local Dependence to Markov Chains'] Under Assumption~(assumption:markovchain of the paper), there exist an accessible small set \(\bar C\subseteq \mathcal X\) and a constant \(\kappa>1\) such that
\begin{equation}
    M(a):=\sup_{x\in \bar C}\mathbb{E}_x\big[a^{\sigma_{\bar C}}\big]<\infty,
    \qquad \forall a\in(1,\kappa],
\end{equation}
where $\sigma_{\bar C}:=\inf\{n\ge 1:x_n\in \bar C\}.$ Moreover, there exist \(m\in\mathbb N\), \(\beta\in(0,1)\), and a probability measure \(\nu\) on \(\mathcal X\), supported on \(\bar C\), such that \(\nu(\bar C)=1\), \(\nu(\bar C^c)=0\) and 
