{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.619794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eaf63afab2b5525213e394c7d4a186c2bd92bccf98f468fb4d8aec7a6099f605","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 9 of arXiv:2511.00679, 'Stochastic solutions to abstract telegraph-type equations involving fractional dynamics'] The Fourier transform of the solution of the problem \eqref{fepd} is given by 
\begin{align*}
\widehat{u}(t,\xi) &= \left(\frac{2}{t ||\xi||^{\beta/2}}\right)^{\lambda-\frac{1}{2}}\Gamma\left(\lambda+\frac{1}{2}\right)J_{\lambda-\frac{1}{2}}\left(t||\xi||^{{\beta}/2}\right)\widehat f(\xi)\\
&= \frac{1}{B(\lambda,\frac12)t}\int_{-t}^{t}\left(1-\frac{w^2}{t^2}\right)^{\lambda-1}\left(\frac{e^{i ||\xi||^{{\beta}/2}w}+e^{-i||\xi||^{{\beta}/2}w}}{2}\right)\widehat f(\xi)\de w. 
