{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.141346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eafc3aae11ee6efba2ff99366a9e174c5b86af4c0cfc99797f16438f490d9a71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.05861, '\LARGE Quantitative bounds for high dimensional entropic CLT'] Let $X_1,\dots,X_n$ be i.i.d.\ $\R^d$-valued random vectors with absolutely continuous densities.
	Assume $\E X_1=0$, $\Cov(X_1)=I_d$, and that $X_1$ has finite Poincar\'e constant $R$ and finite Fisher information $I(X_1)$. 
	Under the assumptions and notation above, 
	\begin{equation} 
\E\left[\Bigl|f\Bigl(Z_n\Bigr)-\frac{1}{\sqrt n}\sum_{i=1}^n g(X_i)\Bigr|^2\right]=\sum_{i=2}^n \Delta_i,
	\end{equation}
    where $\Delta_i:=\E\left[\Bigl|
	f_i\Bigl(\frac{S_i}{\sqrt n}\Bigr)-f_{i-1}\Bigl(\frac{S_{i-1}}{\sqrt n}\Bigr)-\frac1{\sqrt n}g(X_i)\Bigr|^2\right]$ with the following lower bound:
	\begin{equation} 
	\Delta_i\ge\frac{i-1}{nI(X_1)R}\E\left[|g(X_1)-MX_1|^2\right], \quad \quad  M=\mathbb{E}[\nabla g(X_1)].
	\end{equation}
    In particular, as $f(\cdot)=\rho_{Z_n}(\cdot)$, we have 
    \begin{equation} 
    M=-I_M(Z_n),
    \end{equation}
    where $I_M(Z_n)$ is the Fisher information matrix of $Z_n$ defined by \eqref{e:FIMatrix}.","status":"unverified"}

