{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.591746+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb0f3a45490b058e3d85e5f941663bbc3dfbb2e59e8e5a01a050ea626889174b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thma 1 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Fix $S$ to be a sufficiently large finite set of places of $F$ containing all the archimedean and ramified places. For $f=f_0$, an induced 

