{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.288517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb1ba621a29af16ac61081cf4e39d5c95fef01a135255b58152d4fe4bdbdd372","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:cPI of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The (classical) \emph{Poincar\'e inequality (PI)} is satisfied if there exists a constant $\alpha>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \forall f\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}: \ \ \operatorname{var}_\pi(f)\leq \frac{1}{\alpha}\mathscr{E}_\pi(f).
\end{equation}
The supremum over all possible choices of  $\alpha$ is called the \emph{Poincar\'e constant}. We denote it by
\begin{equation}
    \alpha_{\PI}(M) \coloneqq \inf_{\substack{f\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|} \\ f\notin \langle\1\rangle}} \frac{\mathscr{E}_\pi(f,M)}{\operatorname{var}_\pi(f)}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.430806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb1e6322acdfcadc1b293308f28d061633e6255276055410536409077d19d944","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:two.point.barycenter.filtered.gaussian of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] One has
\begin{equation}

\inf_{\mathbb{Z}\in\mathcal{FG}}
\left\{(1-u)\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_0,\mathbb{Z})+u\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_1,\mathbb{Z})\right\}
=u(1-u)\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}_0,\mathbb{X}_1),
\end{equation}
and $\mathbb{G}^{\hat a_u,\hat L_u}$ is a minimizer.  Conversely, if $\mathbb{Z}=\mathbb{G}^{b,M}$ is a minimizer, then $b=\hat a_u$ and there exist $Q\in\mathscr Q(L_0,L_1)$ and $R\in\mathscr O(T,d)$ such that
\begin{equation}

M=((1-u)L_0+uL_1Q)R.
\end{equation}
Thus, the set of two-point barycenters in $\mathrm{FG}$ is the collection of equivalence classes generated by (equation eq:two.point.interpolation of the paper) as $Q$ ranges over $\mathscr Q(L_0,L_1)$.","status":"unverified"}

