{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.952891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb27ef7c9469bf764589ad62cd254f34719638b012e8f969ebc835a481461049","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:xibi of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Using the above $\Xi$, $\Xi_1$, $\Xi_2$, $\Xi_3$, $\Xi_4$ notations, we define
\begin{equation} 
\mathbf I_{\beta,\vec\mathbf k}[\vec\mathbf p,\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon}, \mathbf H]=2^{-\boldsymbol{\delta}-|\{\ell\in\llbracket 1,m\rrbracket: \boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell\neq\varnothing\}|}\prod_{(x,y)\in\Xi} \mathbf I_\beta[x,y],
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation*}
\mathbf I_\beta[x,y]=
