        \p(T(x)\geq t) \leq c_{1} e^{-c_{2} t}, 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.597504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb3e06c0f161941d04e8dab169d506b6a6ca6d40c2233d45bcf535fc28ab1df7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:diffusionType of arXiv:2412.05030, 'Characterization of Subordinate Symmetric Markov Processes'] ([BKKL])

  Assume $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ satisfies the diffusion type heat kernel estimate for a scale function $\phi_c$ and 
  let $S$~ be an independent subordinator whose Bernstein function is given in ((eq:Bernstein function of the paper))
  with $\phi := \phi_c$.
  Then, the jump kernel $J(x,y)$ of the subordinate process satisfies 
