{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.724644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb42b47e280a22b8340587201a6314a0f19225dca4c0806e6e627dfc013204da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem new of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\in [0,T}$ be an $S$-valued jump-diffusion with characteristics $(b,a,K)$ and extended generator $\mathcal A$.  Assume that $b_j,a_{ij}\in\mathcal O(S)$, $K$ is a kernel with holomorphic jump size, and let $F$ be the corresponding non-negative measure on the measurable space $E$. 
Let $G$ satisfy (equation eqnG of the paper) and
for each $h\in H(P_G^d(0))$, $z\in P^d_{R(S)+\varepsilon}(0)$, and $y\in E$ set $\mathcal D(J)$ and $Jh$ as in (equation eqnDJ of the paper).
Set 
 \begin{align*}
     \mathcal{V}&\subseteq\{h\in H(P^d_G(0))\colon e^h\in \mathcal D(J)
     \text{ and } P^d_{R(S)+\varepsilon}\ni z\mapsto Je^h(z,\cdot)\in L^1(E,F) \text{ is continuous}\},
\\  \mathcal{V}^*&:=\{\mathbf{u}\in \mathcal{S}^* \colon h_\mathbf{u}=h|_{{P}^d_{R(S)}(0)},  \ h\in \mathcal{V}\}.
 \end{align*}
Then $X$ is an $S$-valued $\mathcal{V}$-affine-holomorphic process and for all $\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{V}^*$, $$\mathcal{A}\exp(h_\mathbf{u})=\exp(h_{\mathbf{u}})R(h_\mathbf{u})|_S,$$ where $R:\mathcal{V}^*\rightarrow \mathcal{S}^*$ is given by
\begin{align}
    R(\mathbf{u})&:= \sum_{|\beta|=1}\mathbf{u}^{(\beta)}\ast \underline{\mathbf{b}}^{\beta} 
    +\sum_{|\beta_1|,|\beta_2|=1}\frac{1}{(\beta_1+\beta_2)!}\underline{\underline{\mathbf{a}}}^{\beta_1+\beta_2}\ast ({\mathbf{u}^{(\beta_1)}}\ast\mathbf{u}^{(\beta_2)}+\mathbf{u}^{(\beta_1+\beta_2)})\\
    &+\bm{\lambda}\ast \int_{E}\bm{\exp}^*\big(\mathbf{u}\circ^s\underline\mathbf{j}( y)-\mathbf{u}\big)-\mathbf{1}-\sum_{|\beta|=1}\mathbf{u}^{(\beta)}\ast \underline{\bm{j}}( y)^{\ast\beta}\ F(d y) .\nonumber 
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.932113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb42c2cc1e31b465ec552eccff2f29d417420cb0c3113f8158bd44aead444466","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_prepare_loop_decompose of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exists $
	\refstepcounter{newcnstcnt}
	\ensuremath{C_{\thenewcnstcnt}}>0$ such that the following holds. Let $\mathbf{B}_1:=[\widetilde{B}(10\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_prepare_loop_decompose}}}M)]^c$, $\mathscr{B}_1:= \partial B(\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_prepare_loop_decompose}}}M)$, $\mathbf{B}_2:=\widetilde{B}(\frac{N}{10\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_prepare_loop_decompose}}}})$ and $\mathscr{B}_2:= \partial B(\frac{M}{\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_prepare_loop_decompose}}}})$. Then for any $M> N\ge 1$, $j\in \{1,2\}$, $k\in \mathbb{N}^+$, $A_1,...,A_k,D\subset \mathbf{B}_j$ and $\omega_l\in \Omega_l[N,M]$, 
