{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.364195+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb4b480fc3d33eb1c21b695f22fbe6f36285298aec71fb83657311d71f4d122e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:bound_V_Holder of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $F \in \mathcal{C}^2$. There exists a constants $C=C(\|F\|_{\mathcal{C}^2}, \|\sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^2}, H_-)$ and $q=q(H_-)$ such that for all $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, $s\in [0,1]$ and ${\color{blue}M}= (M, M') \in \mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])$, if $V$ is a solution of (equation eq:general_equation_Jacobian of the paper), then 
       \begin{equs}
\|{\color{blue}V}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])} \leq C (1+[{\color{blue}B}]_{\mathcal{R}^{H_-}})^q ( \|V\|_{\mathcal{C}^0([s,1])}+\|{\color{blue}M}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])}).
