[f]_{BMO}:=\sup_{Q}\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}|f-(f)_{Q}|dx,\ (f)_{Q}=\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}f(y)dy,
\end{equation}
the supermum is taken in all cubes in $\R^{d}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.673394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb6068a1fe1e09bc6edce5b1d19954832d3631f38de7c68ba380f5750849ccdb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.04853, 'Minimal-Norm Extensions of Stationary Kernels on Subgroups of Locally Compact Abelian Grou'] Given two bounded operators $T_0:\mathcal{N}(H) \to \mathcal{N}(G)$ and $T_1:L^2(H) \to L^2(G)$ such that $T_0 f =T_1f$ for all $f \in \mathcal{N}(H)$, where the equality is understood in $L^2(G)$, there exists a bounded operator $T_\theta:\mathcal{N}(H)_{\theta} \to \mathcal{N}(G)_\theta$, such that $T_0f=T_\theta f$ for all $f \in \mathcal{N}(H)$ and
\begin{align*}
\Vert T_\theta \Vert_{\mathcal{N}(H)_\theta \to \mathcal{N}(G)_\theta } \leq \Vert T_0 \Vert_{\mathcal{N}(H) \to \mathcal{N}(G)}^{1-\theta} \cdot \Vert T_1 \Vert_{L^2(H) \to L^2(G)}^{\theta}. 
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.815713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb623ae7be97b66e4941a2cc0345cf24e4b3e0cb19756f02750ab8f16d19889d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm l:conditioning-on-less of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Let $X$ be a square-integrable random variable on a probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$, and let $\mathcal{G}_1\subset \mathcal{G}_2\subset \mathcal{F}$ be any nested sub-$\sigma$-algebras.
    We have
