        \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|\mathcal{G}_2)] \leqslant \mathbb{E}[\Var(X|\mathcal{G}_1)].
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.362841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb63d6aba1970964c2b01930db1de4dd0205187d51f0af177c88d3a633bfd37e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: M derivative covariance interp of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $\alpha \in [0,1)$. Then there exists $C>0$ such that, for every $t>0$,
\begin{equation}
|\dot{C}^M_t(x,y)| \leq C \frac{\langle t\rangle ^{\alpha-1}}{|x-y|^{1-\alpha}}, \qquad \forall x,y\in M.
