{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.499220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb83a3c70575dd99e69ede1acf773df0b870c11aed56db503d9b23ed680b3a1a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo lgp of arXiv:2411.07158, 'Markov chains on trees: almost lower and upper directed cases'] Let $\pi^{T{(k)}}$ be  the ${\sf h}$-invariant measure of $\;{\sf U}^{T{(k)}}$ on the finite tree $T{(k)}$, normalized by $\pi_{\varnothing}^{T{(k)}}=1$.
	\begin{itemize} \topsep0pt   \itemsep=0pt   \partopsep=0pt   \parsep=0pt \setcounter{c}{0}
	\addtocounter{c}{1}\item[($\roman{c}$)] 	$(a)$ the measures  $\pi^{T{(k)}}$ and $\pi^{T{(k-1)}}$ coincide on $T{(k-1)}$,\\
