{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb8c71cf9939f2ad4461beb0f81f828404ddf7406afca41582e80f928c971129","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem measurable density of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $p$ be a stochastic kernel on $\mathbb R^d$ such that $p(x,\cdot)$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\mathrm {Leb} $ for all $x\in \mathbb R^d$. Then, $p$ has a jointly measurable density; in other words there exists a function $f:\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d\to[0, \infty)$ that is $\mathcal B(\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d)$-measurable\footnote{$\mathcal B(\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d)$ denotes the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of $\mathbb R^d\times \mathbb R^d$.} and such that 
	\begin{equation*}	
		p(x,A)=\int_Af(x,y)\mathrm {Leb}  (\mathrm d y),\qquad x\in \mathbb R^d, A\in \mathcal B(\mathbb R^d).
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.850042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb8ca38fd584ee2e7ed87601e37b9f0ae8df8b1e764f5a0139760e6928da0e43","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 67 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is countably monotonically bounded;
\item[(ii)] $F$ is countably $r$-monotonically bounded, for some $r\ge 1$;
\item[(iii)] Every countable directed dominable subset of $\Ba_{F_{+}}$ is order bounded;
\item[(iv)] Every countable subset of $F$ which is order bounded in $F^{**}$ is also order bounded in $F$;
\item[(v)] $F$ has a countably monotonically bounded super order dense sublattice.\medskip

Moreover, the countable monotone boundedness implies the $\sigma$-demicontinuity. The countable $r+$-monotone boundedness implies the $r$-$\sigma$-demicontinuity. A super order dense countably monotonically bounded sublattice of $F$ is majorizing.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.764782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb8d9134d62d97e5fa50c36951a9f5ce22bd8a17870fdec1aebafc4a20a40cd6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 57 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For every \(p>1\),
