{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb9c7fcce68b36e963c50c903301dc0691d017c19baa0b46e0009a2a4ea448aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 (Separated $\dot H^{1/2}$ seminorms) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] Let $(f_k)_{k\in \mathbb N}$ be a sequence of measurable functions in $L^1(\R)$ such that
\begin{equation*}
	  \sup_{k\in \mathbb N} \|f_k\|_{L^1 (\mathbb R)} \leqslant A,  \qquad  \supp f_k \subset[X_k-R,X_k+R]
\end{equation*}
for a fixed $A,R>0$, and some sequence of positions $(X_k)_{k \in \mathbb N}$.  
Assume further that 
\begin{equation}
  X_{k+1} - X_k \geqslant 4^k + 2 R, 
\end{equation}
for all $k\in \mathbb N$.
Then, there is a constant $C=C(A,R)$ such that, for every $N$,
\begin{equation}
  \left|  \left\| \sum_{k=1}^N f_k\right\|_{\dot H^{1/2}}^2 -\sum_{k=1}^N \|f_k\|_{\dot H^{1/2}}^2  \right| \leqslant C.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.442987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb9e242d5fb7bfc5b43995fc56937b6a39768f1cfbb21daa9afe842a5fffe9c5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:def4.1 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given a finite subset $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, a collection of conductances $\left( J_{xy} \right)_{xy \in E(\Lambda)} \in [0, \infty)^{E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2)}$, we define the integer-valued Gaussian free field on the set $\Lambda$ with conductances $J = (J_{xy})$ to be the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_\Lambda^\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ given by the identity
(recall the definition of the set $\Omega_\Lambda^\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ given above in~(equation e.ZGFF of the paper))

\begin{equation*} 
    \mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda,J}} \exp \left( - \sum_{x \sim y}  \frac{\left( \varphi(x) - \varphi(y) \right)^2}{2J_{xy}} \right).
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ and write $\mathrm{Var}_{L , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ when $\Lambda = \Lambda_L$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.160567+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eba2e3e9cbe691e2595af05af66590363555b91575d2146e1fd894ca6b776a77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:JordanLowerBoundUpper of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_J$, there exist positive constants $C$ and $c$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, any vertex $v\in [n]$ and any $S\geq 1$, 

