{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.220227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebabe64d7995e36ca67ca380a9b0248fd8ebd8c353bccd6dfafe3bc604a5f5d6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 7 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] \begin{enumerate}
\item [\rm (i)]
 We say condition  ${\rm \bf (Jt)}_{\leq, \bar r, \gamma}$ holds
 with some $\bar r>0$ and $\gamma>0$ if  there is a constant $C=C(\bar r, \gamma)>0$ such that for $r\in (0, \bar r],$
\begin{equation}
J(x,  \sX \setminus B(x,r))\leq Cr^{-\gamma}   \quad\hbox{ for every }x\in\sX.
