\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.221392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebad8e7b68b1ee5ab8663b699485d38e681241b9d04c4c3559aff882e4fc6ff9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem formal of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] $F(x,t;q)$ admits a formal expansion
