{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.711832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebae84036ffda2f5ecaea69c6a162654400c7928e319cfbe2faa1907db71b6c5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition wegner of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Define a block random Hermitian matrix by
\begin{equation}
X = \sqrt{1-\lambda}\,H + \sqrt{\lambda}\,\Lambda,
\end{equation}
where $\lambda\in[0,1)$ may depend on $M$,
for any $i, j \in \mathbb{T}_D^d$, the $(i, j)$-th block of size $M\times M$ is given by
\begin{equation}
    (H)_{i,j} = \delta_{i,j} H_i,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    (\Lambda)_{i,j} = \begin{cases}
        \frac{1}{\sqrt{2d}}A_{i,j}, & \text{if } |i-j|_1 = 1, \\
        0, & \text{otherwise}.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}
Here $|i-j|_1$ denotes the $\ell^1$ distance on the discrete torus (nearest neighbors), and  all non-zero block matrices are independent up to  symmetry  such that diagonal blocks $\{H_i\}$ are   rescaled $M\times M$ GUE (or GOE) matrices and
 off-diagonal blocks $A_{i,j}$ are  rescaled $M\times M$  Ginibre matrices.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.255305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebb05dcfeed9fdf3eeb50a4127437e2da7a5849be490919f6deaa1b9bee8ebf0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.19220, 'Split merge dynamics for expanding intervals and point processes on the real line.'] If  $ 0 \le c \le + \infty,$ 
    $\tau_n/n$ and $\nu_{\tau_n}$ are asymptotically independent~:
