{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebc12cbded5df86d183ff2a8adb60e6811539051923fa682875d93de6ca75606","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:oracle} holds, $\Gamma>0$, and $\lVert G_s\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G_{\mathrm{op}}$ almost surely for every $s$.
