{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.051120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebc132869546e1289399efa916caeccab026f40cf7088913c4e93bc886acf5f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $h\in Z\hat C(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$. Then the map
\[
\mathcal T_h:\{R\in C(\Delta_T^2;B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}\to \{\text{compatible frozen increment families over }h\}
\]
defined by $\mathcal T_h(R):=(\Theta_\tau R)_{\tau\in[0,T]}$ is a bijection. Its inverse is given by
\begin{equation}

(r^\tau)_{\tau\in[0,T]}\mapsto R, \quad R_{ts}:=r^t_{ts}.
\end{equation}
In addition, if $\gamma\in(0,1)$ and $h\in Z\hat C^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$, then
$\mathcal T_h$ restricts to a bijection between $ \{R\in E^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}$ and the compatible frozen increment families over $h$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

\sup_{\tau\in[0,T]}\|r^\tau\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}<\infty, \quad \forall \varepsilon\in(0, \gamma).
\end{equation}
Likewise, if $h\in Z\hat C^{1}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$, then $\mathcal T_h$ restricts to a bijection between $\{R\in E_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha) \mid \hat\delta R=h\}$ and the compatible frozen increment families satisfying
\begin{equation}

\sup_{\tau\in[0,T]}\|r^\tau\|_{1,\log;\tau,\alpha}+\sup_{\tau\in[0,T]}\|r^\tau\|_{1-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}<\infty, \quad \forall \varepsilon\in(0,1).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.355069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebc77d3425b0593d2e6bc54c47d51bb682622f01a6f8a79ace3fcd7786dafe6a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem UniformFCLT-general of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] (Asymptotic equicontinuity - general case)\\
Let $\nu > 2$ and let $\rho$ be a semimetric on $\mathcal F$. Assume the following conditions to hold: 	
\begin{enumerate}[ref = \arabic*]
\item  There exists $g: \mathbb N \times (0, \infty) \to \mathbb R$ such that for each $n \in \mathbb N$, $\delta > 0$, it holds 
\begin{equation}
\EOuter{ \norm{  S_{n,i,j} }_{\mathcal F_\delta}^\nu } \leq g^{\frac{\nu}{2}}(j-i+1, \delta), ~ \forall ~ 1 \leq i \leq j \leq n,
\end{equation}
and there is a universal index $Q_g \in [1,2^{1-2/\nu})$ such that for each $\delta > 0,$ the pair $(\nu/2, g(.,\delta))$ fulfills condition (equation MSS-ConditionM of the paper) with index $Q_g$. 

\item  There exists $h: \mathbb N \to \mathbb R$ such that for each $n \in \mathbb N$, it holds 
\begin{equation}
\EOuter{ \norm{ S_{n,i,j} }_{\mathcal F}^\nu } \leq h^{\frac{\nu}{2}}(j-i+1), ~ \forall ~ 1 \leq i \leq j \leq n,
\end{equation}
and the pair $(\nu/2, h)$ fulfills condition (equation MSS-ConditionM of the paper) with index $Q_h \in [1,2^{1-2/\nu})$.

\item  It holds $$\lim_{\delta \downarrow 0} \limsup_{n \to \infty} \frac{g(n,\delta)}{n} = 0.$$	

\item  There exists a constant $C_h \geq 0$ such that for each $0 < \varepsilon  \leq 1,$ it holds $$ \limsup_{n \to \infty}  \frac{h(\left\lfloor n \varepsilon \right\rfloor)}{n}  \leq C_h \varepsilon $$ (with the convention $h(0) = 0$). 
\end{enumerate}
Then (equation DEF:AEC of the paper) holds for $\tau((s,f),(t,g)) = |s-t| + \rho(f,g).$	If, in addition, $(\mathcal F, \rho)$ is totally bounded, then fidi-convergence of $\mathbb Z_n$ implies weak convergence in $\ell^{\infty}([0,1] \times \mathcal F)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.818506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebc908b9926f62dd8bc132691390f10dd032a045125be410d0340b870d98ef09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:whitenoiseregularity of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] For every $\psi\in L^\infty(\Sigma, \mathbb{R} )$, the random series
