{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.830058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebd30ab643ca9cbfb7a6e13f56341143d2add3153d06c4273cb690a9c6486ddd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Chart invariance of first-order criteria) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Let $\psi:(\widetilde\Theta,\widetilde\theta_0)\to(\Theta,\theta_0)$ be a $C^1$ local reparameterization with invertible derivative at $\widetilde\theta_0$, and let $\widetilde q_{\cQ}^{(m)}:=q_{\cQ}^{(m)}\circ\psi$. Identify a tangent block $\widetilde T\subset T_{\widetilde\theta_0}\widetilde\Theta$ with $T:=D\psi(\widetilde\theta_0)\widetilde T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$. Then for every visible depth $m$,
\begin{equation}
D\widetilde q_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\widetilde\theta_0)|_{\widetilde T} = Dq_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\circ
D\psi(\widetilde\theta_0)|_{\widetilde T}.
