{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.829271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebdd9a297bdfb58fc2f96b8b7f65638ad286785178fd237efbf4d8fa2e6b70da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.13235, 'Mixing Properties of Random Laguerre Tessellations'] Let $b > 0$ and let $\mathsf{B} \in \tailF{-b}^1$. Let $K_3,K_2 > 0$ and $r \geq 1$ be such that $b \geq (K_3+1)K_2r$ and denote $\Tilde{\Theta}_{r,K_3,K_2}\coloneqq (E^3_{K_2r,K_3} \cup E^2_{r,K_2})^c$. Then 
