{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.383572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebe4f3093c4c0a986ac8b43c3e02d2aa8c461c7d0cd4bcc629f6ab249143e8dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lipschitzconcentration of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] There is some $\eta > 0$ as well as constants $C, c > 0$
