{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.590683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebe58e3657b2f3e4b91eb6cf823cabda0ede896bf838559c4c08fc12fa49fe50","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm th:2.3 of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Suppose $\xi = g_\alpha = 1-2\sqrt{\alpha}$, $f$ satisfies Assumption~(assumpt:2.1.1 of the paper) with $\alpha_n = 1$ and $\{x_n^f, n \in \mathbb{N}\}$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.7 of the paper). \\
	Case 1: if $d < \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}$, then it holds
	\begin{equation} 
	\begin{aligned}
	& \lim_{T \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(x^f_{\alpha T}(T) > (1-2\sqrt{\alpha})T - S T^{1/3}) \\
	&= \mathbb{P} \Bigl ( \sup_{\tau \geq 0} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau)-g_n(\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} S \Bigr ) 
	\times  \Phi_{n-1}^{\alpha_0, \dots, \alpha_{n-1}}(S).
	\end{aligned} 
	\end{equation}
	Case 2: if $d = \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}$, then it holds
	\begin{equation}  
	\begin{aligned}
	& \lim_{T \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(x^f_{\alpha T}(T) > (1-2\sqrt{\alpha})T - S T^{1/3}) \\ 
	&= \mathbb{P} \Bigl ( \sup_{\tau \geq 0} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau)-g_n(\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} S, \ \sup_{\tau  \leq 0} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau)-\tau^2 - y(-\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} 	S \Bigr ) \\ 
	& \hphantom{=} \times \Phi_{n-1}^{\alpha_0, \dots, \alpha_{n-1}}(S).
