{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.322470+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebf938e30e9a1f8925e2ae3507c8fc6508c4cf4dd2ed741c14569da49f034c5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2506.21164, 'Instantaneous blowup for interacting SDEs with superlinear drift'] The process $V_t(x)=V^{(n, J)}_t(x),\; x\in Z, \; 0\le t\le 1$ has the following integral formulation.
\be 
\begin{split}
V_t(x) &= \left(G_{\frac{[nt]}{n}}*V_0\right) (x) + \int_0^{\frac{[nt]}{n}} \sum_{y \in \Z} G\left(\frac{1}{n}\left[ n\left(\frac{[nt]}{n}-s\right)+1\right]; y-x \right) b\left(V_s(y)\wedge J\right)ds \\
& \qquad +\int_0^{\frac{[nt]}{n}}\sum_{y \in  \Z} G\left(\frac{1}{n}\left[n\left(\frac{[nt]}{n}-s\right)+1\right]; y-x \right)  V_s(y) dB_s\left(y\right)  \\
& \qquad+ \int_{\frac{[nt]}{n}}^t b\left(V_s(x)\wedge J\right) ds +\int_{\frac{[nt]}{n}}^t V_s(x) dB_s\left(x\right)
\end{split}
\ee","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.364849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebf94a5f8c7fc2fe31d48a1ebc2cc6865b1a396db34c270c4cedfae39908cc16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:L of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let (asn:b of the paper) and (asn:sigma of the paper) hold. Let $\chi\in\mathrm{Cut}_d$,  $p\in[1,\infty)$, $\theta\in[0,1]$,  and let $X$ and $Y$ be two solutions to (equation eq:main of the paper). For $f\in \mathcal{C}^1$ define the process
\begin{equ}
J_t=\int_0^t\chi_{\rho}(X_r-Y_r)f\big(\theta X_r+(1-\theta)Y_r\big)\,dr.
\end{equ}
Then for any $\gamma\in(-1/(2H),0)$ 
there exists a constant $C$ such that for all $(s,t)\in[0,1]^2$ one has
