{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.964344+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec45f5323f17fc5668cdfa916be1fa49470b9a6ce03f411a41eac754a2a59ff2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Approximate Tensorization of Entropy}


    A probability measure $\nu$ on a space $\mathcal X^n$ fulfills ATE with constant $\kappa \geq 1$ if for all $f : \mathcal X^n \to [0,\infty)$,
    \begin{align*}
        \ent[\nu]{f}
        \leq \kappa \cdot  \sum_{i=1}^n \E[\ent[\nu(\cdot | X_{-i})]{f}]. 
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec47a6ea6bef36e6dcaa0b482ee46d1224f534e2e452309898ce82d944400fc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:factorization-criterion of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] For finite $\mathcal A$ and integrable utilities,
