{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec48af059a645138810dd36515f9edfe679d5cd71e31e69e4611f447539de918","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)\subset H=(V',E')$ be two subgraphs of $\mathbb Z^d$. For every $\beta\geq 0$, and every $x,y \in V'$,
