{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.333773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec4a7aafc5d873e2e9e66766315d05d8e066120a55829d0040e52305f8536094","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-first-round-distribution-features of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] Fix $\alpha\geq 1$. Define $A_j = \#\{ 1 \leq i \leq n: \mathbf X^{(i)}_1 = j\}$ for $0 \leq j \leq \aleph + 2$. In addition, define
    \begin{align*}
        \mathtt N = (\log \log n)^2 <\exp(40\alpha \sqrt{\log \log n}), \quad \mathtt N' = \frac{\log n}{(\log \log n)^{30}} \,.
    \end{align*}
    Define $\mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper)}=\mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),1} \cap \mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),2} \cap \mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),3}$, where 
    \begin{align}
        & \mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),1} = \left\{ |\mathbf M_1-\aleph| \leq 2, n \leq \mathbf Z_1 \leq n\log \log n \right\} \,; \\
        & \mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),2} = \cap_{j \geq 0} \left\{ A_{\mathbf M_1-j} \leq \exp(\log\log n \cdot \max\{ \mathtt N, j \}) \right\} \,; \\
        & \mathcal E_{(lem-first-round-distribution-features of the paper),3} = \cap_{10 \leq j \leq \mathtt N'} \left\{ A_{\mathbf M_1-j} \geq \exp( (\log\log n)^{-1} \cdot j ) \right\}\,.
