    \end{align}
    where $\widetilde{\vb}$ is the unique solution of \eqref{stochastic-third-grade-fluids-equations} with $\fb=\widetilde{\fb}$. Moreover, there exists a unique solution $\pb$ of \eqref{eqn-adjoint-pi} with $\gb=\nabla_{\vb}\mathfrak{L}(\cdot,\widetilde{\fb},\widetilde{\vb}),$ such that if $\widetilde{\mfrk}$ is the solution of \eqref{eqn-linearized-pi} for $\vb=\widetilde{\vb}$ and $\boldsymbol{\psi}=\boldsymbol{\psi}-\widetilde{\fb}$, the following duality property 
    \begin{align}
