{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec4ec5e73fab836cf3297c65327b866596add7ba62f419edabf30d3e429dd63b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_heat1 of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded, open subset of $\mathbb{G}$. If $\Omega$ has $C^2$ boundary with no characteristic points, then
