        in $\PSh(T)$ such that $u\in\textbf{\textup{U}}(A)$ (whence $v\in\textbf{\textup{U}}(B)$), the Beck--Chevalley map $v_!g^*\to f^*u_!$ is invertible.
    \end{enumerate}
    Moreover, in this case conditions (1) and (2) hold more generally without the representability condition, i.e.\ for all $A,B\in\PSh(T)$.\qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.310938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec818314c2793056237cb0ae1fcc4a66274bd8707e36e1f2c85e73e2ea1cba1d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}_p$ be an elliptic curve. Let $L|\mathbb{Q}_p^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be the extension previously defined and $\Phi_p:=\Gal(L/\mathbb{Q}_p^{\mathrm{nr}})$. Then for all $p\neq 2,3$ we have:
     {\small
     \begin{enumerate}
         \item $\#\Phi_p = 2\iff \text{ $E$ has Kodaira symbol $I_0^*$} \iff v_p(\Delta) \equiv 6 \mod 12$ 
         \item $\#\Phi_p = 3\iff \text{ $E$ has Kodaira symbol $IV$ or $IV^*$} \iff v_p(\Delta) \equiv 4 \text{ or } 8 \mod 12$
         \item $\#\Phi_p = 4\iff \text{ $E$ has Kodaira symbol $III$ or $III^*$} \iff v_p(\Delta) \equiv 3 \text{ or } 9 \mod 12$
         \item $\#\Phi_p = 6\iff \text{ $E$ has Kodaira symbol $II$ or $II^*$} \iff v_p(\Delta) \equiv 2 \text{ or } 10 \mod 12$
     \end{enumerate}}
If $p=2,3$, then 
\begin{enumerate}
         \item If $p = 3$,  $\Phi_p$ is a cyclic group of order $2,3,4,5,6$ or a non-abelian semidirect product of a cyclic group of order $4$ with a normal subgroup of order $3$.
         \item If $p = 2$, $\Phi_p$ is isomorphic to a subgroup of $\SL_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$ and its order is $2,3,4,6,8$ o $24$. Moreover, $\#\Phi_p = 3$ if, and only if, the Kodaira symbol of $E$ is $IV$ or $IV^*$.
     \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.754020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec82dc786870e379b5b4fc9d4c90da5d33f4c82f4b6398c58a566f273e361d1b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:chfuntheta2 of arXiv:2411.19192, 'Characteristic function and Esscher transform of a switching Levy model for the temperatur'] Let $(T_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the temperature process given by equations ((eq:tempdyna of the paper)), ((eq:seass2 of the paper)) and ((eq:tchlevy2 of the paper)) starting at regime one. Then,  the Esscher measure $\mathcal{Q}^{\theta}$ is an EMM  if  for any $t>0$ the parameter $\theta$ verifies under the conditions $\lambda_{12}>max(\alpha+\theta,0)$ and  $\lambda_{12} < \lambda_{21}$ the equation:
 \begin{equation}
R(t,\theta)= \sigma^{-1} e^{\alpha t}(e^{rt} T_0-C_1(t, \alpha))
   \end{equation}
   where:
  \begin{eqnarray*}
 R(t,\theta)&=& -i  \left[ D_1(t,\theta) C_5(0, \theta)+ D_2(t,\theta) \right]\\

  \end{eqnarray*}
  The expressions $D_1(t,\theta)$ and $D_2(t,\theta)$  are given  by:
  \begin{eqnarray*}
  D_1(t,\theta) &=&  -i \alpha \left[\left(A_{12}(\theta, \alpha)+A_{21}(\theta, \alpha)\right)E_{\theta}[N_t]+
 A_{12}(\theta, \alpha) p^{\theta}_O(t) \right] \\ 
 && \\
 D_2(t,\theta) &:=&  \frac{dC_5(u \sigma^{1}e^{\alpha t}, \theta,k)}{du}|_{u=0} = \sum_{k=0}^{+\infty}   \frac{dJ^{\theta}_3(u \sigma^{-1}e^{\alpha t},k)}{du}|_{u=0}  p^{\theta}_{2k}(t)\\ \nonumber
  &+&  \sum_{k=0}^{+\infty}  \frac{dJ^{\theta}_4(u \sigma^{-1}e^{\alpha t},k)}{du}|_{u=0}p^{\theta}_{2k+1}(t) \\ 
 &&
  \end{eqnarray*}
 where $p^{\theta}_{O}(t)$ is the probability to observe an odd number of regime changes in the  interval $[0,t)$.","status":"unverified"}

