{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.779493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8755505e2390b0d91bf9242ca689e7054bfe16ba61d2304b76bc7571ccfe97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $(\XX,\metr)$ be a non-empty quasi-metric space,
