{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.632751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec88efbc43cb6208e716d2f63ccdfc7ba29a9e6458dca62f175ef185caff17e3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:NL-MC of arXiv:2607.00800, 'Brownian motion in Minkowski normed spaces'] Let $\{\mu^z_t\}_{t\geq 0, z \in \mathbb{R}^d} \subseteq \mathcal P$ be such that $\mu^z_0 = \delta_z$ for all $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $(t,z) \mapsto \mu^z_t$ is injective from $[0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}^d$ to $ \mathcal P$. We call a family $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d} \subseteq \mathcal P(\mathcal C)$ a (\emph{time-homogeneous}) \emph{nonlinear Markov core} for $\{\mu^z_t\}_{t\geq 0, z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ if
        \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item $P^z_t = \mu^z_t$ for all $(t,z)\in  [0,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}^d$;
        \item the family $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal{P}_0}\subseteq \mathcal P(\mathcal C)$, defined by $\mathcal P_0 \coloneqq \{\mu^z_t\}_{t\geq 0, z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and 
        \begin{equation*}
            P^{\zeta} \coloneqq P^z \circ \Pi_t^{-1} \quad \text{for } \zeta = \mu^z_t,
        \end{equation*}
     is a nonlinear Markov process in the sense of Definition (def:NL-MP of the paper). 
    \end{enumerate}
    We call $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal{P}_0}$ from (ii) the nonlinear Markov process \emph{induced by} $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$.
    If for each $(t,z) \in (0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}^d$, $\mu^z_t$ is given by a density as $\mu^z_t = u^z(t,x) \,\mathrm d x$, then we also call $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ a nonlinear Markov core for $\{u^z(t)\}_{t>0, z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$.","status":"unverified"}

