{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.694237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8aaa11dd54d51e6065fbdb98f3eb125b2f58c911eac4f95bbe4aca27f3c3d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:existence_Volterra_V of arXiv:2605.29073, 'Volterra clocks and their pure-jump limits: \\hitting times of curved boundaries'] Let $\lambda \,, \nu\geq 0\,$, $f$ satisfying Assumption (assumption:f of the paper), $K \in L^2_{loc}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}_+\,, \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}_+)$ a completely monotone kernel, and $g_0 \in \mathcal G_K\,$. Then, there exists a continuous, nonnegative weak solution $V$ to 
    \begin{equation}

