and 
\begin{equation*}
    S_2=\sup_{h,g\in C([0,T])}\{L(g_t[1-\Xi_t])+L(h_t\Xi_t)-\int_0^T\zeta_t[h_t-g_t]^2\;dt-\int_0^T\Psi(t,g_t,h_t)\;dt\}.
\end{equation*}
In the above formula, $\zeta_t=1/\langle 1/\sigma(\rho_t) \rangle$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.073625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8f3b50dc8e238c426be03ec77c700b6335692414842eb76c3f4cd0a90eee60","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.formula_cts_incre of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Under~(i.setting of the paper), fix $X_0=0$. 
