{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.368095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec8fad626d437f1f2132fba623b9be1cd88db8a028948cf2adf02aac69e7404b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] Let $\alpha \in (0,1)$. A multiplicative functional $\mathbf{z} : \{(s,t)\in [0,T]^2 : s\leqslant t\} \to T^{([1/\alpha])}$ is called a \textit{weakly geometric $\alpha$-Hölder rough path}
