{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712695+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec960a959ed15b0c8e8d9b3356a2bc361cd450ef09e9a2d87b7630f338d381bf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def.Wp of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Let $(\mathcal{X}, d)$ be a Polish metric space. For every $p \in[1, \infty)$, the $p$-Wasserstein distance between  two probability measures $\mu$ and $\nu$ is
