{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.526787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ec973b4b33415f20a568e49a79ab4ba98f29e94a27147f1126e7382443d4a87d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma PDE_regularity_finite_time of arXiv:2505.21770, 'Gradient-flow SDEs have unique transient population dynamics'] Suppose that the potential of the gradient-flow SDE (equation eq:overdamped_langevin_SDE of the paper) is smooth, i.e. $\Psi \in C^\infty(\mathbb R^d)$. Then, for any positive time $t>0$, it follows that the marginal $p(\cdot, t)$ admits a twice differentiable density, which obeys the Gaussian decay estimates
