{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.686178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecd5a4d4388f2b0ff38d31f3426bf6595d830b4effbeed61fbb24e4601d4efbc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Phasethm t:2.1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For each $n \geq 1$ there exists an $\mathcal F_{t_n^A}$-measurable, $(r_n, n-r_n)$-clustered random subset $\widetilde{{\rm F}}_{n,t_n^A}(0) \subseteq {\rm D}_n^\circ$ such that
\begin{equation}

\bigg( \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\Big|{\rm F}_{n, t_n^A}(0) \,\Delta\, \widetilde{{\rm F}}_{n,t_n^A}(0) \Big| \,,\,\,
	\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\bf \Xi}_{\widetilde{{\rm F}}_{n,t_n^A}(0),r_n} \,,\,
	\frac{{\mathbf T}_{n,t_n^A}/|{\rm D}_n| - t_n^A}{2\sqrt{t_n^A}} \bigg)
