where $\mathcal Z_{\rm D}$ is as in~(equation eq:deflqgm of the paper), $\overline{h}_{\rm D}$ is as in~(equation e:1.7p of the paper) and $C_\star \in (0,\infty)$ is a constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.432710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecdb0f89834558ec67d43f4305dddd2b14ea7f1538884b4f8c239327dd2451d8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:coupling-energy-equivalence of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let \(a=1/2+1/m\). Define the global coupling constants
\begin{equation}
    c_{\mathcal{E},1} := \min\left\{ c_1(a,2), \, c_1\left(a-\frac1m,2\right) \right\}, \qquad c_{\mathcal{E},2} := \max\left\{ c_2(a,2), \, c_2\left(a-\frac1m,2\right) \right\}.
