{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.277539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecde0178e1285e18f1a7b5304e04c134ccbe5784d2a25118c358e5bec791d322","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2604.24677, 'Local Limit of Random Regular Bipartite Planar Maps'] Let $\rt\in\T$. Then, for any $v\in\rV(\rt)$:
\begin{itemize}
	\item If $v\in\rV_{\!\circ}(\rt)$, then $\c(v)=d-1$. Moreover, its ordered offspring consists of $d-1$ elements, each of which is either a closing stem or a black vertex.
	\item If $v\in\rV_{\!\bullet}(\rt)$, then $\c(v)=0$ if $v$ is the root vertex and $\c(v)=1$ otherwise. Moreover, its ordered offspring  consists of a single white vertex together with opening stems, exactly $d-1$ if $v$ is the root vertex and $d-2$ otherwise.
