    where $n_{\gamma}:=\lfloor n^{\gamma}\rfloor$ is the greatest integer less than or equal to $n^{\gamma}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.675865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ece885de181a455659fdd0e383806e2c3f583ca1a3a4ae28a7a569d5a1b468a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] A (conformal) metric $g$ on a surface $\Sigma$ admits a \emph{singularity of order $\beta-1, \beta \in \R $}, at $p \in \Sigma$ if it can be locally written as
\begin{equation*}
g = e^{2u} |z|^{2(\beta-1)} |dz|^2,
\end{equation*}
with 
\begin{equation*}
    u \in L^1, \text{ and }\text{ }  \Delta u \in L^1,
\end{equation*}
where $z$ is a local (conformal) coordinate such that
$z(p)=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.312612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ece89bab2732efdf356e4db36265162ee2502d52c1ac68ddb382e833b02e167c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3.6 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] \textnormal{(i) (Upper bound)} There exist positive constants $c_2(u_1)$ and $n_2(u_1)$ such that for all $n>n_2(u_1)$, $1\le m\le n$, $1\le i, i'\le n$, $1\le j'\le m$, and nonempty set $J\subseteq\{1,\ldots,m\}$, 
