{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.756658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecea25286222a7eafe3b301ed4fb20f90dbde4200a0da8652cdf4ac51ce566cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2512.03884, '2512.03884'] Let $\alpha$ be a badly approximable number, and let $1<\theta< \theta'$ be constants. For any $0< \delta \le 1/2$ and any integer $M \ge 1$,
\begin{align}
\sum_{\substack{m=1 \\ \| m \alpha \|<\delta}}^{\infty} \frac{1}{m^{\theta}} &\ll \delta^{\theta},  \\
\sum_{\substack{m=1 \\ \| m \alpha \| \ge \delta}}^{\infty} \frac{1}{m^{\theta} \| m \alpha \|^{\theta'}} &\ll \frac{1}{\delta^{\theta'-\theta}},  \\
\sum_{\substack{m=M \\ \| m \alpha \| \ge \delta}}^{\infty} \frac{1}{m^{\theta} \| m \alpha \|^{\theta}} &\ll \left\{ \begin{array}{cc} 1+\log \frac{1}{M \delta} & \textrm{if } M \delta \le 1, \\ \frac{1}{(M\delta)^{\theta -1}} & \textrm{if } M \delta >1, \end{array} \right.  \\
\sum_{m=1}^M \frac{1}{m^{\theta} \| m \alpha \|^{\theta}} &\asymp \log M 
\end{align}
with implied constants depending only on $\alpha$, $\theta$ and $\theta'$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.301521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecea298573c737c33b919277a8da233360c6419220b9071e6d556c39cbe0c579","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:HDL weak regime of arXiv:2505.10256, 'Stochastic Oscillators out of equilibrium:\\ scaling limits and correlation estimates'] Let $v_0:\mathbb T\to \mathbb R$ and $e_0:\mathbb T\to (0,\infty)$ be bounded measurable functions.
Let $\{\mu_N\}_{N\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of probability measures on $\Omega_N$ associated to the pair $(v_0,e_0)$, and assume that $\{\mu_N\}_{N\in\mathbb N}$ satisfies Assumption (assump:initial_measure of the paper).  
Moreover, assume $\kappa>1$ where $\kappa$ is the constant appearing in (equation eq:weak_asymmetry of the paper).  
Then, for every $t\in [0,T]$, the sequence of empirical measures $\{(\pi^{v,N}_t, \pi^{e,N}_t)\}_{N\in\mathbb N}$ converges in probability to the absolute continuous measure $(v(t,u)du, e(t,u)du)$, that is, for any $\delta>0$ and for any $G\in C^2(\mathbb{T})$ we have 
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{N\to\infty}
Q^{\sigma,N}_m 
\bigg(\Big|\langle \pi^{\sigma,N}_{t},G\rangle-\int_{\mathbb T} \sigma(t,u)G(u)du \Big|>\delta\bigg) =0 
\end{equation*}
for each $\sigma\in \{e,v\}$ provided $m>5/2$, where recall that the measure $Q^{v,N}_m$ and $Q^{e,N}_m$ were defined for processes taking values on Sobolev space $H^{-m}(\mathbb T)$, see (equation eq:sobolev_empirical_measure_definition of the paper).  
Moreover, the pair $(v(t,u), e(t,u))$ is the unique weal solution of (equation eq:hdl of the paper) under $\alpha=0$ with initial profile $(v_0,e_0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.021789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ececa4c149a2f86f291ea3e905158d469883e938f7955132a40d683ef50f148a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.06193, 'Peng's Maximum Principle for McKean-Vlasov Stochastic Differential Equations with Common N'] If Assumption \ref{Assumption:C^{2,1}} holds, then for any $1 \leq k$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E}\left[\sup _{t \in[0, T]}\left\|X^{\epsilon}_t-X_t-Y^{\epsilon}_t-Z^{\epsilon}_t\right\|^{2 k}\right] \in o(\epsilon^{2k}).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.503443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eced5460ad0d9105a0648294cf760ee6da6696fc98de35c860039a14f997e83f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 64 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each $p \in [2,\infty)$ there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that for all $s,t \in [0,T]$ with $s < t$ the following statements are true:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For each $\bbr^{m \times d}$-valued predictable process $\Phi$ such that
\begin{align*}
\int_s^t | \Phi_r |^2 dr < \infty \quad \text{$\bbp$-almost surely}
\end{align*}
we have
\begin{align*}
\bbe \Bigg[ \sup_{u \in [s,t]} \bigg| \int_s^u \Phi_r dB_r \bigg|^p \Bigg] \leq C_p \cdot \bbe \Bigg[ \bigg( \int_s^t | \Phi_r |^2 dr \bigg)^{p/2} \Bigg].
\end{align*}
\item For each $\bbr^m$-valued predictable process $\Psi$ such that
\begin{align*}
\int_s^t | \Psi_r |^2 dr < \infty \quad \text{$\bbp$-almost surely}
\end{align*}
we have
\begin{align*}
\bbe \Bigg[ \sup_{u \in [s,t]} \bigg| \int_s^u \Psi_r \otimes dB_r \bigg|^p \Bigg] \leq C_p \cdot \bbe \Bigg[ \bigg( \int_s^t | \Psi_r |^2 dr \bigg)^{p/2} \Bigg].
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.056682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecefe296782bd2cfeb842e9327c387e3d5d30099e5733d31777ab47e61b06397","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] For every $t > 0$ and $q \in \mcl Q_1^\D$, there exist $p^+, p^- \in \mcl Q_{\infty,\leq 1}^\D$ such that 
\begin{equation}
p^+=\partial_q\psi(q+t\nabla\xi(p^+)), \qquad p^-=\partial_q\psi(q+t\nabla\xi(p^-)),
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\sP_{t,q}(p^-) \le \liminf_{N \to \infty} \bar F_N(t,q) \le \limsup_{N\to\infty} \bar F_N(t,q)\leq \sP_{t,q}(p^+).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.906747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecf3d784f407eb2d05471fd2befc8decf47ea65f9c4fd4fef7c1afc9871b4b7b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:decompos-b-n of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] For $ x\in \mathsf E(u)$, let $ C_x  $ be the bounded connected component  of $ \mathsf E(u)$ containing $ x$, or the empty set if $ x$ is not in a bounded component. Then, with Definition   (def:topo-func of the paper)

\begin{align*}\beta _n(u;F) = \sum_{(x,v)\in Y^{\partial }(W_n\times [u,\infty ))}\delta (x,v,C_x),
\end{align*}
where $ \delta (x,v,C_x)$ satisfies  {for some $ \kappa <\infty $}
