and $ \delta (x,v,C_x)$ only depends on the isotropy class of $ C_x$ (hence is not modified upon a $ \Delta $-perturbation without stratified quasi critical point by Lemma (lm:Morse of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.745203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecf61a765052db0ae97e216f1f89e42a83a57a83f8ae34006099bd07ab8b073c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Assume that a controlled sequence $(\bar{X}^{\eta, xy}, \nu^\eta)$ converges to $(\bar{X}^{xy}, \nu)$.
    Then this limit satisfies, almost surely, the following integral equation on $[0,1)$
