{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.984776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed580387d3d144e870c7dcb6c4ee93b23e5e6a64d73d707e58436ff1fb17eb93","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local-time of arXiv:2604.13968, 'Divisible sandpiles via random walks in random scenery'] Let~$G = (V,E)$ be an infinite, locally finite, connected graph on which the simple random walk $(X_n)_{n\geq 0}$ satisfies the \textbf{spectral dimension bound}
