{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.832548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed6f008d4f039adc102e22697b33fd4174452b00921c2faad1e45c776ea2a053","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Gaussian permanent anticoncentration) of arXiv:2607.20329, '2607.20329'] For every $\mathbb K\in\{\R,\C,\Hh\}$ and $n\ge1$,
