{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.029823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ed79f77258fd48c49d7fdb03728863589acacd9eb8ee314d607a9a92bb59c11c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $u$ and $A$ be given as in the proof of Theorem~\ref{th:main_theorem}. Then there exists a constant $\tilde c_\eps>0$ such that, for all $x\in A$, one has
