{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.969933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ede50c3d76d4e17da8e2a0d5c2ec76b63b501654ca3d00b06ae3fe6d10d65c2e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_error_ulmc of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Assume that $-\beta I \preceq \nabla^2 V \preceq \beta I$, $\gamma \lesssim \sqrt \beta$, and $h \lesssim 1/\beta^{1/2}$. Then, the strong error for~(eq:ULMC of the paper) is bounded as follows:
