	the diagonal coefficient of the operator $\mathfrak{D}^{\mathrm{scaled}}$ (equation eq:diff_operator_scaling_shifting of the paper) has the following limit:
	\begin{equation}

		\begin{split}
			&\lim_{L\to+\infty}
			C_{\mathsf{x}}\cdot
			\bigl(
				q^{-N+1}(1-q^{N-1})(q^{-T-N}-1)
				-B(\tilde x)-D(\tilde x)
			\bigr)
			\\
			&\hspace{40pt}
			=
			\begin{cases}
				-1, & \mathsf{x}<\tfrac{1}{2}(\mathsf{S}+\mathsf{t}-\mathsf{N});\\
