{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.007712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee003330ef9da2ce2345fc0c11f9b0b06bbe21e69050b5e0cfafe022821666c7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:log-deriv of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] For $h \in H$, the \emph{logarithmic derivative} of $\mu_t$ along $h$ is the function $\beta_h: H \to \mathbb{R}$ defined $\mu_t$-almost everywhere by the integration-by-parts identity
\begin{equation}
  \int_H \ip{\nabla\phi(u)}{h}_H\,\mathrm{d}\mu_t(u) = -\int_H \phi(u)\,\beta_h(u)\,\mathrm{d}\mu_t(u)
