{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.269753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee25ceb5f1cd01592d6a4efbc8e8d36afbb583cb923114aeb1c6e858003e2726","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$  satisfy  $\lambda_{o,y} =\mathcal{O}( \|y\|^{-\alpha})$ for some $\alpha>2d+1$. Then, for each $\epsilon>0$, there exists 
$\theta_0 \in (0,\infty)$ and $N_0 \in \bN$ so that, for all $n\geq N_0$, and for every $A \subset B_n$ and $\delta\geq 0$, 
\begin{equation}
    \bP_{\lambda,\delta} \left( A_t^{A} \subset B_{n\theta_0/2 + t \theta_0}(o) \text{ for all } t>0 \right) \geq 1- \epsilon. 
