{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.765625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee2afc09c4af6f78288f21af3f1a89da1f814ed82eb7375554317e6051d08b8e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For any set $S \in \mathcal{B}(\R)$, $i = 1,\ldots,N$, and $\delta > 0$ sufficiently close to $0$, we have
