{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.051383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee2bb7f6df64cc1f3e6745e8fd44afb5488f706918c480d357b0df3838ecbe1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Decision-boundary representation of the error-rate Hessian) of arXiv:2609.00774, 'Semi-Supervised Classification with Informative Missing Labels in Weibull Mixture Models'] Under \Cref{ass:boundaries}, with $p_Y$ continuous at the boundaries,
\begin{equation*}
 \left.\frac{\partial R(\widetilde\theta;\theta)}
 {\partial\widetilde\theta}\right|_{\widetilde\theta=\theta}=0,
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation}
 H_{R}(\theta)
 :=\left.\frac{\partial^2 R(\widetilde\theta;\theta)}
 {\partial\widetilde\theta\partial\widetilde\theta^\top}
 \right|_{\widetilde\theta=\theta}
 =\sum_{j=1}^K
 \frac{p_Y(y_j;\theta)}{2|\delta_y(y_j;\theta)|}
 g(y_j;\theta)g(y_j;\theta)^\top.

\end{equation}
Let $\widehat\theta$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
 \sqrt n(\widehat\theta-\theta)\xrightarrow{d}N(0,V),
 \qquad
 n\E\{(\widehat\theta-\theta)(\widehat\theta-\theta)^\top\}\longrightarrow V,

\end{equation}
and suppose that, for some $\epsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \E\|\sqrt n(\widehat\theta-\theta)\|^{2+\epsilon}=O(1).

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \E\{R(\widehat\theta;\theta)\}-\err(\theta)
 =\frac{1}{4n}\sum_{j=1}^K
 \frac{p_Y(y_j;\theta)}{|\delta_y(y_j;\theta)|}
 g(y_j;\theta)^\top Vg(y_j;\theta)
 +o(n^{-1}).

\end{equation}
For a correctly specified regular maximum-likelihood estimator satisfying the stated moment conditions,
$V=\J(\theta)^{-1}$, so
\begin{equation}
 \E\{R(\widehat\theta;\theta)\}-\err(\theta)
 =\frac{1}{4n}\sum_{j=1}^K
 \frac{p_Y(y_j;\theta)}{|\delta_y(y_j;\theta)|}
 g(y_j;\theta)^\top\J(\theta)^{-1}g(y_j;\theta)
 +o(n^{-1}).

\end{equation}
For the estimator that ignores the missingness mechanism, the same specialisation holds with $\J=\J_{\mathrm{ig}}$ by \Cref{lem:ig-information}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

