{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.278618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eec8b7a5c46c2a4da8a1d9f51cc3301f1023cab01eb3b8a0dd62bfc60ea65390","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cauchy of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $V \subseteq \mathcal{U}$ be finite and $((\xi^{u}_{0})_{u \in V},R_{0}) \in (\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{|V|} \times [0,R_{\max}]$. Then, there exists a neighborhood $O \subseteq (\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{|V|} \times [0,R_{\max}]$ of $((\xi^{u}_{0})_{u \in V},R_{0})$, and a neighborhood $J \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{+}$ of 0, such that
