}
converges in distribution to a PPP with intensity measure $\D_{\tilde \lambda}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.100804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef1ea389f8a72881fe89dd9cee4fa3a94a548099abad6d563974939466528d45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:continuity of arXiv:2411.13030, 'Classification of the limit shape for 1+1-dimensional FPP'] For a distribution function $G(x)$ and $B>0$, let $G^B$ be the distribution obtained by truncating above at $B$, i.e.
