{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef33367577f14d713fdcac0c87d0c253a5fc1659eae19f8ec9e089912161eef2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] There exists $C \equiv C(T,k,A,\lVert u \rVert_{L^\infty_{x}}, \gamma, d,p)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
