{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.303488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef35d30e1ee483079560fec3a4e31c541ede3a71a9f6655108eae691e0f2dc28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:one-arm of arXiv:2607.18070, 'The Brownian loop-catcher'] Let $(D;a,b)$ be as above. For every $z\in D$ and $0<\lambda<1$, there is a constant
