{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.873521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef36dcaceb07f1f5f300070e4c253934b47aabbcaf3e8c32ded1b267789eca52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop choquet inegral properties of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mu)$ be a capacity space, $f$ and $g$ be two $\mathcal{F}$-measurable functions. Then
	\begin{longlist}
		\item (Positive homogeneity): $\int_\Omega\alpha fd\mu=\alpha \int_\Omega fd\mu$ for each $\alpha \geq 0$.
		\item (Translation invariance): $\int_\Omega (f+\alpha 1_{\Omega})d\mu=\int_\Omega fd\mu+\alpha$ for each $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$.
		\item (Monotonicity): $\int_\Omega fd\mu \geq \int_\Omega gd\mu$ if $f \geq g$.
	\end{longlist} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.013891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef3a964e9daa02d2a92ebdb9554d6646ce46de587ad6c182d06d8b875c54f42d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 (Short-range factorization property) of arXiv:2602.14618, 'Finitary coding and Gaussian concentration\\ for random fields'] We say that a coding satisfies the short-range factorization property with constant $\alpha \in (0,1]$ if, for all $k,\ell,i  \in \Z^d$ such that $\max\{\|\ell-i\|,\|k-i\|, \|\ell-k\|\} = \|\ell-i\|$ 
the following holds
 \begin{align*}
&\E\Big[
\1\!\left\{\|k-i\|_\infty\le r_k(X)\right\}
\1\!\left\{\|\ell-k\|_\infty\le r_\ell(X)\right\}\Big] \\
&\leq \E\Big[
\1\!\left\{\|k-i\|_\infty\le r_k(X)\right\}\Big] \E\Big[
\1\!\left\{\alpha \|\ell-k\|_\infty\le r_\ell(X)\right\}\Big].
 \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.983184+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef3a9ef7b23f7daf16b67480634f16f56e79cad2ab5c3d1ea728748195a2c718","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem prop:3.6-CP of arXiv:2412.00708, 'Stochastic PDE approach to fluctuating interfaces'] For some $C>0$, we have
