{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.022079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef3b9fbc096a6d5ce0080a48ca8fad34e9d9d086170ff1e986a84dfd158eba27","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (\cite{BuckdahnPeng2017} Lemma 2.1) of arXiv:2606.06193, 'Peng's Maximum Principle for McKean-Vlasov Stochastic Differential Equations with Common N'] Let $\varphi \in C_b^{2,1}(\mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^d),\R)$. Then, for any given $X \in L^2(\Omega, \mathbb{R}^d)$ we have the following second-order expansion, for all $Y \in L^2(\Omega, \mathbb{R}^d)$,
        \begin{equation*}
            \begin{aligned}
                \varphi(\cL(Y))- & \varphi(\cL(X)) \\
                = & \E\left[\varphi_{\mu}(\cL(X))( X) [\eta]\right]
                +\frac{1}{2} \E\left[\tilde{\E}\left[\varphi_{\mu\mu}(\cL(X))(\tilde{X}, X)[\tilde{\eta},\eta]\right]\right] \\
                & +\frac{1}{2} \E\left[\varphi_{y\mu}(\cL(X))( X) [\eta , \eta]\right]+R(\cL(Y), \cL(X)),
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation*}
        where $\eta:=Y-X$. Further, for all $Y \in L^2(\Omega, \mathbb{R}^d)$, the remainder satisfies the estimate
        \begin{equation*}
            \begin{aligned}
                |R(\cL(Y), \cL(X))| & \leq C((\E[|Y-X|^2])^{3 / 2}+\E[|Y-X|^3]) \\
                & \leq C \E[|Y-X|^3],
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation*}
        and the constant $C \in \mathbb{R}_{+}$ only depends on the Lipschitz constants of $\varphi_{\mu\mu}$ and $\varphi_{y\mu}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.746476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef3cf278a08cb4e33abf3a16aa395c070730271a5a61f5d8a40bc401c41b2f00","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Suppose that  $\{X_1,\ldots, X_n\}$ is a sequence  of independent random variables
on $\sles$. Set
$A_n(p,y)=\sum_{i=1}^n\mbE[(X_i^+\wedge y )^p]$ and
$ \breve{B}_{n,y}=\sum_{i=1}^n \mbE[(X_i\wedge y)^2]$.   Then  for all $p\ge 2$, $x,y>0$, $0<\delta\le 1$,
\begin{align}
    & \hV\Big( \max_{k\le n}  \sum_{i=1}^k(X_i-\bE[X_i])\ge x\Big)
    \le    \hV\big(\max_{k\le n} X_k> y \big)
    +\exp\left\{-\frac{x^2}{2(xy+\breve{B}_{n,y})   }\right\}.

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
& \hV\Big( \max_{k\le n}  \sum_{i=1}^k(X_i-\bE[X_i])\ge x\Big) \nonumber\\
\le &  \hV\big(\max_{k\le n} X_k> y \big)
  +2\exp\{p^p\}\Big\{\frac{A_n(p,y)}{y^p} \Big\}^{\frac{\delta x}{10y}}
+\exp\left\{-\frac{x^2}{2\breve{B}_{n,y}(1+\delta)   }\right\}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.666504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef3d3b73dc2f899b7e6d989f93e3bf7e105e1a5a06f8095d7cad0b4a586fa874","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Finite torus-bundle covers of the three geometries) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Let \(M\) be a closed connected three-manifold modeled on \(\RR^3\),
\(\Nil\), or \(\Sol\).  Then \(M\) has a finite regular orientable cover
\(M_{\mathrm{fin}}\) which is the total space of a \(\TT^2\)-bundle over
\(S^1\), with monodromy \(H\in\SL(2,\ZZ)\).  The cover may be chosen so
that the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item if \(M\) is modeled on \(\RR^3\), then
      \(M_{\mathrm{fin}}\cong\TT^3\) and \(H=I\);
\item if \(M\) is modeled on \(\Nil\), then \(H\) is nontrivial unipotent;
\item if \(M\) is modeled on \(\Sol\), then \(H\) is hyperbolic.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, the monodromy is elliptic, parabolic, or hyperbolic according
as the original geometry is \(\RR^3\), \(\Nil\), or \(\Sol\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.472600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef40c8c8206d77051a8da5cc4a1404151330a3653c25022fb1e6d7de7bced09a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem func-WU of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Assume (fass1 of the paper), fix $\gamma = \gamma_b/2$ and define
    \begin{equation}
        \Psi(\phi) \coloneqq \ln\Big({1 + \sum_{i=1}^n c_ix_i}\Big) + A_2\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(u))dud\mu(s) \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $x_i = \phi_i(0)$ and $h, \mu$ are as in (fass1 of the paper). 
Then there are $p > 0, K > 0$ so that $W \coloneqq e^{p\Psi}$ and $U \coloneqq e^{2p\Psi}$ satisfy: \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item  $\mathcal{L} W \leq K - W'$,
        \item  $\mathcal{L} U \leq K - U'$,
        \item  $J + \Gamma W \lesssim U'$, where $J$ is as in (fass1 of the paper),
    \end{enumerate}
    where
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        W'(\phi) &\coloneqq pW(\phi)\Big(\gamma_0 + Ah(x) + \frac{A_2\gamma}{2}\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(s))dud\mu(s) + \frac{\gamma_b}{2}J(\phi)\Big) \\
        U'(\phi) &\coloneqq 2pU(\phi)\Big(\gamma_0 + Ah(x) + \frac{A_2\gamma}{2}\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(s))dud\mu(s) + \frac{\gamma_b}{2}J(\phi)\Big)
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and $A = A_1 - A_2 \int e^{-\gamma s}d\mu(s) > 0$ (see (fass1 of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:30:28.842101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef426d586f9044e4146251270a29a254fa9ff1426d0b6238bfe11e87976ef9cb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.02173, 'Bounding Selmer Groups of Superelliptic Jacobians via Class Groups'] The maps \(\delta_F\) and
