{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.415090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef5d423ddbc7506795faa186fe16f3f7b0608fe1831c52e431909365ce9ede96","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 89 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider a variational datum satisfying Assumptions \ref{Assumption_A} and \ref{Assumption_B}. Suppose that for any $g,h \in [H]$, we have $\theta_{g,h} \geq 0$ and there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that $V_h''(x) > c > 0$ for any $x \in (\hat{a}_h',\hat{b}_h')$. Then, for each $h \in [H]$ either the $h$-th segment is void or saturated, or the following properties simultaneously hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $\mu_h$ has at least one band;
\item[(ii)] the support of $\mu_h$ is connected;
\item[(iii)] if there is a void, it cannot be reduced to an interior point of the $h$-th segment;
\item[(iv)] the property 2., the lower bound in 4., and the property 5. of Assumption~\ref{Assumption_C} hold.
\end{itemize}
The constants in (iv) depend on the constants in the assumptions and on a positive lower bound for the length of the bands. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.591982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef5d6b8577d9524e0514e74b38d07a08cb34ac6247cbeb5871754f6eabd4c178","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem permutation_increases_number_of_holes of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Let $\pi$ denote the swap operators corresponding to a permutation of $\mathbb{Z}$ that exchanges $a$ and $b$ for some $a < b \in \mathbb{Z}$ and maps all other integers to themselves. Let $\eta$ be a configuration of a single-species TASEP on $\mathbb{Z}$, and let $x \in \{a, \dots, b-1\}$. Suppose that in $\eta$, there are a hole at a site in $\{x+1, \dots, b \}$ and a particle at a site in $\{a, \dots, x \}$. Then, in $\pi(\eta)$, 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] the number of holes at sites in $\{a, \dots, x \}$ increases by $1$; 
		\item[(ii)] a hole is moved to site $a$; 
		\item[(iii)] a particle is moved to site $b$.
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.401167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef5deb9d960a0fefbc2162c905927376b16b46c4c562bf30bb7a96227f86ef83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem e:condition square-integrable RF of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $Z$ is an invariant $\R^d$-valued random field on $\R^d$, that $\Phi$ is an invariant locally square-integrable random measure, and that $\Psi$ is defined as in~(equation e: definition Psi displacement of the paper). Further, either assume that for some $\vartheta>0$ and strongly log-dominating function $\rho$,
    \begin{equation}
        \BE_0^\Phi[\Phi(B_\vartheta) \|Z(0)\|^d \rho(\|Z(0\|))] <\infty,
    \end{equation}
    or assume that $Z$ and $\Phi$ are independent and that
    \begin{equation}
        \BE[\|Z(0)\|^d] < \infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then $\Psi$ is also locally square-integrable.
    \begin{proof}
        The assertion is a simple specialization of Theorem~(t:main square-integrable of the paper) to the special case of displacement kernels with an application of Proposition~(p:independent square-integrable of the paper) to obtain Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general of the paper) from~(equation e:condition square-integrable RF of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

