{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.851591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef61778946d41543bf491cdeff4926eb4cf88ed22025c2874cbdbd968c829185","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop main_4 of arXiv:2607.10105, 'The four-dimensional Anderson model: a case study for critical SPDEs'] Recall $C_0$ in Proposition (prop.main2_2 of the paper). In the same setting there, let $(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n,m_\mathfrak l)$, and the simple/compound leaf types, be fixed. Also fix $(y_1,\cdots,y_m)$ such that $m=\sum_\mathfrak l m_\mathfrak l$ and the multiset $\{y_1,\cdots,y_m\}=\cup_\mathfrak l \{\textrm{$m_\mathfrak l$ copies of $z_\mathfrak l$}\}$, where $(z_\mathfrak l)$ satisfies Definition (def.hepp_3 of the paper) (a). In addition, assume that
\begin{enumerate}[{(a)}]
\item For each $\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B\backslash\{\mathfrak r\}$ we have (recall $\gamma_\mathfrak n^\infty$ and $\gamma_\mathfrak n^2$ defined in ((eq.mul_1 of the paper)))
\begin{equation}
N_{\mathfrak n^+}\leq 8N_\mathfrak n':=8\sum_{\mathfrak m\leq\mathfrak n}\gamma_\mathfrak m^\infty\cdot N_\mathfrak m;
\end{equation}
\item We also fix a dyadic number $R$ such that $R\geq N_\mathfrak r'$ where $\mathfrak r$ is the root of $\mathcal T$ and $N_\mathfrak r'$ is defined as in ((eq.local_2 of the paper));
\item We also fix a set of \emph{skipped} indices $O\subseteq\{1,\cdots,m-1\}$, with $|O|=s$.
\end{enumerate} Then, we have
\begin{multline}\sum_{\pi}^{(*)}\prod_{\substack{j=1\\j\not\in O}}^{m-1}\frac{1}{\langle y_{\pi(j)}-y_{\pi(j+1)}\rangle^2}\leq C_0^{m/2}((m-s)!)^{1/2}\prod_{\mathfrak l\in\mathcal L^S}(m_\mathfrak l!)^{1/2}\prod_{\mathfrak l\in\mathcal L^C}(m_\mathfrak l!)^{3/4}\cdot\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B} N_\mathfrak n^{-2(\gamma_\mathfrak n^2-1)}\cdot R^{2s}\\
\times\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B\backslash\{\mathfrak r\}}\bigg(\frac{N_\mathfrak n}{N_{\mathfrak n^+}}\bigg)^{3}\cdot (N_\mathfrak r/R)^{\min(2s,3)}.
\end{multline} Here $\pi\in S_m$ (identified with a permutation of $m_\mathfrak l$ distinct copies of each leaf $\mathfrak l$) and satisfies that, there is no $j\not\in O$ such that $\pi(j)$ and $\pi(j+1)$ are
two copies of the same leaf. We do not require $\pi$ to be primitive.","status":"unverified"}

