{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.432264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef8cbfb3fa5b82dc981c3adfb798a291e4038c07a04e8f46ae12a57d60b1b6a6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Th:annealedVillain of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Let $\kappa$ be a probability measure on $(0 , \infty)$. Then the following hold:
