{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.716971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ef9938ef6cd09696e580f905f3581dc11de7b21892d492b2f3d83f5623d21127","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:fs-frame-condition of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] An f-frame $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ is said to be an \emph{FS2}\footnote{Also known by backward confluence [balbiani_constructive_2021], F2 [simpson_proof_1994], back-up confluence [aguilera_gocalculus_2022], and $\textsf{I}_{\Diamond \Box}$-weak [groot_semantical_2025].} frame
