{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.011065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efa18f729f46582dc19dbc09e6e3387c1c9db093fa08f4439d6e83491cf22c8a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem spde WP of arXiv:2605.13479, '\LARGE Dean-Kawasaki Equation with Biot-Savart and Keller-Segel Interactions: Existence an'] Assume that (equation eq:small-KS of the paper) holds. Fix $\varepsilon > 0$ and let $\rho_0 \in \mathrm{Ent}(\mathbb{T}^2)$ be a nonnegative initial datum, where $\mathrm{Ent}(\mathbb{T}^2)$ is defined in (equation eq:def-Ent-space of the paper). We consider the following two cases.
