{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.739858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efa643787a7a55a5fbe4b9f0737b586978b6fa9bc99ed4eab9dfc742b3b767a3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor cortau of arXiv:2605.01878, '\Large Random trade timing and power-law tails in realized prices'] Let $X$ be a real-valued random variable whose Laplace transform $\varphi_X$ satisfy the conditions (lemxpluda of the paper)--(lemxpludc of the paper) of Lemma (lemxplus of the paper). Then there exist finite constants $C_1$ and $C_2$, depending only on
$\alpha$, $\ell$, and $\delta$, such that
\begin{align}
