{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.317070+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efae81c5f7d16217e1ccf3fd802024b945c28f7b116afad04fe710203bde1565","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:thd of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] A bounded domain $D$ is called a twisted H\"older domain of order $\alpha$, $\alpha\in (0,1]$, if there exist positive constants $C_1,\ldots,C_5$, a point $x_0\in D$ and a bounded continuous function $\delta:D\to(0,\infty)$ such that the following properties (i), (ii) and (iii) hold.

(i) $\delta(x)\le C_1\,\mathrm{dist}(x,\partial D)^\alpha$ for all $x\in D$;

(ii) For all $x\in D$, there exists a rectifiable curve $\gamma_x\subseteq D$ connecting $x$ and $x_0$ such that $$\delta(x')\ge C_2\big(\delta(x)+l(\gamma_x(x,x'))\big)$$ for all $x'$ lying on $\gamma_x$, where $l(\gamma_x(x,x'))$ denotes the length of the piece of curve connecting $x$ and $x'$;

(iii) Let $F_a:=\{y\in D:\delta(y)\le a\}$. For any $a\le C_5$ and $x\in F_a$,
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Cap}(B(x,C_3a)\cap F_a^c)\geq C_4\mathrm{Cap}(B(x,C_3a)),
\end{equation}
where $\mathrm{Cap}(\cdot)$ is the Newtonian capacity in $\mathbb{R}^3$ (see Definition 4.31 in [BM1]).","status":"unverified"}

