{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.462046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efcefaca9863e4384ece2407a3668833e61e53af34dce4564fc7a0e810049a71","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 10 ({\cite[Definition 2.2 and 2.9) of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] {Keeler},\cite[Definition 3.1]{Ushiro}}]
Let $L$ be a line bundle on $X$.
We say that $L$ is:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $f$-ample
if there exists an affine open cover $\{ U_{\lambda} \}$ of $S$ such that $L|_{f^{-1}(U_{\lambda})}$ is ample for every $\lambda$;
\item $f$-nef
if $(L.C)\geq 0$ for every irreducible curve $C\subset X$ that is closed in $X$ and satisfies that $f(C)$ is a closed point of $S$;
\item $f$-semiample if $f^{*}f_{*}L^{\otimes m}\rightarrow L^{m}$ is surjective for some $m\in\Z_{>0}$;
\item $f$-$\Q$-effective if $f_{*}L^{\otimes m}\neq 0$ for some $m\in\Z_{>0}$;
\item $f$-big if $f_{*}(L^{\otimes m}\otimes A^{-1})\neq 0$
for some $m\in\Z_{>0}$ and some $f$-ample line bundle $A$.
\end{enumerate}
These notions extend to $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisors $D$ by requiring that some positive multiple $L:=\sO_X(mD)$ satisfies the corresponding properties.","status":"unverified"}

