Y^{\pi,H}(s)=H+\int_{t}^{s}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\pi_{k}(u)\frac{dP_{k}(u)}{P_{k}(u)}+\int_{t}^{s}\left(Y^{\pi,H}(u)-\sum_{k=1}^{n}\pi_{k}(u)\right)\frac{dP_{0}(u)}{P_{0}(u)},\;\forall s\in[t,T].
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.337286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efde2b43459ca86d256e3a1c1ab7108100c3c8f4d31d6e745f4c5716c846df88","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 54 of arXiv:2512.05466, 'Stochastic Flows and Marked Stable Processes'] Let $\alpha =\frac{\delta}{2}\in (0,1)$. 
Fix any $z<0$ and consider the spindle partition of the region to the left of the flow line $(\cR_{z,z+y} (0), y\ge 0)$.  
For $y\ge 0$, set 
\begin{equation}
   \beta^y:= \{ (\cR_{r,z+y}(a-), \cB_{r,z+y}(a)) \colon  
 \cT_{(a,r)}\text{ a spindle, } \, \cB_{r,z+y}(a)\le \cR_{z,z+y} (0))\} .
\end{equation}
Then the process $\big(\beta^y,\, y\in [0,|z|)\big)$ is an $\mathrm{SSIP}^{(\alpha)}(\alpha)$-evolution starting from zero; and $(\beta^y,\, y\ge |z|)$ is an $\mathrm{SSIP}^{(\alpha)}(0)$-evolution. 
The total mass process $\big(\|\beta^y\|,\, y\ge 0)\big)$ is equal to $(\cR_{z,z+y} (0), y\ge 0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.807861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efde56079123db1737d5046712191583b15f235e6b12e9bd068026dd1f631327","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:rep_kernel of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] We have
