By convention, $I(f)=\infty$, if  $\Big\{h\in L^2([0,T];U): f= \mathcal{G}^0(\int^{\cdot}_{0}h(s)\dd s)\Big\}=\emptyset.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.444077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efe70121cef2ab9d6c208f936e526bb10cbe077e87345217eb659b6996202141","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Pn_moments of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let \(X=(H_N + A_N)(H_N + A_N)^*\) be the deformed inhomogeneous Wishart matrix of Definition~(def:wishart of the paper) with Gaussian entries, and let \(\{\mathcal P_n\}_{n\ge0}\) be a   family of polynomials defined by
\begin{equation}
    x^m \;=\;\sum_{n=0}^{m} C_{\mathrm{MP}}(m,n)\,\mathcal P_{n}(x), \quad m=0,1,\ldots,
\end{equation}
then for any nonnegative integers \(n_1,\dots,n_s\),
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\prod_{j=1}^s \mathrm{Tr}\mathcal P_{n_j}(X)\Bigr]
=
\sum_{\Gamma\in\mathscr{D}_{s;\beta}}
\;\sum_{\eta:V(\Gamma)\to [M]\cup[N]}
\;\sum_{\substack{w_e \ge 1 \\ \sum_{e \in \partial D_j} w_e = n_j, \ \forall j}}
\;\prod_{e\in E_{\mathrm{int}}}p_{w_e}\bigl(\eta(x_e),\eta(y_e)\bigr)
\;\prod_{e\in E_b}(A^{w_e})_{\eta(z_e)\eta(w_e)}.
\end{equation}
Here
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=2em]
  \item \(\mathscr{D}_{s;\beta}\) is the set of \(s\)-face ribbon graphs (orientable if \(\beta=2\)) (see Definition (def:diagram of the paper)),  
  \item \(E_{\mathrm{int}}\) denotes the interior edges of \(\Gamma\), and \(E_b\) its boundary edges (see Definition (def:diagram of the paper)),  
  \item for each interior edge \(e=(x_e,y_e)\),  \(p_{w_e}(\eta(x_e),\eta(y_e))\) denotes the \(n\)-step transition probability  (see (equation equ:transition_matrix of the paper) for the Markov chain),  
  \item for each boundary edge \(e=(z_e,w_e)\), \((A^{(w_e)})_{\eta(z_e)\eta(w_e)}\) is defined as in Proposition (prop:wishart_moment of the paper).  
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.558421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efea3114b52e5c5d5cb0df859072e96d75b25520ffc62bc85b798756d29c3db5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:first-counter-example-general of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] Fix $\beta>0$ and $a_1,a_2>0$. Assume that either $0<\beta\le 2$ and $b\neq 0$ is arbitrary, or that $\beta>2$ and
    \begin{align}
        0<|b|<2\sqrt{\beta}\tan\!\left(\frac{\pi}{\beta}\right)\min\{\sqrt{a_1},\sqrt{a_2}\}.
    \end{align}
    Then the functions
    \begin{align}
        f_1(\xi)\coloneqq \left(1+\frac{a_1\xi^2-ib\xi}{\beta}\right)^{-\beta},
        \qquad
        f_2(\xi)\coloneqq \left(1+\frac{a_2\xi^2+ib\xi}{\beta}\right)^{-\beta}
    \end{align}
    are characteristic functions satisfying
    \begin{align}
        \Phi_\beta\bigl(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi)\bigr)
        =
        \left(1+\frac{(a_1+a_2)\xi^2}{\beta}\right)^{-\beta}
        \in \cG_\beta,
    \end{align}
    but neither $f_1$ nor $f_2$ belongs to $\cG_\beta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.733335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_efeb8ef68bc5fda140b0b002e01c3c2cf2e21f7aea3989aea06bf82eacc912e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:logLargeScaleCancellation of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Let $K\ge1$, and recall the $L^\infty L^2(\mu)$ and integral-operator norms of (rem:Ustattail of the paper).
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item\emph{(Riesz case $0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$.)}  The centered kernels of the splitting (equation eq:FourierLowHighDef of the paper) satisfy, uniformly in $0<\eta\le\eta_0$,
\begin{align}
\|\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,>K}\|_{L^2(\mu^{\otimes2})}^2 &\le C_\mu \int_{|\xi|>K}\widehat{{\mathsf{g}}}(\xi)^2\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\xi \le C_\mu K^{2\mathsf{s}-\mathsf{d}},\\
\|\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,>K}\|_{L^\infty L^2(\mu)}^2 &\le C_\mu \int_{|\xi|>K}\widehat{{\mathsf{g}}}(\xi)^2\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\xi \le C_\mu K^{2\mathsf{s}-\mathsf{d}},\\
\|\mathcal{T}_{\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,>K}}\|_{\mathrm{op}} &\le C_\mu \sup_{|\xi|>K}\widehat{{\mathsf{g}}}(\xi) \le C_\mu K^{-(\mathsf{d}-\mathsf{s})},
\end{align}
together with the low-mode diagonal bound
\begin{align}
\sup_x \tilde{{\mathsf{g}}}_{\eta,\le K}(x,x) \le 4\int_{|\xi|\le K}\widehat{{\mathsf{g}}}(\xi)\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d\xi \le C_1 K^\mathsf{s},
\end{align}
for a constant $C_1=C_1(\mathsf{d},\mathsf{s})$.
\item\emph{(Logarithmic case $\mathsf{s}=0$.)}  Assume (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper).  There is a constant $C_{\mu,K}<\infty$ such that, for every $N\ge1$, every $T\ge2$, every $0<\eta\le\eta_0$, and every configuration $X_N$,
\begin{align}
\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N h_{\mu,T}(x_i)
-\frac1{2N}\sum_{1\le i\ne j\le N}\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,T,\le K}(x_i,x_j)
\le C_{\mu,K}.
\end{align}
Moreover,
\begin{align}
\|\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,T,>K}\|_{L^2(\mu^{\otimes2})}^2+\|\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,T,>K}\|_{L^\infty L^2(\mu)}^2&\le C_\mu K^{-\mathsf{d}},
\qquad
\|\mathcal{T}_{\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,T,>K}}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le C_\mu K^{-\mathsf{d}},\nonumber\\
\|\tilde{\mathsf{g}}_{\eta,T,>K}\|_{L^\infty}&\le C\pa[\big]{1+\log(1/\eta)}.
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.127901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eff11681ab58f041cf53f7613254dc2c7decd4bee42f43f41b798f9fcabfb799","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:mapping_into_the_good_direction of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Let $A \subset \subset V(G)$ connected, $x \in \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A$ and $y \in \mathcal{N}_1(x)$ and $z \in \mathcal{N}_2(x)$ fixed in an arbitrary way. Then
\begin{equation}

	\Psi_1(x,A) := 
	\begin{cases}
		x, & \text{if} \quad \mathcal{N}_1(x) \cap \overline{A} = \emptyset, \\
		z, & \text{otherwise}, 
	\end{cases}
	\quad \text{and} \quad
	\Psi_2(x,A) := 
	\begin{cases}
		x, & \text{if} \quad \mathcal{N}_2(x) \cap \overline{A} = \emptyset, \\
		y, & \text{otherwise}.
	\end{cases}
\end{equation}
These can be also extended to any subset $B \subseteq \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A$ of the exterior boundary as 
\begin{equation}

	\Psi_1(B, A) := \big\{ \Psi_1(x,A) : x \in B \big\}
	\quad \text{and} \quad
	\Psi_2(B, A) := \big\{ \Psi_2(x,A) : x \in B \big\}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.575981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eff56ddc7873c1aef752c04f5ca1ec3266d91e593d31ef97ce2b3143d3ee2833","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-inequality for H of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] For any $x\geqslant 0$ and $\varepsilon\geqslant0$, we have 
\begin{align} 
H(x(1+\varepsilon)) \leqslant H(x) (1+\varepsilon)
\end{align}
and 
\begin{align} 
H(x(1-\varepsilon)) \geqslant H(x) (1-\varepsilon).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.186804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eff83fd9faa9626ecd847a908dc4c145f9e5dc92ba5a495610b12804eb7b1f3c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exists $c>0$ such that for any $a>0$, $v\neq w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $|v-w|\le 1$, and $D\subset \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $\mathrm{dist}(D,w)\ge |v-w|$,
