{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.355909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f00f11fc7b845052912320fdb89f0452e8b273194f2639aa2b97d13cfa3bbe3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:scaling_limit_cutoff of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $M\geq 1$, $\mu>0$ and $R>0$. Suppose that $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ satisfy  (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper).

Then, for all $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$, 
\begin{equation}

\lim_{N \to \infty}\sup_{u_0\in \mathcal{B}_{p,q}(M)}{\mathbf P}\big(\|w_{{\rm cut}}^N - w_{{\rm cut,d}}\|_{L^{2p}({\mathbb R}_+;L^{2q}(\mathbb{T}^3;{\mathbb R}^3))}\geq \varepsilon\big)=0,
\end{equation}
where $w_{{\rm cut}}^N$ is the global $(p,q)$-solution to (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff of the paper) with initial data $u_0-\overline{u}_0$, and $w_{{\rm cut,d}}$ is the unique global $(p,q)$-solution to the following deterministic {{\normalfont{3D NSEs}}} with cutoff and \emph{increased viscosity} on $\mathbb{T}^3$:
\begin{equation}

\left\{
\begin{aligned}
\partial_t w_{{\rm cut,d}} 
&+(\overline{u}_0\cdot \nabla) w_{{\rm cut,d}} \\
&+\phi_{p,q}^R (\cdot,w_{{\rm cut,d}}) \,\mathbb{P}\big[ \nabla\cdot (w_{{\rm cut,d}} \otimes w_{{\rm cut,d}})\big] 
= \Big(1 + \frac{3\mu}{5}\Big)\Delta w_{{\rm cut,d}}, \\
w_{{\rm cut,d}}(0)&=u_0-\overline{u}_0.
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.971890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f00f7f60abd22d45e404050744b87862df0162aac242fb917475c7b0fc3f0942","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2606.10313, '\textbf{Invariance principles for additive functionals of voter models}'] (Clifford and Sudbury, 1973; Holley and Liggett, 1975).
For any integer $m\geq 1$, $x_1, x_2, \ldots, x_m\in G$, $0\leq t_1, t_2, \ldots, t_m\leq s$, given $\eta\in \{0, 1\}^G$ and $H:\{0, 1\}^m\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, we have
\begin{align}
&\mathbb{E}_\eta H\left(\eta_{t_1}(x_1), \eta_{t_2}(x_2)\ldots, \eta_{t_m}(x_m)\right) \notag\\
&=\hat{\mathbb{E}}H\left(\eta(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_1, x_1}), \eta(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_2, x_2})\ldots, \eta(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_m, x_m})\right).
\end{align}
Consequently, for any probability distribution $\mu$ on $\{0, 1\}^G$,
\begin{align*}
&\mathbb{E}_{\mu} H\left(\eta_{t_1}(x_1), \eta_{t_2}(x_2)\ldots, \eta_{t_m}(x_m)\right) \notag\\
&=\hat{\mathbb{E}}\mathbb{E}_{\mu}H\left(\eta_0(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_1, x_1}), \eta_0(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_2, x_2})\ldots, \eta_0(\mathcal{X}_s^{s-t_m, x_m})\right).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.503711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f010fff9e2328ef899d3897f1dd41e14fc33a5dfe85768b559f48e570ba05305","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 68 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We introduce the following notions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item We call the $\bbr^{d \times d}$-valued process $\bbb = \bbb^{\rm Strat}$ defined by the Stratonovich integrals
\begin{align*}
\bbb_{s,t} := \int_s^t B_{s,r} \otimes \circ dB_r, \quad s,t \in [0,T]
\end{align*}
the \emph{Stratonovich-enhancement} of Brownian motion.

\item We call the process $\bfb = \bfb^{\rm Strat}$ defined as $\bfb := (B,\bbb)$ the \emph{Stratonovich-enhanced Brownian motion}.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.550379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f01226890a8ba5f25437d316e2ffe5104dad1a81ce70d532f3fc14cfa88dc85a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2609.01402, 'Parabolic Lie algebroid connections on parabolic principal bundles over curves'] Take a compact connected Riemann surface $X$ with a finite set of marked points $S\, \subset\, X$.
Take a connected complex reductive affine algebraic group $G$ and a parabolic subgroup $P\, \subset\, G$.
Let $\mathcal{E}_{G}$ be a parabolic principal $G$--bundle on $(X,\,S)$ which is not semistable. Let
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{E}_{P}\ \subset\ \mathcal{E}_{G}
\end{equation}
be the parabolic 
Harder--Narasimhan reduction of structure group of $\mathcal{E}_{G}$.
Then for any parabolic Lie algebroid $(V_{*},\, \phi_{*})$ on $(X,\,S)$ for which $\phi_{*}$ is not surjective, 
there is a holomorphic parabolic $(V_{*},\, \phi_{*})$--connection on $\mathcal{E}_{P}$.","status":"unverified"}

