{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.663641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f01546e66a5d628cef512bc1ac61e978b52d9fa3f6efc1d4c603ed2cfd19ec6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Macro of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Assume that the edge weights satisfy Assumption~(ass:weight of the paper) and $\ell/n\to \gl\in(0,1/2)$. Let $U_n$ be an independent uniform vertex in $\{1,2,\ldots,n-1\}$, $T_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)$ be the first-passage time defined in~(equation eq:unif-target-Tn of the paper), and let $\mathfrak{a}_\ell$ be as in
(equation eq:aell-def of the paper). Then
\begin{align*}
 \mathfrak{a}_\ell\cdot T_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)-\log n
 \Rightarrow S_\infty\text{ as } n\to\infty,
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align}
 S_\infty\stackrel{d}{=}
 -\log M_\infty^{(1)}-\log M_\infty^{(2)}-G_3-\log\theta,
\end{align}
$M_\infty^{(1)},M_\infty^{(2)}$ are i.i.d.~copies of $M_\infty$ defined in~(equation eq:Minfty-def of the paper), $G_3$ has the standard Gumbel distribution and is independent of $(M_\infty^{(1)},M_\infty^{(2)})$.
In particular,
\begin{align*}
 \frac{n^{1/\theta}}{\log n}\cdot T_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)
 \stackrel{\pr}{\to} \bigl(2\gl\Gamma(\theta+1)\bigr)^{-1/\theta} \text{ as } n\to\infty.
\end{align*}
The same results hold if we replace the random target $U_n$ by a fixed target $\mathsf{u}_n$ as defined in~(equation eq:fixed-target-Tn of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

