{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0189e59eeeb4051fe3680708d41146b0d1af4ffccd824bdcefce9db6f1e35e9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:quadraticvariation of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For $i\in\{1,2\}$, any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$ and any $t\in [0,T]$, the quadratic variation writes under the form
    \begin{equation}
        \langle\mathcal{M}^{N,i}(\varphi )\rangle_t = N^{a-3}\int_0^t \sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}} \begin{pmatrix}
         \mathfrak{c}_i & 1
        \end{pmatrix}\Upsilon_x(s)\begin{pmatrix}
            \mathfrak{c}_i \\
            1
        \end{pmatrix} \left( \nabla_NT_{v_iN^{a-1}s}\varphi \Big(\frac xN\Big)\right)^2\,\mathrm{d} s
    \end{equation}
    where for any $x\in\mathbb{Z}$, $\Upsilon_x=\Upsilon_x(\eta )$ is the $2\times 2$ matrix given by
    \begin{multline*}
        \Upsilon_x(\eta )\coloneq \left[\left(1+\frac{\alpha_p+\alpha_e\eta_x}{2N^\gamma}\right)c_{x\to x+1}^p (\eta )+ \left(1-\frac{\alpha_p+\alpha_e\eta_{x+1}}{2N^\gamma}\right)c_{x+1\to x}^p(\eta )\right]\\
        \hspace{2cm}\times\begin{pmatrix}
            (\xi_x-\xi_{x+1})^2 & (\xi_x-\xi_{x+1})(\eta_x-\eta_{x+1}) \\
            (\xi_x-\xi_{x+1})(\eta_x-\eta_{x+1}) & (\eta_x-\eta_{x+1})^2
        \end{pmatrix}\\
            +\left[ \left( 1+\frac{\alpha_e}{2}\right)c_{x\to x+1}^e(\eta )+ \left( 1-\frac{\alpha_e}{2}\right) c_{x+1\to x}^e(\eta )\right] \begin{pmatrix}
                0 & 0 \\
                0 & 1
            \end{pmatrix}.
    \end{multline*}
    Moreover,  for any $t\in [0,T]$ and any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$, we have the following $L^2$-convergence
    \begin{equation}
        N^{2-a}\langle\mathcal{M}^{N,i}(\varphi )\rangle_t  \xrightarrow[N\to \infty]{L^2} \sigma_i( t )
    \end{equation}
    where $\sigma_i : [0,T]\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}_+$ is the function given by
    \begin{equation}
       \sigma_i(t) =2(\kappa -1)t \begin{pmatrix}
        \mathfrak{c}_i & 1
       \end{pmatrix} \chi(\rho ,\mathcal{E})\begin{pmatrix}
        \mathfrak{c}_i\\
        1
       \end{pmatrix} \|\nabla\varphi\|_{L^2}^2
    \end{equation}
    and $\chi$ is the compressibility matrix given in (equation eq:compressibilitymatrix of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.075946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f01d02550442ef718fb1ae0b139b65b131e1942b718c5c93e3b618ed16a84920","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 4 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] For fixed $h>0$, consider the function $\Phi^{(h)}$ as given by \eqref{eq:Phi}. Then, for any $X \in L^2({\mathbb S})$,  we have
