{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.654086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f031ceb3fd9a5cbc538da044d4e553cba0447a908ae292650d1a554de77ba7d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2608.30859, 'Conservation Laws with Discontinuous Flux:\\ A First Application to Traffic Flow'] Assume that $f'(u_{\max})\neq g'(u_{\max})$. Then the tangent point $u^*$ defined in \eqref{eq:ustar} exists if and only if $u^-<u^-_{\mathrm{lim}}$, where $u^-_{\mathrm{lim}}$ is defined by
\begin{equation}
g'(u_{\max})
=
\frac{f(u^-_{\mathrm{lim}})-g(u_{\max})}{u^-_{\mathrm{lim}}-u_{\max}}
=
\frac{f(u^-_{\mathrm{lim}})}{u^-_{\mathrm{lim}}-u_{\max}}.
\end{equation}

Similarly, assume that $f'(0)\neq g'(0)$. Then the tangent point $v^*$ defined in \eqref{eq:vstar} exists if and only if $u^+>u^+_{\mathrm{lim}}$, where $u^+_{\mathrm{lim}}$ is defined by
\begin{equation}
g'(0)
=
\frac{f(u^+_{\mathrm{lim}})-g(0)}{u^+_{\mathrm{lim}}}
=
\frac{f(u^+_{\mathrm{lim}})}{u^+_{\mathrm{lim}}}.
\end{equation}
If, however, $f'(0)=g'(0)$ and $f'(u_{\max})=g'(u_{\max})$, then
$u^+_{\mathrm{lim}}=0$ and $u^-_{\mathrm{lim}}=u_{\max}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.384731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f032db93c7e9675a60b6193bca6a4f1e047174c0e22df8ec4517ea9d193c77d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] Let $\rho\geq 1$, $\ell\geq 1$, and $b\geq 2$ be integers. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] the sequence $C_b^{\Lambda}(n)$ of $\rho$-color $b$-ary 
partitions of $n$ (where the multiplicity of each part with color $i$ is one 
of $i, 2i, \ldots, \ell i$) and
\item[(b)] the sequence $Y_n$ of ordinary partitions with each part bounded by
$\rho$ and occurring at most $\ell$ times
\end{enumerate}
are connected by the recurrence relation
\begin{equation}
C_b^\Lambda(bn+j)=\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor\lambda/b\rfloor}Y_{bk+j}C_b^\Lambda(n-k)
\qquad (j=0, 1,\ldots b-1),
\end{equation}
where $\lambda=\ell\rho(\rho+1)/2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.750934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03315fa3cbb942e8f6cf028f22e8f64167d3903ad7c0da04d9460bfa5b82598","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:alive-tree-supercritical-support-witness of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Then \(\mathbb{P}(W>0)>1/2\). Hence
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal T^{+}:=\{v\in\mathcal T:Q_v>0\}
\end{equation*}
is a supercritical Galton--Watson tree with offspring law \(\operatorname{Binomial}(2,\mathbb{P}(W>0))\). Moreover, with
\begin{equation*}
A_n:=\#\{v\in\{0,1\}^{n}:Q_v>0\},
\end{equation*}
one has \(A_n\to\infty\) almost surely on \(\{\mu_\circ(\mathbb S^1)>0\}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.074430+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0370da9b5d9380af5d9e8b995064e5b66cfdb1cf18308212ea1528eb2ac1e15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo dqgsrt of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Take the same hypothesis as (theo:excha of the paper). Let $M_0,\cdots,M_{b-1}$ be some non-negative masses. For all $a_0\preceq 0\preceq a_1\preceq \cdots \preceq a_{b-1}\preceq a_0 \preceq 0 \cdots$ and such that
	$\Leb\left( \fleche{[a_i,a_{i+1 {~\sf mod~} b}]}\right)> M_i$ for all $i\in \{0,\cdots,b-1\}$, 
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P}\left( \bA{k}_j \in \mathrm{d} a_j,  \left|\textbf{O}^{(k)}_j\right|=M_j, 0\leq j \leq b-1\right)= \sum_{(J_0,\cdots,J_{b-1}) \in P(k,b)} \prod_{j=0}^{b-1} Q(m(J_j)) \mathds{1}_{W(m(J_j)) = M_j}\, \mathrm{d} a_j
	\end{equation} where $P(k,b)$ is the set of partitions of $\{0,\ldots, k-1\}$ into $b$ parts. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.780267+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03ae4f67c6e9718027209e3ef5d0820b418757652873c11bb77c18ac6098ac4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Semicircular system asymptotics of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For each $n$, let $(M_1,\dots,M_k)$ be a jointly Gaussian family of GOE random matrices such that
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \mathbb{E}\left[(M_i)_{\ell_1,\ell_2} (M_j)_{\ell_1',\ell_2'}\right]= \left(\delta_{(\ell_1,\ell_2),(\ell_1',\ell_2')}+\delta_{(\ell_1,\ell_2),(\ell_2',\ell_1')}\right) \varphi_{i,j}.
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \frac{1}{n^{1+\ell/2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathrm{Tr}(M_{i_1}\dots M_{i_{\ell}})\right] = \sum_{\pi \in NC_2[\alpha]} \prod_{(j,j') \in \pi} \varphi_{i_j,i_{j'}}+O(n^{-1}),
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    as $n \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.657680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f03b020499fead5cb7c54738ad39223eb0a9b937d7573b4689490e4cdf7e5427","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 52 of arXiv:2609.01389, 'K-stability and birational rigidity of Fano 3-fold weighted complete intersections'] The defining polynomials of $X$ can be written as
