{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.184732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f04157af0b43ab9ab9b742ee362f9bbe54802e2971cf61f3965ec58d88f3784d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] Let $B\subset \mathbf N(\mathbbm{X})$ be measurable, and let $X_0,\dots,X_m$ be $\mathbf N(\mathbbm{X})$-valued random variables defined on a common probability space. Then
\begin{align*}
