{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.257276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0485127439b5d0c4b30f048e5515818b9fc84ac68c297e9cd4ad513618e5620","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let $p\geq 2$ and~\eqref{co:1} and~\eqref{co:5} hold. Then pathwise uniqueness holds for~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model}, and any two solutions $I$ and $\tilde{I}$ to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} satisfy
\begin{equation*}
\E\big[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|^{p}\big] \leq e^{\int_{0}^{t}\overline{\lambda}_{p}(s,N(s))\,\mathrm{d}s}\E\big[|I_{0} - \tilde{I}_{0}|^{p}\big]
\end{equation*}
for all $t\geq 0$ with $\overline{\lambda}_{p} := p(\hat{b}_{k+1} + \hat{\lambda}_{k+1} + c_{p}\lambda^{2})$. In particular, the integrability of $\overline{\lambda}_{p}^{+}(\cdot,N)$ entails that $\sup_{t\geq 0}\E[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|^{p}] < \infty$. In this case,
