			\mathsf{acc}_k(x)=\mathsf{acc}_k(k)-\int_x^k(k-t)m(t)\dd{t}
		\end{equation}
		Moreover, $$m(t)=\frac{\mathsf{acc}_k'(t)}{k-t}$$ for all $k\in\mathsf{range}(V)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

