{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.844961+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0950f01277e798a711f2ce67384291e4ade930325c53b06f6ce2bb5d3bb700f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem the: solution of transport equation for null initial condition of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Consider the threshold value defined as follows:
	\begin{equation}

		y_* \vcentcolon= \inf \asetc{y \geq 0}{\lambda_0 \int_0^y S_g(u, u)du \geq 1},
	\end{equation}
	where we let $y_* \vcentcolon= \infty$ if the integral is strictly less than one for all $y \geq 0$.
	There exists a unique $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}^+$ such that $\boldsymbol{\mu}_0$ is the null measure. The threshold function of $\boldsymbol{\mu}$ is:
	\begin{equation*}
		\bar y_*\left(\boldsymbol{\mu}_t\right) =
		\begin{cases}
			\infty & \text{if} \quad 0 \leq t < y_*, \\
			y_* & \text{if} \quad y_* < \infty \quad \text{and} \quad t \geq y_*.
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation*}
	Moreover, $\boldsymbol{\mu}$ is determined by the following integrals:
	\begin{equation}

		\angled{\phi}{\boldsymbol{\mu}_t} = \lambda_0 \int_0^t \phi\left(u \wedge y_*, u\right) S_g\left(u \wedge y_*, u\right)du \quad \text{for all} \quad t \geq 0 \quad \text{and} \quad \phi \in C_b\left(\mathbbm{R}_+^2\right).
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.872164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0976720b35fcac47f4c8dd502884d9a166f4a5842435f67602c6f377823fe68","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 72191 of arXiv:2411.00629, '\Large Transformation of Stochastic Recursions and Critical Phenomena in the Analysis of t'] For sufficiently large $M>M_{\alpha}>0$ and sufficiently small $0<\delta<{\delta}_{M}$, the function
