{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.643535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f09df0e73b94aa1d947eee0fd1997da1248838d1bf212479942e36e20f71164b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj exp_mixing of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] For every $\beta>\beta_c$, there exists $c>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
