for all $X,Y\in\Gamma(\Dtilde)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:08.196967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0a0aabf90829f6e680f500c16a9bfdc1217e880374e99e2d4d0ffe45fd8bf2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tailbnd of arXiv:2608.13452, 'Wasserstein stability of the zero cell of a Poisson hyperplane tessellation under directio'] Let \(\Phi\) be a coupling of \(\phi_1\) and \(\phi_2\) which is antipodally symmetric, i.e., \(\Phi\) is invariant under the antipodal map \(T: (v_1,v_2) \mapsto (-v_1,-v_2)\) for all \((v_1,v_2) \in (S^{d-1})^2\).
    Given the coupling $(Z_0^{(1)},Z_0^{(2)})$ defined by (equation eq:couplingZeroCells of the paper) using \(\Phi\), we have for all $u \in S^{d-1}$ and $t > 0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}[ \rho_{Z_0^{(1)}}(u)- \rho_{Z_0^{(2)}}(u) \geq t]
        &= 2 \gamma \int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-\gamma F_u(y+t,y)} \int_{(S^{d-1})^2} \langle u,v_2 \rangle   \indic{ 0 < \langle  u , v_2\rangle < \frac{y+t}{t} \langle u,v_2-v_1 \rangle} \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} \Phi (v_1 , v_2) \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} y,
    \end{align*}
    where $F_u(\cdot,\cdot)$ is defined as in (equation def:Fu of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.847767+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0a194d13f1166407f91d20be97d9e1e74ee95ef22bea060264e0cdcaa13f130","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Let $B_0^N$ be a deterministic matrix. There exists a constant $C_{\rho,t}$ such that, for any $y\in\R$, we have that
