{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.135033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0ac12823f0c33f92172cad2cda8552376107b204754940cfd0b2d93fa438878","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:poisson_zoo of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Given the $\Gamma$-rotation invariant measure $\nu := \nu_{o}$ and some intensity parameter $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}_{>0}$, let us consider independent Poisson random variables $N_{x,H}^{\lambda} \sim \mathsf{Poisson}( \lambda \cdot \nu_x(H) )$ indexed by $x \in V(G)$ and $H \in \mathcal{H}_x$.
	We say that $N_{x,H}^{\lambda}$ is the number of copies of the animal $H$ (rooted at $x$).
	We call the collection of random variables
	\begin{equation}

		\mathcal{N}_{\nu}^\lambda := 
		\left\{ 
			N^\lambda_{x,H} \, : \, x \in V(G), H \in \mathcal{H}_x 
		\right\}
	\end{equation}
	the {\bf Poisson zoo} at level $\lambda$ (with measure $\nu$) and the random set
	\begin{equation}

		\mathcal{S}_{\nu}^\lambda := 
		\bigcup_{x \in V} \bigcup_{H \in \mathcal{H}_x} \bigcup_{i = 1}^{ N_{x,H}^{\lambda} } \, H
	\end{equation}
	the {\bf trace} of the Poisson zoo at level $\lambda$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.064186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0acb111c3ef60fe19677487b5fc12b6ed5118635065ccabbca100039498931c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmaNeu1 of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Let $t-s<1$, $x\in{\mathbb R}^+$ and $\mu\in\mathcal{P}_0({\mathbb R}^+)$ (i.e.  a probability measure on ${\mathbb R}_+$). For $q\geq 1$, the following $L^q$ estimates hold:
