     \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.010711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0bba656f7f137031b2b8a60c55902f63ada14f91e0276a3314e563b1a4ca05a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Assume $\beta>3$. Given $\varepsilon \in (0, \beta-3)$, there exists $\uc{c:correlation_decay_gf}>0$ such that, for all $n \in \N$, if $A$ and $B$ are events supported in $B(0, 3n)$ and $B(0, 4n)^{c}$, respectively, then
