{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.071329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0c017558d28dc2c7645f7f3c2f9e8b187e2ea0d701a61af472abb3d9886aa79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 (Theorem~\ref{maintheorem} (G)) of arXiv:2606.01832, 'MA(1) processes with uniform innovations conditioned to stay positive in the non-expanding'] For $y>\frac{1}{\theta}$, the limiting process $M'$ exists and is a Markov chain on $S$ with transition kernel
