{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.866225+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0d1fb357069e0502240675cef8567c30f3fe4b853d8bf745fca040a1de3e885","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Suppose that $\E[U]=1$ and $\Var(U)<\infty$. Then, for every $t>0$,
