{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0f0402c71c2fc7c79379d15c2e901a77e797cc353d5d4f3986d29a99d20a672","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 12 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] There is a unique family $\{\G_{\sigma}\}_{\sigma\in\Sigma_0}\subset \mathcal{P}_{V}(E)$, measurable in $\sigma$, such that
