{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.640193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0fc3d30bc16ebc6d1a9bac761dcddf95dcd89beccc3bdf4b95979c3a51736da","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Order of a tempered distribution of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Let \(T\in\mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^d)\) be a tempered distribution (i.e.\ a continuous linear functional on \(\mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R}^d)\)).  We say that \(T\) is of \emph{order} at most \(m\) if there exists a constant \(C>0\) such that
\[
  \bigl|T \varphi\bigr|
  \;\le\;
  C \,\sum_{\substack{|\alpha|\le m \\|\beta|\le m}}
  \;\sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d}
  \bigl|\,x^{\alpha}\,\partial^{\beta}\varphi(x)\bigr|
  \quad
  \text{for all }\varphi\in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R}^d).
\]
The \emph{order} of \(T\) is the least integer \(m\) for which such an estimate holds.","status":"unverified"}

