{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.740099+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f0ffd705e19a19c0f68aab410ed80538bb66de65aaca169c44499e0b3c2ee43f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] [\cite{Minh2024:FisherRaoGaussian}, Lemma 22]

	Let $S,T \in \Sym(\Hcal) \cap \HS(\Hcal)$, with eigenvalues $\{\alpha_k\}_{k \in \Nbb}$, $\{\beta_k\}_{k \in \Nbb}$
	and corresponding orthonormal eigenvectors $\{\phi_k\}_{k \in \Nbb}$, $\{\psi_k\}_{k \in \Nbb}$, respectively.
	Let $A \in \Sym(\Hcal)$.
	Then
	\begin{align}

		\trace(ASAT) =\trace(SATA) = \sum_{k,j=1}^{\infty}\alpha_k \beta_j \la A\phi_k, \psi_j\ra^2.
	\end{align}
	If, in addition, $A \in \Sym(\Hcal)\cap \HS(\Hcal)$, then $\trace(AS) = \sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\alpha_k\la \phi_k, A\phi_k\ra$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.272417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f10b9a1400402728d979ebb91a3583ff07fda5069d279f033769be6416429734","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] For $0\le p<(4a-1)/4a$, we have
