{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.585402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f12944c3bee481f52bb5934790387ea9b6409a3d910ca1deee4d1f03dd1fc5d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $(M,g)$ be a compact manifold with reference process having a spectral gap $\lambda_1> 0$. For $\mu,\nu \in \cP_2(M)$ satisfying Assumption \ref{assumption},   
