{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.315441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f149b8020e0f0277a2529ad024c3edfd7f6f95bdce8d4612a118e3ef47f22ddd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition taut surface of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Let \(M\) be a compact oriented 3-manifold, and let \(S\) be an oriented surface representing nontrivial \(\alpha\in H_{2}(M,\partial M)\).
We say that \(S\) is \emph{taut} (\emph{norm-minimizing}) if
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(S\) contains no null-homologous component in \(H_{2}(M,\partial M)\),
\item \(\chi_{-}(S)=x_{M}(\alpha)\).
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.503356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f14fd9755ffa0d1df1a426197275b796d17fcd25649f78de116d975a3919c382","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.30578, 'Compactly Supported Solutions near a Nehari Critical Value'] Let $D\subset\mathbb R^N$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain and let
$F:D\times(0,+\infty)\to\mathbb R$ be a Carath\'eodory function such that,
for a.e. $x\in D$, the map
\begin{equation}
	s\mapsto\frac{F(x,s)}{s}

\end{equation}
is strictly decreasing on $(0,+\infty)$. Let
$U,V\in H^1(D)\cap L^\infty(D)$, with $U>0$, $V>0$ a.e. in $D$, and assume
the one-sided trace condition
\begin{equation}
	(U-V)^+\in H_0^1(D).

\end{equation}
Suppose that $U$ is a weak subsolution and $V$ a weak supersolution of
\begin{equation}
	-\Delta w=F(x,w)
	\qquad\hbox{in }D,

\end{equation}
that is,
\begin{align}
	\int_D\nabla U\cdot\nabla\varphi\,dx
	&\leq
	\int_DF(x,U)\varphi\,dx,
	\\
	\int_D\nabla V\cdot\nabla\varphi\,dx
	&\geq
	\int_DF(x,V)\varphi\,dx

\end{align}
for every non-negative
$\varphi\in H_0^1(D)\cap L^\infty(D)$ for which the right-hand sides are
finite. Assume, moreover, that
\begin{equation}
	F(\cdot,U),F(\cdot,V)\in L^1_{\rm loc}(D)

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
	\left(
	\frac{|F(x,U)|}{U}
	+
	\frac{|F(x,V)|}{V}
	\right)
	(U^2-V^2)^+
	\in L^1(D).

\end{equation}
Then
\[
U\leq V
\qquad\hbox{a.e. in }D.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524991+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1516d7a947d300bdec3b6b4d9ee0d94239f90e35200590989d94a516a629dd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop e:moment_main_bound of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For any initial data $u[0] = u_{\mathfrak{r}}[0] + u_{\mathfrak{s}}[0]$ with $\|u_{\mathfrak{s}}[0]\| = \lambda$ and $\|u_{\mathfrak{r}}[0]\|_{\mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}} \leq 2\alpha_0$, define $w^{\mathcal{L}}$ and stopping time $T$ as previously. Then there exists some constant $C$ which is independent of $N$, such that for any $0 < a < 1$ and $\alpha_0$ small enough (the smallness is independent of $N$), we have 
