    \end{equation}
    where $\zeta(3) = \sum_{k=1}^\infty k^{-3} = 1.202\dots$ is Apéry's constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.007399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f15d187e51af3acdfb7277a11559e9d892b1699673eec763934bc0eee6f10d3a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Loss without recovery) of arXiv:2608.14802, 'Dynamical Gibbs-non-Gibbs transitions for finite-alphabet models on trees'] Let $\theta>4$, and let $l$ be either an $f$-saddle or the free fixed point. By permutation symmetry, it suffices to consider $l=l_-^{(1)}$ or $l=l_{\text{free}}$, as classified in Lemma \ref{lem: Fixed points normalized simplex Potts model}.

