{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.890674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1653d85ee31e1c4aa8c2ca8610885d8bb9132ccc4fad1779b474f76163dd656","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:wMRWbercanc of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] For any sequence $\eta_\ell\le \ell$, let $\varepsilon_\ell=\varepsilon(\phi_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}^M)$. Then, we have
