{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.380379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1bb8f36be7b6c324ddd04860c0dcef1a7f5d9c98918aeb4680b6048c00817df","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:negative-potential-results of arXiv:2608.18320, 'Asymptotics for Beta-Splitting Trees via Homogeneous Fragmentations and Meromorphic Potent'] For $-2<\beta<0$,
    \begin{equation}
            U_\beta(\mathrm{d} x)
            =\eta_\beta\delta_0(\mathrm{d} x)
            +\left[
            \frac1{\mu_\beta}
            +\sum_{k\ge1}
            \frac{e^{s_{\beta,k}x}}{\phi_\beta'(s_{\beta,k})}
            \right]\mathrm{d} x.
    \end{equation}
    The residues $1/\phi_\beta'(s_{\beta,k})$ are positive, and the series
    converges locally uniformly for $x>0$.  Equivalently, for $\textnormal{Re} z>0$,
    \begin{equation}
            \frac1{\phi_\beta(z)}
            =\eta_\beta+\frac1{\mu_\beta z}
            +\sum_{k\ge1}
            \frac1{\phi_\beta'(s_{\beta,k})(z-s_{\beta,k})}.
    \end{equation}
    In particular,
    \begin{equation}
            \eta_\beta
            -\sum_{k\ge1}
            \frac1{s_{\beta,k}\phi_\beta'(s_{\beta,k})}
            =-\frac{\phi_\beta''(0)}{2\mu_\beta^2}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.290430+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1bfe975eb7dbf6885537572fb112ce1f2190c59d08ef958fed75280cf099074","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:1 of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be an UPPS.  Then the following four statements are equivalent:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item [(i)] $V(\mathcal{I})=\{0,1\}$; 
		\item [(ii)] $V$ is of finite ergodic components;
		\item [(iii)] the set $\mathcal{ M}^e(T)\cap\operatorname{core}(V)=\{Q_1,\ldots,Q_n\}$, and  for any $P\in\mathcal{M}(T)\cap \operatorname{core}(V)$  there exist $0\le \alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{n}\le 1$ with $\sum_{i=1}^{n}\alpha_i=1$  such that 
		\[P=\alpha_1Q_1+\ldots+\alpha_nQ_n,\] where the decomposition is unique;
		\item[(iv)] $\operatorname{ex}(\operatorname{core}(V)\cap \mathcal{M}(T))=\operatorname{core}(V)\cap \mathcal{M}^e(T)\neq \emptyset$.
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.462301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1c1b54bc68d8dd49a185d2ae9f7318365e74128900828a99e7fc34acf7bd785","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 21 (Covariant wave operator of the acoustical metric) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The covariant wave operator $\square_{\gfour}$ 
