{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.120457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f1d09bcac1fd346dc9335f6b39fd545fb2c6171cadc5820fd69d3cefad6d8638","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:iidmax of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Let $G$ be a finite graph. Consider $M_{\mathrm{opt}}$ to be the maximum weight maximum size matching on $G$ when we pick a family $w(e)_{e \in E(G)}$ of weights. Formally, define $W^{\mathrm{bad}}\subseteq \mathbb{R}_+^{E(G)}$ to be the set of weights such that there are ties, and $\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{max}}$ to be the set of maximal matchings on $G$. Then $M_{\mathrm{opt}}$ is the map defined as
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{R}_+^{E(G)} \setminus W^{\mathrm{bad}} &\to \mathcal{M}_{\max} \\
        w(e)_{e \in E(G)} &\mapsto M_{\mathrm{opt}}(w(e)_{e \in E(G)}).
