\varphi_{u}^{(k)}(t-S(u)) \stackrel{a.s.}{=} \mathbb{E}[\varphi_{u}(t-S(u)) \mid \mathcal{C}_{u}^{(k-1)}] \stackrel{a.s.}{=}  \mathbb{E}[\varphi_{u}(t-S(u)) \mid \mathcal{D}_{u}^{(k-1)}]. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.848130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f202bf1c5797ee15c9c0e8ee2a7c05bf3e1bedc3745c530f3311cf60f4f7acd4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: transport equation with constant threshold of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Fix a constant $y_* \in [0, \infty)$ and let $\bar \boldsymbol{y}_t \vcentcolon= y_*$ for all $t \in [a, b]$. In addition, fix $t \in [a, b]$ and $\phi \in C_c^1(U_g)$, and consider the function defined as:
