{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.748223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2352776ccf0c60277d8840cbaaf1b79c2946d64424cfa4619100dac4bb0fe43","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:product_formula of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $\ell \geqslant 1$ be fixed and $k_1,\ldots,k_\ell\geqslant 1$. With the convention $c_x^{(\alpha)}=0,\, x\notin\mathbb N$, then it holds 
    \begin{equation}

        {\mathbb E} \left[ \prod_{r=1}^\ell a_{k_r, n} \right]
        \to \sum_{\pi \in \mathcal{P}_{\ell,2}} \prod_{B \in \pi} \left(  
     \sum_{q | \gcd(k_j:j\in B)} 
         q^{|B|-1}\left(c_{k_B/(2q)}^{(\alpha)} \right)^q \right) \,, \qquad n\to\infty\,,
