{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.962500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2365d71ac9a0b46daed16d4b480ddfd41823d39973b484546a6e884639064f8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2604.00692, 'Uniform-in-time diffusion approximations for multiscale stochastic systems'] Under {\bf (A$^\beta_{\rm SK}$)}, the unique centered solution to the Poisson equation
\begin{equation*}
\sL_1\Phi(\cdot,y)=-H(\cdot,y)=-x
\end{equation*}
is given by
\begin{equation}
\Phi(x,y)=A(y)^{-1}x.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the effective diffusion matrix and drift are
\begin{align}
\cG(y)&=A(y)^{-1}\sigma(y)\sigma(y)^*(A(y)^{-1})^*,\\
\cF(y)&=-A(y)^{-1}\nabla U(y)+\mathfrak B(y),
\end{align}
where $\mathfrak B(y)$ is called the noise-induced term given componentwise by
\begin{equation}
\mathfrak B_i(y)
=
\sum_{j,k=1}^d \Sigma_{jk}(y)\,\partial_{y_j}(A(y)^{-1})_{ik},
\qquad i=1,\dots,d.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.158579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f23681950ba67868bc6424828c564641b51a19771e8fa9105cd56286a8322a64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.02406, 'On the range of competing random walks'] for any $S\subseteq[\![N]\!]$, $|S|\ge2$, such that $|S|(d-\beta)<d$ and any $k\ge1$, we have 
