{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f23d4852e6606362f9a94a42b449790023ceacf30ee71a54db128e2844c744c3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi stitching map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $k\in \mathbb N$. We say that a finite sequence of words $\underline v=(v^1,\ldots, v^k)\in \mathcal W^k$ is stitchable if there exists
	 a nondecreasing function $j:\{1,\ldots, k\}\to\{1,\ldots, r\}$ such that 
	 for each $1\leqslant i\leqslant k$ satisfying $v^i\neq e$, the first and last letter of $v^i$ belong to $K_{j(i)}$. Let $T\in \mathbb N$. We set 
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathcal S_{k,T}=\{\underline v\in \mathcal W^k,\, \hbox{$\underline v$ is stitchable},\ |\underline v|+ k\tau_K\leqslant T\}.
	\end{equation*}
	Let $\underline v\in \mathcal S_{k,T}$. We define the measurable set $G_{k,T}(\underline v)\subseteq \mathcal W_T$ in the following way:
	for each $1\leqslant i\leqslant k$,
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item if $v^i=e$, we set $\tau_{i}=0$;
		\item otherwise, let $y=v^{i}_1$ and let $x$ be the last letter of the last non-empty $v^{j}$ before $v^i$ in the sequence (or $x_{\mathrm{init}}$ if there are none). Then, $(x,y)\in \bigcup_{j=1}^rK_j^-\times K_{j}$ (because the sequence is stitchable) and we set $\tau_{i}=\tau(x,y)$.
	\end{enumerate}
	Finally, we set $\tau_{k+1}=T-(|\underline v|+\tau_1+\ldots +\tau_k)\geqslant 0$ and 
	\begin{equation*}
		G_{k,T}(\underline v)=\mathcal W_{\tau_1}\times \{v^1\}\times \mathcal W_{\tau_2}\times \{v^2\}\times \ldots\times \mathcal W_{\tau_k}\times \{v^k\}\times \mathcal W_{\tau_{k+1}}\subseteq \mathcal W_T. 
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.183916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f23f86376907f50660e5aded0e6de235a1df897b5cc1d119ab34b9f52e3206ed","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SausageIntersection of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There exist a constant $c, C_2 > 0$, depending only on $d$, $m$, and $C$, such that for all $\eta, e_+ \in \mathrm{Centre}(C)$ with $\left\lVert\eta - e_+\right\rVert_1 = i \ne 0$, we have
