    for all $r \in \mathbb{N}$ with $r \leqslant cn$, and $n$ large enough.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.278785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f23fec9ece1e38362fd8f1479d002c91ea8721a3a2364e5c7cb83c63ac5ac581","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:MC-W1 of arXiv:2601.08184, 'Wasserstein-p Central Limit Theorem Rates: From Local Dependence to Markov Chains'] Under Assumption (assumption:markovchain of the paper),  if there exists $\delta>1$ such that $\|h_i\|^{2+\delta} \leq V$ for all $i \geq 0$,
