{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.429583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f27794bd25561a68c689fa7b59faee196860587a79625aea1e9547565e4ec17b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 197 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The even Green function $\textnormal{Gr}^+$ is given for non-real $z_i \in \Sigma^{(q_i,\textnormal{X}_i)}$ with $q_i \in [m]$ and $\textnormal{X}_i \in \{\textnormal{L},\textnormal{R}\}$ for $i = 1,2$ by
