{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.450390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2babf61b6c88f8db1095e4905f9b2c119ce5acbb835589090cbe67ebf208d1c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:exact-point-count of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:dereg-defects}
The point-incoherent exact count is
\begin{equation}
 \widehat{\mathscr C}_{N,L}^J(V)
 :=\mathbb E\sum_{\substack{x:\nabla_SH_N^J(\sqrt N x)=0\\x\in D_{N,L}}}
 e^{-NV(h_N^J(x))}.
\end{equation}
Whenever this quantity is finite and positive, put
\begin{align}
 \widehat Q_{N,L}
 &:=
 \frac1N\log\widehat{\mathscr C}_{N,L}^J(V),\\
 \widehat P_{N,L}(\varepsilon,\eta)
 &:=
 \frac1N\log
 \mathbb E\widehat\mathcal Z_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,\ell_\eta).
\end{align}
For a nonnegative function \(a(\varepsilon,\eta)\), write
\[
 \liminf_{(\varepsilon,\eta)\to(0,0)}a(\varepsilon,\eta)
 :=\lim_{\delta\downarrow0}
 \inf_{0<\varepsilon,\eta<\delta}a(\varepsilon,\eta).
\]
Define the upper and lower transfer defects
\begin{align}
 \delta_{L,\mathrm{dr}}^{J,\mathrm{up}}(V)
 &:=
 \liminf_{(\varepsilon,\eta)\to(0,0)}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}
 [\widehat Q_{N,L}-\widehat P_{N,L}(\varepsilon,\eta)]_+,
 \\
 \delta_{L,\mathrm{dr}}^{J,\mathrm{low}}(V)
 &:=
 \liminf_{(\varepsilon,\eta)\to(0,0)}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}
 [\widehat P_{N,L}(\varepsilon,\eta)-\widehat Q_{N,L}]_+.

\end{align}
Thus only one favorable vanishing-regularizer test sequence is required
in each direction, and the two sequences may differ.  They require
neither a common test sequence nor an iterated absolute comparison of
the uncut pressures.  The frame-slice quantities in
(prop:primitive-dereg of the paper) give checkable upper bounds for them.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.505218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2be6d95c6dc299379151e662ee00d4e953d8bb36c84375f5c6184c040a4515a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Put
\begin{align*}
 s_*=\frac{\alpha_{\rm H}}2-\frac14,
 \qquad s_*<\gamma<\frac{\alpha_{\rm H}}2,
 \qquad \lambda_0=\frac{\alpha_{\rm H}}2+5,
 \qquad t_M=\lambda_0M^{-2}\log M.
\end{align*}
Fix $R_0<\infty$.  Let
$z\in C_0([0,t_M];C^\gamma)$ be a deterministic, mean zero,
divergence free compatible path with
$\|z\|_{C([0,t_M];C^\gamma)}\le R_0$, let $Z^0$ be the
stochastic convolution generated by the radial noise $d_0Q_0\dd W^0$, and
put
\begin{align*}
 D_t=P_tu_0+z_t,
 \qquad X=D+Z^0,
 \qquad U_0=1+\|u_0\|_{C^\gamma}.
\end{align*}
Let $u$ be the Navier--Stokes solution with linear part $X$, and let $\rho$
solve its linearised vorticity equation from $0\ne\rho_0\in L^2$.  There
are deterministic $M_0,K_{R_0},r_0<\infty$ and
$a_0,\alpha_0>0$, depending only on the fixed equation parameters, such
that, whenever
\begin{align}
 M\ge M_0\vee M^{(2)}(\rho_0)\vee K_{R_0}U_0^{r_0},

\end{align}
one has
\begin{align}
 \mathbf P_0\left\{
  \|\Pi_0\rho_{t_M}\|_2
  \ge a_0M^{-3}
       \|\rho_0\|_{H^{-(\alpha_{\rm H}/2+1)}}
 \right\}\ge\alpha_0.

\end{align}
The constants are uniform over all such compatible paths in the fixed
$R_0$ ball.  Here ``compatible'' means a limit, in the displayed topology,
of smooth Fourier truncated velocity paths; this class contains the
residual stochastic convolutions used below.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.872081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2bf2d97c818420d60263ab12dfe7d420fc7c9c064261844509499d2277e315f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For a pointwise measurable class $\mathcal F$ bounded in $[0,B]$ with entropy integral $\Gamma(\mathcal F)$, and for any $\delta\in(0,1)$, independent observations $Z_1,\ldots,Z_n\sim P$ satisfy
