{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:55.077709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2d854cc69aee5125336e85de678f52375513cfcfb27e80fd8a97982fc8d572f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:fik-is-weaker-than-ik of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] $\textbf{FIK} \subsetneq \textbf{IK}$, that is,
  (1) $\textbf{IK} \vdash \textsf{wCD}$ and (2) $\textbf{FIK} \nvdash \textsf{FS2}$.
  \begin{proof}
    (1) Follows from the derivation below:
    \begin{center}
      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{FS2}$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$(\Diamond \varphi \to \Box \psi) \to \Box (\varphi \to \psi)$}

      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{}}
      \UnaryInfC{$(\varphi \to \psi) \to ((\varphi \lor \psi) \to \psi)$}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{M}_\Box$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Box(\varphi \to \psi) \to (\Box(\varphi \lor \psi) \to \Box\psi)$}

      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{Syll.}}
      \BinaryInfC{$(\Diamond \varphi \to \Box \psi) \to (\Box (\varphi \lor \psi) \to \Box \psi)$}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Box (\varphi \lor \psi) \to ((\Diamond \varphi \to \Box \psi) \to \Box \psi)$}
      \DisplayProof
    \end{center}
    (2) By soundness, it suffices to construct a $\Diamond$-p model that falsifies $\textsf{FS2}$.
    Let $\mathfrak{M}_{\textsf{FS2}} = (\set{x, y, y'}, \leq, \sqsubset, V)$, where
    $\mathord{\leq} = \set{ (x,x), (y,y), (y,y'), (y',y') }$,
    $\mathord{\sqsubset} = \set{ (x,y) }$,
    $V(p) = \set{ y' }$, and $V(q) = \emptyset$,
    then $\mathfrak{M}_{\textsf{FS2}}$ is clearly a $\Diamond$-p model.
    The model $\mathfrak{M}_{\textsf{FS2}}$ is visualized in Figure (fig:fs2-countermodel of the paper).
    \begin{figure}[htb]
      \centering
      \begin{tikzpicture}
      \fill (0, 2) circle (2pt);
      \draw (0, 2) node[left]{$x$};

      \fill (2, 2) circle (2pt);
      \draw (2, 2) node[right]{$y \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} p, q$};

      \draw [thick, ->, squig, rel] (0,2) to (2, 2);
      \draw (1, 2) node[below]{$\sqsubset$};

      \draw [thick, ->, rel] (2, 2) to (2, 4);
      \draw (2, 3) node[right]{$\leq$};

      \fill (2, 4) circle (2pt);
      \draw (2, 4) node[right]{$y' \Vdash^{\text{h}} p,\, \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} q$};

      \end{tikzpicture}
      \caption{The model $\mathfrak{M}_{\textsf{FS2}}$.}

    \end{figure}

    Here, $x \sqsubset y \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} p$ implies $x \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} \Diamond p$, so $x \Vdash^{\text{h}} \Diamond p \to \Box q$.
    On the other hand, $y \leq y'$, $y' \Vdash^{\text{h}} p$, and $y' \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} q$ imply $y \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} p \to q$,
    so $x \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} \Box(p \to q)$. Therefore, $x \not \Vdash^{\text{h}} \textsf{FS2}$.
  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.938794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2dfb6b9033671fc82cd8932029e5ed171b71f565577189bdf9f1a89889dc100","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Attached-tree mass inputs) of arXiv:2607.13183, '2607.13183'] For the tree attached to a core vertex $z$, the random mass
