{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.616365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2e48a3040fdaae604028fc6a4c4cb1e0a5689aa9b705d0915a94caf5f0a0bce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 47 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c$ such that for all $n\in \NN$, all $\beta>0$ and $r\leq n^{1/10}$ , we have
