{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.782297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2e5628fb8a4bd7e88c4f9ae3b22411b8d13e0d2e16e0e962736b23b4ff86928","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm smasympexOSp of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] There is a universal constant $C>0$, and a compactly supported 
distribution $\mu_k$ for every $k\in\mathbb{Z}_+$, so that the following 
hold. Fix any $h\in C^\infty(\mathbb{R})$, and let
$f(\theta):= h(K\cos\theta)$. Then
\begin{multline*}
	\left| \mathbf{E}[\mathop{\textnormal{tr}} h(X^N)]- \sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \frac{\mu_k(h)}{N^k} 
	\right| 
	~\vee~
	\left| \mathbf{E}[\mathop{\textnormal{tr}} h(Y^N)]- \sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \frac{\mu_k(h)}{(-2N)^k} 
	\right| 
\\
	\leq 
	\frac{(C\tilde q_0)^m}{u^mN^m}
	\|f^{(m'+1)}\|_{[0,2\pi]} 
	+\frac{(C\tilde q_0)^{2m}}{m!\, u^{2m} N^m} 
	\|f^{(2m'+1)}\|_{[0,2\pi]} 
\end{multline*}
for all $m, N\in \mathbb{N}$ and $u\in (0,1)$, where
$m':=\lceil (1+u)m\rceil$ and $\tilde q_0 := q_0(1+\log q_0)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.996003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2ed8fdcbe7507fb2f61d9cf45da5b05c0af67f59ff04476cd24991a7f2eca89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma simple of arXiv:2412.04013, 'Rate estimates for total variation distance with applications\thanks{The author gratefully'] Let $X$, $X_{n}$, $n\in\mathbb{N}$ be $\mathbb{R}^{d}$-valued
random variables with $X_{n}\to X$ in law as $n\to\infty$. Let $\phi_{n}$ denote the
characteristic function of $X_{n}$. 
Assume that
\begin{equation}
\sup_{n\in\mathbb{N}}|\phi_{n}(u)|\leq \psi(u),\ u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\mbox{ and }
\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\psi(u)\, du<\infty
\end{equation}
for some measurable $\psi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}$. 
Then $d_{TV}(X_{n},X)\to 0$, $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:49:24.957973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2edf82977dea6e4587053838f10c1f6bec8fc59109f8ed68eac6cca18f90d6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sparse-row-sum of arXiv:2609.03264, 'Certified Spherical MUSIC for 3D Localization under Adversarial Subspace Perturbations'] The coherence row sum defined as
		\[
		\sigma_X:=
		\max_{1\le j\le s}
		\sum_{k\ne j}\abs{K_\kappa(\bm{x}_j-\bm{x}_k)}
		\]
		satisfies the bound
