{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.657729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2efb20c6fdf71f8847b0909f78d3adb8fec7d31d52aee90e41f10187ccb47d2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 ($\delta$-smooth margins \cite{barvinok2010does}) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] An $m\times n$ margin $(\r,\c)$ with total sum $N := \|\r\|_1 = \|\c\|_1$ is \textit{$\delta$-smooth} for some $\delta>0$ if 
		\begin{align}
			\frac{\delta N}{m} \leq \r(i) \leq \frac{N}{\delta m}, \qquad \frac{\delta N}{n} \leq \c(j) \leq \frac{N}{\delta n}
		\end{align}
		for all $i \in [m]$ and $j \in [n]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.333799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2efcf352b3051f579d6b88ef75eebfc77760069e924183c5d614558031bc8e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Let $K$ be a compact such $K \subset \{\lvert z \lvert >1\}$. Then, a.s,
     \begin{equation*}
