\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.413450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f308a477d751596e9666a5016209356723f49d121a3fca2d2d4e831eef1d0467","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 68 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under Assumption~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, there exists $C > 0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions, such that for any $\boldsymbol{\ell} \in \amsmathbb{W}_\N$, there exists an absolutely continuous nonnegative measure $\tilde{\mu}_{\N}$ with the following properties:
