{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.908615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f35615813d96cf3e8410de84f2ebdb13b1babd36b924707181b80eadaad9e823","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2608.01081, 'The Optimal Rate in the Averaged Random-Marginal Central Limit Theorem for Log-Concave Mea'] Let $n\ge2$, let $G=(G_1,\ldots,G_n)$ have independent standard Gaussian
