{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.100918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3567bc00ac15780d0f451cf673f5e9b987438c372b924f48f96f46c39ec754e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem workload-difference of arXiv:2505.04942, '\textbf{Randomized Routing to Remote Queues}'] Assume the conditions of Theorem~(theorem:load-balancing of the paper) hold. Then for $T > 0$, $ \sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} \tilde{\Gamma}^{\star}_{n}(t) \Rightarrow 0 $ as $ n \to \infty $. If conditions~(equation eq:fourth-moments of the paper) and (equation eq:log-log-n-bound of the paper) also hold, then with probability 1, 
