{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.321580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f35dbdab773176322751b13cfe6f1438ea89e6beca76e29f7ec108f405eb5db9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.04943, '\textbf{Approximation of Random Differential Equations Driven by Physical Brownian Motion '] For each $0<\ep\leq 1$, let $\pe: [0,\infty)\times [0,\infty)\to L^1(\Omega,\F,P)$ be a two-parameter real random process such that $\pe(s,t)\in\F^{(t/\ep)\vee(s/\ep)}$ for all $s,t\geq 0$. Assume that for each $T>0,$
