{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.241487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f371204109120b948cd3b10df06dfa7e775ea7633efb2f9312ac17286fa3c66f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Solution of the Equation) of arXiv:2604.14893, 'Well-Posedness of Generalized Mean-Reflected McKean--Vlasov Backward Stochastic Differenti'] We say that a triplet $(Y,Z,K)$ is a solution to equation \eqref{equation} if:
