{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.098497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3859863f4af87101e3f596dccd3b428797ad1649a359bedba7af83bec9966d4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:R of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Take $\mu_v \in \mathcal{L}(\mathcal{G}^{\star})$ such that $0<m := \int_{\mathcal G^{\star}} \deg (o) \, \mathrm{d} \mu_v(G,o) < \infty$. Let $R(\mu_v) \in \mathcal{L}(\hat{\mathcal{G}}^{\star})$  be the unique measure such that,
