{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.766036+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f391d1caaec472fcca52de36d15b891ee0770b39717fb0c219bc52fbe4f62ece","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 of arXiv:2608.26723, 'Extrinsic upper bounds for the harmonic mean of eigenvalues in curved manifolds'] Let $M$ be an $m(\ge 2)$-dimensional closed orientable submanifold in an $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold $N$ of the sectional curvature $K_N \le \delta$, where $\delta > 0$.
	We assume that $M$ is contained in a convex ball of radius $\le \frac{1}{2\sqrt{\delta}}\arctan \frac{m}{\sqrt{2m+1}}$.
	Then we have
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathfrak{H}(\lambda_1,\cdots,\lambda_m)\le \frac{m}{\vol(M)}\int_M\big(\delta+|\mathbf{H}|^2\big).
	\end{equation*}
	Equality holds implies that $\lambda_1=\cdots=\lambda_m$ and $M$ is minimally immersed in a geodesic sphere of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.120448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f396f6b5336b712ac7ea6bfeafa4666e4dac57d7f61966ac9c7a23bee01cb438","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] Let $f\in C(\R)$. The following assertions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item There exists a constant $C$ such that the function $f$ satisfies the Fredholm equation
\begin{align}

f(x)
=C+\int_K f(y)h(x-y)\,\mu(dy)\qquad \text{for}\ x\in \R,
\end{align}
with the normalization condition
\begin{align}

  \mu[f]=1.
\end{align}
\item The function $f$ satisfies the growth condition
\begin{align}

f-h\in C_b(\R)
\end{align}
(which implies $f\in \mathscr{A}_0$) and the Sturm--Liouville equation
\begin{align}

\mathscr{L}f
=f\cdot \mu,
\end{align}
that is,
\begin{align}
\langle \mathscr{L} f,g\rangle =\int_\R g(x) f(x)\,\mu(dx)\qquad \text{for}\ g\in C_c^\infty(\R).
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}
If either, and hence both, of these conditions holds, then we have $f=\varphi^\mu.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.889438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f39b3cfe7e5d73393a056a9f62407331c5a706b75cfd733e0a0184d6225c67f6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:chart of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] A \emph{chart of dimension $n$} on a metric measure space $(X,d,\mu)$ is a pair $(U,\phi)$ where:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item $U \subset X$ is measurable, $m(U) >0$, and $\phi:X \to \mathbb{R}^n$ is Lipschitz.
			\item For every Lipschitz function $f: X \to \mathbb{R}$, there exists a measurable function $\partial_\phi f: U \to \mathbb{R}^n$ such that $f$ is differentiable with respect to $\phi$ at $m$-almost every $x_0 \in U$ and with derivative $\partial_\phi f(x_0)$.
		\end{enumerate}
		A \textbf{measurable differentiable structure}	on $(X,d,\mu)$ is a  countable collection $\{(U_\alpha,\phi_\alpha)\}$ of charts with uniformly bounded dimension such that $$\mu \left( X \setminus \bigcup_{\alpha} U_\alpha\right)=0.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.172556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f39cadeda0730827fe2fa29c24293d4c501d9fdf13a96f1fc7037a7e73da3b1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_TransversalityCriterion_HarmonicSpinors_4D of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let $B$ be a manifold and $\Gamma \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace B \to \mathbf{Dir}$ a smooth map.
  The following are equivalent:
