{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.036292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f39ee6280b70839d55f9e343501262f5334ada5e6ebc8a6818c06cda34dcaf72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP:OUN of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $L_\varepsilon=\varepsilon^{-\frac 12+\eta}$ and let $g$ be a real-valued, smooth, compactly supported function. Under the conditions   
\begin{align}
\textup{dist}(\supp g, \xi_j) \ge \varepsilon^{-\frac 12 +2\eta} 

\end{align}

\noindent
for every  $1 \le j \le k$,  we have 
\begin{align}
&\mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k } } \Big[ e^{i \langle v,g \rangle } e^{\frac 1\varepsilon \mathcal{E}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}( \sqrt{\varepsilon}v ) } \textup{Det}_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}(\sqrt{\varepsilon}v)  , \; A_\varepsilon, \;  \| \sqrt{\varepsilon}v\|_{L^2}<\delta_\varepsilon  \Big] \notag \\ 
