uniformly in $\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k \in [-\overline L_\varepsilon, \overline L_\varepsilon]$ and $\overline L_\varepsilon$. Here  $A_\varepsilon=\big\{ \|v \|_{L^\infty} \le K \sqrt{|\log L_\varepsilon|} \big\}$, defined in Lemmas (LEM:T1 of the paper), and $\delta_\varepsilon=\sqrt{\varepsilon \log \frac 1\varepsilon}$ in (equation LDPIN2 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.251844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3a189ea3cfa2ff4d5d052bf98d5299a015f79a255e16a71ac6d5f7e415da7e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro: refinement JSQ of arXiv:2603.14163, '\LARGE \bf Tail Bounds for Queues with Abandonment: Constant, Moderate, Large Deviations, '] Under the assumption (ass:heavy_overload of the paper), with $\gamma\leq \gamma_1$ defined in (equation eq: gamma assumption for JSQ W-p of the paper), and same notations as in Theorem (thm: JSQ Tail bound of the paper). Let $\boldsymbol{\phi}\in\mathbb{R}^n$ with $\|\boldsymbol{\phi}\|=1$ and $\boldsymbol{\phi}\geq 0$ coordinate-wise. Then, for any $a \geq e^2n\sqrt{\lambda}/\sqrt{\gamma}$, we have
