{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3a49ece1379d7ae330ec3d8abb7c75dc7c9d2606c3bcf4012eb5115efd6ea45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $\sigma=\frac{3}{4}+\gamma$ with $\gamma\in(0,\frac{1}{4})$. For any $v_0\in L_\sigma^2(\IR^2)\cap H^\sigma(\IR^2)$ and
\begin{equation}
\beta>1-2\gamma,
\end{equation} 
there exists a time $T>0$ until which there exists a unique solution
\begin{equation}
v\in\CC([0,T],L_\sigma^2(\IR^2)\cap H^\sigma(\IR^2))\cap L^2([0,T],W^{\gamma,6}(\IR^2))
\end{equation}
to the mild formulation
\begin{equation}
v_t=S_tv_0-i\int_0^tS_{t-s}v_s\cdot V_\beta*|e^Xv_s|^2\drm s
\end{equation}
where $V_\beta\in W^{\beta,1}$. Moreover, the solution depends continuously on the initial data $v_0\in L_\sigma^2(\IR^2)\cap H^\sigma(\IR^2)$. In particular, there exists a unique mild solution for $\sigma_\beta<\sigma<1$ with
\begin{equation}
\sigma_\beta=\frac{5}{4}-\frac{\beta}{2}
\end{equation}
for any $\beta>\frac{1}{2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.166673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3a60446e1a0ff87d8a70272d481af3521246111638d13720dcfd1ea192085bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:1 of arXiv:2608.30848, '\huge \bf Limit Laws of the Iterated Logarithm Under Sub-linear Expectations'] Assume that there exists a family of probability measures $\mathscr{P}$ on $(\Omega,\sigma(\mathscr{H}))$ such that the sub-linear expectation $\widehat{\mathbb E}$ satisfies ((eqexpressbyP of the paper)). Assume conditions ((eqLILmomentcondition1 of the paper)), ((eqLILmeanzerocondition of the paper)), ((eqLILmomentcondition2 of the paper)), and ((eqLILmomentcondition3 of the paper)) hold. Then for any $P\in \mathscr{P}$, we have
