{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.330598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3a8e7bf63bc55179c2538241be5cdc824c2fd4aa8b1088a0846937d3a9def12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\xi^R,\Xi^R)$ be the underlying MAP of $R$ from (\ref{ssMp_from_item_c_specific}) with respect to the norm $\|\cdot\|_1$. Then, the operator $A:\mathcal{D}\to C^2_b(\mathbb{R}\times\mathcal{S}^{d,+}_{1})$ defined by
\begin{align*}
