where $(J_\nu)_{\nu\in \mathbb{R}}$ are the Bessel functions of the first kind and $C=C(n,\alpha)>0$ is a constant depending only on $\alpha$ and $n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.274299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3c6ff1368a2e3d8166482618a8072a80c2d0f35974a6e6c9823980b015d4563","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_uniform_bound_time_Omega of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $t \in (0,\infty)$. There almost surely exist $m_0 \geq 1$ and a sequence $(C_{k,t})_k$ such that, almost surely, for any $m \geq m_0$ and any $k \geq 1$,
