{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3d91927658833338cf9eddc7e46864dfc6a5c5ce0ef8a69e5a947d19c83f7e3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Power4 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $a=(a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n)\in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfy $\sum_ka_k^2=1$. For each integer $q\geq 2$, 
