        D_{4,\lambda,\mu}' \cdot \frac{p\sqrt{\gamma}}{\log(1+\gamma p/\lambda)} & $p \in [D_{5,\lambda,\mu}/\gamma, \infty)$
    \end{subnumcases}
    Where $\delta \in(0,1/2-\alpha)$ is any small constant, and all constants independent of $p,\gamma$, with closed forms in (equation eq: D_4, lambda, mu SSQ of the paper), (equation eq: constants for Wasserstein-$p$ JSQ of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.063575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3f4ed95a20702b43a3e8321e9b69f34cd13489cf394d70fb072a24d2a0f2da2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem general_crit_behavior of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] For every $X, Y \in {\mathbb R} \setminus \{0\}$, the critical points of the function
\begin{equation} 
    \mathrm G_{X,Y}(z) = -aX \log(1+z) + bY\log z + \frac12 \left[ X(\ell+a-b-\sqrt{D}) + Y(\ell-a+b+\sqrt{D}) \right] z
\end{equation}
are
\begin{equation}  
    \mathsf{w}_c = -\frac{\frac{Y}{X}}{\frac1{\mu}+ \frac{Y}{X}} \quad \text{and} \quad   
    \mathsf{z}_c = - \frac{\ell-a+b-\sqrt{D}}{2\ell}. 
\end{equation}
Furthermore, they satisfy the following properties: 
\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
    \item If $ \frac{Y}{X}<- \frac1{\mu}$, then $\mathsf{w}_c < -1 < \mathsf{z}_c < 0$. 
    \item If $-\frac{1}{\mu}<\frac{Y}{X}<0$, then  $-1< \mathsf{z}_c < 0 < \mathsf{w}_c$.
    \item If $0< \frac{Y}{X}<\frac{1}{\mathrm m}$, then $ -1 < \mathsf{z}_c < \mathsf{w}_c < 0$. 
    \item If $\frac{Y}{X}> \frac{1}{\mathrm m}$, then $ -1 < \mathsf{w}_c < \mathsf{z}_c < 0$. 
\end{enumerate}
Furthermore, 
\begin{equation} 
    \frac{ \mathrm G_{X,Y}''(\mathsf{z}_c)}{ \mathrm G_{1,1}''(\mathsf{z}_c)} 
    = \frac{\mathrm m Y- X}{\mathrm m-1}. 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.481226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3f5583b2e2e1481c744fad8978dbf571737a5c67df68f13aebab2b1d7107401","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 14 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] There is a universal constant $C>0$,
such that for every $D\subset \C$ open, non-empty, bounded, connected and simply connected domain,
