{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.650992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3f8887bac9417bb0b99e64c24b6997b197996c62f9491058262babd376c046b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture Pure partition function- Coulomb gas integral of arXiv:2506.01306, 'Asymptotic of Coulomb gas integral, Temperley-Lieb type algebras and pure partition functi'] For irrational $\kappa \in(0,8)$, the pure partition functions are related to Coulomb gas integrals by affine meander matrix:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{J}_\beta^{(m,n)}(\boldsymbol{x})=\sum_{\alpha \in \operatorname{LP}(n,m)} \mathcal{M}_{\kappa}(\alpha, \beta) \mathcal{Z}_\alpha(\boldsymbol{x}), \quad  \beta \in \mathrm{LP}(n,m).
\end{equation}

Conversely, we have 

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{Z}_\beta(\boldsymbol{x})=\sum_{\alpha \in \operatorname{LP}(n,m)} \mathcal{M}_\kappa(\alpha, \beta)^{-1} \mathcal{J}_\alpha^{(m,n)}(\boldsymbol{x}), \quad  \beta \in \mathrm{LP}(n,m).
\end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.878813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3fd628689c3fb709f5e74b987478824595e035b26729e66c6a5159ffef523d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop CDFboundsconverge of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Under the setup of (cor:cdfbounding of the paper), we have 
