{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.313201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f3fd8909c9c24a904b30efcb7b68cce2838c5ee656ef59696a4df08f4a63083d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem WP_H^1 of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] For every $p>2$, $T>0$ and $\phi_0\in L_{\mathcal{F}_0}^{2p}(\Omega, V)$ there exists a pathwise unique solution of (eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper). Moreover $\phi$ is a Markov process in $V$ and it satisfies,  
