        &\mathbb{E}\left[ \left\| \phi(t)\right\|_V^2 + 2\int_0^t|A^{1/2 }\phi(s)|^2ds\right] =  \mathbb{E}\left[ \left\| \phi_0\right\|_V^2 \right] + \kappa t \\
        &\mathbb{E}\left[ \sup_{t\in [0, T]} \|\phi(t)\|_V^p + \left(\int_0^T |A^{1/2} \phi(t)|^2 dt\right)^{p/2}\right] \lesssim 1
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.986522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f400a686e72240ef66a6be0985ab9f59559832db0396a779468cafc0a1ec2f48","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:merge_term_asymptotics of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] If $d\geq 3\alpha$ and $\alpha<2$ then 
\begin{multline*}
\mathbb E_r \sum_{y\in \mathbb Z^d}\sum_{x\in K} \sum_{z\in K_y} \mathbbm{1}(0\nleftrightarrow y, \|x-z\| \leq r) |K||K_y| P(y)
