{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.996611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f406a726e42b1e274659c35851d0374fb7bd653b8707758e75b44576625f908e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] A $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function $K(z,w)$  defined for $z,w$ in some non-empty set $\Omega$ is said to be a positive definite
