{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.256239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f41101eb2f362a440af8f8aae21b376ed9476412fa0b9810889b14cd03ed5b34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lem:weyl2 of arXiv:2609.04092, 'Short character sums of inhomogeneous polynomials'] Let $\underline{s}=(s_1,...,s_{k-1})\in \{1,2\}^{k-1}$ where $s_i=1$ for $1\leq i \leq k-(I+1)$ and $s_i=2$ for $k-I\leq i \leq k-1$.
  Then
    \begin{align*}
          |S(\alpha)|^{2^{k-1}}\ll_n  (L_1^n L_2^n)^{2^{k-1} -1}
        (\prod_{i=1}^{k-1} L_{s_i}^n )^{-1} L_{2}^n\sum_{\substack{{\bf h}_1,...,{\bf h}_{k-1} \\ {\bf h}_i\in [-\mathbf{L}_{s_i},\mathbf{L}_{s_i}]}} \prod_{m=1}^n \min \{2L_{1},\|\alpha_{I} C(k) \Psi_m({\bf h}_1,...,{\bf h}_{k-1}) \|^{-1}\},       
