{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f41c2cd0cb22ba01d1003db3e788cafc4b1c915a7bb3321a36c5acca575ecb29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem le:high_freq_func of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $p \in [1, \infty]$, $\alpha \in \mathbf{R}$ and $\varepsilon > 0$. There exists some constant $C$ such that for any $M \geq 1$, we have
