{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.666657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f425c5dbed1bc48da6c3a9611beb015e4615f412392561b6ad633fee48796045","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 28 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $u$ be a continuous function defined on $[0,T]\times \mathbb{R}$. It is called a viscosity:\\
	\noindent (i) subsolution  of \eqref{PDE} if $u(T,x)\leq \phi(x)$, $x\in\mathbb{R}$, and at any point $(t,x)\in(0,T)\times\mathbb{R}$, for any $(p,q,X)\in\mathcal{P}^{2,+}u(t,x)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\max\bigg(u(t,x)-h'(t,x), \min\big(u(t,x)-h(t,x), -p-F(X,q,u(t,x),x,t)\big)\bigg)\leq 0;
