Hence, the scaled field under the Gibbs measure $\rho_L$ converges in distribution to white noise in the infinite volume limit. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.922681+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f43c1ee95e71db4ffd059fa8b6e7ac49539877b0095fdf0031cdb491b15c40f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop_new_QM of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, there exist constants $
	\refstepcounter{newcnstcnt}
	\ensuremath{C_{\thenewcnstcnt}}(d)>
	\refstepcounter{cnstcnt}
	\ensuremath{c_{\thecnstcnt}}(d)>0$ such that the following hold. When $3\le d\le 5$, for any $N\ge 1$, $A_1,D_1\subset  \widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{c_{\ref*{const_new_QM2}}}N)$ and $A_2,D_2\subset [\widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_new_QM1}}}N)]^c$,
		\begin{equation}
	\begin{split}
			\mathbb{P}^{D_1\cup D_2}\big( A_1\xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} A_2\big) 
			 \asymp  \mathbb{P}^{D_1}\big( A_1 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big) \mathbb{P}^{D_2}\big( A_2 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big).	
			 \end{split}
	\end{equation}
When $d=6$, for any $N\ge 1$, $A_1,D_1\subset  \widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{c_{\ref*{const_new_QM2}}}N^{1-\varsigma(N)})$ and $A_2,D_2\subset [\widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_new_QM1}}}N^{1+\varsigma(N)})]^c$,
\begin{equation}
N^{-10\varsigma(N)}	\lesssim \frac{\mathbb{P}^{D_1\cup D_2}\big( A_1\xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} A_2\big)}{\mathbb{P}^{D_1}\big( A_1 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big) \mathbb{P}^{D_2}\big( A_2 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big)}\lesssim N^{\varsigma(N)}.
\end{equation}
When $d\ge 7$, for any $N\ge 1$, $A_1,D_1\subset  \widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{c_{\ref*{const_new_QM2}}}N^{\frac{2}{d-4}})$ and $A_2,D_2\subset [\widetilde{B}(\ensuremath{C_{\ref*{const_new_QM1}}}N^{\frac{d-4}{2}})]^c$,
	\begin{equation}
	\begin{split}
			\mathbb{P}^{D_1\cup D_2}\big( A_1\xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} A_2\big)
			 \asymp  N^{6-d} \mathbb{P}^{D_1}\big( A_1 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big) \mathbb{P}^{D_2}\big( A_2 \xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(N) \big).	
			 \end{split}
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.751588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f43d95811d435efb1226dd54426809e2cdcecfcd39b2f9b01067e9d9f51dbe01","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 128 (Cutoff tails for the integrated first-chaos kernel) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Fix the projection flags
$(\epsilon_{\mathrm P},\epsilon_{\mathrm O})\in\{0,1\}^2$.  Let
$\mathcal K_{a,>\Lambda}$ denote any term in the difference between the
cutoff kernel in \eqref{eq:cubic-integrated-kernel} and its limiting kernel,
after the finite-product telescope of
\cref{lem:finite-product-cutoff}.  Put
\[
 N:=\langle\xi\rangle,
 \qquad
 L_\Lambda(N):=\max\{N,c\Lambda\},
\]
where $c>0$ depends only on the cutoff plateau and the resonant support.  For
every sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{0\le u\le t\le T}
 |\mathcal K_{a,>\Lambda}(\xi;t,u)|
 \lesssim_{T,\varepsilon}
 N^{-1+\beta_{a^\perp}}
 L_\Lambda(N)^{-1+2\beta_a+\varepsilon}.
\end{equation}
Let $0<\theta<1/2$ and assume
$2\beta_a+\theta+\varepsilon<1$.  Then
\begin{align}
 \sup_{0\le u\le t}
 |\mathcal K_{a,>\Lambda}(\xi;t',u)
  -\mathcal K_{a,>\Lambda}(\xi;t,u)|
 &\lesssim_{T,\varepsilon,\theta}
 |t'-t|^\theta
 N^{-1+\beta_{a^\perp}}
 L_\Lambda(N)^{-1+2\beta_a+\theta+\varepsilon},
 \\
 \sup_{t<u\le t'}
 |\mathcal K_{a,>\Lambda}(\xi;t',u)|
 &\lesssim_{T,\varepsilon,\theta}
 |t'-t|^\theta
 N^{-1+\beta_{a^\perp}}
 L_\Lambda(N)^{-1+2\beta_a+\theta+\varepsilon}.

\end{align}
Consequently the static and increment covariance-density differences admit
majorants
\begin{align}
 q_{a,>\Lambda}^{(1)}(t,\xi)
 &\lesssim_{T,\varepsilon}
 N^{-2+2\beta_{a^\perp}}
 L_\Lambda(N)^{-2+4\beta_a+\varepsilon},
 \\
 \frac{q_{a,>\Lambda}^{(1),\Delta}(t,t';\xi)}
 {|t-t'|^{2\theta}}
 &\lesssim_{T,\varepsilon,\theta}
 N^{-2+2\beta_{a^\perp}}
 L_\Lambda(N)^{-2+4\beta_a+2\theta+\varepsilon}.

\end{align}
The bounds are uniform over the four projection conventions.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.458029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f440d1882669d9d238f5b8484c161b45f40207075859deeb179d0d269979f171","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 34 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma \geq 1$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, $\delta \in [0, \; 1]$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}_+
