{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.312957+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4505f6bc9877bc605e9024b33fa2399058d13b6723b5caf179e455298c61361","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition l:cumuredu of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] (Cumulant reduction, [Krishnapur2007])

Assume that ${\mathcal X}$ is a simple point process on $\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying Assumption (asmpt:integrationofrhokT of the paper).  Let $Y_i={\mathcal X}(h_i), i =1,\ldots,m$ for some compactly supported \textcolor{black}{continuous} functions $h_i:\mathbb{R}^d\to \mathbb{R},  $ and $Y = (Y_1,\ldots,Y_m)$ be the corresponding random vector.   Then we have that,  

\begin{equation}

{\boldsymbol \kappa}_m[Y] = \<Q_m[(h_i(x_j))_{1\le i,j\le m}], \rho_m^T\>,  
\end{equation}
where 
\[
Q_m[(y_{i,j})_{1\le i,j\le m}]=\sum_{\tau:[m]\to [m-1]}c_{\tau} \prod_{i=1}^{m}(y_{i,\tau(i)}-y_{i,m})
\]
with $c_{\tau}=(-1)^{m-\ell(\tau)}\frac{(\ell(\tau)-1)! \ (m-\ell(\tau))!}{m! \ (m-1)!}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

