{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.640766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f451fd523ccc9657d6fb6b46eb03e2f2753b0b6aa28a936a7f918002cfbfb866","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2605.31344, 'Subcritical sharpness for real-valued spin models'] Suppose $n \geq 1$ and $\Lambda \supset \Lambda_{2n}$. Let $\mu$ be a measure on $(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{\Lambda} \times \{0, 1\}^{\overline{E}(\Lambda)}$ that satisfies weak monotonicity and \eqref{eq: zero conditioning}. Then
