{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.055025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f469a43344df3a1da961b21dbd975518f21dce60cf5b86ffa1946d8fd6fb493d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:half-normalized of arXiv:2607.13990, 'Effective Resistance in Fixed-Rank External-Field Measures\\ and Constant-Stretch Correlat'] For every fixed-rank external-field law with positive weights,
\begin{equation}
    \Sigma
\succeq
    \frac12\left(D-\frac{vv^\top}{V}\right).

\end{equation}
Equivalently, every nonzero eigenvalue of $D^{-1/2}\Sigma D^{-1/2}$ is at least $1/2$.
Since this matrix is a normalized graph Laplacian, its eigenvalues are also at most $2$, and hence
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{spec}\left(D^{-1/2}\Sigma D^{-1/2}\right)
\subseteq
    \{0\}\cup[1/2,2].

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.046206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f46bafb94668c3be3c517d8f4650ff991d193f745d284646c215ee414f90db50","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] Let $V\subseteq\bbR^n$ be an open bounded strongly regular set. Let $B$ be an open ball such that $B \supseteq \overline{V}$. Then,    
