{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.655242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f47c38d0ffe2c6fcf504a1454c32cccf07fa8d828f32685cc922d0f15a2c1d2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Error bound for the truncated expectation) of arXiv:2604.23133, 'High-Precision Framework for Expected Hitting Times Analysis in the Dice-Sum Process'] Assume there exist finite constants $L_N < U_N$ (depending on $N$ and the geometry of~$\mathcal{H}$) such that 
