for all choices of \(p_1, \ldots, p_{2^u}\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}(\O)\) with  \(m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p_i) = m\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.706609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f47eb82092d52e71ac1722f810d172068ace74039a0ba3ca4890c3fa2dc1c1f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem cA7 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] For any $q\in(0,p)$,
