{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.637984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f485ee591156ca237293d3bf93a8f53db152b2574568e8fed364cb95a16f6598","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:jackson of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Fix any $D\ge 1$. 
For any $f\in C^k([0,2\pi])$ such that $f^{(l)}(0) = f^{(l)}(2\pi)$ for all $l\le k$ and $\norm{f^{(k)}}_\infty \le M$, there exists a trigonometric polynomial $T_D$ of degree $D$ on $[0,2\pi]$ such that 
