    \end{lemenum} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.682116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f49be4480a0e1f1602abff209e5c010726a047706278a4e9d85694e63a299da1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:stochastic_intensity of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Let $\Phi$ be a simple locally finite point process and $\mathcal{F}_t$ a history of $\Phi$. If there exists a locally integrable $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process $\lambda(t)\geqslant 0$ satisfying:
  \begin{gather} 
    \E{\Phi((s,t])\;\middle|\; \mathcal{F}_s} = \E{\int_s^t \lambda(u)du \;\middle|\; \mathcal{F}_s},
  \end{gather}
then $\lambda(t)$ is called an $\mathcal{F}_t-$\emph{stochastic intensity} of $\Phi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.577309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f49fd936f24ad968ea443b1ed5b604308d1fa64daca0f4fbdb19512c08edc69d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] In addition to Assumption \ref{assumption}, suppose that 
