{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.762226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4c5bff7085bfaa40f13984252c9329f1b62960166e64e1df35fa1f218580ff8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For $\delta < \min\{\gamma/4, 1/8C_\sigma^2 T\}$, where $\gamma$ is the constant in \cref{ass: ASSUMPTIONS FROM SOJMARK SPDE PAPER APPLIED TO THE NEUROSCIENCE SETTING} \eqref{ass: ASSUMPTIONS FROM SOJMARK SPDE PAPER APPLIED TO THE NEUROSCIENCE SETTING FOUR}, and any $i = 1,\ldots, N$, there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that
