{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.748191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f506a30c862120d679a443ecca20fc0773ad2355edc1d4ae0bef13d51a7b0811","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 38 of arXiv:2609.02197, '2609.02197'] Let $\left(\alpha,U\right) \in \mathbb{R}\times \mathbb{R}_+.$ We define $$\text{\gls{pc6}}:=\left\{g \in C_U\mathscr{C}^{\max\left(\alpha,0\right)},\exists\mu\in\mathbb{R}_+,\forall\left(r,q\right)\in\left[0,U\right]^2,\left\Vert g\left(r\right)-g\left(q\right)\right\Vert_{\mathscr{C}^0}\leq\mu\left|r-q\right|^{\frac{1}{16}}\right\}$$
