{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.141861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f514689024e126bdae9f3f0712a59e2640e9d551c15e6d75d2e31cc384572ddd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:block of arXiv:2510.13572, 'Coalescence in Markov chains'] Let  $\mu\in M(\mathcal F_S)$. For a partition 
$\mathcal S = \{S_r: r\in I\}$ of $S$ with index set $I=\{1,2,\dots,\ell\}$, we call $\mu$ 
an \emph{$\mathcal S$-block measure} if
\begin{letlist}
\item
	for $f \in \text{\rm supp}(\mu)$, 
	there exists a unique permutation $\pi=\pi_f$ of $I$
	such that, for $r\in I$,  $fS_r \subseteq S_{\pi(r)}$, and
\item $k(\mu)=\ell$.
\end{letlist}
An $\mathcal S$-block measure $\mu$ is said to be \emph{trivial} if $\mathcal{S}$ is trivial.

A measure $\mu$ is
called a \emph{block measure} if it is an $\mathcal S$-block measure for some partition $\mathcal S$.\hfill $\blacktriangleleft$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.794497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f519c6a348633c90a8e7f62c55752a9d9bc3546703a27eb2832812262060f67a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:scale-exit_2 of arXiv:2608.05105, 'Cluster-Cluster model in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] Let $d\geq2$. There exist constants $A<\infty$, $q>0$, and
$\kappa<\infty$, depending only on $d,p,\alpha$, such that the following
holds for all sufficiently large $n$.

Let $t\in[\mathcal T_{n-1},\mathcal T_n)$, and let $C$ be a black cluster
with
\begin{equation*}
    |C|\in I_n=[m_n,2m_n).
\end{equation*}
Assume that there is another black cluster $D\neq C$ with
\begin{equation*}
    |D|\in I_n,
    \qquad
    \operatorname{dist}(C,D)\leq r_n.
\end{equation*}
Then, conditional on the configuration at time $t$, the cluster $C$ exits
the scale $I_n$ within time
\begin{equation*}
    Am_n^\alpha r_n^dn^\kappa
\end{equation*}
with probability at least
\begin{equation*}
    qn^{-\kappa}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.137641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f51ae451d832487e1dcb9d677aa496bc39e8d735dea10ca288dcd7e8ace1546d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Triangular tail system) of arXiv:2608.10992, '2608.10992'] Each $q_k$ is non-decreasing and continuously differentiable in $t$,
while $k\mapsto q_k(t)$ is non-increasing. Moreover, $q_1\equiv1$,
$q_k(0)=0$ for $k\geq2$, and
\begin{equation}

        q_k'
        =
        \sum_{u=1}^{k-1}q_u(q_{k-u}-q_k)+q_k(1-q_k),
        \qquad k\geq2.
\end{equation}
In particular, the marginal law of the avalanche range is uniquely determined by this triangular system.","status":"unverified"}

