{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.341081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f53e0319f72d226f2a0fe2638a3d57f713e27947892af537a8d58efe79c55745","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:solution of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] An $H$-valued continuous $({\mathcal F}_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$-adapted process $(X_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ is called a \emph{solution} to~(equation eq:model of the paper) if for its $\mathrm{d} t\otimes\mathbb{P}$-equivalence class $\widehat{X}$, we have
