{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.134516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f54baa9183f000ee3d9495788fb3750e52e098b99dbd62485fd2410b30bd3c27","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 28 (Empirical Fourier sums) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:ball-fourier-clt}, suppose that
$\eta$ is a point process with $\rho_\eta>0$. Then, for every
