{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.680415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f553671434dd7c42e122d233d7ceaa0cfa4ae56d891de95ad4a5195b980e1519","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] For $\e>0$, $x\in \R^2$ and $t>0$ fixed and for
$s\in [0,t]$ and $y\in \R^2$, set 
$$
\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)=\theta(\nabla \phi_\e \ast K^{\theta,\lambda}_{t-s})(x-y)\in\R^2.
$$
It holds that (these are equalities in $\R^2$)
\begin{equation}
\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
\partial_s \varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)+\frac1\theta(\Delta_y \varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y) -\lambda 
\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y))=0, & s\in [0,t],y \in \R^2,\\[3pt]
\varphi^\e_{t,x}(t,y)=\nabla \phi_\e(x-y),&y \in \R^2.
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation}
For all $r\geq 2$, there exists $A_{r}$ (also depending on $\theta$)
such that for all $t\geq s \geq 0$, all $y\in \R^2$,
\begin{gather}
\int_{\R^2} |\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \leq \frac{A_r}{(\e+t-s)^{\frac{3r}2-1}}
\quad \text{and} \quad 
\int_{\R^2} |\nabla_x\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \leq \frac{A_r}{(\e+t-s)^{2r-1}},\\
\int_0^t \int_{\R^2} |\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \dd s \leq \frac{A_r}{\e^{\frac{3r}2-2}}
\quad \text{and} \quad 
\int_0^t \int_{\R^2} |\nabla_x\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \dd s \leq \frac{A_r}{\e^{2r-2}},\\
\int_0^t \int_{\R^2} |\nabla_y\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \dd s \leq \frac{A_r}{\e^{2r-2}}
\quad \text{and} \quad 
\int_0^t \int_{\R^2} |\nabla_x\nabla_y\varphi^\e_{t,x}(s,y)|^r \dd x \dd s \leq \frac{A_r}{\e^{\frac{5r}2-2}}.

\end{gather}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.073629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f553edc47bccde55c926769d369e95542e318403cabc7a7f1888f91a744a965b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:deformation-discrete of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Let $\mathcal{S}$ be an $s$-embedding of $(S,(x_e)_{e\in E})$ associated to the propagator $\mathcal{Y}$. Consider the Ising model on $(S,(\hat{x}_e)_{e\in E})$, where the set of coupling constant only differ at an edge $e_0$. Using the parametrisation (equation eq:x=tan-theta of the paper), define the abstract angles $x_{e_0}=\tan \frac{\theta_0}{2} $ and $\hat{x}_{e_0}=\tan \frac{\hat{\theta}_0}{2}$. Following the identification of double covers made in Section (sub:2-point-fermion of the paper) , fix a 'south-eastern' corner $a_0^+ \in \Upsilon^\times $ such that the branching structures of the double-covers $\Upsilon^\times_{(a_0)}$ and $\Upsilon
	^{\times} $ don't coincide on $z_0$. Similarly, fix a 'north-western' corner $c_0^+ \in \Upsilon^\times $ such that the branching structures of the double-covers $\Upsilon^\times_{(c_0)}$ and $\Upsilon
	^{\times} $ don't coincide on $z_0$. Let $X^{(a_0)}_{\hat{S}}$ (respectively $X^{(c_0)}_{\hat{S}}$) the Kadanoff-Ceva fermions normalised such that $X^{(a_0)}_{\hat{S}}(a_0^+)=1$ (respectively $X^{(c_0)}_{\hat{S}}(c_0^+)=1$). Then, as long as $y_{a_0}$ and $y_{c_0}$ are chosen as in (equation eq:choice-mismatch-prefactor of the paper),(equation eq:choice-mismatch-prefactor-2 of the paper), then $\hat{\mathcal{Y}}:=\mathcal{Y}+  y_{a_0} X^{(a_0)}_{\hat{S}} + y_{c_0} X^{(c_0)}_{\hat{S}}$ is an s-embedding of $(S,(\hat{x}_e)_{e\in E}) $.	\begin{align}
	y_{a_0}& := \sin \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2} \Big(  \mathcal{Y}(a_0^+) \sin \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2} + \mathcal{Y}(c_0^+) \cos \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2}\Big) \\
	y_{c_0}&:=\sin \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2} \Big(  -\mathcal{Y}(a_0^+) \cos \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2} + \mathcal{Y}(c_0^+) \sin \frac{\hat{\theta}_0-\theta_0}{2}\Big).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.524989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f555a06489bdfc22df958cefe30fd88bc1fbf9d6ac6f8796d092fe5ab66a77a5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:lower_semi_continuity of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:lower_semi_continuity}
