{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.298923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f556a51b14e7ac86712c3111249eb2414f8fa86544a28f2bc075d27bc3eb2733","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 (High-noise reverse-path proximity) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Under Corollary~\ref{cor:reverse-path-kl}, assume
$\Tr\Cov(X_0)<\infty$, and set
\[
\gamma_t=\frac{a_t^2}{\Delta_t},
\qquad
Y_{\gamma_t}=\frac{X_t}{\sqrt{\Delta_t}}.
\]
Then, for every $T>t>0$,
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
\E_R\KL\!\left(
\mathbb Q^{R,\mathrm{rev}}_{[t,T]}
\middle\|
\mathbb P^{\mathrm{rev}}_{[t,T]}
\right)
&=\MI(R;X_t)=\MI(R;Y_{\gamma_t})\\
&\le \MI(X_0;Y_{\gamma_t})\\
&\le \frac12\log\det\!\left(\Id_d+\gamma_t\Cov(X_0)\right)\\
&\le \frac{\gamma_t}{2}\Tr\Cov(X_0).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Consequently, if $d^{-1}\Tr\Cov(X_0)\le C_0$ and
$\Delta_t\ge\Delta_0>0$, the average reverse-path KL per coordinate is at
most $C_0a_t^2/(2\Delta_0)$.  Pinsker's inequality and Jensen's inequality also
give
\begin{equation}

\E_R\left\|
\mathbb Q^{R,\mathrm{rev}}_{[t,T]}
-
\mathbb P^{\mathrm{rev}}_{[t,T]}
\right\|_{\rm TV}
\le
\sqrt{\frac{\gamma_t}{4}\Tr\Cov(X_0)}.
\end{equation}
Here
\(\|\mu-\nu\|_{\rm TV}:=\sup_B|\mu(B)-\nu(B)|
=\tfrac12\int|\dd\mu-\dd\nu|\).
The KL bound is naturally normalized by dimension.  The total-variation bound
vanishes in fixed dimension as \(a_t\to0\), and along dimension sequences for
which \(d a_t^2\to0\) on the high-noise window. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.947513+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f55c4e685052aaf7faffc589dfbcd95533878ba69ad6a305ad177a2362421089","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.24599, '\bf Perron--Frobenius theorem for a general tree-valued growth-fragmentation-isolation pro'] \begin{enumerate}
