{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.289602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f565c4454db13acd9a53c7f6daf034c3e5eaf160598f38ae1217ecf41b17a17b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop gPI-char of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The gPI constant $\alpha_{\gPI}$ defined in~(equation def:PI-LSI-con of the paper) is continuous on $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$. Moreover, we have the following alternative characterisations for any $\zeta \in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$
    \begin{align}
