{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.569578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f56c7707fcefb6f67605db26666e8b9e04a76e140298207ffe4aab1846abb839","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 (Uniqueness of the Reflection Map) of arXiv:2605.16868, '\ttl'] For a given $X\in\mathcal{D}_T(L_1)$ and $\boldsymbol{F}\in\mathcal{R}$, there exists a unique fixed point $W^*$ of the map $\pi_{X,F}$, that is,
