{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.042194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f57143a779b22e48dfc312613e5e439a4b1200222a402a946971f549a92f789e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 (The Brownian subtree may take over) of arXiv:2606.27035, 'R\'emy's diffusion on Brownian trees'] For any $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $c_\varepsilon>0$ such that if the initial tree $\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}^{\, \bullet}_0$ is $\varepsilon$-good, then with (annealed) probability at least $c_\varepsilon$, the following two events hold:
