{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.568400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f574b1f6ec6ccd5a852bc12f4fdc78ed5f1323664a869f5bd891e0d0713f1bb7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 (Uniform-in-time fixed-marginal chaos in total variation) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:concentration}, together with either kernel assumption, for fixed $k$ and $N\ge2k$,
