{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f57d4cca5348f9f3177c3af2096986fa1afb0ea9be4c79609660eac0293de481","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem-cvg-RFIM-partition-function of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$, $a,b \in \partial D$ and $(D_{\delta};a_{\delta},b_{\delta})_{\delta}$ be as in Section (sec_assumptions_domain of the paper). Let $\lambda: \bar D \to (0,\infty)$ be a bounded and continuous function. Let $(H_{x})_{x \in \mathbb{Z}^2}$ be independent Gaussian random variables with mean $0$ and variance $1$ and set, for $x \in D_{\delta}$, $h_x = H_{x/\delta}$. Let $\xi \in \{-,\pm,+\}$.  Then, the rescaled partition function
    \begin{equation} 
        \tilde{\mathcal{Z}}_{\delta}^{\xi,\lambda, h}:= \exp\big(-\frac{\|\lambda\|_{L^{2}}^2}{2}\delta^{-\frac{1}{4}}\big) \mu_{\delta}^{\xi}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\delta^{\frac{7}{8}}\sum_{x \in D_{\delta}}\lambda(x)h_{x}\sigma_{x}\bigg)\bigg]
    \end{equation}
    converges in distribution as $\delta \to 0$ to a random variable $\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda}$ with Wiener chaos expansion
    \begin{equation} 
