{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f57fd47cb63fd8a0feb0ae00daeb284cd586d9686e63def97d5678b5065e1bab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition largeDeviation of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Fix $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $e\in S^{d-1}$. Let $\lambda_e>0$ be the minimizer in (equation eq:prelimCriticalSpeed of the paper), and recall that $\zeta_e = \lambda_e e$. Let $(Y_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution of (equation eq:SDETiling2.0 of the paper) under the measure $\mathbb{P}_x^{\zeta_e}$. Let $\hat{Y}_t:=(1/t)e\cdot(Y_t-Y_0)$. Let $I_e:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow (-\infty,+\infty]$ be the function defined by
    \begin{equation}
        I_e(\lambda)=\sup_{\eta \in \mathbb{R}} \{ \eta \lambda - [\gamma((\lambda_e+\eta)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]\}=[\gamma((\lambda_{e}+\cdot)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]^{*}(\lambda).
    \end{equation}
    For a set $A\subset \mathbb{R}$, let $I_e(A):=\inf_{\lambda\in A}I_e(\lambda)$. The following holds:
