{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.240971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f58f80db61432f9e6fe907788f70acfbda60a4bc8562c3e78e82c644d9656cf0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:L2_strato of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Suppose that $h \in L^2(\Omega \times Y \times [0,T])$ and $\mathbf{D} h \in L^2(\Omega \times Y \times [0,T]^2)$, and that there exist processes $\mathbf{D}^+ h, \mathbf{D}^- h \in L^2(\Omega \times Y \times [0,T])$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} \int_Y \int_0^T
\sup_{\substack{s < u < T \\ |u-s| \le 1/n}}
\mathbb{E}\!\left[ \big| \mathbf{D}_s h(y,u) - (\mathbf{D}^{+} h)(y,s) \big|^2 \right]
ds\, \nu(dy) &= 0, \\
\lim_{n \to \infty} \int_Y \int_0^T
\sup_{\substack{0 < u < s \\ |s-u| \le 1/n}}
\mathbb{E}\!\left[ \big| \mathbf{D}_s h(y,u) - (\mathbf{D}^{-} h)(y,s) \big|^2 \right]
ds\, \nu(dy) &= 0.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Then, the Stratonovich integral $\int_0^T h(y,s)\circ dW_s$ is well-defined in $L^2(\Omega \times Y)$ as the limit of the Riemann sums $S^\pi(s \mapsto h(\cdot,s))$ as $|\pi| \to 0$.","status":"unverified"}

