{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.828629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bb7762a19b87d55f589bf3f6c2570782798f0d41a78d349fcb8da7d2a9621b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:hoffman-exact of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $z_1,\ldots,z_n\in\mathbb{R}^d$ be increments and let $X^{\rm PL}$ be the piecewise-linear path that traverses the increment $z_a$ on the $a$-th segment. Then
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}(X^{\rm PL})_{0,T}
=\exp_{\otimes}(z_1)\otimes\cdots\otimes\exp_{\otimes}(z_n)
=\Phi\big(\mathrm{Sig}^{\rm sum}(z_1,\ldots,z_n)\big),

\end{equation}
where $\Phi$ is Hoffman's exponential from the quasi-shuffle character to the shuffle character. Thus the Hoffman step has no discretization error; it is an algebraic identity.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.704383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bbb42a401216abe4ec22945bd21d839bf1f52d84762f48a56f06c1c5108360","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.02711, 'Differentiability of the Leading Lyapunov Exponent \\ of a linear differential equation wi'] Assume that Hypothesis~\ref{hyp:un} is satisfied and that for a
