{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.190543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bbfafe0d7d6c47c4468ea902878c90f9184242a4533c9e4031793919bc5eba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exist $\Cl,\Cl,\Cl,\cl >0$ such that for any $v\neq v'\in \widetilde{B}(\Cref{const_additional_lemma_two_arm0})$ and any sufficiently large $N\ge 1$,
