{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.334185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bbfccbe92ecd6115499ef8e4309500be2f9dcad49b297b8835b3324f33412b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor-core-lemma-alpha>=2 of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Given $\alpha \geq 2$, define 
    \begin{align*}
        &\mathfrak T_{\mathsf{crit}}= \left\{ (M,\delta):(M,\delta) \mbox{ satisfying } (equation eq-assum-lem-2.4 of the paper) \right\} \,; \\
        &\mathfrak T_{\mathsf{unique}} = \Big\{ (M,\delta) \in\mathfrak T_{\mathsf{crit}}: (\log\log n)^{-300-2\alpha} < \tfrac{\delta^{-1}}{\log n} < (\log\log n)^{300+2\alpha} \Big\}\,;  \\
        &\mathfrak T_{\mathsf{mult}} = \Big\{ (M,\delta) \in\mathfrak T_{\mathsf{crit}}: (\log\log n)^{-300-2\alpha} < \tfrac{\delta^{-1}}{(\log n)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}}} < (\log\log n)^{300+2\alpha} \Big\} \,.
