{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.060071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ed2aec5e936c75d1b9b00aa94009821acb32458f06e6776d7d0e132c2aa8da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:simplified-left-kernel of arXiv:2606.19507, 'The $t$-Split Two-Periodic Aztec Diamond Model'] For $m,\,m' < tN$, the correlation kernel of the $t$-split model can be written as
    \begin{multline} 
        \left[\mathbb{K}_N(4m',2\xi'+j;4m,2\xi+i)\right]_{i,j=0,1} = \frac{\1_{m\leq m'}}{2\pi \mathrm{i}} \oint_{\gamma_{0,1}}\frac{\mathrm{d}z}{z} z^{\xi'-\xi}\Phi_{\alpha}(z)^{m-m'} \\
        -\frac{1}{(2\pi\mathrm{i})^2}\oint_{\gamma_1}\mathrm{d}w\oint_{\gamma_{0,1}} \frac{\mathrm{d}z}{z(z-w)}\frac{w^{\xi'+N}(z-1)^N}{z^{\xi+N}(w-1)^N}r_{\alpha,2}(w)^{tN-m'}r_{\beta,2}(w)^{(1/2-t)N} \\
        \times c(w) F_{\alpha,2}(w) F_{\beta,2}(w) \Phi_{\beta}(z)^{(t-1/2)N} \Phi_{\alpha}(z)^{m-tN}.
    \end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.834724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5eecca74016bdfc8ccabc5aedef2b0e66f015608db33d334dc7f01bca0483a6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.13359, 'Fractional moments of the Stochastic Heat Flow and\\2D Directed Polymers'] Let \(Z\geq0\) satisfy \(\EE[Z]=1\).
