{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.833540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5ffc7a5d93049bd0de432755385756e6518c149cd8dcec91a90c2fd4fcb7b32","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 36 (Minimal informative window equals exact depth under global coordinate-rank loss) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}, and let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block. Assume:
