{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.997882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f652573ef0d2f176356a7546a2d80e3532aa10d909c3b74873e3f9b0350cad75","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 20 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] With $t,T$ be such that $T^{-1}+tT>0$, the function $F\in\mathcal{HP}_{T,t}$ if and only if the $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued
