{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.364834+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f666098c23e7d7aaf4f08925c460678c549b0db51d7502b86de0c2a250902a57","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:TV-llr of arXiv:2601.07045, 'From Continuous to Discrete: \\ a No-U-Turn Sampler for Permutations'] Let $p$ and $q$ be probability mass functions on a finite set $\mathcal{I}$ such that
\[
  e^{-\varepsilon}
  \;\le\;
  \frac{q(t)}{p(t)}
  \;\le\;
  e^{\varepsilon}
  \qquad
  \text{for all }t\in\mathcal{I}
\]
for some $\varepsilon\ge0$.
Then
\[
  \TV(p,q) \;\le\; \tanh\!\bigl(\varepsilon/2\bigr).
\]","status":"unverified"}

