{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.480895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f66ba74283ccf2b37ca67fb43270d7b6d8b4fed6fc6e06796eef3ff39d673a1a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 42 ($2$ shift operator) of arXiv:2604.04267, 'On Sharpest Tail Bounds for Functions \\ of Tail Bounded Random Variables'] The $2$ shift operator $\mathscr{S}_2$ is defined as
\begin{align*}
   \mathscr{S}_2: (f,G,c) \mapsto (X_1,...,X_n)
\end{align*} 
where $f = \big((f_1^-,f_1^+),...,(f_n^-,f_n^+)\big) \in \mathcal{B}_2^n, \ G \ni 0$ and is closed, $c=(c_1,...,c_n) \in [0,\infty]^n$, and for $k=1,...,n$, 
