{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.784610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f676c34b9100f451d57706f4c45bca3145e260200579d237ba8d4b128239cb9c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem stationary-plus-bc-stationary-mixing of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Consider the Ising model with $+$ boundary conditions on a centered box of side-length $r$, denoted $\Lambda_r \subset \mathbb Z^d$. There exists $C(d)>0, \beta_0(d)<\infty$, such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, one has  
