{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.972894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f69125bc53f072b795c29c778ce1bce33e202abd749a72c3b772fc2cf56ca42c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (\cite{GS18}, Corollary 2.3) of arXiv:2606.10336, 'From Pitman's local times representation to the Gorin-Shkolnikov identity and beyond'] Let $\{e(t)\}_{0 \le t \le 1}$ be a Brownian excursion on $[0,1]$
and $\{l_x\}_{x \ge 0}$ be local times process\footnote{Here $\ell_y$ is the local times of $\{e(t)\}_{0 \le t \le 1}$ at level $y \ge 0$. See e.g., \cite[Chapter VI]{RY} for background.}.
