{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.282020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f69e05ded73e3395e22b76ffc4c87530c9ccd5c691aac5de78af500ba2e8496c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] (\cite[Lemma 3.10]{Hairer-Li})Let \(p\ge 2\) and \(\alpha>\frac{1}{2}\). Assume that \(x_{\cdot}\in \mathcal{B}_{\alpha,p}\), let \(f\in \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa,\gamma}\)(deterministic) for some \(\kappa, \gamma\) such that \(\eta=H-\kappa>\frac{1}{2}\) and \(\bar \eta=H-\kappa+\gamma\alpha\) and define
