{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6ded2f4378411ff4efb37d0b32d3be37cc7ca83d928869aa26733c4674dd247","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cross-area-affine of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For a multivariate exponential Hawkes process with common decay, $\mathbb{E}[A_T^{12}]$ is a coordinate of the affine expected-signature closure in (prop:affine-sig of the paper). Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
