and the vector of moments $\mathbb{E}[N^i_s\lambda^j_s]$ closes linearly after adjoining the Hawkes memory variables.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.344395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6e0fba8d36273c78f8a5bf89b2654701c3ff31118f9797c2b5d2605e179008c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eqNullset of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] The measure space $ (\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mu) $ is called complete (and $ \mu $ is said to be complete on $ \mathcal{F} $), if $ \mathcal{F} $ includes all subsets of null sets, i.e., 
    \begin{align}

        \mathcal{N} = \{ G \subset \Omega \mid  G \subset E \text{ for some $ \mu $-null set } G \} \subset \mathcal{F}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.767238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6e10133cbc84eef0f423adb43d9f2d246c7ce28cc0b314469459a758944309c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.26803, 'On bubbling of Fueter maps'] The incidence locus 
  \begin{equation*}
    \cI_n \coloneq \{ (f, \bx) \in \cB \times \cC_n \, | \, f(x_j) \in Z \text{ and } T_{x_j}f(v) \in T_{f(x_j)}Z \text{ for all } j\}
  \end{equation*}
  is a $C^1$ Banach submanifold of $\cB \times \cC_n$ of codimension $4n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.639478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6e3acdf36b055a1891a9706114c9de59ff3b38129a064af7faa4b5b808642e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 of arXiv:2506.17979, '\large\bf A remark on subharmonicity for symmetric Dirichlet forms'] If $u\in  D(\mathscr{E})^{\diamond}_{e,\loc}$ satisfies \eqref{eq:2.3}, 
then for $U\Subset D$
