{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.343148+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6f6bbbcdd5f47b8fb6b123bb66a9fec90285b769e4e20fac04c5169e76581ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Let $K'$ be a graph over $V$. Then:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item if $K \subseteq K'$, then $w_K \leq w_{K'}$;
        \item if $|K \Delta K'| \leq \eps |V|$ for some $\eps > 0$, then there exists $\mc{A} \subseteq V$ such that $|\mc{A}| \leq 2 \sqrt{\eps} |V|$ and, for $v \notin \mc{A}$, $|w_K(v) - w_{K'}(v)| \leq 2\sqrt{\eps}$.
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.592457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6fc6d903ec00f21064a3107ace114f706142b75b1d8355b9b583fb632142aef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-bound-UL-J4 of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] For any  $\varepsilon \in [0,\frac{1}{2}]$, there exists a constant $c=c_{\varepsilon}>0$ 
such that for any $n\geqslant 1$ and $x\in \bb R$,
\begin{align} 
J_4  \leqslant \frac{V(x) L\left(\frac{x}{\sigma\sqrt{n}} \right) }{\sigma\sqrt{n}}  \left( 1+ c n^{-\varepsilon} \log n  \right). 
\end{align}
Moreover, choosing $\varepsilon = \frac{\delta}{4(3+\delta)} < \frac{1}{4}$,  
we have that there exists a constant $c>0$ such that for any $n\geqslant 1$ and $x\in \bb R$,
\begin{align} 
J_4 \geqslant 
 \frac{V(x) L\left(\frac{x}{\sigma\sqrt{n}} \right) }{\sigma\sqrt{n}} 
\left( 1- c n^{- \frac{\delta}{4(3+\delta)}} \log n  \right)
- \frac{c}{n^{\frac{1}{2}+ \frac{\delta}{4}}  }. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.551185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6fde9180d22caadf1fcf83ca249bf4c1c45ac7ec025be4e9174d1b11e8df78e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Let $\varphi \in C^{4}((\S^{d-1})^{n}).$ There exists a constant $C>0$ such that 
