{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.939452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f705b44085fb3027b3432ed7ed37fb8891bfc35c66ce27a92b247129f90fe561","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] [Variational formula for entropy] 

      Let $(\Omega, \mathcal{F},\mu)$ be a probability space, and let $f : \Omega \rightarrow (0,\infty) $ be a $\mu$--integrable function such that $\int_{\Omega} f \dd \mu = 1.$ Then 
      \begin{displaymath}
          \Ent_{ \mu } (f) = \sup_{g} \Big\{ \int f g \dd \mu - \log \Big( \int e^{g} \dd \mu \Big) \Big\}
      \end{displaymath}
      where the supremum is taken over measurable and bounded functions $g : \Omega \rightarrow \R.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.795005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f70654b63c190c0f5e78a0f9a5ddff6f0c429a87fa23d44a505f2d82b314e766","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2605.18198, 'Large deviations of crowding in finite $\beta$-ensembles'] Let $Q\in C^{1,1}_{loc}(\R^2)$ and $\mu_Q$ be the corresponding weighted equllibrium measure. Then there exists a positive constant $C_2$ such that  
  	\[
  	\mu_Q(A)\le C_2m(A), \mbox{ for all $A\subset \mathbb C$}
  	\]
  	where $m$ is the Lebesgue measure on the complex plane.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.762709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f707b80607f02268f1b571a6153f3968bb0e52f72f1de028fbcc011c45bc9bdf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.02541, 'The hockey-stick conjecture for\\ activated random walk'] \thlabel{lem:min.bounds}
      Let $\sigma$ consist of $\ceil{\rho n}$ active particles placed independently
      and uniformly at random on $\ii{1,n}$ for $\rho\in(0,\rho_{\mathtt{FE}}]$.
      Let $\rho'\leq\rho$, and
      let $\mathfrak{m}$ be the minimal odometer of $\mathcal{O}_{n+1}(\mathsf{Instr},\sigma,u_0,f_0)$
      with $u_0=0$ and $f_0=-\floor{(\rho-\rho')n/2}$.
      For any $j\in\ii{1,n+1}$ and $\delta>0$,
      \begin{align*}
        \mathbf{P}\Biggl(\rt{\mathfrak{m}}{j} \geq  \frac{(\rho-\rho')jn - \rho j^2}{2}  -\delta n^2\Biggr)
        \geq 1- Ce^{-cn}
      \end{align*}
      for constants $c,C>0$ that depend only on $\delta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.793738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f708778545930e1031f7025206ddf43f933618b6ceba3e8dc33db73a0e3af60d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:harmonic-grad of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Under (lem:tailrl-regularity of the paper), for every $T\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_\theta J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}^{(T)}(\theta;x)
=
