{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.092651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f71aa27b11da4336d3c0594a109630ef30e0696f51f940491eef1f444c05c822","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem prop:Q:mathcal:N of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix a   continuous function $h:\mathbb{R}_+\to \mathbb{R}_+$ satisfying  $\sigma_h \in(0, \infty)$, with $h(0) = h(\sigma_h) = 0$ and set  $h_{\sigma_h \shortminus \hspace{0,2mm}  \mathpalette\mathpalette\bigcdot@{.5}@{.5}}:= (h((\sigma_h - t)\vee 0) : t\geq 0)$. The following properties hold: 
