{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.578271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7387e4bcb18ca33c0f91af3c499dd91ed242346bb1a3c4f52a1e9f96acc57d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb$, $f\in \Sob^k(\Rbb^n,\gamma_n)$ with $\left\|f\right\|_{\Leb^\infty}\leq 1$, and $1\leq q\leq p\leq 2$,
\begin{equation}
    \frac{\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^p}^{p}}{\big[1+\frac{q}{2k(2-q)} \ln^{+}(\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^p}^{p}/\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^q}^{2})\big]^{kp/2}} \geq C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Lp-Lq-Gaussian}}}(p,q)^k \Wop^{\geq k}(f),
\end{equation}
and further,
