with $C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Lp-Lq-Gaussian}}}(p,q) = C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Lp-Lq-energy-Boolean}}}(p,q) \gtrsim 2-q$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:12.369631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7404f2e08b37fc38dbfc92f408cb3657196d38dba85cde544714e441afc611d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2607.04467, 'Bernstein Functions at Work: Coalescents, Copulas, and Subordination' (problem environment labelled prob:townes).] For \(\eta=10^{-4}\), set
