{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.360539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f74d37266af1c0036ae5ac3712f3aa609bcadfe630f25c77d3275ed9ee9ee1e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Comparison theorem for thresholds SDEs) of arXiv:2604.21389, 'Existence and uniqueness for \\ singular stochastic differential equations \\ with piecewi'] Let $X^{(1)}, X^{(2)}$ be two non-explosive weak solutions to the following SDEs with respect to the same Brownian motion $B$, on the same probability space: for $i\in \{1,2\}$
