{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.813004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f76f475abb668a4004369c6defed28cc9c5f50455f76f76d4ef01899e22bed53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor: technical on graphs of arXiv:2512.18435, 'Indistinguishability for recurrent clusters'] Let $G$ be a Cayley graph of a finitely generated group $\Gamma$, $\eta$ an invariant labelling of $G$ and $\omega$ an $\eta$-measurable percolation process such that $(\eta,\omega)$ is jointly $\Gamma$-invariant.

