{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.328481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f788f8fecca6f9c172d364239eefdf4a7513f1cc593fd534f475e11ce3b6827f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CAF of arXiv:2411.06571, 'Moment-based approach for two erratic KPZ scaling limits'] Let $\mathbf E_{\mathrm{BM}}^x$ denote expectation with respect to a standard Brownian motion on $\Bbb R$, started from $x\in\Bbb R$. There exists some universal constant $C>0$, such that uniformly over all smooth functions $\phi\ge 0$ with $\int_{\Bbb R} \phi =1,$ and all $s,t ,q\ge 0$, one has 
