{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.709252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f79088fb294cfe8e11723eb9b25fae5b0cabf0d420a1b6e27cb14420d7137069","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thrm:path of arXiv:2411.18749, 'A star is born: Explosive Crump--Mode--Jagers branching processes'] Recall $\mu_n^w$ from~(equation eq:mu of the paper). If, for some $c>1$ and all $w\geq 0$, we have 
