{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.061943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f796e5205df6885206220f881d81b9a32185596cdb608aecec67949c4436a705","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:zxk-ineq of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $x \in \mathbb Z^d, 1 \leqslant k \leqslant N$ and $n \in \mathbb N^*$ as well as $\beta \in \mathbb R_+^*$. Let $l_0 \in \llbracket 1, M \rrbracket$ such that for all $s, t \in \llbracket 1, N \rrbracket$ we have $(\zeta(s, t) \geqslant 1) \wedge (s \geqslant k) \implies \zeta(s, t) \geqslant l_0$. Then
