{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.252272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f79a27f3ff4b41ebef32ab58d7b6727ed4e03bda1511e7aada1c8daf6b03b3e9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let $ x,y\in X $, $t\in\RR$, 
