{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.304099+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7a348ee3236ac840d5c5a0c7d8d5541588ab8f96ab0c02d34194c2eeb93ae8c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition space of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] Let $(V, \|\cdot \|_V)$ be a Banach space.
For any $T>0$ and $0<\gamma \leq 1$ we set
\begin{align*}
	 |f|_{\gamma,V}:=& \sup_{0 \leq s <t \leq T} \frac {\|{\delta f}_{t,s}\|_V}{|t-s|^\gamma }, ~~f\in C([0,T];V),\\
	 \|f\|_{\gamma,V}:=& \sup_{0 \leq s <t \leq T} \frac {\|{\hat{\delta} f}_{t,s}\|_V}{|t-s|^\gamma }, ~~f\in  C([0,T];V), \\
	 |g|_{\gamma,V}:=& \sup_{0 \leq s <t \leq T} \frac {\|g_{t,s}\|_V}{|t-s|^\gamma }, ~~g\in C_2(V).
\end{align*}
Next we define the spaces as follows
\begin{align*}
	& C^\gamma ([0,T];V):=\{ f \in C([0,T];V) : |f|_{\gamma,V} < \infty \},\\
    & \hat{C}^\gamma ([0,T];V):=\{ f \in C([0,T];V) : \|f\|_{\gamma,V} < \infty \}, \\
	&  C_2^\gamma ([0,T];V):=\{ g \in C_2(V) : |g|_{\gamma,V} < \infty \}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.981446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7a6784cd565ea9c03586a0174d63dfacc53b82a86ef61d510c370f55b27054b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] Fix \(R<\infty\).  There exist smooth functions \(c_2,c_3\) on
\([0,R]\) and a function \(\mathcal R_{\mathrm{end}}\) such that, with
