{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7c1a30130e3da3727c8cd5b99f8ba0af7b9ea6690e6491298d490ca38ed7775","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Markov property) of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Suppose that~$x_1,\dots,x_m\in\T_n$ are vertices such that the subtrees $\T^{(1)},\dots,\T^{(m)}$ of~$\T_n$ rooted at these vertices are vertex-disjoint. Write~$n_i$ for the depth of~$\T^{(i)}$ and denote
