{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.598882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7de8a76891ba09e05de6b0a8128ff5564bd94bc4e120069a664db3e64934b7b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dcm-matrix-form of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] An MMPP is DCM if and only if $v^*\preceq x\preceq y$ implies that, for all $t>0$, 
