{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.635804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7e8125f9f2047df8a89241d6d5ba611b2579839a74c4d2a7b6aef3520eb44f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:allbutone of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] Let $a,\delta>0$ and let $J$ be a kernel such that
    if $j$ is sufficiently large then $J(e) \geq (a+\delta) L\log(j)L^{-2j}$  for every edge $e$ with $|e|=L^j$. Then there exists $k_0 = k_0(\delta, L) < \infty$ such that for all $k \geq k_0$ there exists $N =N(k,J)$ and $C=C(k,J)$ such that
