 for all $n \geq N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.428064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7e900ce265d1f5189335e1cd7155cf9a19026458cfc4fa6c29d909933b8e47c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def_ALKYUtility of arXiv:2411.16464, 'Generating social networks with static and dynamic utility-maximization approaches'] We consider the set $\mathcal{U}^{\text{ALKY}}_I$ of applications $U : [0,1)^{I-1} \times (\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})^{I-1} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$:
\begin{equation*}
