\mathcal{U}^{\text{ALKY}}_I = \left\{\kappa>1, \gamma>1, \delta>1, \right. \\ U\left(\alpha, c \right)= \left. \sum^{I-1}_{j=1} \left[ \kappa \alpha_{j} c_{j} - \frac{\alpha_{j}^{\gamma}}{1-\alpha_{j}^{\gamma}} \right] - \left( \sum^{I-1}_{j=1} \alpha_{j} \right)^{\delta}\right\}    
\end{split}
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.372694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7eaa9a3335509c56ec3afdc5a15d6ba203d9f533ed1a3af9af900921cee71bb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Large increment correlation bound) of arXiv:2606.04179, 'Functional Scaling Limits of Interpolated Correlated Random Walks in Hölder Topology'] Let \(\interpF_t^n\) be the interpolated random walk defined in \eqref{eq:
