{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.711425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f81ae97084d9b8079444b308212727e255f35d99f77d4ed0a6c1b1a703acc7c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mix of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under (main_assm of the paper), given any $k\in[\![{1,DN}]\!]$, suppose there exists a constant $\varepsilon_A>0$ such that
