{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.024420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f81f3e7f2e6a1ced342cc1359ecd68ba62ceb31924e842d28ce11dfff5b61944","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (\citeauthor{D65}, \citeyear{D65}, \S6.10) of arXiv:2606.06739, 'The relationship between the transition functions of the labeled and unlabeled versions of'] Let $E$ and $E_0$ be complete separable metric spaces, and let $\Phi:E\mapsto E_0$ be Borel measurable and surjective.  Let $P(t,x,\cdot)$ be the transition function for a Markov process $X$ in $E$. If for each $t>0$ the condition 
