{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.665253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f842b8ebd5e03f77e081503be2e51b59335b8027b7813ecdb247e031f4c7b9de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $\xi,g$ satisfy (H1) and (H3). Assume that $(Y,Z,A,A')$ solves
