with respect to ${\mathcal P}$ in $D([0,1])$, where on the right-hand side the process $\mathcal{Z}_{\alpha}$ is as in (equation eq:calZ of the paper) and independent from ${\mathcal P}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.845756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85a38b1911bdb7c68e1ef0cc1f17ad494225229245548ab92828b249d03c733","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: increasing sequence of stopping times of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Given a stopping time $T$, there exist stopping times $\setc{T_k}{k \geq 0}$ such that $T_k \uparrow T$ as $k \to \infty$ almost surely and the following properties hold surely for each $k \geq 1$.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(a)] There exists a constant $K \geq 0$ such that $T_k \leq K$.

		\item[(b)] There exists $\eta \in (0, \kappa)$ such that $a_i \wedge T_k - a_{i - 1} \wedge T_k \leq \eta$ for all $i \geq 1$.

		\item[(c)] There exists a compact set $(0, 0) \in C \subset U_g$ such that
		\begin{equation*}
			\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(t), \boldsymbol{y}_i(t)\right) \in C \quad \text{for all} \quad 1 - M \leq i \leq \mathcal{R}\left(T_k\right) \quad \text{and} \quad t \in [0, T_k].
		\end{equation*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.318309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85a7796d91b143964d724ecf56cba4c92387d1eecb95b42c1f872ee49007bb1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Full-path tube closure) of arXiv:2608.30261, 'Estimating Population-Risk Curves Along Nonconvex Gradient Flows from the Training Sample'] \label[lemma]{lem:full-path-tube}
Under \cref{ass:tube}, for every $i\in[n]$ and $\lambda\in\Lambda$ the deleted flow
$\theta_{-i,t}^\lambda$ and the response $d_{i,t}^\lambda$ exist uniquely on
$[0,T]$.
Moreover, for $0\leq t\leq T$,
\begin{equation}
 \max\{\|\theta_{-i,t}^\lambda-\theta_t^\lambda\|,\|d_{i,t}^\lambda\|\}
 \leq(n-1)^{-1}M\phi_\kappa(t)<r_{\rm tube}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, at each time $t$, the line segments joining any two of
$\theta_t^\lambda$, $\theta_{-i,t}^\lambda$, and
$\theta_t^\lambda+d_{i,t}^\lambda$ are contained in
$B(\theta_t^\lambda,r_{\rm tube})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.780238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85b80cfe3a00c8203982e01080c8652d5e6f828971bb9211b4cca249869bf80","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 5 of arXiv:2609.02261, 'Quantization and process'] i)  Let $F\in C^{\infty }(\R^{2n})$
   satisfying for all    multi-indices  $(\alpha , \beta)\in(\N^n)^2$,

