{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.787858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85c89663099d713135504d67e02f1ee85b4476e0cc3ca1e322019afe2a5c364","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tailrl-threshold-reparameterization of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Define
\begin{equation}
F_w(t)
:=
\int_0^t w(s)\,ds,
\qquad
\widetilde r(x,z):=F_w\!\left(r(x,z)\right).

\end{equation}
Then $F_w$ is a strictly increasing map from $[0,1]$ to $[0,1]$, and
\begin{equation}
J_w(\theta;x)
=
\int_0^1
\log
\Pr_{z\sim\pi_\theta(\cdot\mid x)}
\!\left(\widetilde r(x,z)>u\right)
\,du.

\end{equation}
Thus, weighted TailRL on $r$ is exactly uniform TailRL on the monotone rescaling $\widetilde r=F_w(r)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.964878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85e3279c3de5270b9ff2356d99101308e7235323616bbfd9ad91c00724e4c83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2607.28614, 'Tampered Memory Elephant Random Walk on one-dimensional integer lattice'] Let $S_n$ be a TMERW. Assume that $\DD$ is a collection of nested sequences having an underlying renewal structure, that is,  
