		$C$ is a positive constant depending only on $p,b,\delta$ and $\|\mu\|_0:=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.992583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8753164bd6fd908e40a83ba4653dcf6e1d593daceb265cb88c3e3344f4c04b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 119 (Lemma \ref{L:TVgap}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Assume $\omega$ is such that $\cC_1(p_0) \subseteq \cC_1(p_1)$. Denote by $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ the laws of $\ClCp{1}{p_0}$ and $\cT_{p_1 \mid p_0}$, respectively. Then
