{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f894f80b1ef183a024038e3f7d942119d4ab4e6aac77b0072ea752ac51fb30d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Define the \textbf{patched last passage times} $\Tpat$ on $(R_n)^2_{\uparrow}$ of length $N^{3/2}$ via a maximization procedure over the last passage times on the restricted rectangles. More precisely, we take $\Tpat_{u,v}$ when $u,v \in R_{n}^{i}$ for some $i\in \lbr n\rbr$ as in \eqref{def:PatchedShort}. For all $u,v \in R_n$ such that $u \in R_n^{i}$ and $v \in R_n^{j}$ with  $1\leq i<j \leq n$, we proceed by induction as in Definition~\ref{def:PatchedDLExt}. When $j=i+1$, 
\begin{equation}
\Tpat_{u,v} :=   \sup_{w\in \partial \bar{R}_n^{i}} \big(\Tpat_{u,w} +  \Tpat_{w,v}\big).   
\end{equation} 
When $k=j-i>1$, suppose that the patched last passage times have been defined for all $i^{\prime},j^{\prime}<k$, and set
\begin{equation}
\Tpat_{u,v} :=   \sup_{w\in \partial \bar{R}_n^{j-1}} \big(\Tpat_{u,w} +  \Tpat_{w,v}\big).   
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.492026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f89cc8d06ef1bb979b79107618b4ca336b2b3f79558b62c9e85089c9848b6d76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 28 (\cite{spencer2007birth}*{Theorem~3.1(2)}) of arXiv:2509.09589, 'Geometry of critical discrete structures: long-range percolation on the hierarchical latti'] Suppose $c_0, c_1, c_2$, and $t$ are positive numbers with $t c_0>1$.
Let $H_n$, $n\geq 1$, be graphs (we view $H_n$ as the seed graph) with $|H_n| = n$ satisfying the following for all $n$:
\begin{enumeratei}
\item 
$n^{-1}\sum |\cC|^2 \geq c_0$, where the sum is over all connected components $\cC$ of $H_n$, and
\item 
$n^{-1}\#\big\{
v\in V(H_n)\, :\, | \cC( v; H_n ) | \geq s 
\big\}
\leq 
c_1 \exp(-c_2 s)$
for all $s\in\bZ_{>0}$.
\end{enumeratei}
Place edges with probability $t/n$ independently between all $u\neq v\in V(H_n)$ such that $\{u, v\}\notin E(H_n)$;
let $E_n^+$ denote the set of edges thus created.
Let $\cC_{\max}^+$ denote the largest component of the graph $(V(H_n), E(H_n)\cup E_n^+)$.
Then there exists $a_0>0$ depending only on $c_0, c_1, c_2$, and $t$ such that 
$ | \cC_{\max}^+ | \geq a_0 n $ whp. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.875380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f89e60428e275221b8bfa26df96acbf9bb37928e9b7700ac4bb9d774e2f49856","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem genbb of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $P,Q$ be distinct plaques, with separating sides $g_P\subset\partial P$ and $g_Q\subset\partial Q$ oriented parallel.  The change of canonical snake basis of $g_P$ to that of a side $g_Q^\prime$ of $Q$ is given by a matrix 
\begin{equation}
 T\bigl(t_\rho(Q)\bigr)^{\delta}
 \;\Sigma_\rho(g_Q,g_P)\;
 E\bigl(e_\rho(P,Q)\bigr),
 \qquad \delta\in\{+1,-1\},
\end{equation}
where $\Sigma_\rho(g_Q,g_P)$ is a slithering map.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.318378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f89ec28b68ce877810eb1c62b6764af4a23d07ed87f53b0caa8fcc392fc9883a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be any homomorphism of compact Lie groups. Then $\alpha^*\colon\cat{$\bm{G'}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}\to\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}$ sends $G'$-global ${\mathcal{F}}$-weak equivalences to $G$-global ${\mathcal{F}}$-weak equivalences.
    \begin{proof}
        In light of Lemma~(lemma:restr-right-Quillen of the paper), it suffices to consider the case of $G'$-global ${\mathcal{F}}$-weak equivalences $f\colon X\to Y$ of \emph{closed} orthogonal $G'$-spaces. But indeed, if $H\in{\mathcal{F}}$ and ${\mathcal{U}}_H$ is any complete $H$-universe, then $\alpha^*f({\mathcal{U}}_H)$ is a $\mathcal G_{H,G}$-weak equivalence by Example~(ex:graph-restr-rQ of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.163645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8a099ee02b745b6c04087bf16c1a87dff3580e677f34af074dfcc805cfccf8d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def_UniversalSpaceOfDiracBundles of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Denote by $\mathbf{Met} \subseteq \Gamma\paren{X,\Hom(S^2TX,\mathbb{R})}$ the space of Riemannian metrics on $X$.
  The \defined{space of Dirac bundle structures} on $S$ is the tame Fréchet submanifold
  \begin{equation*}
    \mathbf{Dir}
    \coloneq
    \set*{
      (g;\gamma,\nabla) \in \mathbf{Met} \times \Gamma\paren{X,\Hom(TX,{\mathfrak o}(S))} \times \mathscr{A}(S)
      :
      \begin{aligned}
        & (\gamma,\nabla)
        ~\text{is a Dirac bundle structure} \\
        & 
        ~\text{with respect to}~
        g              
      \end{aligned}
    }.
  \end{equation*}
  In the following a triple $(g;\gamma,\nabla) \in \mathbf{Dir}$ is often abbreviated to ${\mathbf{p}}$
  (which, of course, stands for parameter).
  \qedhere","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.288850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8a10e981e80cd387d15f0eb39f32d5808a9319b634be8dd29ce4469f277596b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop approx_maximal of arXiv:2608.30048, 'Counterexamples for generalizations of the non-elliptic Schr\"{o}dinger maximal operator'] Let $0<c_0<1/2$ be a small constant and $\delta_0$ be as in (equation eqn:phi_delta of the paper). Suppose $\sigma \leq 1$, if $Q_{k-i}$ vanishes for all $d\leq i \leq k$, and otherwise, suppose $\sigma\leq (d-1)/d$. Then there exist constants $0< c_1(\delta_0,P_k),c_2(P_k)<1$ such that for all  $c_1<c_1(\delta_0,P_k),c_2<c_2(P_k)$ and $0<c_3<1$ as small as we like, the following holds. 

Let $R$ be sufficiently large depending on $c_1,c_2,\phi,\sigma,P_k$.
Let $x\in [-c_1,-c_1/2]\times [-c_1,c_1]^{n-1}$ and suppose $t\in (0,1)$ satisfies  
    \begin{align*}
        t &= \frac{-x_1}{\partial_1 P_k(0,R')} + \tau, \qquad \text{where } |\tau| \leq \frac{c_2\delta_0}{S_1R^{k-1}},\qquad \text{and }
        t \leq \frac{c_3}{R^{k-1}},
    \end{align*}
    where $R'=(R_2,...,R_n)$ with $R_j=0$ for $2\leq j \leq m$ and $R_j = N_j R$ for $m+1\leq j \leq n$.

Then $ |T_t^{P}f(x)| \geq (2\pi)^{-n}(1-c_0)^n + E$, where $ E \ll_{\phi,n,P_k}c_3.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.492083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8a3b7b15e467ff388d8b02ecacd3a85064756b6a558a996dc4bebb0b363ff90","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.04012, 'Hölder regularity for backward stochastic Volterra integral equations and applications to '] Suppose that Assumption \ref{assumption-Holder-BSVIE} holds, and let $(Y,Z)$ be the unique solution to the BSVIE \eqref{eq:bsvie-intro}. 

    Let $\pi$ be a partition of $[0,T]$. For each $k\in\{0,\dots,N-1\}$, define
    \begin{gather}
        \Psi_k^\pi
        \coloneqq
        \frac{1}{\Delta_k}
        \int_{t_k}^{t_{k+1}}\Psi(t)\,dt.
    \end{gather}
    Moreover, for $0\leq k\leq N-1$ and $s\in[t_k,T]$, define
    \begin{gather}
        G_k^\pi(s,y,z)
        \coloneqq
        \begin{cases}
        0, & s\in[t_k,t_{k+1}), \\[0.4em]
        \displaystyle
        \frac{1}{\Delta_k}
        \int_{t_k}^{t_{k+1}}
        G(r,s,y,z)\,dr,
        & s\in[t_{k+1},T].
        \end{cases}
    \end{gather}
    Let $\big(Y^\pi(t_k,\cdot),Z^\pi(t_k,\cdot)\big)_{k=0}^{N-1}$ be the solution of the BSDE system associated with the data $(\Psi^\pi,G^\pi)$. Then
    \begin{flalign}
        \mathbb E\bigg[
        \int_0^T |Y(t)-Y^\pi(\tau(t),t)|^2\,dt
        \bigg]
        +
        \mathbb E\bigg[
        \int_0^T\int_t^T
        |Z(t,s)-Z^\pi(\tau(t),s)|^2\,ds\,dt
        \bigg]
        \longrightarrow 0
    \end{flalign}
    whenever $|\pi|\to0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.633106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8a47440635ee42f2ab3502f9a36e6a4628c30e0ef4daa19bda2479adc765c99","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:convergenceXtilde of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let 
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \widetilde{X}^+_n=&(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}_0^W(W[1,\infty)\cap\eta[1,n]=\varnothing\mid \eta),\\
        \widetilde{X}_n=&(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}_0^W(W[1,\infty)\cap\eta[0,n]=\varnothing\mid \eta),
