{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.100873+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8d6ffc28082ac6ffda745559ec0820c0f89ae4fa0b4a4f46748c13ca72a704d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma shifting RW of arXiv:2411.14350, 'Randomized Geodesic Flow on Hyperbolic Groups'] Let $(X_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a random walk on a hyperbolic group $G$ with symmetric step distribution $\mu$ whose support is finite and generates $G$ and starting point $X_0=o$. Fix $m\in \mathbb{N}$ and set
\begin{align*}
\bar Z^m_n &:= X_m^{-1}X_{m-n} &&\text{ for } n=0,...,m;\\
Z^m_n &:= X_m^{-1}X_{m+n} &&\text{ for } n\geq m\\
\end{align*}
Then the following hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\big(\bar Z^m_n\big)_{n=0}^m$ and $\big(Z^m_n\big)_{i=0}^{\infty}$ are independent for any $m\in\mathbb{N}$. 
\item Furthermore, they converge in distribution to independent random walks $\big(\bar Z_n\big)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ and $\big(Z_n\big)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ with step distribution $\mu$ and starting point $o$.
\item Finally, $\big(\bar Z_n\big)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ and $\big(Z_n\big)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ converge a.s to points $Z_{\infty}$ and $Z_{-\infty}$ on $\partial G$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.123357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8d8835f831ab483182f15d1ce61103b1cf33aaf0120e87fee6bfb255fcd94b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2605.27713, 'Lower path regularity in all dimensions'] If $\mu$ is a finite Borel measure on $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ such that $\mu\ll \mathcal{L}^d$, then 
