{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.645348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8d9fd3b1f1ce81f3a27a65dc393d072f056680a58a470740cabadca86d5017a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor joint-conv of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] In the above setup, the joint law
    \begin{equation}
        \big(h_\delta,\ \delta^{-1/8}\sigma_\delta,\ \delta^{-1/8}\tilde\sigma_\delta,\ \delta^{-1/4}\tau_\delta,\ \delta^{-1/8}\sigma_\delta^\dagger,\ \delta^{-1/8}\tilde\sigma_\delta^\dagger,\ \delta^{-1/4}\tau_\delta^\dagger\big)
    \end{equation}
    converges as $\delta\to0$ to
    \begin{equation}
        \big(1/(\pi\sqrt{2})h,\ \sigma,\ \tilde\sigma,\ \field{\cos((1/\sqrt{2})h)},\ \sigma^\dagger,\ \tilde\sigma^\dagger,\ \field{\sin((1/\sqrt{2})h)}\big),
