  \lim_{M\to\infty} M^d \int_0^1 e^{-\frac{M^d}{d-1}\big((1-\beta)^{1-d}-1\big)} \,\mathrm{d}\beta =1.
 \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.585356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e33f435f98d604224343febb2f3e500fec9073f201e01eb3ad372ab639c51a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-quantum-cone of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Fix $W > 0$ and let $\alpha = Q - \frac{W}{2\gamma}$. Sample independent standard Brownian motions $(B_t)_{t \geq 0}, (\tilde B_t)_{t \geq 0}$ conditioned on $\tilde B_{t} - (Q-\alpha) < 0$ for all $t>0$. Let
	\[Y_t := \left\{ \begin{array}{rcl} 
				B_{t}+(Q-\alpha) t & \mbox{for} & t\ge 0\\
				\tilde{B}_{-t} -(Q-\alpha) |t| & \mbox{for} & t<0
			\end{array} 
			\right. \]
	Let $\hat \psi = \psi_1 + \psi_2$ where $\psi_1$ is the distribution on $\mathcal{C}$ which is constant on each line segment $\{t\} \times [0,2\pi]$ satisfying $\psi_1(z) = Y_{\mathrm{Re}(z)}$, and $\psi_2$ is an independent copy of $h_\mathcal{C}^2$. The \emph{weight $W$ quantum cone} is $(\mathcal{C}, \hat \psi, -\infty, +\infty)/{\sim_\gamma}$, and we define the probability measure $\mathcal{M}^\mathrm{cone}(W)$ to be its law.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.553457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e3ff45edfcbcd5f33966e04f8be357b1dd6f09a913b9ac6e1e4ba3fc6ecf8e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 11 (Solution for $\theta=0$) of arXiv:2604.02129, 'Realisation of constraints in underdamped Langevin dynamics'] Let $c^2 = 4ab$ with $\theta$ defined in~\eqref{def:theta}. Then~\eqref{eq:lemsollangevin} admits the solution 
\begin{align*}
    q_t &= e^{-\frac{c}{2}t}\Bigl[\Bigl(1+\mfrac{c}{2}t\Bigr)q_0 + atp_0  \Bigr] -\int_0^t e^{- \frac{c}{2} (t-s) }a(t-s) \nabla V(q_s,\tilde q_s) ds + \tilde c\int_0^t e^{- \frac{c}{2} (t-s) }a(t-s) dB_s,\\
    p_t &=  e^{-\frac{c}{2}t}\Bigl[-btq_0 + \Bigl(1-\mfrac{c}{2}t\Bigr)p_0  \Bigr] - \int_0^t e^{- \frac{c}{2} (t-s) }\Bigl[1-\mfrac{c}{2}(t-s)\Bigr] \nabla V(q_s,\tilde q_s) ds \\
    &\qquad + \tilde c\int_0^t e^{- \frac{c}{2} (t-s) }\Bigl[1-\mfrac{c}{2}(t-s)\Bigr] dB_s.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.839789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e44d94403a087294adf17619eb93784a5efa577b6ad11a396798806bb567b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-ccmt of arXiv:2607.25567, 'Random Trees in Hyperbolic FPP'] Let $L$ be a non-amenable hyperbolic locally compact group. If $L$ contains
	a cocompact amenable closed subgroup, then there exists a unique maximal compact normal
	subgroup $W \subset L$, such that 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item Either $L/W \subset Isom (X)$ where $X$ is a rank one symmetric space of noncompact type, and $L/W$ acts transitively on $X$.
		\item Or $L/W \subset Isom ({\mathcal T})$, where ${\mathcal T}$ is a locally finite
		non-elementary tree. Further, 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item $L/W$ acts faithfully and properly discontinuously by simplicial automorphisms without inversions on ${\mathcal T}$ with exactly two orbits of vertices,
			\item The $L$ action on the boundary $\partial {\mathcal T}$ is 2-transitive, i.e.\ it is transitive on $\partial^2 T$. 
		\end{itemize}
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

