{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8e901258be90e6112facb17adaeb69188e62fb223eeefb0ba5ed0327bdcc80c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:8.3 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let ${\rm A} \subseteq{\rm D}_n^\circ$ be an $(r_n,n-r_n)$-clustered set and ${\mathbf A}$ a minimal $r_n$-cover of it in the sense of~(equation e:2.10t of the paper) such that $|{\mathbf A}|\leq n^{1/2+\eta_0/4}$, where $\eta_0$ is as in~(equation e:2.3 of the paper). Then, as $n \to \infty$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}_\partial \Big(\tau_{\partial {\rm B}(x;r_n)} < \overline{\tau}_\partial \wedge \min_{y \in {\mathbf A} \setminus \{x\}}
