{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.615175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f915c208936a61cb7eafd822cf81fb3d73a28f07dc56fb1f7683ba551276bc4b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 87 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Let $0<\delta<1$ with $\delta=o(1)$ and $\tfrac1{\delta}=o(\log\alpha)$. Let $0\leq\widetilde{k}\leq k-1$ and $\widetilde{K}\leq n_{\tilde{k}}$ with $K\leq n_k-\delta(n_k-\widetilde{K})$. Consider the event $$\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}^{\delta}:=\{n_{\alpha-r}-\Psi_r\geq\delta(n_{\alpha-r}-\widetilde{K}),\ \forall r=0,\ldots,\alpha-k-1\}\subset\mathcal{P}.$$ Then for $C=O(1)$, we have
		\begin{align}
			&\mathbb{E}\left(1_{\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}^{\delta}}\exp\left(C\sum_{r=0}^{\alpha-k-1}\frac{(K-\widetilde{K})^+}{n_{\alpha-r}-\Psi_r}\right)\right)
			\\&\leq\exp\left((\tfrac{C}{2}+o(1))k\log\log\alpha+O(\tfrac{1}{\delta}\widetilde{k})\right).
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f91972e95fdae27967937f10873923a63366b1f2b3bed7568d169d7088e7cd64","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-iteration-trick of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $R>0$, $N,M\in \mathbb{N}$. Let $V,E, A, \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i=1}^N, \left\{F_j\right\}_{j=1}^M$ be non-negative, locally bounded functions defined on $[0,R)$ such that $A,F_j$ are non-increasing for all $j=1,\dots, M$. We assume that there exist $L_i,c_i, \tilde c, \ell_j\in [0,\infty)$, such that for any $s\ge 0$ and $\delta>0$ with $s+\delta \leq R$ we have  
    \begin{equation}

        \begin{split}
        V(s+\delta) + E(s+\delta)& \leq A(s) + \sum_{i=1}^N \left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)^{L_i} U_i\left(s+\frac{\delta}{2}\right) \\
        & \leq A(s) + \varepsilon\sum_{i=1}^N c_i\left(\frac{4}{\delta}\right)^{L_i}U_i\left(s + \frac{\delta}{4} \right) + \varepsilon \, \tilde c \, E\left(s\right) + C_\varepsilon\sum_{j=1}^M \left( \frac{2}{\delta}\right)^{\ell_j} F_j(s),
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}for any $\varepsilon>0$ and a constant $C_\varepsilon<\infty$. Then, there exists a  constant $C^*\in (0,\infty)$ depending only on the preceding parameters, such that for any $s,\delta$:
    \begin{equation}

        V(s+\delta) \leq C^* \left(A(s) + \sum_{j=1}^M\delta^{-\ell_j} F_j(s)\right).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.060039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f91f47c371fd2f741538207a517ddc925f573fe1e4f690ace44fa8d805d480ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Banach-valued time lift) of arXiv:2606.16662, '2606.16662'] Let \(X(t,s)\), \(0\le s\le t\le T\), be a random field with values in a finite-dimensional Banach space \(B\).  Assume that for some \(A_N\), all \(p_0\ge2\), some \(\eta\in(0,1]\), and some \(\chi\ge0\),
\begin{align}
        \|\|X(t,s)\|_B\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega)}&\le C_{p_0}A_N,\\
        \|\|X(t,s)-X(t',s')\|_B\|_{L^{p_0}(\Omega)}
        &\le C_{p_0}A_NN^{\chi\eta}
        (|t-t'|^\eta+|s-s'|^\eta),
\end{align}
whenever both pairs \((t,s)\) and \((t',s')\) lie in the Volterra simplex.  Then, for every fixed \(p\ge2\) and every \(\eps>0\), if \(\chi\eta<\eps/4\),
\begin{equation}
        \|\|X\|_{C_{t,s}B}\|_{L^p(\Omega)}
        \le C_{p,T,\eps}A_NN^\eps .
\end{equation}
The same statement holds for a separable Banach-valued modification.  In the application below \(B=\cL(\ell_q^2,\ell_n^2)\), a finite-dimensional matrix space; the continuous-time norm is obtained from rational time skeletons.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.079015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9218a2db2abdaf29c77a499a070c3e58e4a4787b34b695ca6229d761bec20a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition GWS of arXiv:2601.15223, 'Large time behaviour for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids of different'] A stochastic process $\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Y}}(t):=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Y}}(t;\mathfrak{r},\omega,\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Y}}_{\mathfrak{r}})$ is a $\textsl{global (analytic) weak solution}$ of the system (equation STGF of the paper) for $t\geq\mathfrak{r}$ and $\omega\in\Omega$ if for $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. $\omega\in\Omega$
