{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.462755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9241dd8921c5d7bf02a46288ce9f70cbfb8908b78e05f55bd647dcbd8c4e169","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 25 (Outgoing eikonal function and inverse foliation density) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The \emph{outgoing eikonal function} $u$ is the solution of the following fully nonlinear hyperbolic initial value problem,
where $\gfour$ is the acoustical metric defined in \eqref{E:ACOUSTICALMETRIC}
and the PDE is known as the \emph{acoustic eikonal equation}:
\begin{align} 
\begin{cases}
(\gfour^{-1})^{\alpha \beta} \partial_{\alpha} u \partial_{\beta} u = 0, 
	\\
\p_t u > 0, 
	\\
u|_{\Sigma_0} = - x^1.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
We define the \emph{outgoing inverse foliation density} $\upmu$ by:
\begin{align} 
	\upmu 
	& 
	\eqdef 
	- 
	\frac{1}{(\gfour^{-1})^{\alpha \beta} \partial_{\alpha} t \partial_{\beta} u} > 0.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f925ce43acf67f3ebc1d7c2c2f8c3151cd9602175ce5a382c0492ac84e34c08c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 46 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_{+,0}$ is a regular right edge for $\Pi_0$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. With high probability, $Y_0$ is $\eta_*$-regular around $\la_{1,0}$ in the sense of \cite[Definition~1]{ding2022edge} or \cite[Definition~1]{ding2022tracywidom}. More explicitly, there exist constants $c,C>0$ such that
        \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
                \item For $z=E+\ii\eta$ with \begin{align}
