{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.134275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f938f584593fb858e119eb414e0c7c6223733e66b8241d74eb9ad4059d168cbb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:positive_constant_speed_of_SRW_on_nonamenable_transitive_graphs of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Given a nonamenable and transitive graph $G$, there exists a constant $c(G) > 0$ such that 
