{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.743519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f939ee62b46fd139745ad43bbe6a506d6b3a0c3c6c05134d6b9be7e1e741a048","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] Let $\ccG\! \subset \! \ccF$ be a $\sigma$-field and let $(Z^{_{(n)}}_s)_{s\in \bbR_+}$, $n\ino \bbN^*$, be a sequence of $\bbR$-valued continuous processes such that $Z^{_{(n)}}_0\eqo 0$. Let $\ttb\ino (1, \infty)$ and $\gamma \ino (0, 1]$. Let us assume that for all $p\ino \bbN^*$, there exists a $\ccG$-measurable r.v.~$\mathtt C_p$ such that for all $n\ino \bbN^*$, 
