{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.157295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f96e921fda39c1fdb636b54e13a9c66b8ecf0ae22db91cb86f3c54f5259486e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma right-adjoint-right-Bousfield of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be a cleft and let $X\in\Spc_T$. Then the $S$-parametrized right adjoint $R$ of the inclusion $\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T/X}\hookrightarrow\ul\Spc_{T/X}$ is $S$-cocontinuous. Moreover, if $X$ is equipped with a commutative monoid structure, then the lax symmetric monoidal structure on $R$ (with respect to the slice symmetric monoidal structures) is strong.
