{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.241938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f977518620541b2e41206702ccc185b163933fea718691880ffefd5cd718505b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (A Priori Estimates for the Penalized Equations) of arXiv:2604.14893, 'Well-Posedness of Generalized Mean-Reflected McKean--Vlasov Backward Stochastic Differenti'] Under Assumptions (A1)--(A5), for a given $k\ge{}1$ and any $n\ge{}1$, let $(Y^{n,k},Z^{n,k})$ be the solution to the penalized equation. Then there exist a constant $\alpha>0$ and a constant $C_k>0$ depending on $k$ but independent of $n$, such that the following a priori estimates hold:
