{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.431895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f98354578f199ef42256d2f42a7dbd44b151ad4e1e917450ac29f3a25a1b0eb8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:explicit-constrained-mgle-barycenter-final of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] Let \(\mathbb{X}^k=\mathbb{G}^{0,L^k}\in\mathcal{FG}(T,d)\), \(k\in[K]\), be arbitrary centered
