{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.286174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9cb4b3f7cb2b2023727f30cac281ac6bf6e776fdfae189b7ab595a48b3ff4e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 (Homogeneous $\alpha$-H\"{o}lder norm) of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$. For any path $\mathbf{x}:[0,T]\rightarrow G^{\lfloor p\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k)$, the homogeneous $\alpha$-H\"{o}lder norm of $\mathbf{x}$ is defined as
    \begin{equation*}
        \lVert \mathbf{x}\rVert_{\textup{hom $\alpha$-H\"{o}l};[0,T]} := \sup_{0\leq s<t\leq T}\frac{d_{cc}(\mathbf{x}_s,\mathbf{x}_t)}{|t-s|^\alpha}.
