{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.672058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9f9a2012f035382a6ee743938b76700bc0760ce81713e80864fc7adb2908b44","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (transition distribution) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] For $x>0$, the transition distribution $P_x(u_{T_\alpha}\in\cdot)$
  admits the resolvent representation
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}(u_{T_\alpha}\in A\mid u_0=x)
    = \frac{\alpha}{\mu}\,G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(x,0)\,\mathbf{1}_{0\in A}
    + \alpha\int_{A\cap(0,\infty)} G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(x,y)\,m'(y)\,dy,
  \end{equation}
  equivalent to the three-component mixture
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb P(u_{T_\alpha}\in A\mid u_0=x)
    = w_0(x)\,\mathbf{1}_{0\in A}
    + w_<(x)\,\nu_<(A)
    + w_>(x)\,\nu_>(A),
  \end{equation}
  where $\nu_<$ and $\nu_>$ are the probability measures with Lebesgue
  densities
  \[
    \frac{d\nu_<(y)}{dy}  \propto  f_0^{\rm sticky}(y)\,m'(y)\,\mathbf{1}_{(0,x)}(y),
    \qquad
    \frac{d\nu_>(y)}{dy}  \propto  U(a,b,z_y)\,m'(y)\,\mathbf{1}_{(x,\infty)}(y),
  \]
  and the weights are
  \begin{align}
    w_0(x) &= -c_\mu\,U(a,b,z_x), \\
    w_<(x) &= \frac{\alpha\,U(a,b,z_x)}{|\mathcal{W}|}
               \int_0^x f_0^{\rm sticky}(y)\,m'(y)\,dy, \\
    w_>(x) &= \frac{\alpha\,f_0^{\rm sticky}(x)}{|\mathcal{W}|}
               \int_x^\infty U(a,b,z_y)\,m'(y)\,dy, 
  \end{align}
  satisfying $w_0(x)+w_<(x)+w_>(x)=1$.","status":"unverified"}

