{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.586120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9fd27db0ee2782c89c12c6a678dba0423a5b4507cb981613a94c1133c2b49e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm convnex_entropy of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\Pi_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}( \mathsf{S})$, $i=0,1$ and assume that $\mathscr  W_{gap,p}(\Pi_0,\Pi_1)<\infty$ for $p>1$. Then, there exists an optimal coupling  $\mathsf U\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_s(\Pi_0,\Pi_1)$, such that for any $0\leq t\leq 1$ \begin{align}
