       \mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_t)\leq (1-t)  \mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_0)+t\mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_1)
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.188292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9fdbe3cade32435cf8d2789033a639b161b52753cca62d9b7a770c59c2d7728","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 148 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $x_{\cdot}$   be a solution  of
