{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.583369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa49fb911bbd27f079d7d7aaca368619b379618590cd107b7c21c9520d302acb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 434 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Assume that $G(t,y)=F(t)\cdot y$ for some locally bounded function $F$ on $\mathbb{R}_+$. 
 If  
 \begin{eqnarray}
   \int_0^\infty \frac{y^2}{n^2}\, \mu_n(dy) \to \sigma^2  \in (0,\infty)
 \quad \mbox{and}\quad 
 X^{(n)} \to X^* \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+) \mbox{ weakly in $D(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)$},
 \end{eqnarray} 
 as $n\to\infty$,   we have $Z^{(n)}  \overset{\rm f.d.d.}\longrightarrow Z^*$ with the limit process $Z^* $ given by
