 where $B^* (ds,dz)$ is Gaussian white noise with intensity $ \sigma^2\cdot ds\, dz$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa4ba5506ca8a546f0dd53a7615fa627973a89d2a0bfe401cb8cf619c50e60e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 33 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] There exists a universal constant such that for any martingale difference sequence $D_i$ adapted to a filtration $\mathcal{F}_i$---so $D_i$ is $\mathcal{F}_i$ measurable and $\E[D_i \mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}] =0$---we have for all $p \geq 2, n \geq 1$, the bounds
    \begin{equation}

        \Big\|\sum_{i=1}^n D_i\Big\|_{L^p_\omega} \leq C \sup_{ 2  \lor \frac{p}{n} \leq q \leq p} \frac{p}{q} \Big(\frac{n}{p}\Big)^{1/q} \max_{1 \leq i \leq n} \big\|\E[|D_i|^q \mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}]^{1/q}\big\|_{L^\infty_\omega}.
