{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.821307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa5821c6a3864c773001d1c7db6f22908e278be36eabc3872b544055e8ec1eab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:jump_path of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] Given a healing rate $\delta \in [0, \infty]$, a \emph{genealogical path} is a càdlàg function
  $\gamma:[s_{0},s_{1}] \to \mathbb{Z}^d$ ($0 \leq s_{0} \leq s_{1}$) such that:
  \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item whenever $\gamma(t)\neq\gamma(t-)$ for $t \in [s_{0}, s_{1}]$, a particle at position $\gamma(t-)$ jumps to $\gamma(t)$ at
      time $t$;
    \item $\eta_t(\gamma(t)) \ge 1$ for all $t \in [s_{0}, s_{1}]$;
    \item for every $t \in [s_0,s_1]$ such that $\eta_{t}(\gamma(t)) = 1$, $t$ is not an arrival of the Poisson process $\mathcal{R}_{\gamma(t)}$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.623989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa595e652f3f082472f96c82229dcd9b3733a052224f10b241949c49f48fae94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_IW-Theorem II.7.4-PRM of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Assume that
\[
\mathfrak{A}=\bigl( {\Omega}, {\mathscr{F}}, {\mathbb{P}}, {\mathbb{F}} \bigr), \mbox{ where } {\mathbb{F}}=({\mathscr{F}}_t)_{t\geq 0} ,
\]
is a  filtered probability space. Assume that $(\mathbf{X},\mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X})$ is a measurable space and
$\eta$ is a  random measure on $\mathfrak{A}$ and $(\mathbf{X},\mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X})$.
Assume that $\eta$ is of class \textbf{(QL)} and there exists
an $\mathbb{F}$-predictable generalized process
\begin{equation}

q\colon (0,\infty)\times \mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X} \times \Omega \to [0,\infty]
\end{equation}
such that  the compensator $\widehat{\eta}$  of $\eta$ satisfies, for  $\mathbb{P}$-almost every  $\omega\in \Omega$
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
\widehat{\eta}\bigl((0,t]\times A;\omega\bigr)&=\int_{(0,t]}\int_A q(s,\mathrm{d} x,\omega) \, \mathrm{d}s, \mbox{ for all $t\in (0,\infty)$, $A\in \mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X}$}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Suppose  that $(Y,\mathscr{Y})$ is a standard measurable space and  $m$ is a  $\sigma$-finite non-negative measure on it. Suppose  also that
\[
\theta\colon  (0,\infty) \times Y\times \Omega \to \mathbf{X}^\ast\coloneqq\mathbf{X} \cup \{ \partial\}
\]
is another  $\mathbb{F}$-predictable generalized process
such that for  $\mathbb{P}$-almost every  $\omega\in \Omega$
\begin{equation}
  m(\{ u \in Y: \theta(t,u,\omega) \in A\}) = q(t,A,\omega),  \mbox{ for all } t\in (0,\infty), \;\; A\in \mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X}.
\end{equation}
Then there exists an extension $\bigl(\tilde{\mathfrak{A}}, \pi  \bigr)$ of  $\mathfrak{A}$,
where
\[
\tilde{\mathfrak{A}}=\bigl( \tilde{\Omega}, \tilde{\mathscr{F}}, \tilde{\mathbb{P}}, \tilde{\mathbb{F}}  \bigr), \mbox{ with } \tilde{\mathbb{F}}=(\tilde{\mathscr{F}}_t)_{t\geq 0},
\]
 and there exists an  $Y$-valued stationary Poisson point process $\tilde{p}$ on $\tilde{\mathfrak{A}}$,
with  the  corresponding  Poisson random measure  denoted by ${\eta}_{\tilde{p}}$,  such that
\begin{trivlist}
\item[(i)] the characteristic measure of $\tilde{p}$ is equal to the measure $m$,
\item[(ii)] and the following equality holds for 
{$\widetilde{\mathbb{P}}$}-almost every  
{$\tilde{\omega}\in \widetilde{\Omega}$}
 \end{trivlist}
 \begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 \eta\bigl((0,t]\times A, \pi(\tilde{\omega})\bigr)&=
 \int_0^t \int_{Y} (\1_A\circ \theta)(s,u,\pi(\tilde{\omega}))\, {\eta}_{\tilde{p}}(\mathrm{d} s, \mathrm{d} u)
 \\&= \# \bigl\{ s \in \mathrm{Dom}({\tilde{p}(\tilde{\omega})}) \cap (0,t]: \theta(s,{\tilde{p}}(s,\tilde{\omega}),\pi(\tilde{\omega})) \in A \bigr\},
 \\&\mbox{for all  $t\in [0,\infty)$, $A\in \mathscr{B}_\mathbf{X}$}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.745034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa5babd73c56fd016f8b6c748dc39a44694278065ed4239256be0454861f4f59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tme of arXiv:2507.20324, 'Non-existence of several random fractals in Brownian motion and Brownian loop soup'] For all three cases, there exists $c>0$, such that for all $n\geq N(\delta)$ and any $n$-boxes $S,T,U\subset\mathcal{A}(0,\iota,1-\iota)$ such that $S,T,U\in\mathcal{S}_{n}$, we have
