{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.702268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa677fef3e24636b653b4ee7f3f2f3963d2d929f4f09ec9d16938e679321a531","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:coord of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Let $L\ge 1$. Given small $\varepsilon_1>0$, there exists $\varepsilon=\varepsilon(\varepsilon_1)>0$ such that
\begin{align*}
U_\varepsilon^L\subset \Big\{ \phi \in L^2(\mathbb{T}_{L^2}): \; \phi=e^{i\theta}Q^{\eta_L}_{x_0}+h \quad &\text{for some $x_0\in \mathbb{T}_{L^2}$, $\theta\in \mathbb{R}$,}\\
&\text{  and $h\in V^{L^2}_{x_0,\theta}$ with $\|h \|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}_{L^2})}<\varepsilon_1$} \Big\},
\end{align*}

\noindent
where, at each point $e^{i\theta}Q^{\eta_L}_{x_0}$ on the manifold $\bar \mathcal{M}_L$, $V^{L^2}_{x_0,\theta}$ represents the normal space to the soliton manifold
\begin{align}
V_{x_0,\theta}^{L^2}=\big\{\phi \in L^2(\mathbb{T}_{L^2}): \;  &\jb{\phi, (1-\partial_x^2) \partial_{x_0}( e^{i\theta}Q^{\eta_L}_{x_0} )  }=0 \notag \\  
&\jb{\phi, (1-\partial_x^2) \partial_{\theta}( e^{i\theta}Q^{\eta_L}_{x_0})  }=0 \big\}.

\end{align}

\noindent
Here, the inner product on $L^2(\mathbb{T}_{L^2})$, defined in (equation INER of the paper), means the real inner product. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa68cc8f45ca869caf729fc74ea99ec89f11275029b7598941f7c452d4b31cdb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 16 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] Assume Assumption \ref{a.050201}. For $m$-a.e. $\sigma\in\Sigma$,
