{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008873+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa69375f69a30528ececf258dfeab20d94855e2f56ce68f3d0eb165e62c650a0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a PP in $\mathbb{R}$. Suppose that there exists a function $K:\mathbb{R}^2\rightarrow\mathbb{C}$ such that, for almost every $x_j\in\mathbb{R}$,
