{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.526293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa6ed4e2fa44a91d819a0d8a33773e04b20d2315ecef2467e657350a9ab1d5ee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: alpha-mixing GSDE of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] If Assumption (Assumption G-SDE of the paper) holds, then the sublinear Markovian system $\{T_t\}_{t\geq 0}$ defined by (equation def: T_t by G-SDEintroduction of the paper) has a unique invariant sublinear expectation $\tilde{T}$, and for any $m\geq 1$, the $m$-dimensional sublinear expectation system $(\Omega, (Lip(\Omega))^m, (U_t)_{t\geq 0}, \hat{\mathbb{E}}^{\tilde{T}})$ is $\alpha$-mixing, continuous and regular.

