{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.291561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa98244e68bce035a08605b149341145b19e34ce1645ae4d483b8a5b3398bb2d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:rwcre_kernel of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] Given a resampling map $\tau$ and an i.i.d. environment sequence
$\bar{\omega}\sim\mu^{{\mathbb {N}}}$, the \emph{random walk in cooling random
environment} (RWCRE) is the Markov chain $X=(X_n)_{n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0}$ on ${\mathbb {Z}}$
with transition kernel
\begin{equation}
P^{\bar{\omega},\tau}(X_{n+1}=x+e\mid X_n=x)=
\begin{cases}
\omega_{\ell_n}(x), & e=+1,\\
1-\omega_{\ell_n}(x), & e=-1,
\end{cases}
\quad x\in{\mathbb {Z}},\ n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0,
\end{equation}
where $\ell_n$ is given by (equation eq:ell_def of the paper). We denote by
$P_x^{\bar{\omega},\tau}$ the quenched law and by
\begin{equation}
P_x^{\mu,\tau}(\,\cdot\,):=\int_{[(0,1)^{{\mathbb {Z}}}]^{{\mathbb {N}}}}
P_x^{\bar{\omega},\tau}(\,\cdot\,)\,\mu^{{\mathbb {N}}}(d\bar{\omega})
\end{equation}
the corresponding annealed law.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa9936f057afe42f270d75dc293cdf69abd3fa633c0dd34e49406e1b4472d79d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: markov of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] A map $T: \mathbb{R}_+\times C_{lip}(\mathbb{X})\to C_{lip}(\mathbb{X})$ is called a sublinear Markovian system if
		\begin{itemize}
			\item [(i)] for each fixed $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_+\times\mathbb{X}$, $T_t[\cdot](x)$ is a sublinear expectation on $C_{lip}(\mathbb{X})$;
			\item [(ii)] $T_0[\phi](x)=\phi(x)$ for each $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{X})$;
			\item [(iii)] $\{T_t\}_{t\geq 0}$ satisfies the following Chapman semigroup formula:
			\begin{equation*}
				T_t\circ T_s[\phi]=T_{t+s}[\phi], \ \text{ for all } \ \phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{X})\text{ and }s,t\ge0.
			\end{equation*}
		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.321163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa9a0720f82c74797f408bf657264544790e9716f04e74b6a9617076443acb9c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-conclave of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    The random process $\mathbf{X}_k=(\mathbf{X}_k^{(1)},...,\mathbf{X}_k^{(n)})$ for $k \in \mathbb Z_{\geq 0}$ (with size $n$ and weight function $\mu$) is a Markov process on $\Omega_n$ defined by the following evolution:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item For $k=0$, set $\mathbf{X}_0:=(1,1,...,1)$. 
        \item For $k\ge 1$, given that $\mathbf{X}_{k-1}=(a_{k-1}^{(1)},...,a_{k-1}^{(n)})\in \Omega_n$, sample i.i.d.\ random variables 
        \begin{align}
            \{\mathbf{B}_{k,j}\}_{j=1}^{n} \mbox{ such that } \mathbb{P}(\mathbf{B}_{k,j}=i)=\frac{\mu(a_{k-1}^{(i)})}{\sum_{1\le l\le n}\mu(a_{k-1}^{(l)})}  
        \end{align}
        for all $i,j\in [n]:=\{1,2,...,n\}$, and then define $\mathbf{X}_{k}^{(i)}:=\sum_{j=1}^{n} \mathbf{1}_{ \{ \mathbf{B}_{k,j}=i \} }$ for $i\in [n]$. 
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.366366+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa9f6e9bea1c94872574c455272d1bc8b818266db90cb3a856506d823780db15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\tilde \sigma_1, \tilde \sigma_2 \subset \RR^D$ be two embedded $C^2$ simplices of reach $\reach$, and assume that they share a face. Let $z \in \tilde \sigma_1 \cap \tilde \sigma_2$ and let following be unit vectors: $u \in \nincone^1_z(\tilde \sigma_1)$, $v_\normspc \in \nincone_z^1(\tilde \sigma_2)$, $v_\tanspc \in \tanspc_z(\tilde \sigma_2)$. Assume that the angle $\theta = \angle(u, v_\normspc)$ satisfies $\theta \in (0, \pi]$. Let $\epsilon, \ell, \lambda_\normspc, \lambda_\tanspc$ be numbers in the following range: $\epsilon \in (0, \sin(\theta/4)]$ and $\ell, \lambda_\normspc, \lambda_\tanspc \in [0, \min(1/5, \epsilon) \cdot \reach]$. Then the following holds:
    \begin{align*}
        \|x-y \| \ge \ell(\sin\theta_+ - 3\epsilon)
    \end{align*}
    where $x, y, \theta_+$ are defined as follows:
    \[ x = \exp_z^{\sigma_1}(\ell u), \quad y = \exp_z^{\sigma_2}(\lambda_\normspc v_\normspc + \lambda_\tanspc v_\tanspc), \quad \theta_+ = \min \bigg( \theta, \frac{3\pi}4 \bigg) \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.530383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faa9931f34dc4c4129364cee485bbdf60bdfba09139c255479fcd21160d89939","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_PRM of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] A measurable function  
\begin{equation}
    \eta\colon \Omega \to M_{\overline{\mathbb{N}}}(E)
    \end{equation}
    is a Poisson random measure if and only if 
\begin{enumerate}
\item for any $A\in \mathscr{E}$, the function
\begin{equation*}
\eta(A)\colon \Omega \ni \omega \mapsto \eta(\omega)(A) \in \overline{\mathbb{N}}
\end{equation*}
 is a Poisson random variable with parameter $\mathbb{E} \left[ \eta(A) \right]$ if $\mathbb{E} \left[ \eta(A) \right] < \infty$, and $\eta(A)=\infty $ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.\ otherwise.
\item[(ii)] For every finite family $A_1,A_2,\ldots A_n \in \mathscr{E}$ of pairwise  disjoint sets, the random variables $\eta(A_1),\ldots, \eta(A_n)$ are independent.
\end{enumerate}
By the \emph{intensity measure} of a PRM $\eta$  we understand   the measure
\begin{equation}
\mu\colon \mathscr{E} \ni A \mapsto   \mathbb{E} \left[ \eta(A) \right] \in \overline{\mathbb{N}}_+.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.220579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faaae03c59c34f3ab258df4f0439a207537d211abacbd1af537480031b051b7c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_qPochas of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Let $\varepsilon=-\log q$. For every $q\in(0,1)$ and $x\in \mathbb{C}\backslash [1,+\infty)$
\begin{align}
\log(x;q)_\infty = -\frac{1}{\varepsilon}{\operatorname{Li}}_2(x)+\frac{1}{2}\ln(1\!-\!x)
+  \varepsilon R_{1}(x,q)

\end{align}
where ${\operatorname{Li}}_2(x)$ is the principal branch of the dilogarithm function defined by the integral in (equation dilog of the paper) and
\begin{align}
|R_{1}(x,q)| \le \frac{1}{6} \int_0^1 \frac{|x| du}{|1-xu|^2} \:.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.740361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faac10a39c5b7886f8b5f6fb68e1d3251060ca4a8d17ddd76748a5980504a7e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem trim_twist of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\xi$ and $T$ be as above.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Trim) There exists a positive contact structure $\xi'$ which is $C^\infty$-close to $\xi$ and such that $\partial \xi \prec \partial \xi'$ along $T$.
        \item (Twist) Suppose $\xi$ is $\Phi$-horizontal for some smooth nonsingular flow $\Phi$ on $M$. For any smooth $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ on $\partial M$ satisfying $\mathcal{G} \prec \partial \xi$, there is a $\Phi$-horizontal positive contact structure $\xi'$ with $\partial \xi' = \mathcal{G}$.
    \end{enumerate}
    In both cases, we can arrange that $\xi'$ coincides with $\xi$ away from an arbitrarily small neighborhood of $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.974888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fab18169b03bdff806c537738d0c71fd85937453c1beada18eaa2e3ff47ff63b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Under Assumption~(assu:LyapunovRd of the paper), assuming furthermore that,
\[ \lambda   \leqslant  \min\left( \frac{r}{3}, \frac{2\alpha}{3}, \frac{ r\alpha c_0^2}{176(1+\alpha)^3} \right) \,,\]
there exists $C\in\mathcal C(\mathfrak{p})$ such that 
for any $N\in\mathbb N$ and $\mathbf{z}\in\mathbb R^{2dN}$,
\[\mathbf V(\bar{\mathbf{z}}) \leqslant  \left( 1 + \textcolor{magenta}{h\lambda}\right) \mathbf V(\mathbf{z})  + \rouge{ h \sum_{i=1}^N \left[  -  \frac{r\alpha c_0^2}{11}   |x_i|^6 + \alpha A' |v_i|^6 \right] }     
  + \textcolor{blue}{ C   \left[  h N d^3
