{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.155354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_facfb490385a4669c278c56f7f1150756286de340bb5421d92de1685584d0187","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:interp of arXiv:2607.05345, 'The local product condition implies cutoff'] Fix two measures $\mu,\pi\in\mathcal {P}({\mathbb{X}})$ with $\mathrm{d}_{\textsc{tv}}(\mu,\pi)<1$. Then, there is a   measure $\nu\in\mathcal {P}({\mathbb{X}})$ which is absolutely continuous w.r.t. both $\mu$ and $\pi$, such that
