{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.684887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fad8c3f0429c3244a529702746738451564bc69b342166213e9faa1cdc040d07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:typeI of arXiv:2609.01920, 'Isospectral and not strongly isospectral spherical space forms with non-cyclic fundamental'] {Wolf-book}}]
		Let $m$, $n$, $r$ be positive integers satisfying $\gcd((r-1)n,m)=1$ and $r^n \equiv 1 \pmod{m}$. Then the group $\Gamma$ generated by elements $A$, $B$ with relations
		\begin{equation}
			A^m=B^n=1 \quad \text{and} \quad BAB^{-1}=A^r
		\end{equation}
		has order $mn$ and is of Type~I. Conversely, every Type~I group is isomorphic to one of this form. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.221793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fadb9efbdb90777788491936aa75a76ab244901abbfbcba21ebf6397897ccd35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:der-mart-lower of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] For all $\underline{c} \in (0, 1]$, there exists $t_{\textnormal{max}} \leq -1$ such that the following holds.
  For all $\mathfrak{t} \leq t_{\textnormal{max}}$, there exists $\underline{T}(\mathfrak{t}) > \abs{\mathfrak{t}}$ and a function $\underline{u}(t,x; \mathfrak{t}) \geq 0$ defined where $t \in [-\underline{T}(\mathfrak{t}), \mathfrak{t}]$ and $x \geq 2 \log \left |t \right|$ satisfying the following properties:
  \begin{enumerate}[label = \textnormal{(\roman*)},itemsep = 2pt]
  \item $\underline{u} = 0$ where $x \geq \left |t \right|$;

  \item

    $\underline{u} \leq \underline{c} \mathrm{e}^{-x}$ where $t = -\underline{T}$ or $x = 2 \log \left |t \right|$;   

  \item $\underline{u}$ is a subsolution of (equation eq:ancient of the paper);

  \item $\partial_x \underline{u} \leq 0$; and

  \item for all $x \in [4 \log \abs{\mathfrak{t}}, \abs{\mathfrak{t}}/4]$,
    \begin{equation}

      \underline{u}(\mathfrak{t}, x; \mathfrak{t}) \geq 2^{-8} \underline{c} x \mathrm{e}^{-x}.
