{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faec3cd7a2d69cb3672036fb3a9c61f90ba9ab93c83335fd5d8264e0dd37b76d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, suppose that $E_{+,0}$ is a regular right edge for $\Pi_0$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. There is a unique critical point $\zeta_t$ satisfying $\zeta_t-E_{+,0}\sim t^2$. Moreover,
