{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.203327+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faf0f84b3cc12a3ee9a566c84f442830699a5554dfe68e8618d20d4d6f220229","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For every $T>0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $f\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D;\R^2))$, the solution $v$ of \eqref{eq l2} satisfies
