{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.280152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_faf5fe8eda86d0dd2a4245835bbbac37387504dbd3f68fb250d3281c6b15fa3e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 of arXiv:2604.22461, 'Large deviation principles for stationary solutions and invariant measures of a class of S'] The stationary solution $\cY^{\epsilon}$ satisfeis LDP on the space $\sC_{-\infty}$ with rate function $\mathcal{I}_{-\infty}$ given by (\ref{def: rate func 2}), if the following items hold:
 \begin{description}
