{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.999034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb91f2c0e422c431d909264215c86fa128ed279abc31ab868bd2e1f0aaa31d4b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let      $(A_\zeta,\mathcal B_-,\mathcal B_+)\in\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times a_\zeta}\times\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m}\times\mathbb C^{a_\zeta\times m}$ with
      $\sigma(A_\zeta)\subset\mathbb C_r$. There exists a
      $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function $\sigma$ analytic and contractive in $\mathbb C_r$
      and such that
\begin{equation}

  \sum_{z_0\in\mathbb C_r} {\rm Res}_{{z}=z_0}\,(zI_{a_\zeta}-A_\zeta)^{-1}\mathcal  B_+\sigma(z)=-\mathcal  B_-.
\end{equation}
            if and only if the unique solution of the Lyapunov equation
            \begin{equation}

    GA_\zeta^*+A_\zeta G=\mathcal B_+\mathcal B_+^*-\mathcal B_-\mathcal B_-^*
      \end{equation}
