{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.306144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb98ea87069dc1fec614bd4e8ed63e75ffe03920bc0f6c0be4e78d2968ce2978","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:2BM of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$ and $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$ satisfy the assumption of Theorem (thm:main of the paper) ((item:1 of the paper)) {and ${\mathbb{E}}_{\nu_\mathbf{q}}\left[ {s_{\infty}\left(1\right)}^2 \right] < \infty$}. Then, for any $u, v \in {\mathbb{R}}$ and $\mathbf{T} > 0$, we have the following weak convergence in $D\left([0,\mathbf{T}]\right)^2$ under $\nu_{\mathbf{q}}$.
