{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.636538+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb99858640718efd6df666cc5fee9cd849e1dff80ed7a32a6a185d205a933a71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2506.17470, 'The coalescent of a sample from a linear-fractional branching process'] Let $m \ge 0$ and $\tau$ be an ultrametric oriented tree with node depths $x_1, \dots, x_{k-1}  \in  \{1,\ldots, T\}$ and  $x_0=T$. The likelihood function of the parameters $(p,r)$ given $\{\mathbf{T}_k = \tau, N_T=k+m\}$ is

