where $\mathbf{M}_{k,m}:=\{(m_0,m_1,\dots, m_{k-1})\in\mathbb{Z}_+^k: m_0+\cdots +m_{k-1}=m\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.589005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fb9a66006086d5f59214eee4839494dbf356e01d52470e641b6ebbb6bba5ab3a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] For any $0\leq t\leq T$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$, it holds that 
