{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.401331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc105131f53c23440817a8d1c927c6ef1396816c54d96dc7777e9eb234a26368","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 25 (\cite{Motivic_Igusa_Zeta_Function}) of arXiv:2609.03976, '2609.03976'] Let $X$ be a smooth complex algebraic variety, let $\mathfrak a\subseteq\mathcal O_X$ be a nonzero coherent ideal sheaf, and let
		$\mu:Y\longrightarrow X$ be a log resolution of $\mathfrak a$. Suppose $E_{i}(i \in S)$ are the irreducible components of $\mu^{*}(\mathfrak{a})$ and relative canonical divisor $K_{Y/X}$ such that $\mu^{*}(\mathfrak{a})=\sum_{i \in S}N_{i}E_{i}$ and $K_{Y/X}=\sum_{i \in S}(\nu_{i}-1)E_{i}$. Then the motivic zeta function of $\mathfrak{a}$, denoted by $Z^{\mathrm{mot}}_{\mathfrak{a}}(s)$, can be calculated by
		\begin{flalign*}
			Z^{\mathrm{mot}}_{\mathfrak{a}}(s)=\sum_{J \subset S}[\mathring{E}_{J}]\prod_{i \in J}\frac{\mathbb{L}-1}{\mathbb{L}^{N_{i}s+\nu_{i}}-1},
		\end{flalign*}
		where $\mathring{E}_{J}:=(\cap_{i \in J}E_{i})\setminus (\cup_{j \notin J}E_{j})$. Here we call $(N_{i},\nu_{i})(i \in S)$ the data of the log resolution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

