{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc430517a9cec09130f03cbe6eaab2d16facbac96b8b3b50ac5d44c8b3b69cde","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $q\geq 2$ be an integer and $a\in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfy $\sum_ka_k^2=1$. Then for all $n$, 
