{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.739551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc460dacf05144636859eb228dfce70693e6be4e7378c9617f9af54d99aac714","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] Let $\gamma\in \R, \gamma > 0$ be fixed. Let $0 < \alpha < 1$. Then
		\begin{align}
			&\JS_{G_{\alpha}}^{\gamma}(\mu_0||\mu_1) \geq 0 \;\;\forall \mu_0,\mu_1 \in \Gauss(\Hcal),
			\\
			&\JS_{G_{\alpha}}^{\gamma}(\mu_0||\mu_1) = 0 \equivalent \mu_0 = \mu_1 \equivalent m_0 = m_1, C_0 = C_1.
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.296956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc48d4623c2ef57ea636dd19c778cef7eee71dfc3c5b7ffa3f78e7d8e70b248c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:characterization of arXiv:2601.00291, 'The probability of connection between two vertices cannot be monotone with the distance fo'] Let $a,b,c\in[0,1]$ and $\lambda\in (0,\infty)$ arbitrary, define the function:
\begin{align*}
    f_{\lambda}(t)=ae^{-t\lambda}+be^{-(1-t)\lambda}-ce^{-\lambda},\ \forall t\in[0,1].
\end{align*} 
Then, it holds
\begin{align*}
    \min_{t\in[0,1]}f_{\lambda}(t)=\begin{cases}
    f_{\lambda}(1) &\text{, if } \frac{b}{a}\leqslant  e^{-\lambda};\\
    f_{\lambda}(0) &\text{, if } \frac{b}{a}\geqslant e^{\lambda};\\
    f_{\lambda}(t_0) &\text{, for some } t_0\in(0,1)\text{ if } e^{-\lambda}< \frac{b}{a}<  e^{\lambda}.
