{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.703344+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc6879d0e71e8b362b7fd8e49a3da60ac9e935226a1b0e0e5a06433c98fbaf55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 38 of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] Let $G_i$ be a sequence of Lie groups and  $\phi _i : G_i \to G$ a sequence of good approximations. Assume $G$ is a Lie group and the sequence $G_i$ has the NSS property. Then $\mathfrak{g}$, the  Lie algebra of $G$, admits an ideal $\mathfrak{h} \trianglelefteq \mathfrak{g}$ with $\mathfrak{g}/ \mathfrak{h}$ nilpotent and 
