{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.775139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc73ca1a0a4e8766289c73591769a4a32f3307178b21fef707c862047afd70ce","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For any $h\le 0$, $x>0$, and $r\in(0,1/2]$, we have
