        A^B_{ij} \overset{a.s.}{=} \mathbf{1}\{U_{ij}\le W_B(U_i,U_j)\}, \qquad i,j \in \nbb.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.555163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc870793358f44d360929d4b5432025a834bb559a887190a560bf566832962c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma compare_towers_final of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Let $s\geq r\geq 1$ be integers and let $a_1, \dots a_r$ and $ b_1,\dots, b_s>0$ be (strictly) positive real numbers.
	Let 
\begin{align}
	h_a(u)&=f(a_1f(a_2\dots f(a_r u)\dots))\\ h_b(u)&=f(b_1f(b_2\dots f(b_s u)\dots)).
\end{align}	
	Then if $r<s$, we have $h_a(u)\lll h_b(u)$. 
	The same is true if $r=s$ and if the largest $i\in [r]$ such $a_i\neq b_i$ is such that $a_i<b_i$ and $i>1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.628525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc8cfb903fa490a00b4c568595d524ef230ca362cd67d1c1dc3584381207be3e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] We consider the class $\Ec$ of potentials $P$ which can either be written as 
	\begin{equation}
	P(x) = \begin{cases}
		C \int_0^{|x|}{ g(t) \d t} \quad & |x| \leq A\\
		\infty \quad & |x| > A
	\end{cases} 
	\end{equation} 
	for some $A \in (0,\infty]$, $C > 0$ and a convex function $g : [0,A] \to \R$ with $g(0) = 0$, or are the weak limit of such measures.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.323975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc97829bf02472043ebeadb74fb47d348283fd7f33876d01ad5c9f86062e6126","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor SpR-initial of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] There exists a unique $S$-presentably symmetric monoidal structure on $\ul\Sp_{S\triangleright T}^{\mathcal R}\coloneqq\ul\Sp_{S\triangleright T}^{\mathcal R}(\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T,*})$ with unit $\mathbb S\coloneqq\Sigma^\infty(1_+)$, and this makes it into the initial ${\mathcal R}$-stable $S$-presentably symmetric monoidal $T$-$\infty$-category. 
    \begin{proof}
        Existence and uniqueness of the symmetric monoidal refinement were recalled in Remark~(rk:idempotent-algs-are-algs of the paper), and this is initial by Lemma~(lemma:unique-algebra-structure-initial of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.832236+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fc996d96461c60fc9e9d1051a1175743332b12d8d1be0c1874c805896f2d30ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma w infity of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] Let $\gamma>0$. 
