{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.719971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcbca423522759eb72388270079d9fbdf7f0ea932b315013e977d21f296514dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: main of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] Let $(\mathcal X_\omega,\mathcal E_\omega)_{\omega\in\Omega}$ be a random graph in $\mathbb{R}^n$ with random weights $(\sigma_\omega\colon \mathcal E_\omega\to[\lambda,\Lambda])_{\omega\in\Omega}$ and random means $(\theta^\omega)_{\omega\in\Omega}$ with $0<\lambda<\Lambda$, satisfying the graph Assumption (ass: graph of the paper) almost surely, such that $(\mathcal X_\omega,\mathcal E_\omega,\sigma_\omega,\theta_\omega)$ is stationary.

For every $\varepsilon>0$ let $({\mathcal X_{\omega,\varepsilon}},\mathcal E_{\omega,\varepsilon})$ be the rescaled random graph and $\mathcal{A}_{\omega,\varepsilon}$ be the rescaled action functional defined in Section (sec: rescaled graph of the paper). Let $A_\omega$ be the homogenized action functional given in (equation eq: hom action of the paper).
Then we have almost surely $\mathcal{A}_{\omega,\varepsilon}\stackrel{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}_{\varepsilon\to 0} A_\omega$ in the sense that the following two conditions hold almost surely:
\begin{enumerate}
