{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313447+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc5345b073f7142a2a09073128ff6ad72f2028488b9f9da7f67bb73ba718156","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 35 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] For each $N \in \N$, we let $U^N : [0,1] \times \T^d \to \R^d$ denote the truncated sum
