{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.725526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fce029fbd10d2dbedd7272126f80a20407401f7030fc24a73d80796733fa5691","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma expansion-curvature-0 of arXiv:2609.00108, 'The double sphere solution in the liquid drop model'] Let $\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}$ be the surface parametrized as in (equation defSigma0ve12 of the paper), with $P$ and $Q$ defined as in (equation defPQ of the paper). Let $h = h(r)$ be a $C^{2, \alpha}$-small normal perturbation of $\Sigma_0^{\varepsilon, +,1}$ as in (equation def-np of the paper). Then: for all $r \in (1,2)$ we have
