{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.127518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fce7f9332a79deef21641631c0f0eab9ed231740e1c187c92b610d2925d5576e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 (Empirical Fourier CLT) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] There is a $\lambda_d$-conull set $E_\eta\subset\bR^d$ such that, for every
$\xi\in E_\eta$, every $m\geq1$, and every
$h_1,\ldots,h_m\in C_c^\infty(\bR^d;\bC)$,
\begin{equation}

    \bigl(Z_R(\xi;h_1),\ldots,Z_R(\xi;h_m)\bigr)
    \dto \bigl(G_\xi(h_1),\ldots,G_\xi(h_m)\bigr)
    \qquad\text{in }\bC^m,
\end{equation}
where the vector on the right is complex Gaussian with mean zero and
\begin{align}

    \E\!\left[G_\xi(h_a)\overline{G_\xi(h_b)}\right]
