{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.304674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd00a71b425d83291861d29775671ff02a3a69557a21c0591db9d3cc531526cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition jtpdf of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] For any $t>0,$ the joint probability density function of $A_t^{(\eta)}$ and $\left(\eta t+B^{(e)}_t\right)$ is given by
\begin{eqnarray*}
\!\!\!&\!\!\!&\mathbb P\left(A_t^{(\eta)} \in \mathrm{d} y, \eta t+B^{(e)}_t \in \mathrm{d} x\right) =\mathrm{e}^{\eta x-\frac{1}{2} \eta^2t} \frac{1}{y} \exp \left(-\frac{1+\mathrm{e}^{2 x}}{2 y}\right) \theta\left(\frac{\mathrm{e}^x}{y}, t\right) \mathrm{d} y \mathrm{d} x,
\end{eqnarray*}
where $$\theta(r, t)=\frac{r}{\sqrt{2 \pi^3 t}} \int_0^{\infty} \mathrm{e}^{\frac{\pi^2-u^2}{2 t}} \mathrm{e}^{-r \cosh u}\sinh (u) \sin \left(\frac{\pi u}{t}\right) \mathrm{d} u,\quad r>0,\,t>0.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

