{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.997980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd12ae1d7c35a4606f7b8ec8f2232867e3a757dc6e218f5e146ee83314cddd70","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:TGRAM of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $t_1,\dots, t_k$ be obtained by applying the Gram–Schmidt orthonormalization in $L^2$ to $\partial_{\xi_1}m^\varepsilon_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k}, \dots, \partial_{\xi_k} m^\varepsilon_{\xi_1,\dots, \xi_k}$, as described in (equation GRAM of the paper). Then, for each $j$, we have 
