{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.067421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd30cbf21c28c97aa4919df8a941459fac0c04adda396e17e53d5f135fbc5590","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:local_well_nonlinear of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $4\leq p<+\infty$ and $\theta$ satisfying (hyp_noise of the paper). Then for all $\omega_s\in L^0_{\mathcal{F}_s}\big(\Omega, B^{-\frac{2}{p}}_{g,2,p}\big),$ there exists a unique local p-solution $(\omega,\tau)$ of (equation main_ito of the paper) satisfying $\tau>s$ $\mathbb{P}-a.s.$ and
