{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.762122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd492ff6bac7af3b585dc3a50c4bb99c6e28c7ee44fca61f45c09e4a24e1c4d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dissipativemomentbound of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Suppose Assumption (ass:dissipative of the paper) holds and $X$ solves (equation eq:main_d of the paper).
Then, for $q\geq  1$, we have 
\begin{equation*}
   \expect{\|X(t)\|^{2q}} \leq 
   \begin{cases}
   \|X_0\|^{2q}e^{-q\alpha_2t}+
   R_q,& \text{if}\ q>1;\\
