{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.439164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd4cdca16d478dd6218e65bef9d728c2fb561d26dfdead3bc19248f35aebbea6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition neq gamma/gamma+1 joint invariance of arXiv:2505.05921, 'Limit Theorems for step reinforced random walks\\ with regularly varying memory'] {}
Let $\{S_n\}_{n\geq 0}$ be the SRRW-RVM with zero mean, unit variance innovation sequence $\{\xi_n\}$. Then:
    \begin{align*}
        \left(\overline{\boldsymbol{T}}_{n,\lfloor nt\rfloor}:t\geq 0\right)&\to_{\rm{w}} \left(\mathcal{\overline{W}}(t): t\geq 0\right) \quad \text{in $(D([0,\infty)),\mathcal{D})$,} \quad \text{for $p\in[0,\widehat{p})$},\\
        \left(\widetilde{\boldsymbol{T}}_{n,\lfloor nt\rfloor}: t\geq 0\right)&\to_{\rm{w}} \left(\widetilde{\mathcal{W}}(t): t\geq 0\right) \quad \text{in $(D([0,\infty)),\mathcal{D})$,} \quad \text{for $p=\widehat{p}$},\\
