{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.381103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcdd45a5e1cf4eca72e2f129f2ce9e132c475e61b6f056cc8d66aad3857ba5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2609.03116, '\bf \boldmath On the reconstruction of $n$-quasigroups of order $4$ and upper bounds on th'] Let $n \geq 2$, and $(A,G'''_n,p)$ be a partial $n$-quasigroup. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item if $(A,G'''_n,p)$ has more than one extension then all the extensions are cubical;
\item if $(A,G'''_n,p)$ has more than two extensions then it has a bicubical extension.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.982883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcf86f4e81719f441273e19a199b799244dc818aff6869180d127be41678b3b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1.2 of arXiv:2412.00708, 'Stochastic PDE approach to fluctuating interfaces'] We have
\begin{align}  
b_G^N(\eta,\varphi) & = \frac{K}{N^d} \sum_{p\in{\mathbb{T}}_N^d} 
\bar c_{p}(\eta)\varphi\left(\tfrac{p}N\right), \\

\Gamma_G^N(\eta,\varphi) & = \frac{K}{N^{2d}} \sum_{p\in{\mathbb{T}}_N^d} 
c_{p}(\eta) \varphi\left(\tfrac{p}N\right)^2.
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}  
\bar c_p(\eta) := c_p(\eta) (1-2\eta_p) = c_p(\eta) \Big(1_{\{\eta_p=0\}}
- 1_{\{\eta_p=1\}}\Big).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.619526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcfaac78d3c269d18ff3c4675b7797e78bf4486a4a09f685bf917db279f484f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] There exists a unique Borel measure $\lambda_g$ on $M$ such that for every chart $(V, \varphi)$ of $M$, with $\varphi = (x^1, \dots, x^d)$, and every $B \in \Bcal(M)$ with $B \subseteq V$,
    \begin{equation} 
        \lambda_g(B) = \int_{\varphi(B)} \varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} \; d\lambda_d,
    \end{equation}
    where $G \coloneqq \det[g_{jk}]$ is the determinant of the metric components $g_{jk} \coloneqq g\!\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x^j}, \frac{\partial}{\partial x^k}\right)$ in the chart $(V, \varphi)$, and $\varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} = \sqrt{\abs{G}} \circ \varphi^{-1}$ denotes the pushforward of $\sqrt{\abs{G}}$ on $V$ along $\varphi$. Moreover, $\lambda_g$ is diffuse, $\sigma$-finite, and satisfies $\lambda_g(B) < \infty$ for every $B \in \widehat{\Bcal}(M)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd3fe469b3a9e3d37a646650617b0d4de3b3bd3d9845ea1acc535cc78620e7b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop compatibility of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $V,V'\in\mathfrak{C}$, $V\subset V'$, and $x,y\in\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ such that for every $u\in V'\setminus V$ there is a point $z\in\overline{V}$ that separates $u$ from $x,y$ in $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V'}$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \mathfrak{d}_{V'}(x,y)=\mathfrak{d}_V(x,y).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.801203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd68b72cf64a8c3b715f4bbad57a4b56eb34864b20d4a090f058cc739188352","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Cf. Theorem 4.6, \cite{ab0}) of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
