{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.606977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdea442df01598223bb5e1999b9d686ce4e4cd248a73dd4e5a6e1654946346c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:MainTheorem of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] (Mean field large-population limit) Let $0<T<\infty$ be given and let Assumptions (A:molarBdd of the paper)-(A:AssumptionMomentFiniteness of the paper) hold. Then, the sequence of measure-valued processes $\{\bm{\mu}_{t}^{\zeta}\}_{t \in[0, T]} \in \mathbb{D}_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ is relatively compact in $\mathbb{D}_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ and it converges in distribution to $\{\boldsymbol{\xi}_t\}_{t \in [0,T]} \in C_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ as $\zeta \rightarrow 0$, where each $\xi_t^j$ is the unique solution to
\begin{align}
   &\left\langle  f, \xi_{t}^{j}\right\rangle = \left\langle f, \xi_0^{j}\right\rangle + \int_0^t \left\langle (\mathcal{L}_{j}f)(x,v), \xi_{s}^{j}(dx,dv)\right\rangle ds\notag\\
      &\phantom{=} + \sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\int_0^t \int_{\tilde{\mathbb{X}}^{(\ell)} \otimes \tilde{\mathbb{V}}^{(\ell)}}\frac{1}{\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}!}K_\ell(\bm{x},\bm{v})\biggl(-\sum_{r=1}^{\alpha_{\ell j}}f\left(x_r^{(j)},v_r^{(j)}\right)+\int_{\mathbb{Y}^{(\ell)} \otimes \mathbb{V}'^{(\ell)}}\left(\sum_{r=1}^{\beta_{\ell j}}f\left(y_r^{(j)},{v'}_{r}^{(j)}\right)\right)\\
      &\phantom{=}\times m_{\ell}\left(\bm{y},\bm{v'}|\bm{x},\bm{v}\right)d\bm{y}d\bm{v'}\biggr)\lambda^{(\ell)}[\xi_{s}](d\bm{x}, d\bm{v}) ds.\notag
