{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.957675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdebb4e002f89b1bf712afdf7c3c24ddd3b66ce10615a9b54df44e996a0e73c4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:graph-matrix-for-shape of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] Given a shape \(\tau\), its graph matrix \(M_\tau\) is indexed by boundary labelings.
For boundary labelings \(S\) of \(U_\tau\) and \(T\) of \(V_\tau\), define
\[
    \mathsf{M} _{\tau}[S,T]
    =
    \sum_{\substack{
        \sigma:\,V(\tau)\to \mathbb N \\
        \sigma \text{ is a mapping of } \tau \\
        \sigma(U_\tau)=S,\ \sigma(V_\tau)=T
    }}
    \prod_{e\in E(\tau)}
    \chi_{t(e)}\bigl(G[\sigma(e)]\bigr).
\]
Here, if \(e=\{x,y\}\) is an edge between a square vertex and a circle vertex, then
\(G[\sigma(e)]\) denotes the corresponding entry \(G[\sigma(x),\sigma(y)]\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.795356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdeec1e787407df4133ba64e66a93cbdebff5e5640db7a1ffe6de473041112cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2608.17509, '2608.17509'] Let \((T_L)_{L\geq1}\) be positive trace-class contractions on a Hilbert space. Assume that
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item \(\sup_{L\geq1}L^{-1}\operatorname{tr}(T_L)<\infty\);
\item there is a measurable \(r:(0,\infty)\to[0,1]\) with \(r\in L^1(0,\infty)\) such that, for every \(m\geq1\),
\[
\lim_{L\to\infty}
\frac{1}{L}\operatorname{tr}(T_L^m)
=
\frac{1}{2\pi}
\int_0^\infty r(\xi)^m\,\mathrm{d}\xi.
\]
\end{enumerate}
Then, for each \(t>-1\),
\[
\lim_{L\to\infty}
\frac{1}{L}\log\det(\operatorname{Id}+tT_L)
=
\frac{1}{2\pi}
\int_0^\infty \log\bigl(1+t\,r(\xi)\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\xi,
\]
locally uniformly for \(t\) in compact subsets of \((-1,\infty)\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.970997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdf2af602caa2ffe81bc9020a315262d3714abf3c24b8b701cbf99d671ec377d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rmulmc_discretization of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}$, $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}{}'$ denote the kernels for~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) and~(eq:ULMC of the paper) respectively, and let $\boldsymbol{P}$ denote the kernel for~(eq:ULD of the paper) run for time $h$.
