{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.322827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe2aca9ffa960b1bc048c6d95ff72c475ac9f7b115603509dbe63357cd4c31ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:canonical-tensoring of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $S\subset T$ be any cleft, and let ${\mathcal{C}}$ be any pointed $S$-cocomplete $T$-$\infty$-category. Then there exists a unique $S$-bilinear bifunctor 
