    such that $1_+\otimes{-}$ is the identity of ${\mathcal{C}}$.
    \begin{proof}
        Passing to adjuncts, the claim translates to saying that there is a unique $S$-cocontinuous $T$-functor $\theta\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to\ul{\textup{Fun}}_T^\text{$S$-cc}(\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T,*},{\mathcal{C}})$ such that postcomposing with $\smash{\ev_{1^+}\colon{\textup{Fun}}_T^\text{$S$-cc}(\ul\Spc_{S\triangleright T,*},{\mathcal{C}})\to{\mathcal{C}}}$ recovers the identity. But $\ev_{1^+}$ is an equivalence by Proposition~(prop:univ-prop-*-cc-param of the paper), so this is obvious.
