{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.582578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe3441d17104e251769b9fa43bbc84b1a716172bb0a8ba664447bc8063e31744","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Assume that $D(\mathcal F_{\beta})\cap X^{a}_{p}\neq \emptyset$ and  let $\mathsf{P}_\beta\in X^{a}_{p}$ be the unique minimizer of $\mathcal F_{\beta}$ on $X^{a}_{p}$. Put $\Pi_\beta:= \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_\beta)$.
   Then for any $\mathsf{P}\in X^{a}_{p}\cap D(\mathcal F_{\beta})$
   \begin{align*}
       \frac{\beta }{2a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}} \mathscr W_{gap,p}^2( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}),\Pi_\beta)\leq \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P})-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_\beta)\leq \frac{a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}}{2\beta } \abs{\partial \mathcal F_{\beta}}^2(\mathsf{P}).
    \end{align*}
    Moreover, any curve of maximal slope $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t>0}$ w.r.t. $\abs{\partial \mathcal F_{\beta}}$ in $X^{a}_{p}$ satisfies for every $t\geq t_0>0$
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\beta }{2a^{\frac{2-p}{p}}}\mathscr W_{gap,p}^2( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_t),\Pi_\beta)\leq \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_t)-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_\beta)\leq (\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t_0})-\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_\beta))e^{-2\beta a^{\frac{p-2}{p}}(t-t_0)}.
    \end{align*}
Moreover, for $0<\beta<\beta'$ 
\begin{align*}
       \mathscr W_{gap,p}^2(\Pi_{\beta},\Pi_{\beta'})\leq \frac{2(\beta'-\beta)}{\beta}\max\left(\int f( \mathsf{s}_0)^{\frac{p}{p-2}}\Pi_\beta(d \mathsf{s}) ,\int f( \mathsf{s}_0)^{\frac{p}{p-2}}\Pi_{\beta'}(d \mathsf{s}) \right)^{\frac{2-p}{p}}\mathcal W^{int}(\mathsf{P}_{\beta})
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.667168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe35656f9d11451ffd88ae3d3ed7de373eb6ad7ec4abbc110fbf3d94a87eb748","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:single-concentration of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) holds,   $\Exp ( X^2) < \infty$, and $\Exp X =0$. There exists $\varepsilon_0 \in (0,1)$ such that the following holds. 
