\end{equation}
where $p_i(k) = n_i(k)/E_k$ is the modal distribution defined in (equation eq:modal-distribution-def of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.575781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe54344b21fec65d625f773b7d658a5aaab57082955dbf79829c1fc4a0187474","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Coroll-probtauUN-002b of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] Assume conditions of Theorem (Theor-probIntUN-002 of the paper). 
