{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.646872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe5c6659f1f65fd5f1c2c6d1ce03a48f1cf3d25207025824b63d6d0ba48d1187","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 104 (Auxiliary fixed-sample critical boundary) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] Assume $T>0$ and $C\ne0$.  Let $G_C\sim N(0,C)$ and
