{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.763260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe68efdc82fd82aca1180a4ec356f8cc8deba9ded4cf555090e6bf0a36f25d3d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Integration by parts bound) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $Y\geq1$, $X, Z>0$, and suppose that $w$ is a smooth function of compact supported on $[Z, 2Z]$ so that $w^{(j)}(t)\ll \left(\frac{X}{Z}\right)^j$. Also suppose that $\phi$ is a smooth function and satisfies, for $j\geq 2$, $\phi^{(j)}(t)\ll \frac{Y}{Z^j}$, for some $R$ with $Y/X\geq R$ and all $t$ in the support of $w$. If $|\phi^\prime(t)|\gg Y/Z$ for all $t\in [Z, 2Z]$, then 
