{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.012146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe6acc2d216b75c1f0ca920ca692229afbe03a123245a3aab2f2c9d98a2a24b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] For $\eps \in (0,1)$ small enough, $t \in [0,\sfT]$, we have
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{aligned}
			|R^\eps_{\lambda^\eps_t}-r(t)|\cdot \ind_{G^\eps_\sfN} & \le C\left\{\|J^\eps_\cdot-1\|_\infty+\eps \sup_{0 \le s \le \sfT} |W_s|\right\}e^{Ct}\cdot \ind_{G^\eps_\sfN},\\
			|\Theta^\eps_{\lambda^\eps_t}-\theta(t)|\cdot \ind_{G^\eps_\sfN} &\le \left\{ \sum_{k \ge 1} \ind_{[t_{k-1},\thinspace t_k)}(t)\left(2\delta+ 2\varepsilon^p \sup_{[0,\thinspace \sfT]} |B_t|\right)\right\}\cdot \ind_{G^\eps_\sfN}.
