{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.747024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe823f3a61c46e355b7b40dc92593c73f72fd279d6338a43cdc1bbfc33cecce0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:conv_carac_poly of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $X_{11}$ be regularly varying with index $\alpha\in (0,2)$ and consider the characteristic polynomial $p_n(z) := \det ({\bf I} - z{\mathbf Y}_n)$. Then, we have the convergence in distribution, for the topology of local uniform convergence in $\mathbb{D}$
