{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.726979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe9fe4dc10f46cf304302d5da8825cb803522e1cddfb5f1643dfdbd6bb65d97a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:full HOMFLY complex of arXiv:2608.29986, 'Khovanov-Rozansky homology over $\F[U,V]$'] Let $K \subset S^3$ be a knot. There is a $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} \oplus\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} \oplus\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} $-graded finitely generated free chain complex $(\mathit{CH}(K), \partial)$ over $\ensuremath{\mathbb{F}} [U,V]$ such that
