\end{equation}
where $\mu_{n}$ denotes the sample Fr\'{e}chet\ mean of $(x_1, x_2, \ldots x_n) \in M^n$, and $\|\cdot\|_{x}$ denotes the Riemannian norm induced by the Riemannian metric $\langle ~,~\rangle_{x}$ on $T_{x}M$. The inequality in ((ineq:key of the paper)) is strict unless $x,x_1,…,x_n$ all lie in a single totally geodesic flat submanifold of $M$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.256828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee1b18603588cc01979ed6a5eb0d1327e938e01f77afc4773c4b6638aa92157","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma jnestimate of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\mathrm{D}=\mathrm{O}(1)$}, and recall {\small$\mathfrak{t}_{\mathbf{Av}}=N^{-2/3-10\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}$}. With high probability, we have 

