{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.243967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee80312b97bc18ae680080a630b8fa223965a1a6b7694c4707c492877506a9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:poles of arXiv:2607.01463, 'Two Multi--Draw Coupon Collector models with different retention rules'] Set
\begin{equation}
\phi_{N}(s):=\Bigg(1-\frac{\binom{N-s}{d}}{\binom{N}{d}}\Bigg)^{-1}=\Bigg(1-\prod_{j=0}^{d-1}\left(1-\frac{s}{N-j}\right)\Bigg)^{-1}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation} 
Q_{N}(s):=1-\prod_{j=0}^{d-1}\left(1-\frac{s}{N-j}\right).
\end{equation}
Then, the poles of $\phi_N(s)$ are the zeros of the polynomial $Q_N(s)$. Clearly, $s=0$ is a simple pole of $\phi_{N}(s)$. Moreover, if \(d\) is odd, then the only real pole is \(s=0\). In case where \(d\) is even, then the only real poles are
    \[
    s=0
    \qquad\text{and}\qquad
    s=2N-d+1;
    \]
In particular, all poles of $\phi_N(s)$ are simple. The $d-1$ nonzero zeros of $Q_{N}(s)$ are denoted as $\omega_{1,N},\, \omega_{2,N},\cdots,\omega_{d-1,N}$ (for all positive integer values of $d$; when $d=1$ there are none, and $s=0$ is the only pole). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.329735+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee915597f7fef25c901763a802d3cd488fb48c6cef247be861ba2f0ab0f0c1d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.23585, 'The one-period Kyle model has one equilibrium'] If $(\phi,P)$ is a quasi-equilibrium, then
	\begin{equation}
		\phi(v)=\frac{\sigma}{\tau}(v-\mu)
		\qquad\text{for Lebesgue-almost every }v\in\R\,,
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		P(Y_\phi)=\mu+\lambda Y_\phi
		\qquad\text{almost surely}\,,
	\end{equation}
	where
	\[
		\lambda
		=\frac{\Cov(V,Y_\phi)}{\Var(Y_\phi)}
		=\frac{\tau}{2\sigma}\,.
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.186185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_feea07beaa6439cc51e5fd35a8f00489975ebe32251608a217ce4712bb16dad9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 ({\cite[Lemma 5.3) of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] {cai2024quasi}}]
