{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.705773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fef4688b2456adb307b3e4429929556fc53266b2bc4289e84f489589d21499ee","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem derivative of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $D$ be one of the divisors $F_\infty$ and $nQ$, $Q$ a point of $S$, and put $S'=S$, respectively $S'=S-Q$. Then

