{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.556192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff21f6ce700916f7a84e735208987758fd504a82031a7308188181bbc551a8f7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Let 	$1\leq r \leq p \leq m$ and let $m_1,\dots,m_p\geq 1$, $p_1,\dots,p_r\geq 1$ with $m_1+\dots+m_p=m$ and $p_1+\dots+p_r=p$. Let $\sigma=(\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_p)$ be a permutation of $[p]$. Let $\mathcal{P}=(P_1,\dots, P_R)$ be a random partition of $[p]$ and $\Pi=(R;|P_1|,\dots,|P_r|;\Sigma)$, where $\Sigma$ is the valid ordering associated to $\mathcal{P}$.
