	where the $o(1)$ holds as $s\to\infty$, uniformly in $t,x,y,f$ (but depending on $\alpha,\beta,L,a,b,\varepsilon$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.867963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff408d4179ae99f5c64b1a414e7c9eddda653c32cc43a9e6adb2dc08100f5b01","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem tree-two-edge-residual of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] Let $1<p<2$, let $x_0,x_1\ge0$, let
