{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.824256+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff69394e58d9be8305db46970b014a9ed434bd347dc5054436223c281a1a525a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 39 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] Under the assumption of Theorem \ref{thm-DJ}, there exists a constant $C>0$ depending on $\Lambda$ and $\delta$ such that for any $J\in{\mathcal J}$, the following estimate holds:
