{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.647820+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffa1cf7c9ef5f13f4ded88d314d138d5dfffb7163e2f9c5981649b8c1c7d76b2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def Surface tension of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $L,M\geq 1$ and $\beta>0$. The surface tension of the model on $\mathcal{R}(L,M)$ at inverse temperature $\beta$ is defined as
