{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.356969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffb28ee8828bf7599c1763cfba235420f28a9a6559d4036617aa87907bf04c86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that  Assumption {\rm\ref{A2}} holds. Then the class of measures $\{\mu^x_{t}\}_{t\in\RR}$ given in Lemma $\ref{Le3.3}$ is an evolution system of measures for $\{P^x_{s,t}\}_{t\ge s}$. Moreover, for any Lipschitz continuous function $\phi$ on $\RR^m$, $t\ge s$ and $x\in \RR^m$,
