{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.283608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffbf132d0aea5bd02cb44e4bda693c6c3c59b5d622042f2aedfe3d1095d6e405","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Fix \(H\in(\frac{1}{2},1)\) and \(\beta<H\). Assume that \(G,H\) are Lipschitz continuous and globally bounded, \(F \) is $\gamma$-H\"older continuous \(\gamma<1\) such that \(\gamma+\beta>1\). Then, there exists a unique weak solution to the following Young-It\^o SDE
