{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.189069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffdddff8387fdd26328750807f59514ed27222770cd568203e63eea8e287d995","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2606.30938, 'Poissonian potential measures for refracted-reflected L\'evy processes'] Let $p,q \geq 0$ and $\lambda, \gamma> 0$. Then, for $x,b \in [0,a]$, we have that
